  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 24d13becfb3100d4d8970a3eb64c00bc, type: 3}
  m_Name: PlaytestTexts
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Clover.Runtime::Clover.UI.PlaytestTexts
  Version: Combat Playtest 0.4 (unreleased)
  WhatsNew: "<color=#E8C77A>What this playtest is</color>\n\nA testbed for the combat. It grows with each update as the fighting is reworked. Everything is open: try anything, and tell us what felt good, what felt wrong and what you did not understand.\n\n<color=#E8C77A>New in 0.4 (phase 3: reactions)</color>\n\n\u2022  <b>Reactions, all 55.</b> When an affliction lands on an enemy that already carries another element's, the two react, and every pair of elements does something of its own: <b>Flashover</b> (Fire and Lightning: the Static discharges through the flame), <b>Steam</b> (Fire and Water: a scalding puff), <b>Thermal Shock</b> (Fire and Ice: it cracks, and your next heavy splits it), <b>Capsize</b> (Wind and Water: it goes down), <b>Smoulder</b> (Dark and Fire: the fire sinks in, deepens, then flares), <b>Fish Poison</b> (Poison and Water: the heavily dosed float up stunned) and 49 more. The guide to effects has an entry for each, with its numbers.\n\u2022  <b>Many ask for your weapon.</b> A reaction often leaves a state on the enemy for a few seconds: a crust of rime your heavy blows out of its far side, a crack your heavy splits, a stone that rocks until your third blow throws it down, coils your blows draw tighter. Some answer its death (Smoulder flares, Shut in the Dark's jar breaks, Drowned Weight bursts).\n\u2022  <b>Where you stand matters.</b> Several throw things away from you, past the enemy (Carried Embers, Rime, Red Hot, Golden Feathers, Thunder Gust): put the enemy between you and the others.\n\u2022  <b>How they come.</b> A reaction comes once, then rests on that enemy for a few seconds (most 4 s, the pairs three apart 6 s, a few their own: Steam 3 s, Shut in the Dark and The Grudge 8 s). What a reaction lays starts no reaction of its own. Anything can set one off: your weapon, spells, marks, the charged blade, strikes, even an enemy wet from the river. The order never matters, but Seized (Lightning and Water) and The Grudge (Dark and Lightning) need two Static or more on the enemy.\n\u2022  <b>The great resist.</b> What holds or slows an enemy takes half on an elite and nothing on a god; some reactions give elites and gods their own numbers instead (each entry says).\n\u2022  <b>You see the name.</b> A reaction's name rises over the enemy for a moment. Each reaction's own look comes later: for now there is a puff in its two colours and whatever it does (a discharge, a burst, fires, a slick).\n\u2022  <b>Weave to react.</b> Carry two elements: your weapon lays the first and your spells, the charged blade and the R2 strike lay the second.\n\u2022  <b>Not yet:</b> the duo branches' shapes that change a reaction come in a later update. Many reactions are simpler than their full design, and each entry in the guide says what is still to come under \"Not yet\": the side a blow comes from (Rime, Mock Suns), things to pick up (Shining Herb, Firebloom), standing stones and trunks (Anvil Stone, Frost Heave, Girdled), The Grudge's cloud answering the enemy's blow, Black Chain's shared wounds, and others.\n\n<color=#E8C77A>New in 0.3 (phase 2: two elements and the Hand)</color>\n\n\u2022  <b>Two elements at once.</b> Carry a first and a second element (the same one twice is all in). Each spell is cast in its own element, lays its own affliction and is drawn in its own colour and stuff.\n\u2022  <b>The altars set both.</b> Carrying one element, use another altar to carry its element as your second; use the altar of the element you carry to go all in. Carrying two (or all in), an altar starts again with its element alone. Before you press, the altar's prompt says which it will do (\"Carry Lightning as second\", \"Carry Fire all in\", \"Carry Ice alone\"). You arrive carrying Fire.\n\u2022  <b>Your weapon lays the first element only.</b> Weapon blows lay the first element's affliction, even with the second's root mark learned. A mixed branch's own marks are the exception: Biting Wind, Wet Seed and the rest lay both of theirs. The second comes from your spells, the charged blade and the R2 strike, so two afflictions meet on an enemy when you weave weapon and spell.\n\u2022  <b>The charged blade takes the landed spell's element.</b> Flame Wave charges it with Fire, Thunderclap with Lightning; only that cast's own first landing counts. A duo spell charges it with the first of its pair.\n\u2022  <b>Strikes for each element.</b> L2 with R1 (RB) is the first element's strike, L2 with R2 (RT) the second's, and neither costs mana. Carrying one element, or all in, R2 is the deep strike for 20 mana as before.\n\u2022  <b>The rest menu.</b> A rest fire now opens a menu: Set the Hand, The chart, Leave the fire. Closing the chart brings you back to it.\n\u2022  <b>The Hand.</b> Your four spells in a diamond laid out like the buttons, the surge in the middle. Choose a slot to see only what can go there, grouped by element with each spell's role and one line; the weapon skill button shows the numbers. Pick the surge from either element. Suggested Hand fills it for you; three saved Hands keep a Hand for each kind of fight (use wears one, the heavy attack keeps yours there). Once you set a Hand the slots stop filling themselves. The Hand never changes which elements you carry.\n\u2022  <b>The spell diamond</b> colours each slot by its own spell's element and names the R2 strike for the second element.\n\u2022  <b>Duo branches</b> (Plasma and the other mixes) are in force only while both of their elements are carried; a duo spell sits in a slot like any other.\n\u2022  <b>Slots open as you go, outside the playtest.</b> In the full game you start with two slots (West and North) and the surge; East opens when the Champion of the Gate falls and South when the Fire god falls, and they stay open from then on. The Hand shows a shut slot and says what opens it. In the playtest every slot is open.\n\u2022  <b>Not yet:</b> in the full game the second element is still chosen nowhere (the hub's braziers give one element); it comes when the hub's choice is reworked. Duo surges, shapes and the designed starter Hands for each element come with the reshaped trees.\n\n<color=#E8C77A>New in 0.2 (phase 1: spells on cooldowns, mana for big moves, the charged blade, infused strikes and the spell diamond)</color>\n\n\u2022  <b>The charged blade.</b> A spell from one of your four slots that lands charges your weapon with its element. Your next three blows that land carry it: each hits 20% harder and lays the element's affliction, and the third does one thing more (Fire leaves the ground burning, Light throws a ray, Poison makes the poison bite at once, and so on). You see it on the weapon: flame and embers along the edge for Fire, lightning crackling along it, frost for Ice. Three pips beside the spell diamond count the blows left. A new spell that lands gives three fresh blows.\n\u2022  <b>Infused strikes.</b> Hold L2 (LT) and press R1 (RB): your weapon's own move with your element on it, shaped by the weapon (the Katana's drawing cut throws Burning Edge along its arc, the Hammer's drop lays it in a circle, the Spear's thrust in a line). L2 with R2 (RT) is the deep strike, the heavier version, for 20 mana. Each button waits 8 s, and fighting with the weapon shortens the wait as it does a spell's. A strike counts as a weapon blow (mana, shorter spell waits) but never charges the blade. On the keyboard: hold Left Ctrl and click the left or right mouse button. Every element has its own pair; the guide to effects lists them.\n\u2022  <b>The spell diamond</b> in the bottom-right corner replaces the spell line: your four slots laid out like the face buttons, each with its picture, its button and a shade that sweeps back as its wait runs out, the surge in the middle, the two strikes under it. It is small at all times and grows while L2 is held, with each spell's name. Buttons are named for the pad or keys you use last, and follow your rebinding.\n\u2022  <b>Hunger</b> (Dark's surge, paid in health) now waits 25 s after it ends before it can be lit again.\n\n\u2022  <b>Four spell slots on the L2 layer.</b> Hold L2 (LT) and press Square, Triangle, Circle or Cross (X, Y, B, A) to cast the spell in that slot. On the keyboard, 1, 2, 3 and 4 cast them directly. While L2 is held the face buttons are spells only: no flask, skill, dodge or use.\n\u2022  <b>The surge is a tap of L2.</b> Tap it and let go quickly. On the keyboard it stays on F.\n\u2022  <b>The weapon skill has its own button:</b> Triangle (Y), or Q. Holding the heavy button now gives the charged heavy only.\n\u2022  <b>Basic spells cost no mana.</b> Each slot waits 6 to 12 s after a cast instead. Fighting with the weapon brings spells back sooner: a light blow that lands takes 0.3 s off every waiting slot, a heavy blow 0.6 s, a perfect guard 2 s, a perfect dodge 1.5 s, a finisher 3 s.\n\u2022  <b>Mana is for the big moves:</b> the surge, the weapon skill and each element's one larger spell (Meteor Leap, Seven Flashes, Sky Dance, Winter Wall, Poured Blade, Elder Tree, Grave of Swords, Daybreak, One by One; the built duo spells too). You enter each area at half. Out of a fight mana rises to half and stops there; above half it is kept. A fight always starts with at least half.\n\u2022  <b>Filling the slots.</b> Your element's own spell starts in West, and each spell you learn fills the next empty slot. At a rest fire, choose a learned spell on the chart and press use to put it in the next slot round. The Hand screen comes in the next update.\n\u2022  <b>Controls:</b> the pause menu's controls page has rows for the spell layer and the four slots, on the pad and on the keys.\n\u2022  <b>Not yet:</b> marks that only made the base spell cheaper do nothing for now, and some spell details on the chart still describe the old way of casting; the trees are reshaped later. Two elements at once and the Hand screen come in the next update.\n\n<color=#E8C77A>New in 0.1</color>\n\n\u2022  <b>The Proving Ground</b>, where the playtest begins: a rest fire, a rack of every weapon (the Storm Katana and the Sun-Spear among them), altars for every element, training dummies (one still, one that fights back with red and pale blows, and one carrying each element's affliction), pens to let out the castle's soldiers and the Fire land's people, gates to Narukami and Khepharu, and doors to the Castle, the Summit, Sun City and the Sun Court.\n\u2022  <b>Playtest rules.</b> Resting gives unlimited Shards, so every mark can be bought, the gods' gifts included. The chart can be walked into every tree and branch. A fall puts you back at the last fire with nothing lost.\n\u2022  <b>Back to the Proving Ground</b> from any level: pause, then Return to the Proving Ground.\n\u2022  <b>The guide to effects</b>, from the pause menu and from the chart: every affliction, state and resource, with its numbers, what sets it off, how to use it and how it looks.\n\u2022  <b>Details for the high-level marks</b> on the chart: what a mark does, when, the numbers, what it works with and an example. Written in full for the Fire and Lightning trees and their mixes; the other trees show what their data says for now.\n\u2022  <b>Not built yet</b>: empty slots on the rack and on the chart show where the gods' weapons and boughs still to come will be.\n\u2022  This title, with the version and what is new."
  Effects:
  - Id: burn
    Title: Burn
    Group: Afflictions
    Body: '<b>What it is.</b> Fire''s affliction. A burning enemy takes steady damage until the fire goes out. Depth makes it hurt more each second.


      <b>The numbers.</b> 5 damage a second. Each stack adds 30%, up to 5 stacks (12.5 a second at full depth). Laying it again keeps whichever time is longer, never past 8 s. When it goes out, its stacks go with it. Set off, it deals 10, plus 10 for each stack, all at once.


      <b>What sets it off.</b> Flame Wave burns what it touches for 5 s, and its burning ground burns too. Each blow during Kindle burns for 3 s. With Fire''s root mark learned, every weapon blow burns for 4 s and adds a stack. Some marks set a burn off.


      <b>How to use it.</b> Burn works while you guard and dodge. Light it, then fight safely. Stack it before a mark sets it off, so the burst lands harder.


      <b>How it looks.</b> Flames lick up the enemy''s body. An orange diamond sits under its bars, larger the deeper the burn.'
  - Id: static
    Title: Static
    Group: Afflictions
    Body: '<b>What it is.</b> Lightning''s affliction. Charge builds up on an enemy and waits to be set off. When it goes, it arcs into the enemy and everyone near it.


      <b>The numbers.</b> Up to 5 stacks, 6 s, and each new stack starts the time again. A discharge deals 7 damage and 5 stagger for each stack to everyone within 4 m (35 damage and 25 stagger at full charge).


      <b>What sets it off.</b> With Lightning''s root mark learned, each light blow adds a stack. A heavy blow or a finisher on a charged enemy discharges it. Some marks set it off in other ways. Static laid on a Soaked enemy also spreads to everyone within 4 m.


      <b>How to use it.</b> Chain light blows up to five, then end with a heavy blow. Do it in a crowd: the discharge hits them all, and its stagger opens them up for finishers.


      <b>How it looks.</b> Small bolts jump over the enemy''s body. A pale blue diamond sits under its bars. A discharge strikes the enemy with a bolt.'
  - Id: unsteady
    Title: Unsteady
    Group: Afflictions
    Body: '<b>What it is.</b> Wind''s affliction. An unsteady enemy loses its footing: it is easier to stagger, flies further when struck, and turns slowly.


      <b>The numbers.</b> Up to 5 stacks, 6 s. Each stack means 6% more stagger taken, a 15% longer shove and 8% slower turning. At full depth that is 30% more stagger, 75% longer shoves and 40% slower turning.


      <b>What sets it off.</b> Gust lays it two deep. With Wind''s root mark learned, every weapon blow adds a stack. During Tailwind, every weapon blow adds one more.


      <b>How to use it.</b> Slower turning lets you circle behind an enemy and hit its back. Longer shoves help you throw enemies into hazards and walls. The extra stagger works with every heavy blow.


      <b>How it looks.</b> Streaks of pale air circle the enemy''s feet. A pale green diamond sits under its bars.'
  - Id: chill
    Title: Chill and Frozen
    Group: Afflictions
    Body: '<b>What it is.</b> Ice''s affliction. Each stack of Chill slows an enemy. At full depth it is Frozen: held still in ice until it thaws or a heavy blow shatters it.


      <b>The numbers.</b> Up to 5 stacks, 6 s. Each stack slows it by 7%. At 5 it freezes for 2.5 s. Elites thaw after 1 s. A god thaws sooner still: as a man after 0.75 s, in its godly form after 0.3 s, a hitch in whatever it was doing, which then carries on where it was. After a god thaws it cannot be frozen or held again for 3 s (as a man) or 5 s (in its godly form); its Chill still builds, and the next cold after that freezes it. A heavy blow on a frozen enemy shatters it for 45 more damage. A thaw or a shatter ends the Chill. Nothing can chill a frozen enemy further.


      <b>What sets it off.</b> Hoarfrost lays two stacks, and a weapon blow among its crystals breaks them for one more. With Ice''s root mark learned, every weapon blow adds a stack. During Glaze, every weapon blow adds one more.


      <b>How to use it.</b> Freeze a dangerous enemy to buy time, then shatter it with a heavy blow. Soaked spreads Chill to everyone close by.


      <b>How it looks.</b> Frost crystals grow at the enemy''s feet. Frozen, it glows a steady pale blue inside a cage of tall white crystals, and its diamond turns white and grows. A god''s godly form glows the same blue for its moment, and the crystals burst where it was last struck.'
  - Id: soaked
    Title: Soaked
    Group: Afflictions
    Body: '<b>What it is.</b> Water''s affliction. A soaked enemy takes more from spells, and passes Static and Chill on to everyone close to it.


      <b>The numbers.</b> On or off, 8 s. Spells deal it 25% more damage. Static or Chill laid on it is also laid on everyone within 4 m.


      <b>What sets it off.</b> Riptide soaks everything its wave carries. With Water''s root mark learned, every weapon blow soaks. During Wellspring, every weapon blow soaks too.


      <b>How to use it.</b> Soak a group, then charge or chill one of them, and it reaches them all. Cast your spells on soaked enemies.


      <b>How it looks.</b> Water drips off the enemy and rings of water spread on the ground at its feet. A deep blue diamond sits under its bars.'
  - Id: seeded
    Title: Seeded
    Group: Afflictions
    Body: '<b>What it is.</b> Life''s affliction. A seed grows in the enemy. Each of your weapon blows on it mends you, and when it dies it bursts into thorns.


      <b>The numbers.</b> Up to 3 stacks, 8 s. Each weapon blow on it heals you 1 for each stack. When it dies, it deals 12 for each stack to everyone within 3 m (36 at full depth).


      <b>What sets it off.</b> Briar Patch seeds whatever stands in it. With Life''s root mark learned, every weapon blow adds a stack. During Regrowth, every weapon blow adds one more.


      <b>How to use it.</b> Quick weapons gain the most, since every blow heals. Kill a fully seeded enemy in the middle of a group, so its thorns hit the rest.


      <b>How it looks.</b> Vines grow at the enemy''s feet and pink flowers open on it. A green diamond sits under its bars.'
  - Id: tremor
    Title: Tremor
    Group: Afflictions
    Body: '<b>What it is.</b> Earth''s affliction. The ground shakes under the enemy. It is slowed, and its balance does not come back while the shaking lasts.


      <b>The numbers.</b> Up to 3 stacks, 6 s. Each stack slows it by 10%. While it lasts, the enemy''s stagger meter does not drain.


      <b>What sets it off.</b> Stone Rise lays a stack. With Earth''s root mark learned, every heavy blow adds a stack and a finisher lays all three. During Bedrock, every weapon blow adds one more.


      <b>How to use it.</b> Tremor keeps stagger from fading, so you can step back, guard or heal, and the meter waits for you. Use it on enemies with a big stagger meter.


      <b>How it looks.</b> Pebbles hop around the enemy and the ground cracks under it. A brown diamond sits under its bars.'
  - Id: sundered
    Title: Sundered
    Group: Afflictions
    Body: '<b>What it is.</b> Metal''s affliction. Notches in the enemy''s armour let your weapon bite deeper.


      <b>The numbers.</b> Up to 3 notches, 8 s. Each notch means 8% more damage from weapon blows (24% at full depth). Spells are not affected.


      <b>What sets it off.</b> Flung Blade adds a notch when your next weapon blow drives the blade in. With Metal''s root mark learned, every heavy blow and every perfect guard adds a notch, and a finisher lays all three. During Temper, every weapon blow adds one more.


      <b>How to use it.</b> Notch the armour first, then spend your hardest blows. Sundered and a critical blow multiply each other.


      <b>How it looks.</b> Splinters of plate fall from the enemy. A steel grey diamond sits under its bars.'
  - Id: marked
    Title: Marked
    Group: Afflictions
    Body: '<b>What it is.</b> Light''s affliction. A mark of light makes your weapon blows on the enemy critical, until the mark is spent or fades.


      <b>The numbers.</b> One deep. It lasts 8 s or three weapon blows, whichever ends first. Each weapon blow on it is critical (one and a half times damage) and gives 2 more mana. Laying it again refills the three blows.


      <b>What sets it off.</b> Glare marks what its ray strikes. With Light''s root mark learned, the last blow of a chain and every perfect guard mark. During Clarity, every weapon blow marks.


      <b>How to use it.</b> Save the mark for your three hardest blows. A heavy blow or a finisher on a marked enemy hits hardest. The extra mana pays for your next spell.


      <b>How it looks.</b> A ray of white light stands over the enemy''s head. A pale gold diamond sits under its bars. Each critical blow shows a gold star.'
  - Id: cursed
    Title: Cursed
    Group: Afflictions
    Body: '<b>What it is.</b> Dark''s affliction. A cursed enemy hits more weakly, and killing it feeds you.


      <b>The numbers.</b> One deep, 8 s. It deals 15% less damage. Killing it heals you 6.


      <b>What sets it off.</b> Grasp curses what it reaches. With Dark''s root mark learned, every weapon blow curses. During Hunger, every weapon blow curses too.


      <b>How to use it.</b> Curse the enemy that hits hardest, and its blows take less of your health. Curse enemies that are nearly dead to heal as you kill them. This pairs well with Hunger, which costs health.


      <b>How it looks.</b> Dark violet smoke sinks over the enemy. A violet diamond sits under its bars.'
  - Id: poisoned
    Title: Poisoned
    Group: Afflictions
    Body: '<b>What it is.</b> Poison''s affliction. Doses build up, and on a slow beat the poison bites for all of them at once.


      <b>The numbers.</b> Up to 8 doses, 6 s. Each new dose starts the time again. Every 2 s it bites for 2 for each dose (16 at full depth). The first bite comes 2 s after the first dose. Set off, it deals 6 for each dose at once.


      <b>What sets it off.</b> Miasma doses whatever stands in its cloud once a second. With Poison''s root mark learned, every weapon blow adds a dose, a heavy blow adds one more, and a finisher adds two more. During Fever, every weapon blow adds one more. Some marks set it off.


      <b>How to use it.</b> Keep adding doses so the time never runs out. The deeper the poison, the harder each bite. Then dodge, guard and let the beat work.


      <b>How it looks.</b> Yellow-green bubbles rise off the enemy, larger the deeper the poison. A yellow-green diamond sits under its bars.'
  - Id: staggered
    Title: Staggered and the finisher
    Group: States
    Body: '<b>What it is.</b> Every enemy has a balance meter. Blows fill it. When it is full, the enemy is staggered: it kneels, helpless, for a few seconds. A heavy blow on it then is a finisher.


      <b>The numbers.</b> Ordinary enemies stagger for 3.2 s, elites for 3 s and gods for 2.8 s. The meter starts to drain 2 s after the last blow, at 25 a second. While staggered, light blows deal one and a half times damage. A finisher reaches up to 5 m, deals three times damage, costs no stamina, gives 15 mana, and nothing can hit you while it lasts. On a god it takes at least a fifth of his health, and on an elite at least a third.


      <b>What sets it off.</b> Every blow fills it. Heavy blows, perfect guards and some spells fill it most. Unsteady makes everything fill it more. Tremor stops it draining.


      <b>How to use it.</b> Watch the balance bar under the enemy''s health. When the enemy flickers, one or two more blows will open it. Save your heavy blow for the finisher.


      <b>How it looks.</b> At 70% the enemy flickers amber. Staggered, it pulses gold and carries a broken gold ring.'
  - Id: grey-health
    Title: Grey health
    Group: States
    Body: '<b>What it is.</b> A blocked blow still takes a little health, but that part turns grey and can be won back. Deal damage soon and it comes back. Wait too long and it fades.


      <b>The numbers.</b> 35% of a blocked blow''s damage turns grey. Each point of damage you deal wins back 0.6 of grey health. The grey starts to fade 2.5 s after your last block or regain, at 10 a second. A blow you do not block removes all of it. Grey can never take your last point of health, so guarding alone cannot kill you.


      <b>What sets it off.</b> Blocking with the guard button. Regrowth and Clarity turn all grey health back into real health at once.


      <b>How to use it.</b> After a block, strike back straight away to win the grey back. Do not take an unblocked blow while you have grey health, or you lose it.


      <b>How it looks.</b> A grey stretch at the end of your health bar, between your health and the empty part.'
  - Id: guard-broken
    Title: Guard broken
    Group: States
    Body: '<b>What it is.</b> A held guard costs stamina for every blow it blocks. If you do not have the stamina to pay for a blow, the guard breaks and the blow lands in full.


      <b>The numbers.</b> A block costs 0.9 stamina for each point of damage, for most weapons. When the guard breaks, the blow deals full damage, your stamina empties, and you are stuck for 0.8 s (an ordinary flinch is 0.35 s).


      <b>What sets it off.</b> A blocked blow that costs more stamina than you have. A ward takes the blow instead, if you have one.


      <b>How to use it.</b> Watch your stamina while you guard. Against long chains, dodge some of the blows or perfect-guard them, since a perfect guard costs nothing. Stop attacking and let stamina refill before you block a big blow.


      <b>How it looks.</b> The guard arc pulses red, a danger flash shows, and the words "Guard broken" appear.'
  - Id: perfect-guard
    Title: Perfect guard
    Group: States
    Body: '<b>What it is.</b> Press the guard button just before a blow lands. The blow is turned aside for nothing and the attacker loses its balance.


      <b>The numbers.</b> The blow must land within 0.18 s of the press, for most weapons. Pressing guard again within 0.4 s of the last press gives no perfect window, so mashing does not work. A perfect guard costs no stamina and no health, gives 15 mana, and adds a large amount of stagger to the attacker (40 to 55 on the castle''s enemies). Clarity makes the window half again as long.


      <b>What sets it off.</b> A fresh press of the guard button, timed to the blow. It also turns red attacks, which a held guard cannot stop.


      <b>How to use it.</b> Learn each enemy''s rhythm and press at the moment of impact, not at the wind-up. It is the best source of mana and stagger in the game, and several marks reward it.


      <b>How it looks.</b> The guard arc flashes gold, a ring and a pale flash burst from it, the world stops for an instant, and the words "Perfect guard" appear.'
  - Id: perfect-dodge
    Title: Perfect dodge
    Group: States
    Body: '<b>What it is.</b> Roll through a blow at the last moment and time slows for a moment, giving you mana and an opening.


      <b>The numbers.</b> A roll goes 4.5 m in 0.35 s for 25 stamina. Blows pass through you from 0.03 s to 0.25 s into the roll. A blow that passes through in the first 0.13 s is a perfect dodge. It gives 12 mana and slows time to 0.3 speed for 0.35 s.


      <b>What sets it off.</b> A dodge started just as a blow arrives. Red attacks can be dodged this way like any other.


      <b>How to use it.</b> Roll into or across the attack, not away from it, so you come out close enough to punish. Tailwind halves the dodge''s cost, sends it 30% further and keeps you safe 25% longer.


      <b>How it looks.</b> The world slows briefly and the words "Perfect dodge" appear.'
  - Id: red-attacks
    Title: Red attacks
    Group: States
    Body: '<b>What it is.</b> Some enemy attacks cannot be guarded. A held guard does nothing against them: the blow lands in full and you flinch.


      <b>The numbers.</b> They hit as hard as any other attack, and often harder. The lunges, charges, leaps, bolts and roars of the castle''s enemies and gods are among them.


      <b>What sets it off.</b> The enemy chooses them, often at range or as the last blow of a chain.


      <b>How to use it.</b> Dodge them, or perfect-guard them, since a perfect guard turns even these. A ward also takes one. Many leave the attacker open for a long time afterwards, so punish.


      <b>How it looks.</b> As the enemy commits, a red flare shows over its head instead of the white glint of a blow you can guard. The warning shape on the ground is drawn in red.'
  - Id: critical
    Title: Critical blows
    Group: States
    Body: '<b>What it is.</b> A critical blow is a weapon blow that lands for one and a half times its damage.


      <b>The numbers.</b> One and a half times damage. You start with no chance of a critical blow. Some marks add a chance, some make certain blows always critical, and Marked makes every weapon blow critical for three blows.


      <b>What sets it off.</b> Weapon blows on a Marked enemy, the chance that marks give, and blows that marks promise (for example a counter cut on an enemy showing its attack).


      <b>How to use it.</b> Put your hardest blows on a critical: a heavy blow or a finisher on a Marked enemy. Critical blows stack with Sundered and with the surge.


      <b>How it looks.</b> A gold star with long points and a spray of gold sparks where the blow lands.'
  - Id: wards
    Title: Wards
    Group: States
    Body: '<b>What it is.</b> A ward turns aside one blow that would have hurt you. It is spent instead of your health.


      <b>The numbers.</b> You can hold up to 3 wards. Each one takes a blow you did not guard, or a blow that would have broken your guard. Wards stay until they are spent, until you rest, or until you change element.


      <b>What sets it off.</b> Glaze (Ice''s surge, 40 mana, 12 s) gives one ward when you light it. Some marks give wards too.


      <b>How to use it.</b> Light Glaze before a big attack you cannot avoid, or when you want to trade blows. A ward also takes a red attack, which a held guard cannot.


      <b>How it looks.</b> The status line by your bars reads "Ward" or "Wards 2". When one is spent, a pale blue ring and sparks burst in front of you with a clang, and the word "Warded" appears.'
  - Id: hurt
    Title: Hurt (the flinch)
    Group: States
    Body: '<b>What it is.</b> A blow that lands makes you flinch. You are pushed back and cannot act for a moment.


      <b>The numbers.</b> A flinch lasts 0.35 s and pushes you back 1.1 m. A broken guard holds you for 0.8 s. A blow that arrives during a flinch is ignored, so two enemies cannot keep you down.


      <b>What sets it off.</b> Any blow that is not blocked, dodged or warded. The flinch cuts off your attack, spell, dodge or drink, and drops your guard. Some heavy moves are poised: during their wind-up and swing a small blow hurts but does not stop them.


      <b>How to use it.</b> Do not start a slow drink or a long chain next to an enemy that is about to swing. Enemies flinch too: most at every blow, some only after a few light blows.


      <b>How it looks.</b> A red flash at the screen''s edges, a spray from the wound and a shake of the camera.'
  - Id: health
    Title: Health
    Group: Resources
    Body: '<b>What it is.</b> Your life. It drops when blows land, partly turns grey when you block, and comes back from flasks, from some marks and from resting.


      <b>The numbers.</b> 100 to begin with. Some marks raise it. Below 30% the screen''s edges darken red, and they darken more below 15%.


      <b>What sets it off.</b> Unblocked blows take it for good. Blocked blows turn some of it grey (see Grey health). Flasks, Seeded enemies, Cursed kills, Regrowth, Hunger and Fever give it back. A rest fire fills it.


      <b>How to use it.</b> Win back grey health by attacking, and drink only when you are safe. In the playtest: a fall returns you to your last rest fire with nothing lost, so try risky things freely.


      <b>How it looks.</b> Your health bar in the corner of the screen. What a blow just took stays pale for a moment before it drains, so you can read how big the blow was.'
  - Id: stamina
    Title: Stamina
    Group: Resources
    Body: '<b>What it is.</b> What you spend to attack, dodge and block. When it runs out, you cannot dodge, and the next blocked blow breaks your guard.


      <b>The numbers.</b> 100. It refills at 30 a second, starting 0.8 s after you last spent any. A dodge costs 25. Attacks cost about 12 each, more for the heavier weapons. A block costs 0.9 for each point of damage, for most weapons. A broken guard empties it.


      <b>What sets it off.</b> Attacking, dodging and blocking spend it. Waiting refills it. A rest fire fills it.


      <b>How to use it.</b> Never empty it completely in front of an enemy. Keep enough for one dodge. Short pauses between chains let it refill.


      <b>How it looks.</b> The bar under your health bar.'
  - Id: mana
    Title: Mana
    Group: Resources
    Body: '<b>What it is.</b> The power behind your big moves: the surge, each element''s one larger spell, the built duo spells and your weapon skill. Basic spells never cost mana: they run on cooldowns instead (see Spell cooldowns).


      <b>The numbers.</b> Up to 100. You enter every area at half (50). Out of a fight, mana below half rises by 5 a second until it reaches half; mana above half stays where it is. A fight always starts with at least half: if you have less when an enemy notices you, it is raised to 50 at once. A fight ends when no enemy within 12 m has been aware of you for 8 s. Weapon blows that land give 3 to 16, depending on the move. A perfect guard gives 15, a perfect dodge 12 and a finisher 15. A Marked enemy gives 2 more for each blow. Blocked blows give nothing. Surges cost 30 to 40 (Hunger costs health instead, and waits 25 s after it ends), weapon skills 25 to 35, the deep strike 20, and the larger spells 30 to 50 (the built duo spells 40 to 60).


      <b>What sets it off.</b> Landing blows and timing guards and dodges well earn it; an infused strike''s blow earns it like any weapon blow. The surge, the weapon skill, the deep strike and a larger spell spend it.


      <b>How to use it.</b> Basic spells are free, so cast them whenever their clock is ready. Save mana for the surge or your element''s larger spell; what you earn above half in one fight is still there in the next. Perfect guards and perfect dodges fill it fastest.


      <b>How it looks.</b> The bar under your stamina, in the colour of the element you hold (grey with none). On the spell diamond a price is written in blue under the slot that pays it, and turns red, with the slot dimmed, when you hold less.'
  - Id: spell-slots
    Title: Spell slots and the spell layer
    Group: Spells and cooldowns
    Body: '<b>What it is.</b> You carry four spells, one in each slot: West, North, East and South, laid out like the pad''s face buttons. Hold L2 (LT) and press a face button to cast that slot''s spell. On the keyboard, 1, 2, 3 and 4 cast them directly. While L2 is held, the face buttons are spells only: the flask, the weapon skill, the dodge and use wait until you let go. A quick tap of L2 on its own lights the surge.


      <b>The numbers.</b> A tap of L2 counts if it is let go within 0.25 s and no spell was cast while it was held; the surge is lit as you let go. Held longer, letting go does nothing. On the keyboard the surge stays on F, and Left Ctrl is the layer for the infused strikes (Left Ctrl with a mouse button). With L2 held, R1 and R2 are the infused strikes, not attacks.


      <b>What sets it off.</b> At a rest fire, Set the Hand: choose what sits in each slot from the spells of the elements you carry (see The Hand). Until you first set a Hand, the slots fill themselves: each carried element''s own spell first, then each spell you learn in the next empty slot; choosing a learned spell on the chart and pressing use still puts it in the next slot round.


      <b>How to use it.</b> Keep spells of different jobs in your four slots: one to open a fight, one to break a guard, one to finish, one to escape. A spell slot can be rebound in the pause menu''s controls, on the pad and on the keys.


      <b>How it looks.</b> The spell diamond in the bottom-right corner: four round slots laid out like the face buttons, each with its spell''s picture (or its initials) and its button, the surge in the middle, the two infused strikes under it. It is small at all times and grows while L2 is held, with each spell''s name. The buttons are named for the pad or keys you use, and follow your rebinding.'
  - Id: the-hand
    Title: The Hand and the rest menu
    Group: Spells and cooldowns
    Body: '<b>What it is.</b> Your build: the four spells in your slots and the surge a tap of L2 lights, chosen from the elements you carry. Resting at a fire opens the rest menu: Set the Hand, The chart (where Shards are spent) and Leave the fire.


      <b>The numbers.</b> Four slots and one surge. A slot takes any learned spell of an element you carry, or that element''s own spell, or a duo spell while both of its elements are carried; nothing goes in two slots at once. The surge is either carried element''s. Three saved Hands. In the full game the slots open as you go: West and North at the start, East when the Champion of the Gate falls, South when the Fire god falls, and each stays open from then on; a shut slot holds nothing, is shown shut on the Hand with what opens it, and is never filled. In the playtest every slot is open.


      <b>What sets it off.</b> Use a rest fire, then Set the Hand. Choose a slot and press use for its list, grouped by element, each spell with its role and one line; press use on one to wear it at once. The weapon skill button shows the numbers. On a saved Hand''s row, use wears it and the heavy attack (or a right click) keeps the Hand you wear there. Suggested Hand fills the slots with each element''s own spell and then your learned spells in order. The stick, the d-pad, W and S, the wheel and the mouse all choose; dodge (or Esc) backs out. The world is stopped meanwhile.


      <b>How to use it.</b> Read your Hand like a hand of cards: an opener, a breaker, a detonator, a counter, a way to move. Keep a saved Hand for each kind of fight and swap at the fire. The Hand never changes which elements you carry: that is chosen in the hub (in the playtest, at the altars).


      <b>How it looks.</b> The four slots in a diamond laid out like the face buttons, named by your own bindings, each ringed in its element''s colour; the surge in the middle; the elements you carry along the top; the suggested and saved Hands on the right.'
  - Id: two-elements
    Title: Two elements
    Group: Spells and cooldowns
    Body: '<b>What it is.</b> You carry two elements at once, the first and the second; the same one twice is all in. Each spell is cast in its own element and lays its own affliction, in its own colour. Your weapon''s blows lay only the first element''s affliction: the second comes from your spells, the charged blade and the R2 strike, so mixing comes from weaving weapon and spell.


      <b>The numbers.</b> The weapon''s blows lay the first element''s affliction only, even with the second element''s root mark learned, except from a mixed branch''s own marks, which lay both of theirs (the owner''s decision of 2026-11-19) (Lightning''s Static is built by the weapon only while Lightning is first; a heavy blow still sets off Static laid another way). Marks of both elements are in force; a duo branch''s marks need both elements carried, and a duo spell also needs a slot. The surge you wear strengthens the weapon while it burns; if it is the second element''s surge, the blows still lay only the first element''s affliction. R1 strikes with the first element, R2 with the second; all in or with one element, R2 is the deep strike for 20 mana. The mana bar takes the first element''s colour.


      <b>What sets it off.</b> The elements you carry are picked in the hub; in the full game the hub''s braziers still give only the first. In the playtest the altars round the rest fire set both: carrying one element, another altar carries its element as your second and the altar of the one you carry goes all in; carrying two (or all in), an altar starts again with its element alone. You arrive carrying Fire, and each altar''s prompt says what it will do before you press. A Hand''s spells of an element no longer carried leave their slots, and a surge of one falls back to the first element''s.


      <b>How to use it.</b> Put the element you want on every blow first. Use the second''s spells and strike to lay its affliction beside the first; a charged blade carries a spell''s element on your next three blows beside your own. All in, you trade the mix for depth.


      <b>How it looks.</b> Each spell, ground and burst in its own element''s stuff and colour. An enemy carrying two afflictions shows both diamonds under its bars.'
  - Id: cooldowns
    Title: Spell cooldowns
    Group: Spells and cooldowns
    Body: '<b>What it is.</b> Basic spells cost no mana. After a spell is cast, its slot waits a few seconds before it can be cast again. Fighting with your weapon shortens the wait of every slot that is waiting.


      <b>The numbers.</b> Basic spells wait 6 to 12 s (the tree spells 7 to 12 s, each element''s own spell 6 to 9 s, the spare mixed spells 12 s). Each element''s one larger spell costs mana instead and has no wait: Meteor Leap 45, Seven Flashes 45, Sky Dance 45, Winter Wall 35, Poured Blade 30, Elder Tree 40, Grave of Swords 50, Daybreak 45, One by One 50. Pawned Heart is paid in health and waits 40 s. Earth''s larger spell (Cairn) is not built yet. The built duo spells (Ball Lightning, Eye of the Storm and the others) cost 40 to 60 mana. Weapon play takes time off every waiting slot: a light blow that lands 0.3 s, a heavy blow 0.6 s (once per move, however many it strikes), a perfect guard 2 s, a perfect dodge 1.5 s, a finisher 3 s. The two infused strikes wait 8 s each, cut by weapon play the same way (a strike''s own blow cuts every other wait, not its own). Hunger, Dark''s surge, waits 25 s from the moment it ends. Resting at a fire ends every wait.


      <b>What sets it off.</b> Casting a spell starts its slot''s wait. Landing blows, perfect guards, perfect dodges and finishers shorten it. A slot pressed while it waits says "Not ready".


      <b>How to use it.</b> Weave: cast, fight with the weapon until the spell is back, cast again. Perfect guards and dodges bring spells back fastest. Marks that only made a basic spell cheaper do nothing now; the trees are reshaped in a later phase.


      <b>How it looks.</b> On the spell diamond a waiting slot is shaded, and the shade sweeps back like a clock hand as the wait runs out, with the seconds left written in it. The slot''s ring swells for a moment when it is ready again.'
  - Id: charged-blade
    Title: The charged blade
    Group: Spells and cooldowns
    Body: '<b>What it is.</b> Magic feeds the weapon. When one of your four spells lands on an enemy, it charges your weapon with its element. The next three moves of the weapon that land carry the element: each hits 20% harder and lays the element''s affliction, and the third does one thing more, its element''s own.


      <b>The numbers.</b> Three moves, each 1.2 times the damage. Each lays one stack of the element''s affliction (two of Poison), on top of what the blow lays already, or beside it when that is another affliction. A move counts once however many it strikes, and carries the charge to all of them. A blow turned on a guard spends nothing. A new spell that lands replaces the charge with a fresh three. Resting ends it. What each element adds: Fire''s third blow leaves the ground under the enemy burning for 3 s. Lightning''s each leap on to one more enemy within 4 m for half the damage, with Static. Wind''s each shove the enemy 1.5 m along the swing, the third 4 m. Ice''s each shatter an enemy already Frozen, light blow or heavy. Water''s each splash everything within 1.5 m for a fifth of the blow, and soak it. Life''s third throws thorns round the enemy (2 m, Seeded). Earth''s each throw a 2 m spray of gravel. Metal''s pass any guard. Light''s third throws a ray 5 m along the swing that Marks. Dark''s third Curses twice more. Poison''s third makes the poison bite at once.


      <b>What sets it off.</b> A spell from one of your four slots that lands on an enemy, within 8 s of being cast (the first thing that cast strikes), charges it with that spell''s own element: with Fire and Lightning carried, Flame Wave charges it with Fire and Thunderclap with Lightning. A duo spell charges it with the first of its pair. Ground left burning by an earlier cast, the surge, an infused strike and marks'' effects never charge it.


      <b>How to use it.</b> Weave: cast, then strike three times, then cast again while the weapon brings the spell back. A spell on cooldown and a charged blade are the same fight seen from two sides.


      <b>How it looks.</b> The element runs along the weapon''s edge: tongues of flame shedding embers for Fire, bolts that jump along it for Lightning, rime feathers and breath-fog for Ice, the element''s own stuff in its colour for the rest. Fewer as the blows are spent. Three pips beside the spell diamond, lit in the element''s colour, one put out with each charged blow.'
  - Id: infused-strikes
    Title: Infused strikes
    Group: Spells and cooldowns
    Body: '<b>What it is.</b> Hold L2 (LT) and press R1 (RB) for an infused strike: your weapon''s own move, its carrier, played with your element on it. L2 with R2 (RT) is the deep strike, the heavier version, which also costs mana. On the keyboard, hold Left Ctrl and press the left or right mouse button.


      <b>The numbers.</b> Each strike button has its own 8 s wait, which weapon play shortens like a spell''s (a light blow 0.3 s, a heavy 0.6 s, a perfect guard 2 s, a perfect dodge 1.5 s, a finisher 3 s). The deep strike costs 20 mana. A strike counts as a weapon blow: it gives mana and takes time off your spells, but it never charges the blade and does not spend a charge. The carriers: the Katana''s drawing cut (made at once, 22 damage, 170 degrees), the Massive Sword''s rising cut, the Scythe''s full turn, the Great Spear''s first thrust, the Great Hammer''s drop, the Twin Knives'' crossing, the Great Bow''s shot, the Chain Sickle''s snap, the Fists'' and the Armament''s kick. Each element''s strike, then its deep strike: Fire, Burning Edge (a sheet of flame along the swing and 3 m beyond, 2 Burn on all it reaches, the ground burning 3 s), then Burnt Offering (a pillar of flame on the enemy struck: 30 damage and its burn set off). Lightning, Flash Cut (a 5 m lunge through enemies as a line of lightning, half again the blow, 2 Static), then Down the Channel (bolts come down the whole line 0.4 s later). Wind, Cutting Wind (a crescent out to 7 m, 60% of the blow, 2 Unsteady, a 1 m push), then Whirl Cut (the first enemy held in the air 1 s). Ice, Frost Bite (a spike of ice through each enemy struck: 2 Chill, held 0.8 s), then Ice Through (frozen at once if it carries three Chill). Water, Lash (a whip twice the weapon''s reach, 80% of the blow, Soaked, pulled 1.5 m in), then Thrown on the Reef (thrown 5 m away). Life, Grown Into It (2 Seeded and a green shoot), then Briar Root (rooted 1 s). Earth, Broken Ground (four slabs heaved up in a 4 m line: 14 damage, 25 stagger, Tremor), then Mountain Cleaver (6.5 m, 55 damage, 70 stagger, Tremor 2). Metal, Struck Plate (a ripple 3 m round the one struck, 10 damage, Sundered), then Red Iron (half the blow again and two Sundered on it). Light, Ray Along the Edge (a ray 6 m out: 10 damage, 15 stagger, Marked), then The Sun on the Blade (the same cut at half strength on every Marked enemy within 8 m). Dark, Taken (everything struck dragged 2 m toward you: 12 damage, 20 stagger, Cursed), then Yama''s Noose (40 damage and 50 stagger to the enemy you face within 8 m). Poison, Venom Flick (a string of venom 5 m ahead and a puddle that doses once a second for 3 s), then Nine Times Refined (six doses on what the cut struck).


      <b>What sets it off.</b> L2 with R1 or R2 (Left Ctrl with a mouse button). A strike pressed while its button waits says "Not ready"; a deep strike without 20 mana says "No mana".


      <b>How to use it.</b> The strike is your element at the weapon''s reach and in the weapon''s shape: a hammer''s drop lays it in a circle, a spear''s thrust in a line. Use it to open a fight or to lay your affliction on a crowd. With two elements, R1 (RB) is the first element''s strike and R2 (RT) the second''s, and neither costs mana: the strike is how your weapon lays the second element. Carrying one element, or the same one twice (all in), R2 is the first element''s deep strike for 20 mana.


      <b>How it looks.</b> The carrier''s arc in the element''s colour, then the element along what it covered: flame, lightning, wind, ice, water, vines, stone, ripples, a ray, shadow or venom. Under the spell diamond, two small rings, one for each button, with their waits.'
  - Id: spell-diamond
    Title: The spell diamond
    Group: Spells and cooldowns
    Body: '<b>What it is.</b> Your spells on the screen, in the bottom-right corner: the four slots laid out like the face buttons that cast them, the surge in the middle, the two infused strikes under them and the charged blade''s pips beside them.


      <b>The numbers.</b> Small at all times, so the waits can be read in a fight; it grows to full size while L2 (or Left Ctrl) is held, with each spell''s name, and shrinks back when you let go. Each slot shows its spell''s picture or initials, its button, its wait and its mana price.


      <b>What sets it off.</b> Always shown while you hold an element. The buttons are named for whatever you used last: the pad''s (Xbox or PlayStation) or the keys (1 to 4, and Ctrl with the mouse for the strikes). Rebind a slot in the controls and its new button shows at once.


      <b>How to use it.</b> Glance at it between blows: a clear slot is ready, a shaded one is waiting. Hold L2 to read the names before you cast.


      <b>How it looks.</b> Round dark buttons, each ringed in the colour of its own spell''s element (with two elements carried, a slot of each colour); the surge ringed in the colour of the surge you wear; the R2 strike named and coloured for the second element, or for the deep strike. A waiting slot is shaded, the shade sweeping back as a clock hand. A ready slot''s ring swells for a moment. Prices in blue, red when you hold too little. The surge''s ring brightens while it burns and is shaded while it waits.'
  - Id: flasks
    Title: Flasks
    Group: Resources
    Body: '<b>What it is.</b> Your healing draughts. Drinking takes a moment, so drink when you are safe.


      <b>The numbers.</b> 3 flasks, 45 health each. A drink takes 0.8 s and heals at 0.4 s. If a blow or a roll stops the drink before then, the flask is not used. At full health the button does nothing, so a flask is never wasted. With none left, dealing 120 damage earns one back. Wellspring makes flasks heal half again as much.


      <b>What sets it off.</b> The flask button. A rest fire refills them all.


      <b>How to use it.</b> Drink after a dodge has put distance between you and the enemy, or while it is staggered. With every flask gone, keep fighting to earn one back. Some enemies come for your flask when they see you drink.


      <b>How it looks.</b> Flasks drawn beside your bars, one for each you carry. With none left, the first slowly fills as you earn it back, and the words "Flask earned" appear when it is full.'
  - Id: shards
    Title: Shards
    Group: Resources
    Body: '<b>What it is.</b> The currency of the upgrade chart. Spend them at a rest fire to learn marks on your element''s tree.


      <b>The numbers.</b> Most enemies give 1 the first time they fall, the stronger gilded ranks up to 3, an elite 3 and Narukami 5. Marks cost 1 (minor), 2 (root), 3 (major), 4 (spell), 6 (keystone), and 3 to 5 on a mixed branch.


      <b>What sets it off.</b> Killing enemies. In the full game, unspent Shards are lost when you fall. In the lands, the enemies you killed since your last rest carry them back, glowing, and killing them returns the Shards. Falling again first loses them for good.


      <b>How to use it.</b> In the playtest: resting gives unlimited Shards and a fall loses nothing, so learn anything you want and try every tree.


      <b>How it looks.</b> "Shards" and a count on the HUD. Motes fly from each body to you, and the count swells as they land.'
  - Id: memories
    Title: Memories
    Group: Resources
    Body: '<b>What it is.</b> The second currency, earned by beating people. It will buy the weapon tree, the Way, and the Body branch of health, stamina, flasks and poise. Memories do not exist yet.


      <b>The numbers.</b> None yet. Memories arrive in a later phase of the playtest (phase 5), with the Way.


      <b>What sets it off.</b> The plan is that Memories come from beating each kind of enemy for the first time, and from elites, named fighters and gods, so they cannot be farmed.


      <b>How to use it.</b> In the playtest, Memories will be unlimited, like Shards, so every technique can be tried. In the full game they are kept when you fall.


      <b>How it looks.</b> Not shown yet.'
  - Id: reactions
    Title: Reactions
    Group: Reactions
    Body: '<b>What it is.</b> When an affliction lands on an enemy that already carries another element''s, the two react, and each of the 55 pairs of elements does something of its own. The entries below go round the ring: neighbours first, then the pairs two apart, and so on to the farthest.


      <b>The numbers.</b> A reaction comes once, then rests on that enemy before it can come again: 4 s for most and 6 s for the pairs three apart on the ring, with some resting their own time (Steam 3 s; Cold Short, Red Hot and The Bolt Runs True 5 s; Shut in the Dark and The Grudge 8 s; each entry gives its own). The rest is kept for each enemy and each pair, so a crowd can react one after another. What a reaction lays starts no reaction of its own.


      <b>What sets it off.</b> The second affliction landing, laid by anything: a weapon blow, a spell, a mark, the charged blade, a strike, or the world (an enemy wet from the river reacts to your fire). The order does not matter, except that Seized and The Grudge need two Static or more on the enemy.


      <b>How to use it.</b> Carry two elements. Your weapon lays the first and your spells, the charged blade and the R2 strike lay the second, so weave blade and spell on the same enemy. Many reactions then leave a state on the enemy for a few seconds (a crust, a crack, coils) that your next blow, its time running out, or its death sets off: a heavy to break or split it, a few quick blows to rock or coil it. Wait out the rest, or turn to another enemy.


      <b>How it looks.</b> The reaction''s name rises over the enemy for a moment. Twenty-four reactions have a look of their own, drawn in both elements'' stuff on the enemy and on the ground at its feet for about a second. The rest show each element''s own burst together, with a mark on the ground, until theirs is drawn.'
  - Id: reaction-flashover
    Title: Flashover (Fire and Lightning)
    Group: Reactions
    Body: '<b>What it is.</b> Static meets Burn. Flame carries current: the fire on the enemy goes live and its Static discharges through it at once.


      <b>The numbers.</b> The Static is spent: 7 damage for each stack to everyone within 3 m, and 4 stagger for each stack (20 at full charge). The enemy flinches for 0.4 s, which breaks a wind-up (not a steadfast enemy''s). The Burn is not spent and keeps burning. Rests 4 s.


      <b>What sets it off.</b> Burn landing on a charged enemy, or Static on a burning one.


      <b>How to use it.</b> Burn first with your blade, then charge it with a spell, or the other way round: the discharge comes without a heavy blow and leaves the fire burning. Catch a wind-up with it.


      <b>How it looks.</b> Its name over the enemy and a discharge where it stands. Not yet: the live flame that draws other discharges near into it.'
  - Id: reaction-thunder-gust
    Title: Thunder Gust (Lightning and Wind)
    Group: Reactions
    Body: '<b>What it is.</b> Static meets Unsteady. A crack of thunder and wind throws the enemy away from you, and its charge goes off where it lands.


      <b>The numbers.</b> Thrown 3 m straight away from you (the great move less, and what cannot be shoved stays). 0.4 s later its Static goes off as a heavy blow sets it off: 7 damage and 5 stagger for each stack to everyone within 4 m. Rests 4 s.


      <b>What sets it off.</b> Static landing on a Unsteady enemy, or Unsteady on a charged one.


      <b>How to use it.</b> Charge it deep first, then stand so it is thrown into the crowd: the discharge lands among them.


      <b>How it looks.</b> Its name over the enemy and a discharge where it lands. Not yet: what it hits on the way taking the discharge first.'
  - Id: reaction-rime
    Title: Rime (Wind and Ice)
    Group: Reactions
    Body: '<b>What it is.</b> Chill meets Unsteady. A crust of rime grows on the enemy, and your heavy blow blows the ice out of its far side.


      <b>The numbers.</b> The crust lasts 5 s. Your next heavy blow on it breaks it: a fan of ice about 4 m long beyond the enemy, away from you, deals 10 damage, 2 Chill and 1 Unsteady to everything in it. A light blow does not break it. Rests 4 s.


      <b>What sets it off.</b> Chill landing on a Unsteady enemy, or Unsteady on a chilled one.


      <b>How to use it.</b> Put the enemy between you and the others, then bring the heavy: the ice lands on them.


      <b>How it looks.</b> Its name over the enemy, then a burst of ice beyond it. Not yet: the crust growing only on the side facing you, so that a heavy from behind wastes it.'
  - Id: reaction-supercooled
    Title: Supercooled (Ice and Water)
    Group: Reactions
    Body: '<b>What it is.</b> Chill meets Soaked. The water on the enemy goes still below freezing, and the next blow freezes it.


      <b>The numbers.</b> For 6 s, your next weapon blow on it freezes it outright, whatever its Chill, and spends the Soaked. An elite takes 3 Chill instead and a god 2. Rests 4 s.


      <b>What sets it off.</b> Chill landing on a Soaked enemy (your Water, or the river''s), or Water on a chilled one.


      <b>How to use it.</b> One touch of cold on a wet enemy, then any blow: it freezes, ready for a heavy to shatter.


      <b>How it looks.</b> Its name over the enemy, then the freeze.'
  - Id: reaction-quickening
    Title: Quickening (Water and Life)
    Group: Reactions
    Body: '<b>What it is.</b> Soaked meets Seeded. The soaked seed splits its coat and flowers at once.


      <b>The numbers.</b> Its Seeded goes to full depth (3). For 4 s a flower opens on it, and a heavy blow bursts it: you heal 10, and everything within 3 m is Soaked and Seeded. Left alone, the flower withers. Rests 4 s.


      <b>What sets it off.</b> Water landing on a Seeded enemy, or a seed on a Soaked one.


      <b>How to use it.</b> Water a seeded enemy in a crowd, then heavy it: a heal, and the whole crowd wet and seeded.


      <b>How it looks.</b> Its name over the enemy. Not yet: the white flower on its back.'
  - Id: reaction-split-rock
    Title: Split Rock (Life and Earth)
    Group: Reactions
    Body: '<b>What it is.</b> Seeded meets Tremor. Roots wedge into the shaken ground and hold the enemy, and a heavy splits the floor.


      <b>The numbers.</b> Held 2 s (an elite 0.8 s; a god as a man 0.6 s, in its godly form 0.24 s, and not at all while its guard lasts). A heavy blow while it is held splits the floor: 10 damage, a Tremor and a Seeded to everything within 3 m. Rests 4 s.


      <b>What sets it off.</b> A seed landing on a shaken enemy, or Tremor on a Seeded one.


      <b>How to use it.</b> The hold is your window: bring the heavy before it ends.


      <b>How it looks.</b> Its name over the enemy, then a burst of earth when the floor splits.'
  - Id: reaction-anvil-stone
    Title: Anvil Stone (Earth and Metal)
    Group: Reactions
    Body: '<b>What it is.</b> Tremor meets Sundered. An anvil heaves up at the enemy''s back, and your heavy drives it on.


      <b>The numbers.</b> For 5 s, your next heavy blow on it breaks its armour to full (three notches) and rings out sparks: 10 damage, 15 stagger and a notch to everything within 3 m. Rests 4 s.


      <b>What sets it off.</b> Tremor landing on a notched enemy, or a notch on a shaken one.


      <b>How to use it.</b> Shake a notched enemy, then heavy it: the whole crowd notched for your Metal.


      <b>How it looks.</b> Its name over the enemy, then a ring of sparks. Not yet: the stone itself standing at its back.'
  - Id: reaction-glint
    Title: Glint (Metal and Light)
    Group: Reactions
    Body: '<b>What it is.</b> Marked meets Sundered. The light catches in the broken armour and is thrown at the next enemy.


      <b>The numbers.</b> A ray to the nearest other enemy within 6 m: 10 damage, 15 stagger, a Mark and a notch. It never strikes the first. Rests 4 s.


      <b>What sets it off.</b> A notch landing on a Marked enemy, or a Mark on a notched one.


      <b>How to use it.</b> Mark a notched enemy to Mark the one beside it too, ready for your critical blows.


      <b>How it looks.</b> Its name over the enemy and a strike where the ray lands.'
  - Id: reaction-diamond-ring
    Title: Diamond Ring (Light and Dark)
    Group: Reactions
    Body: '<b>What it is.</b> Marked meets Cursed. Dark closes over the enemy and a bead of light breaks at the rim.


      <b>The numbers.</b> Half a second on, 16 damage and 30 stagger to it. For 4 s its Mark is not spent by your blows, so every blow in that time is critical. Rests 4 s.


      <b>What sets it off.</b> A Mark landing on a Cursed enemy, or a curse on a Marked one.


      <b>How to use it.</b> Curse a Marked enemy, then strike it again and again while the ring holds.


      <b>How it looks.</b> Its name over the enemy, and for a moment the black disc ringed in gold with one burning bead at its rim. Not yet: the disc staying for the 4 s.'
  - Id: reaction-shut-in-the-dark
    Title: Shut in the Dark (Dark and Poison)
    Group: Reactions
    Body: '<b>What it is.</b> Cursed meets Poisoned. A black ring seals the enemy as a jar.


      <b>The numbers.</b> For 8 s its doses stop fading. When the 8 s end, or it dies, the jar breaks: 5 damage for each dose to everyone within 3 m, and half its doses (rounded up) spill onto all it reaches. Rests 8 s.


      <b>What sets it off.</b> A curse landing on a poisoned enemy, or poison on a Cursed one.


      <b>How to use it.</b> Dose it deep before you curse it: the deeper, the bigger the break. Killing it breaks the jar at once.


      <b>How it looks.</b> Its name over the enemy, then a burst when the jar breaks. Not yet: the black ring on the floor, and the poisoned that die inside crawling to it to feed it.'
  - Id: reaction-fire-medicine
    Title: Fire Medicine (Poison and Fire)
    Group: Reactions
    Body: '<b>What it is.</b> Burn meets Poisoned. The poison catches like powder and bangs.


      <b>The numbers.</b> A fuse of 0.6 s, then the bang: 4 damage for each dose and 6 for each Burn stack to everyone within 2.5 m, with 30 stagger, and everyone reached is set burning. Half its doses (rounded up) are spent. Rests 4 s.


      <b>What sets it off.</b> Poison landing on a burning enemy, or Burn on a poisoned one.


      <b>How to use it.</b> Dose first, then light it: deep poison makes the biggest bang.


      <b>How it looks.</b> Its name over the enemy, then the bang a moment later.'
  - Id: reaction-carried-embers
    Title: Carried Embers (Fire and Wind)
    Group: Reactions
    Body: '<b>What it is.</b> Burn meets Unsteady. The wind strips three embers off the enemy and carries them on, away from you.


      <b>The numbers.</b> The embers land 4, 5 and 6 m past the enemy, on your line to it, and burn there as small fires for 3 s (1 m across, 3 damage and 1 Burn a bite, two bites a second). Anything within 1.5 m of a landing is set alight as they land. The fire they lay starts nothing more. Rests 4 s.


      <b>What sets it off.</b> Burn landing on an Unsteady enemy, or Unsteady on a burning one.


      <b>How to use it.</b> You aim it by where you stand: put the enemy between you and the ones behind it, and the fire lands among them.


      <b>How it looks.</b> Its name over the enemy, then three small fires springing up beyond it.'
  - Id: reaction-sleet-charge
    Title: Sleet Charge (Lightning and Ice)
    Group: Reactions
    Body: '<b>What it is.</b> Static meets Chill. The frost on the enemy charges itself until a bolt falls.


      <b>The numbers.</b> For 3 s it gains one Static every half second (to full). Then a bolt discharges it all: 7 damage and 5 stagger for each stack to everyone within 4 m, and everything reached takes a Chill. A heavy blow sets the Static off early, as always. Rests 4 s.


      <b>What sets it off.</b> Static landing on a chilled enemy, or Chill on a charged one.


      <b>How to use it.</b> Wait out the 3 s for a full charge, or take it sooner with a heavy.


      <b>How it looks.</b> Its name over the enemy, then the discharge. Not yet: the bolt falling at once if it freezes.'
  - Id: reaction-capsize
    Title: Capsize (Wind and Water)
    Group: Reactions
    Body: '<b>What it is.</b> Soaked meets Unsteady. Wet and off balance, the enemy goes down.


      <b>The numbers.</b> It goes down for 1.2 s and can do nothing. An elite only staggers (25 stagger), and a god takes 15 stagger. Rests 4 s.


      <b>What sets it off.</b> Water landing on a Unsteady enemy, or Unsteady on a Soaked one.


      <b>How to use it.</b> Free blows: bring your heaviest.


      <b>How it looks.</b> Its name over the enemy, and it falls flat on its back, lies there, and gets up when its time is over.'
  - Id: reaction-winter-seed
    Title: Winter Seed (Ice and Life)
    Group: Reactions
    Body: '<b>What it is.</b> Chill meets Seeded. The seed sleeps under the frost and wakes as thorns at the thaw.


      <b>The numbers.</b> While the Chill lasts its Seeded stops fading. When the Chill ends (a freeze thawing or shattered ends it too) thorns burst from it: 12 damage for each Seeded stack (36 at most) to everyone within 2.5 m, seeding them, and you heal 3 for each stack. Rests 4 s.


      <b>What sets it off.</b> Chill landing on a Seeded enemy, or a seed on a chilled one.


      <b>How to use it.</b> Seed it deep, chill it, then shatter the freeze for the quickest waking.


      <b>How it looks.</b> Its name over the enemy, then a burst of thorns at the thaw.'
  - Id: reaction-the-ground-gives
    Title: The Ground Gives (Water and Earth)
    Group: Reactions
    Body: '<b>What it is.</b> Tremor meets Soaked. Shaken wet ground turns to sand and the enemy sinks to the knees.


      <b>The numbers.</b> For 4 s it moves and acts at half speed (an elite three quarters; a god is not sunk). A heavy blow while it is sunk holds it fast for 0.5 s. Rests 4 s.


      <b>What sets it off.</b> Tremor landing on a Soaked enemy, or Water on a shaken one.


      <b>How to use it.</b> Sink it, then come in with heavy blows: each one pins it for a moment. Not yet: sunk, it should be unable to dodge, leap or step back, and others wading in should slow too.


      <b>How it looks.</b> Its name over the enemy, and for a moment the floor tipping into a pit round it, wet at the rim. Not yet: the ring of sand staying round its feet.'
  - Id: reaction-iron-thorns
    Title: Iron Thorns (Life and Metal)
    Group: Reactions
    Body: '<b>What it is.</b> Seeded meets Sundered. Iron thorns grow out through the broken armour and fly off with each blow.


      <b>The numbers.</b> For 6 s, each of your weapon blows on it snaps a thorn off at the nearest other enemy within 6 m: 6 damage, a Seeded and a notch. Three thorns. Rests 4 s.


      <b>What sets it off.</b> A seed landing on a notched enemy, or a notch on a Seeded one.


      <b>How to use it.</b> Fight the thorned one: the others around it take the thorns.


      <b>How it looks.</b> Its name over the enemy and a strike where each thorn lands. Not yet: one thorn for each notch it carried.'
  - Id: reaction-earthlight
    Title: Earthlight (Earth and Light)
    Group: Reactions
    Body: '<b>What it is.</b> Tremor meets Marked. Light breaks up through cracks in the floor under the enemy.


      <b>The numbers.</b> Its Mark is renewed (three more critical blows). Half a second on, 14 damage, 25 stagger and a Mark to everyone within 3 m. Rests 4 s.


      <b>What sets it off.</b> Tremor landing on a Marked enemy, or a Mark on a shaken one.


      <b>How to use it.</b> Shake a Marked enemy in a crowd: they are all Marked for your critical blows, and the first keeps its three.


      <b>How it looks.</b> Its name over the enemy, then light bursting up round it. Not yet: only those standing on the star of cracks struck (for now a circle).'
  - Id: reaction-black-chain
    Title: Black Chain (Metal and Dark)
    Group: Reactions
    Body: '<b>What it is.</b> Cursed meets Sundered. A black chain binds the enemy to the nearest other.


      <b>The numbers.</b> The nearest other enemy within 6 m is chained to it for 5 s. Rests 4 s.


      <b>What sets it off.</b> A notch landing on a Cursed enemy, or a curse on a notched one.


      <b>How to use it.</b> Not yet: what the chain does. It will pass 30% of your weapon damage on either to the other, and keep the two within 4 m of each other.


      <b>How it looks.</b> Its name over the enemy. Not yet: the chain between them.'
  - Id: reaction-burning-sap
    Title: Burning Sap (Light and Poison)
    Group: Reactions
    Body: '<b>What it is.</b> Marked meets Poisoned. The sun wakes the sap, and your critical blows raise weals that burst.


      <b>The numbers.</b> For 3 s each of your weapon blows on it (each critical, for it is Marked) raises a weal. At the end its poison bites at once, and each weal bursts, laying two doses on everyone within 2.5 m. Rests 6 s.


      <b>What sets it off.</b> A Mark landing on a poisoned enemy, or poison on a Marked one.


      <b>How to use it.</b> Land the Mark''s three blows inside the 3 s for three weals.


      <b>How it looks.</b> Its name over the enemy, then a burst of poison at the end. Not yet: the poison holding back for the 3 s and landing doubled.'
  - Id: reaction-smoulder
    Title: Smoulder (Dark and Fire)
    Group: Reactions
    Body: '<b>What it is.</b> Cursed meets Burn. The fire sinks in out of sight and deepens, then flares.


      <b>The numbers.</b> While the curse lasts its Burn keeps biting, stops fading, and deepens by one every 2 s (a god''s every 3 s), to full. When the curse ends, or it dies, it flares: 10 damage for each Burn stack to everyone within 3 m, setting them burning. Rests 4 s.


      <b>What sets it off.</b> A curse landing on a burning enemy, or Burn on a Cursed one.


      <b>How to use it.</b> Light it, curse it, and leave it: the longer the curse runs, the bigger the flare. Killing it flares it at once.


      <b>How it looks.</b> Its name over the enemy, then the flare. Not yet: the fire hidden as a dark glow until it flares.'
  - Id: reaction-nerve-fire
    Title: Nerve Fire (Poison and Lightning)
    Group: Reactions
    Body: '<b>What it is.</b> Poisoned meets Static. Each bite of poison jolts the enemy.


      <b>The numbers.</b> While both last, each bite of poison spends one Static and jolts it: 7 damage, 5 stagger and a 0.3 s flinch that breaks a wind-up (not a steadfast enemy''s). An elite flinches once every 4 s; a god never flinches and takes 11 stagger instead. Rests 4 s.


      <b>What sets it off.</b> Poison landing on a charged enemy, or Static on a poisoned one.


      <b>How to use it.</b> Charge a poisoned enemy deep: five Static is five jolts, one at each bite.


      <b>How it looks.</b> Its name over the enemy and a jolt at each bite.'
  - Id: reaction-thermal-shock
    Title: Thermal Shock (Fire and Ice)
    Group: Reactions
    Body: '<b>What it is.</b> Burn meets Chill. The body cracks, and the next heavy splits it.


      <b>The numbers.</b> 14 damage at once, and it is Cracked for 5 s: your next heavy blow splits it for 30 damage and 40 stagger. Both afflictions stay. Rests 6 s.


      <b>What sets it off.</b> Burn landing on a chilled enemy, or Chill on a burning one.


      <b>How to use it.</b> Cold on a burning enemy, or fire on a chilled one, then a heavy inside the 5 s.


      <b>How it looks.</b> Its name over the enemy, a crack, then the split.'
  - Id: reaction-seized
    Title: Seized (Lightning and Water)
    Group: Reactions
    Body: '<b>What it is.</b> A Soaked enemy carrying two Static or more. The current locks its muscles, and the water runs off it live.


      <b>The numbers.</b> Held 1 s (an elite 0.4 s; a god as a man 0.3 s, in its godly form 0.12 s, and not at all while its guard lasts). The water runs into a live film 2.5 m round its feet for 3 s, giving one Static every half second to whoever stands in it. Its own Static is not spent. Rests 6 s.


      <b>What sets it off.</b> A second Static on a Soaked enemy, or Water on one already carrying two. One Static is not enough, and nothing rests until there are two.


      <b>How to use it.</b> Charge a wet enemy twice in a crowd: it is held, and the film charges everyone near for your Lightning.


      <b>How it looks.</b> Its name over the enemy and the film on the floor. Not yet: the film sparing the seized one (for now it charges it too).'
  - Id: reaction-windthrow
    Title: Windthrow (Wind and Life)
    Group: Reactions
    Body: '<b>What it is.</b> Unsteady meets Seeded. The seed roots the enemy, and the next heavy tears it out.


      <b>The numbers.</b> Rooted 2 s (an elite 1 s; a god not at all): it cannot walk or be shoved, but it can still turn and swing. Your heavy blow while it is rooted tears it out: 14 damage and 35 stagger, it is thrown 6 m away from you, and a torn pit 1.5 m across stays 5 s where it stood, seeding whatever walks in. The pit counts as a thing you grew. Rests 6 s.


      <b>What sets it off.</b> Unsteady landing on a Seeded enemy, or a seed on a Unsteady one.


      <b>How to use it.</b> Root it, step round so it is thrown where you want it, then heavy.


      <b>How it looks.</b> Its name over the enemy, then a burst of earth as it is torn out. Not yet: any shove (a Gust, a ram) tearing it out, not only a heavy.'
  - Id: reaction-frost-heave
    Title: Frost Heave (Ice and Earth)
    Group: Reactions
    Body: '<b>What it is.</b> Chill meets Tremor. The cold gets into the ground and heaves the enemy up.


      <b>The numbers.</b> 0.4 s on, the floor heaves up under it: 12 damage and 25 stagger, and it is thrown into the air for 1 s (an elite for less; a god only reels). Rests 6 s.


      <b>What sets it off.</b> Chill landing on a shaken enemy, or Tremor on a chilled one.


      <b>How to use it.</b> Strike it while it hangs in the air.


      <b>How it looks.</b> Its name over the enemy, then the heave. Not yet: the rimed mound left standing for 6 s.'
  - Id: reaction-rust
    Title: Rust (Water and Metal)
    Group: Reactions
    Body: '<b>What it is.</b> Soaked meets Sundered. The wet cuts rust, and the rust spreads.


      <b>The numbers.</b> While it is Soaked its notches do not fade and the rust adds a notch every 2 s. Once it is rusted through (three notches) a plate falls: for 6 s it takes 16% more from your weapon, wet or dry. Rests 6 s.


      <b>What sets it off.</b> Water landing on a notched enemy, or a notch on a Soaked one.


      <b>How to use it.</b> Keep it wet and let the rust work, then come in with the weapon.


      <b>How it looks.</b> Its name over the enemy. Not yet: notches past three (up to five), and the plate seen falling.'
  - Id: reaction-shining-herb
    Title: Shining Herb (Life and Light)
    Group: Reactions
    Body: '<b>What it is.</b> Seeded meets Marked. A shining herb springs up by the enemy.


      <b>The numbers.</b> The herb stands 6 s. Left alone, it flowers at the end and Marks and Seeds everyone within 3 m of the enemy. Rests 6 s.


      <b>What sets it off.</b> A seed landing on a Marked enemy, or a Mark on a Seeded one.


      <b>How to use it.</b> Let it flower in a crowd. Not yet: walking over the herb to pick it, for 8 health and a critical next blow.


      <b>How it looks.</b> Its name over the enemy, then a puff when it flowers. Not yet: the herb on the floor.'
  - Id: reaction-turned-to-stone
    Title: Turned to Stone (Earth and Dark)
    Group: Reactions
    Body: '<b>What it is.</b> Tremor meets Cursed. Stone climbs the enemy from the feet up.


      <b>The numbers.</b> Over 2 s it slows (30%, then 60%), then it stands as stone for 1.5 s: it neither walks nor begins an attack, takes double stagger and half damage from spells. A heavy blow breaks it out at once for 50 stagger. An elite is slowed half as much and stands half as long; a god is not turned. Rests 6 s.


      <b>What sets it off.</b> Tremor landing on a Cursed enemy, or a curse on a shaken one.


      <b>How to use it.</b> Wait for the stone, then heavy it: often enough to break its balance.


      <b>How it looks.</b> Its name over the enemy. Not yet: the stone climbing its legs.'
  - Id: reaction-quicksilver
    Title: Quicksilver (Metal and Poison)
    Group: Reactions
    Body: '<b>What it is.</b> Sundered meets Poisoned. Mercury runs into the cracks, and every blow makes the poison bite.


      <b>The numbers.</b> While it carries both, each of your weapon blows makes its poison bite at once, at its depth, besides its own beat (no more than once every half second). The doses are not spent. Rests 6 s.


      <b>What sets it off.</b> A notch landing on a poisoned enemy, or poison on a notched one.


      <b>How to use it.</b> Dose it deep and keep hitting: every blow is a bite.


      <b>How it looks.</b> Its name over the enemy and a bite at each blow.'
  - Id: reaction-kindling-point
    Title: Kindling Point (Light and Fire)
    Group: Reactions
    Body: '<b>What it is.</b> Marked meets Burn. The light gathers to one burning point.


      <b>The numbers.</b> Each of your weapon blows on it (critical, for it is Marked) deepens its Burn by one. The third sets it alight: all its Burn bursts out, 10 damage for each stack, and it burns on two deep. Rests 6 s.


      <b>What sets it off.</b> A Mark landing on a burning enemy, or Burn on a Marked one.


      <b>How to use it.</b> Three quick blows: the third is the payoff.


      <b>How it looks.</b> Its name over the enemy, then the flame bursting out at the third blow.'
  - Id: reaction-the-grudge
    Title: The Grudge (Dark and Lightning)
    Group: Reactions
    Body: '<b>What it is.</b> A Cursed enemy carrying two Static or more. A black cloud gathers over its head.


      <b>The numbers.</b> The cloud waits over it for 8 s. Rests 8 s.


      <b>What sets it off.</b> A second Static on a Cursed enemy, or a curse on one already carrying two. One Static is not enough, and nothing rests until there are two.


      <b>How to use it.</b> Not yet: what the cloud does. It will answer the next blow the enemy lands on you or your guard with a black bolt (its Static at double, and a stop), and drift to the next enemy if it dies first.


      <b>How it looks.</b> Its name over the enemy. Not yet: the cloud itself.'
  - Id: reaction-ill-wind
    Title: Ill Wind (Poison and Wind)
    Group: Reactions
    Body: '<b>What it is.</b> Poisoned meets Unsteady. Its poison goes loose like dust.


      <b>The numbers.</b> While it carries both, your heavy blow on it shoves it and it sheds all its poison at once in a plume behind it, away from you: grit 1.2 m wide that lies 3 s and doses everyone in it once a second. Rests 6 s.


      <b>What sets it off.</b> Poison landing on a Unsteady enemy, or Unsteady on a poisoned one.


      <b>How to use it.</b> Stand so the plume lands on the others, then heavy.


      <b>How it looks.</b> Its name over the enemy, then the plume on the floor. Not yet: every shove and throw shedding it, the plume laid along its path, and the doses shared among those it settles on.'
  - Id: reaction-steam
    Title: Steam (Fire and Water)
    Group: Reactions
    Body: '<b>What it is.</b> Burn meets Soaked. The water on the burning body flashes off in a scalding puff.


      <b>The numbers.</b> The Soaked is spent and half the Burn with it (rounded up). The puff deals 8 damage, and 4 more for each Burn it took, with 15 stagger, to everyone within 2.5 m. Rests 3 s, the shortest of all.


      <b>What sets it off.</b> Fire on a Soaked enemy (from your Water, or the world''s water), or Water on a burning one.


      <b>How to use it.</b> Deep Burn makes a bigger puff, but takes half of it. Soak a crowd and set them steaming one by one. Its short rest means it comes back often.


      <b>How it looks.</b> Its name over the enemy and a burst of water where it stands.'
  - Id: reaction-lightning-flower
    Title: Lightning Flower (Lightning and Life)
    Group: Reactions
    Body: '<b>What it is.</b> Static meets Seeded. A red fern of lightning flowers on its skin.


      <b>The numbers.</b> The fern throws a bolt to the nearest other Seeded enemy within 8 m: 8 damage, 10 stagger and a Static. The enemy keeps both afflictions. Rests 4 s.


      <b>What sets it off.</b> Static landing on a Seeded enemy, or a seed on a charged one.


      <b>How to use it.</b> Seed two enemies, then charge one.


      <b>How it looks.</b> Its name over the enemy and a strike where the bolt lands. Not yet: your grown things (briars, saplings, lilies) throwing bolts into it.'
  - Id: reaction-logan-stone
    Title: Logan Stone (Wind and Earth)
    Group: Reactions
    Body: '<b>What it is.</b> Unsteady meets Tremor. It rocks on its feet like a balanced stone, and your third blow throws it down.


      <b>The numbers.</b> For 3 s it rocks: your blows break its balance harder (the first at 1.25 times, the next at 1.5). The third weapon blow throws it down hard for 1.8 s, and its fall strikes 20 damage, 30 stagger and a Tremor in 3 m. An elite rocks and then reels (40 stagger); a god takes only the harder stagger. Rests 6 s.


      <b>What sets it off.</b> Unsteady landing on a shaken enemy, or Tremor on a Unsteady one.


      <b>How to use it.</b> Three blows inside 3 s: the weapon fells it.


      <b>How it looks.</b> Its name over the enemy, then the fall: it lies flat on its back, and gets up when its time is over.'
  - Id: reaction-cold-short
    Title: Cold Short (Ice and Metal)
    Group: Reactions
    Body: '<b>What it is.</b> Chill meets Sundered. Frost fills the notches and the armour goes brittle.


      <b>The numbers.</b> Brittle 5 s: its notches do not fade. Your next heavy blow cracks the plates off: for 6 s it takes 25% more from your weapon, and its notches stay (for two minutes, for now). Rests 5 s.


      <b>What sets it off.</b> Chill landing on a notched enemy, or a notch on a chilled one.


      <b>How to use it.</b> Chill a notched enemy, then heavy it, then fight it.


      <b>How it looks.</b> Its name over the enemy. Not yet: the plates dropping away.'
  - Id: reaction-caught-light
    Title: Caught Light (Water and Light)
    Group: Reactions
    Body: '<b>What it is.</b> Soaked meets Marked. A net of light lies on the wet floor.


      <b>The numbers.</b> For 4 s the net lies 3 m round the enemy: everyone in it is Marked, and everyone standing in it as it falls moves a quarter slower for the 4 s (a god is not slowed). The Mark that made it is not spent. Rests 6 s.


      <b>What sets it off.</b> Water landing on a Marked enemy, or a Mark on a Soaked one.


      <b>How to use it.</b> Wet the crowd, Mark one: all of them Marked for your critical blows, and slowed.


      <b>How it looks.</b> Its name over the enemy and the net on the floor. Not yet: enemies walking onto the net later slowed too.'
  - Id: reaction-girdled
    Title: Girdled (Life and Dark)
    Group: Reactions
    Body: '<b>What it is.</b> Seeded meets Cursed. Black fig roots coil round the enemy and tighten with each blow.


      <b>The numbers.</b> One coil at once: 25% slower (a god is not slowed), and it takes 6% more from your weapon. Each of your weapon blows draws the roots a coil tighter (6% more each) and mends you 1. At four coils (the third blow) it is girdled: held 1.5 s while the roots crush (an elite 0.6 s; a god as a man 0.45 s, in its godly form 0.18 s, and not at all while its guard lasts), 20 damage and 40 stagger, and you heal 4. The roots wait 8 s for your blows. Rests 6 s.


      <b>What sets it off.</b> A seed landing on a Cursed enemy, or a curse on a Seeded one.


      <b>How to use it.</b> Three blows: each one opens it more and mends you, and the third crushes it.


      <b>How it looks.</b> Its name over the enemy, then the crush. Not yet: no dodge or leap while it is coiled, and the hollow trunk left where it dies girdled.'
  - Id: reaction-chokedamp
    Title: Chokedamp (Earth and Poison)
    Group: Reactions
    Body: '<b>What it is.</b> Tremor meets Poisoned. The cracked ground breathes out a heavy damp that runs to the other shaken.


      <b>The numbers.</b> The damp pools under it and runs to up to three other shaken enemies within 7 m. For 5 s each one in it takes a dose every second and moves 20% slower (a god is not slowed). Rests 6 s.


      <b>What sets it off.</b> Tremor landing on a poisoned enemy, or poison on a shaken one.


      <b>How to use it.</b> Shake the crowd first, then poison one: the damp finds them all.


      <b>How it looks.</b> Its name over the enemy. Not yet: the pools staying on the floor where they settle.'
  - Id: reaction-red-hot
    Title: Red Hot (Metal and Fire)
    Group: Reactions
    Body: '<b>What it is.</b> Sundered meets Burn. The notched armour heats red.


      <b>The numbers.</b> For 5 s each heavy blow on it throws sparks out of its far side, away from you, in a cone about 3 m long: 6 damage and a Burn to each enemy in it. Rests 5 s.


      <b>What sets it off.</b> A notch landing on a burning enemy, or Burn on a notched one.


      <b>How to use it.</b> Put it between you and the others and heavy it: each heavy lights them.


      <b>How it looks.</b> Its name over the enemy, then sparks beyond it at each heavy. Not yet: its burns biting twice as hard while it glows.'
  - Id: reaction-the-bolt-runs-true
    Title: The Bolt Runs True (Light and Lightning)
    Group: Reactions
    Body: '<b>What it is.</b> Marked meets Static. A thread of light stands from the enemy, then a straight bolt runs from it down a lane straight away from you.


      <b>The numbers.</b> Half a second on, the lane: 8 m long and 1.2 m wide, starting at the enemy. 20 damage, 35 stagger and a Static to it and to every enemy on the lane, each struck once. Then its own Static discharges at full (7 damage and 5 stagger for each stack to everyone within 4 m). The Mark is not spent. Rests 5 s.


      <b>What sets it off.</b> A Mark landing on a charged enemy, or Static on a Marked one.


      <b>How to use it.</b> Charge it deep before you Mark it, or Mark it before you charge it: the bolt sets the charge off for you. Stand so the others are behind it: the bolt runs on through them.


      <b>How it looks.</b> Its name over the enemy, the thread and the bolt on it, then the bolt coming down again and again as it runs away from you down the lane, and the discharge.'
  - Id: reaction-breath-taken
    Title: Breath Taken (Dark and Wind)
    Group: Reactions
    Body: '<b>What it is.</b> Cursed meets Unsteady. A black gust draws the enemy''s breath out.


      <b>The numbers.</b> Winded for 1.5 s (an elite 0.6 s): it begins no attack (one already swung is finished) and takes 30% more stagger. Rests 6 s.


      <b>What sets it off.</b> A curse landing on a Unsteady enemy, or Unsteady on a Cursed one.


      <b>How to use it.</b> Wind it, then break its balance while it cannot answer.


      <b>How it looks.</b> Its name over the enemy. Not yet: the breath torn away on the wind.'
  - Id: reaction-venom-rime
    Title: Venom Rime (Poison and Ice)
    Group: Reactions
    Body: '<b>What it is.</b> Poisoned meets Chill. The poison will not fade, and each bite chills it toward a freeze.


      <b>The numbers.</b> While both lie on it, its poison does not fade and each bite lays a Chill, until it freezes. Rests 4 s.


      <b>What sets it off.</b> Poison landing on a chilled enemy, or Chill on a poisoned one.


      <b>How to use it.</b> Dose it and chill it once: the poison freezes it for you.


      <b>How it looks.</b> Its name over the enemy and a Chill at each bite.'
  - Id: reaction-firebloom
    Title: Firebloom (Fire and Life)
    Group: Reactions
    Body: '<b>What it is.</b> Burn meets Seeded. The heat splits the seeds and they grow into flame lilies.


      <b>The numbers.</b> The Seeded is spent: one lily for each stack (one to three) springs up 2.5 m round the enemy and stands 5 s, burning whatever is within 1 m (3 damage and a Burn every half second). They count as things you grew. Its Burn stays. Rests 4 s.


      <b>What sets it off.</b> Burn landing on a Seeded enemy, or a seed on a burning one.


      <b>How to use it.</b> Seed it deep before you light it: more seeds, more lilies.


      <b>How it looks.</b> Its name over the enemy and the lilies round it. Not yet: walking past a lily to pick its fire up.'
  - Id: reaction-earthed
    Title: Earthed (Lightning and Earth)
    Group: Reactions
    Body: '<b>What it is.</b> Static meets Tremor. The charge runs to ground as a burnt fern.


      <b>The numbers.</b> All its Static runs into the floor at once: 5 damage and 3 stagger for each stack to everyone within 4 m, and a Tremor. It is rooted 1 s (an elite half that; a god not at all). Rests 4 s.


      <b>What sets it off.</b> Static landing on a shaken enemy, or Tremor on a charged one.


      <b>How to use it.</b> Charge it deep in a crowd, then shake it: the charge goes to everyone near.


      <b>How it looks.</b> Its name over the enemy and a burst round it. Not yet: the fern on the floor, and sparing the grounded one (for now it takes its own).'
  - Id: reaction-sickle-wind
    Title: Sickle Wind (Wind and Metal)
    Group: Reactions
    Body: '<b>What it is.</b> Unsteady meets Sundered. The wind tears its loose plates off and whirls them round it.


      <b>The numbers.</b> For 3 s the plates whirl 1.5 m round it, cutting everything they pass, the enemy too: 3 damage for each shard (one for each notch, plus one) and 4 stagger every 0.4 s. Rests 4 s.


      <b>What sets it off.</b> Unsteady landing on a notched enemy, or a notch on a Unsteady one.


      <b>How to use it.</b> Notch it deep first: more notches, more blades. Keep clear of the whirl, or fight inside it.


      <b>How it looks.</b> Its name over the enemy and the whirl round it.'
  - Id: reaction-mock-suns
    Title: Mock Suns (Ice and Light)
    Group: Reactions
    Body: '<b>What it is.</b> Chill meets Marked. Two mock suns hang beside the enemy.


      <b>The numbers.</b> For 4 s your weapon blows on it lay two Chill and do not spend its Mark, so they stay critical. Rests 4 s.


      <b>What sets it off.</b> Chill landing on a Marked enemy, or a Mark on a chilled one.


      <b>How to use it.</b> Strike as often as you can inside the 4 s: each blow is critical and chills it.


      <b>How it looks.</b> Its name over the enemy. Not yet: the suns turning with it, and only blows from its flanks counting.'
  - Id: reaction-drowned-weight
    Title: Drowned Weight (Water and Dark)
    Group: Reactions
    Body: '<b>What it is.</b> Soaked meets Cursed. The curse turns the water black and heavy, and the enemy swells.


      <b>The numbers.</b> Swollen 5 s: 20% slower (a god is not slowed) and 15% more from your weapon. When it dies, or a heavy blow lands while it is swollen, it bursts in black water: 14 damage and 20 stagger, Soaked and Cursed, to everyone within 4 m. Rests 4 s.


      <b>What sets it off.</b> Water landing on a Cursed enemy, or a curse on a Soaked one.


      <b>How to use it.</b> Kill it in a crowd, or heavy it there: the black water spreads the pair to the rest.


      <b>How it looks.</b> Its name over the enemy, then the burst. Not yet: only a finisher bursting it (for now any heavy blow).'
  - Id: reaction-rot-roots
    Title: Rot Roots (Life and Poison)
    Group: Reactions
    Body: '<b>What it is.</b> Seeded meets Poisoned. Roots run from the enemy''s feet to its neighbours, and its poison runs down them.


      <b>The numbers.</b> Up to three other enemies within 5 m (the nearest) are joined for 6 s, each Seeded once as the roots reach it. Every bite of poison on the first enemy bites each joined one for half. Rests 4 s.


      <b>What sets it off.</b> Poison landing on a Seeded enemy, or Seeded on a poisoned one.


      <b>How to use it.</b> Poison one enemy deep, then seed it in a crowd: one body''s poison hurts four. The joined ones carry Seeded, ready for Life''s own marks.


      <b>How it looks.</b> Its name over the enemy and a poison puff on each joined one at every bite. Not yet: the pale roots on the floor.'
  - Id: reaction-burnt-mound
    Title: Burnt Mound (Earth and Fire)
    Group: Reactions
    Body: '<b>What it is.</b> Tremor meets Burn. The shaken floor throws up three stones and its fire heats them red.


      <b>The numbers.</b> Three hot stones lie 1.5 m round the enemy for 6 s and burn whatever touches them (3 damage and a Burn each half second). Rests 6 s.


      <b>What sets it off.</b> Tremor landing on a burning enemy, or Burn on a shaken one.


      <b>How to use it.</b> Fight it among its stones: what steps on them burns.


      <b>How it looks.</b> Its name over the enemy and the stones round it. Not yet: batting the stones with your weapon into the crowd.'
  - Id: reaction-live-iron
    Title: Live Iron (Metal and Lightning)
    Group: Reactions
    Body: '<b>What it is.</b> Sundered meets Static. The enemy''s broken armour goes live, and a blow on it arcs only from iron to iron.


      <b>The numbers.</b> For 6 s, each of your weapon blows on it throws an arc to the nearest other Sundered enemy within 8 m (never to a clean one) for 35% of the blow, laying a notch of Sundered where it lands; from there it leaps once more to another notched enemy. At most one arc every 0.3 s. Spells do not arc. Rests 4 s.


      <b>What sets it off.</b> Static landing on a Sundered enemy, or Sundered on a charged one.


      <b>How to use it.</b> Notch the crowd first, then make one of them live and fight it: every blow reaches the others. The arc''s notches lay the wire for the next.


      <b>How it looks.</b> Its name over the enemy and a strike where each arc lands.'
  - Id: reaction-golden-feathers
    Title: Golden Feathers (Light and Wind)
    Group: Reactions
    Body: '<b>What it is.</b> Marked meets Unsteady. Its Mark breaks into golden feathers that ride the wind.


      <b>The numbers.</b> Three feathers ride 6 m on past the enemy, away from you; each Marks what it touches and makes it Unsteady. The first enemy keeps its Mark. Rests 4 s.


      <b>What sets it off.</b> A Mark landing on a Unsteady enemy, or Unsteady on a Marked one.


      <b>How to use it.</b> Stand so the others are behind it: they are Marked for your critical blows.


      <b>How it looks.</b> Its name over the enemy, then the feathers landing beyond it. Not yet: the feathers fanned across 40 degrees, each stopping at the first it touches.'
  - Id: reaction-stolen-warmth
    Title: Stolen Warmth (Dark and Ice)
    Group: Reactions
    Body: '<b>What it is.</b> Cursed meets Chill. The curse takes its warmth, and each blow draws it into you.


      <b>The numbers.</b> While both last, its Chill does not fade, and each of your weapon blows lays a Chill and draws 2 health into you (8 a second at most; a god gives half). Rests 6 s.


      <b>What sets it off.</b> A curse landing on a chilled enemy, or Chill on a Cursed one.


      <b>How to use it.</b> Keep hitting: every blow heals you and chills it toward a freeze.


      <b>How it looks.</b> Its name over the enemy. Not yet: the last warmth torn out of it when it freezes.'
  - Id: reaction-fish-poison
    Title: Fish Poison (Poison and Water)
    Group: Reactions
    Body: '<b>What it is.</b> Soaked meets Poisoned. The water runs off it fouled, and the heavily dosed float up stunned.


      <b>The numbers.</b> A fouled slick 3 m across lies 5 s and Soaks whoever stands in it. If the enemy carries four doses or more as it reacts, it floats up stunned: lifted and held 1.5 s (an elite 0.5 s; a god takes 30 stagger instead), and your next weapon blow on it is critical and spends two doses for 6 damage each. Rests 6 s.


      <b>What sets it off.</b> Poison landing on a Soaked enemy, or Water on a poisoned one.


      <b>How to use it.</b> Dose it four deep before you wet it, then be ready with the blade.


      <b>How it looks.</b> Its name over the enemy and the slick on the floor. Not yet: others in the slick floating as they reach four doses.'
  Marks:
  - Id: blight.wither
    Title: Wither
    Group: 
    Body: '<b>What it does.</b> Poison bites a quarter harder on a Cursed enemy, and does not fade from it while the curse lasts. Your heavy blows also lay a Curse and poison together, whichever of the two you carry first.


      <b>When it happens.</b> Always on once learned, while you carry both Dark and Poison. The heavy-blow laying comes with every heavy blow or finisher that lands.


      <b>The numbers.</b> Mix, 3 Shards. Poison on a Cursed enemy bites 25% harder and keeps its doses for as long as the curse holds. A heavy blow lays a Curse and two doses of poison. Of your first element''s affliction, once its root is learned, it adds only what goes beyond the root''s own stack: with Dark first the Curse, one deep at most, adds nothing; with Poison first the poison adds one dose. A mixed branch''s marks are the exception to the rule that weapon blows lay only your first element''s affliction.


      <b>Works with.</b> Curse or Venom, Feeding Rot, Carrion Flies, The Reaping, Grasp and Miasma, and the infused strikes (R2 lays the second element).


      <b>Example.</b> Poison first: lay eight doses with blade and heavy blows; the heavy blows Curse the soldier as they go. While it stays Cursed the poison never runs out and bites for 20 at a time.'
  - Id: blight.feedingrot
    Title: Feeding Rot
    Group: 
    Body: '<b>What it does.</b> Each time poison bites a Cursed enemy, a little of it comes back to you as health.


      <b>When it happens.</b> Every bite of poison, on its slow beat, on an enemy that is Cursed.


      <b>The numbers.</b> Mix, 3 Shards. Half a point of health for each dose that bit: 4 at eight doses, every 2 seconds.


      <b>Works with.</b> Wither (the poison does not fade while the curse holds), Curse, Long Curse, One Death Feeds, Wasting Grip.


      <b>Example.</b> Three Cursed soldiers at eight doses each: every two seconds you heal 12 while you guard.'
  - Id: blight.wastinggrip
    Title: Wasting Grip
    Group: 
    Body: '<b>What it does.</b> You brace and pour a short stream of rot at what stands before you, biting again and again and laying Curse. While you hold this mark, any spell of yours that strikes a poisoned enemy also feeds you.


      <b>When it happens.</b> From a spell slot: cast it with that slot''s button (hold L2 and a face button, or 1 to 4). While it pours, the stick or the cursor turns it slowly. A dodge lets it go, and a blow that lands on you breaks it. The feeding comes whenever a spell of yours strikes a poisoned enemy.


      <b>The numbers.</b> Mix, 4 Shards, 40 mana. A bar 2.5 metres long and 1.2 metres wide, after a 0.3-second brace, for 2.5 seconds. It bites every half second for 8 damage, 6 stagger and a Curse: five bites on what stays in it. A spell striking a poisoned enemy heals 5, at most once a second. As built it does not yet take hold of an enemy, drink its poison or throw it.


      <b>Works with.</b> Wither, Feeding Rot, Blood Price (pay in health when short of mana), Miasma and Grasp (both feed it when they strike the poisoned), and the charged blade (it charges with Dark).


      <b>Example.</b> A poisoned brute in front of you: pour the rot over it and it is Cursed through the bites while every spell you land on it heals 5.'
  - Id: blight.carrionflies
    Title: Carrion Flies
    Group: 
    Body: '<b>What it does.</b> An enemy that dies both Cursed and poisoned bursts a moment later. Everyone near takes the doses it carried, and a curse.


      <b>When it happens.</b> The moment an enemy carrying both Curse and poison dies; the burst follows 0.8 seconds later.


      <b>The numbers.</b> Mix, 3 Shards. Everything within 5 metres of where it fell is Cursed at once. Then the burst, 5 metres round: 3 damage and as many doses of poison as the dead one carried, up to eight. At most twice a second.


      <b>Works with.</b> Wither, Feeding Rot, One Death Feeds, Dread, The Reaping.


      <b>Example.</b> Kill a Cursed soldier at eight doses in a crowd, and the others are eight deep and Cursed before they reach you.'
  - Id: blight.gravesoil
    Title: Grave Soil
    Group: 
    Body: '<b>What it does.</b> You foul the ground round your feet. For a while, whatever stands on it is bitten every two seconds and Cursed.


      <b>When it happens.</b> From a spell slot: cast it with that slot''s button (hold L2 and a face button, or 1 to 4).


      <b>The numbers.</b> Mix, 4 Shards, no mana: it waits 12 seconds after a cast, less with weapon play. A circle 5 metres in radius, half a metre ahead of you, for 8 seconds. It bites 0.3 seconds after the cast and then every 2 seconds, four bites in all: 3 damage and a Curse each, with no stagger. It always lays Curse, whichever element you carry first, and does not hurry the poison''s beat.


      <b>Works with.</b> Wither (poison never fades from what stands in it), Feeding Rot, Carrion Flies, One Death Feeds, Long Shadows.


      <b>Example.</b> Plant it where you mean to fight a pack: everyone who steps in is Cursed, so Wither keeps their poison running.'
  - Id: blight.onedeathfeeds
    Title: One Death Feeds
    Group: 
    Body: '<b>What it does.</b> When a Cursed enemy dies, the poison in every other enemy near it bites at once, out of turn, and you are fed for each one bitten.


      <b>When it happens.</b> The moment a Cursed enemy dies, whatever killed it; at most twice a second.


      <b>The numbers.</b> Mix, 5 Shards. Every poisoned enemy within 12 metres of where it fell bites at once for its doses, and you heal 4 for each one bitten. Each poison keeps its own beat afterward.


      <b>Works with.</b> Wither, Feeding Rot (each extra bite on a Cursed one feeds again), Carrion Flies, Dread, Curse.


      <b>Example.</b> Five soldiers at eight doses: kill one Cursed, and the other four bite for 16 each at once while you heal 16.'
  - Id: blight.reaping
    Title: The Reaping
    Group: 
    Body: '<b>What it does.</b> Your finisher on an enemy both Cursed and poisoned reaps the field. A blade as long as the field sweeps once round it, time slows, and all the poison in every enemy near lands at once. Half of all it deals comes back to you as health.


      <b>When it happens.</b> Every finisher (a heavy blow on a staggered enemy) that lands on an enemy carrying both Curse and poison.


      <b>The numbers.</b> A god''s gift, never sold; in the playtest it can be bought. The sweep takes 0.42 seconds and reaches 9 metres round the finished enemy. Each poisoned enemy in it has its poison set off and spent: 9 damage a dose (72 at eight) and 4 stagger a dose. Half the total heals you.


      <b>Works with.</b> Wither, Carrion Flies (spread the doses first), Feast, Miasma, Grasp, Long Shadows.


      <b>Example.</b> Four soldiers at eight doses round a Cursed brute: finish the brute and each takes 72 while you heal half of it.'
  - Id: blizzard.biting
    Title: Biting Wind
    Group: 
    Body: '<b>What it does.</b> Your weapon blows lay Unsteady and Chill together, whichever of the two you carry first. A mixed branch''s marks are the exception to the rule that weapon blows lay only your first element''s affliction.


      <b>When it happens.</b> Every weapon blow that lands, while you carry both Wind and Ice.


      <b>The numbers.</b> Mix, 3 Shards. One stack of Unsteady and one of Chill a blow. Your first element''s own is not laid twice: once its root is learned, the root''s stack is the one a blow lays. Unsteady: 6% more stagger, 15% longer shoves and 8% slower turning a stack. Chill: 7% slower a stack, Frozen at five.


      <b>Works with.</b> Windchill (it needs both, and your blows lay both), Sliding Ice, Gust or Hoarfrost from a slot for more of either, the charged blade.


      <b>Example.</b> Wind first: four blows leave a soldier four deep in Unsteady and Chill, and with Windchill it goes on growing colder by itself until it freezes.'
  - Id: blizzard.windchill
    Title: Windchill
    Group: 
    Body: '<b>What it does.</b> The enemy you face, while it is both Unsteady and chilled, grows colder by itself, a stack at a time, until it freezes. As built only the enemy you face grows colder.


      <b>When it happens.</b> Every 2 seconds in a fight (an enemy within 12 metres), on the enemy you face if it carries both Unsteady and Chill.


      <b>The numbers.</b> Mix, 3 Shards. One stack of Chill every 2 seconds. At five it is Frozen for 2.5 seconds (elites and gods 1 second).


      <b>Works with.</b> Biting Wind, Cold Front, Sliding Ice, Hoarfrost and Gust, Diamond Dust (a frozen enemy to shatter).


      <b>Example.</b> Gust a soldier and Hoarfrost it, then keep facing it while you guard: eight seconds later it freezes without a blow from you.'
  - Id: blizzard.front
    Title: Cold Front
    Group: 
    Body: '<b>What it does.</b> A perfect dodge leaves a gust of ice behind you. It strikes the attacker in a cone and leaves it two deeper in Chill, while everything round you is knocked two deeper in Unsteady and thrown back.


      <b>When it happens.</b> A perfect dodge: a blow passes through the very start of your roll. The cone goes at the one who struck, or at the enemy you face when the blow came from afar.


      <b>The numbers.</b> Mix, 3 Shards. A cone 4 metres long and 90 degrees wide: 10 damage, 20 stagger and two stacks of Chill. Every enemy within 4 metres of you takes two stacks of Unsteady and is pushed 3 metres away.


      <b>Works with.</b> Windchill (both afflictions at once), Biting Wind, Empty Air, Rushing Wake, Thin Air, Tailwind.


      <b>Example.</b> Roll through a brute''s swing at the last moment: it is two deep in both and being pushed off you before it has recovered.'
  - Id: blizzard.sliding
    Title: Sliding Ice
    Group: 
    Body: '<b>What it does.</b> A light blow on a chilled enemy throws everything close to you back, and half a second later ice bursts where the one struck stood. As built it does not yet send a Frozen enemy sliding into a wall to shatter; the push and the burst stand in for it.


      <b>When it happens.</b> A light blow that lands on an enemy carrying Chill, at most once every 1.5 seconds.


      <b>The numbers.</b> Mix, 4 Shards. Every enemy within 3.5 metres of you is pushed 5 metres away. The burst is 2.5 metres in radius, 0.5 seconds later: 20 damage and 20 stagger. It lays no affliction.


      <b>Works with.</b> Biting Wind, Windchill, Hoarfrost, Strong Arm (pushes 30% further), Avalanche.


      <b>Example.</b> Surrounded, cut a chilled soldier: the ring is thrown 5 metres back and you have room to raise your guard.'
  - Id: blizzard.whiteout
    Title: Whiteout
    Group: 
    Body: '<b>What it does.</b> You call driving snow down on a wide circle round you for eight seconds. Shards of ice fall inside it again and again, each warned by a ring closing on its spot, each a small bite. Half of them fall where an enemy stands. As built the snow does not yet hide you or slow the enemies'' turning.


      <b>When it happens.</b> From a spell slot: cast it with that slot''s button (hold L2 and a face button, or 1 to 4).


      <b>The numbers.</b> Mix, 4 Shards, no mana: it waits 12 seconds after a cast, less with weapon play. The circle is 7 metres in radius, centred just ahead of you, for 8 seconds. A shard every 0.6 seconds, 0.34 seconds after its ring, 1.2 metres in radius: 3 damage, 4 stagger and one stack of Unsteady.


      <b>Works with.</b> Windchill (it keeps a crowd Unsteady), Against the Wall (a burst on each enemy a shard strikes), Rising Cut, Biting Wind.


      <b>Example.</b> Call it as a pack pours through a gate and fight on in the middle: they stay Unsteady while you work.'
  - Id: blizzard.avalanche
    Title: Avalanche
    Group: 
    Body: '<b>What it does.</b> A great head of snow, shaped like a dragon, runs down a lane ahead of you. It strikes everything it passes and carries it along, then its jaws close where it stops and bite hard. As built what it carries is not buried Frozen where it stops.


      <b>When it happens.</b> From a spell slot: cast it with that slot''s button (hold L2 and a face button, or 1 to 4).


      <b>The numbers.</b> Mix, 5 Shards, 50 mana. The lane is 9 metres long and 2 metres to each side; the head takes about 1.3 seconds to run it. Passing: 12.5 damage, 15 stagger and four stacks of Unsteady, once each, and shoved along. The bite at the end is 3 metres in radius: 25 damage, 30 stagger, a heavy blow and four stacks of Unsteady.


      <b>Works with.</b> Rising Cut (it leaves the bitten five deep), Hammer Down, Sliding Ice, Windchill, the charged blade (Wind''s shoves).


      <b>Example.</b> A line of soldiers on a bridge: send it down the bridge, and the whole line is heaped together at its end and bitten.'
  - Id: blizzard.dust
    Title: Diamond Dust
    Group: 
    Body: '<b>What it does.</b> Shards from an enemy you shatter do not fall. They hang turning round you, and your next dodge throws them all down its path.


      <b>When it happens.</b> Each time a frozen enemy is shattered, four shards join the ring round you. The next dodge throws them.


      <b>The numbers.</b> A god''s gift, never sold; in the playtest it can be bought. Four shards for each shatter, twelve at most; they wait up to 40 seconds after the last shatter. The dodge throws them down a lane 9 metres long and 1.1 metres to each side, in volleys of four: each volley deals 24 damage, 16 stagger and one stack of Chill to everything in the lane.


      <b>Works with.</b> Windchill, Cold Front, Biting Wind (Ice first), a heavy blow on a frozen enemy to shatter it, Ice''s charged blade (its blows shatter), Long Stride.


      <b>Example.</b> Shatter three frozen soldiers, then roll toward the archers: twelve shards go with you and strike each archer three times.'
  - Id: bloom.wetseed
    Title: Wet Seed
    Group: 
    Body: '<b>What it does.</b> Your blows lay Soaked and Seeded together, whichever of the two you carry first. A mixed branch''s marks are the exception to the rule that weapon blows lay only your first element''s affliction.


      <b>When it happens.</b> Every weapon blow that lands, while you carry both Water and Life.


      <b>The numbers.</b> Mix, 3 Shards. One stack of Soaked and one of Seeded a blow. Your first element''s own is not laid twice: once its root is learned, the root''s stack is the one a blow lays. Soaked lasts 8 seconds; Seeded holds up to three stacks for 8 seconds, and each of your weapon blows on it heals you 1 a stack.


      <b>Works with.</b> Flowering and Drowned Roots (they need Seeded, and Soaked as well), Riptide and Briar Patch for more of either, Strangling Vine, Great Lotus.


      <b>Example.</b> Carrying Life first, every blow seeds and soaks, so a perfect guard soon binds the enemy for Drowned Roots.'
  - Id: bloom.flower
    Title: Flowering
    Group: 
    Body: '<b>What it does.</b> A heavy blow on a Seeded enemy bursts its seed: you are mended, and everyone near it takes a burst of thorns and is Seeded and Soaked. It can happen once every seven seconds. As built no flower is shown and the burst comes at once.


      <b>When it happens.</b> A heavy blow or finisher that lands on an enemy carrying Seeded, at most once every 7 seconds.


      <b>The numbers.</b> Mix, 3 Shards. You mend 12. Everything within 3.5 metres of the one struck takes 12 damage, no stagger, and a stack of Seeded. Soaked on everything within 3.5 metres too, whichever element you carry first. The enemy''s own Seeded stays.


      <b>Works with.</b> Wet Seed, Briar Patch, Seeded''s own burst of thorns when a seeded enemy dies, Drowned Roots, Strangling Vine.


      <b>Example.</b> Seed a soldier in a crowd and land a heavy blow: you mend 12 and the soldiers round it are seeded for your next cuts.'
  - Id: bloom.roots
    Title: Drowned Roots
    Group: 
    Body: '<b>What it does.</b> A perfect guard against an enemy that is both Soaked and Seeded binds it in roots, held where it stands for a moment.


      <b>When it happens.</b> A perfect guard (press the guard button just before a blow lands) against an enemy carrying both Soaked and Seeded.


      <b>The numbers.</b> Mix, 3 Shards. Held still for 1.2 seconds.


      <b>Works with.</b> Wet Seed, Riptide and Briar Patch (one affliction each), Flowering, Lotus Step, Great Lotus, every Water and Life mark that answers a perfect guard.


      <b>Example.</b> Soak and seed a duellist, then guard its next thrust perfectly: it stands rooted while you land two cuts.'
  - Id: bloom.dew
    Title: Morning Dew
    Group: 
    Body: '<b>What it does.</b> Drinking a flask gives you a ward that turns aside one blow. And your blows throw a short blade of water toward the enemy struck that soaks what it passes, now and then. As built the dew does not yet gather in your health bar.


      <b>When it happens.</b> The ward with every flask you drink; the blade of water with a weapon blow that lands, at most once every 0.8 seconds.


      <b>The numbers.</b> Mix, 4 Shards. One ward a flask; you hold three at most. The blade flies 3.5 metres at 14 metres a second, 0.8 metres wide: 4 damage, no stagger, and Soaked.


      <b>Works with.</b> Spilled Water, Wellspring, Clear Water, Deep Well, Catch the Rain, Drowned Roots.


      <b>Example.</b> Drink before the brute''s red overhead: the ward takes it, and your answering cuts soak it.'
  - Id: bloom.lotus
    Title: Lotus Step
    Group: 
    Body: '<b>What it does.</b> You open a lotus on the ground just ahead of you. For twelve seconds it cuts every enemy standing on it and keeps it Soaked. As built it is one patch; the lotus left by each dodge, and its mending, are still to come.


      <b>When it happens.</b> From a spell slot: cast it with that slot''s button (hold L2 and a face button, or 1 to 4). It opens under an enemy within 2 metres, or 2 metres ahead.


      <b>The numbers.</b> Mix, 4 Shards, no mana: it waits 12 seconds after a cast, less with weapon play. 1.5 metres in radius, for 12 seconds. It bites once a second for 10 damage, with no stagger, and lays Soaked. If it lands, it charges your blade with Water.


      <b>Works with.</b> Drowned Roots (hold them on it), Wet Seed, Undertow (pull them onto it), Heavy Water, Great Lotus.


      <b>Example.</b> Open it at your feet in a doorway and hold the doorway: every enemy that reaches you is bitten and Soaked.'
  - Id: bloom.vine
    Title: Strangling Vine
    Group: 
    Body: '<b>What it does.</b> A great vine bursts up under the enemy nearest you. It strikes hard and throws that enemy and anything beside it into the air for a moment. As built the three-second hold and the greater mending are still to come.


      <b>When it happens.</b> From a spell slot: cast it with that slot''s button (hold L2 and a face button, or 1 to 4). It marks the spot under the enemy and follows it until the vine rises.


      <b>The numbers.</b> Mix, 5 Shards, 45 mana. The nearest enemy within 5 metres, or 5 metres ahead with none. It rises 0.5 seconds after the cast, 3 metres in radius: 20 damage and 50 stagger, a heavy blow, and Soaked. What it strikes is thrown up for 0.8 seconds. If it lands, it charges your blade with Water.


      <b>Works with.</b> Spring Tide (it is paid in mana, so it grows), Flowering, Heavy Water, Undertow, Wet Seed.


      <b>Example.</b> A brute and two soldiers close in: the vine throws all three up, and you cut the brute as it comes down.'
  - Id: bloom.great
    Title: Great Lotus
    Group: 
    Body: '<b>What it does.</b> A flask drunk while your surge burns opens a great lotus under you. Inside it you mend, and enemies are Soaked and Seeded. Each perfect guard you make inside closes a petal on the attacker and holds it. When the last petal closes, or its time is done, the lotus bursts, harder for every petal closed.


      <b>When it happens.</b> Drink a flask while Wellspring or Regrowth burns.


      <b>The numbers.</b> A god''s gift, never sold; in the playtest it can be bought. The lotus is 3 metres in radius and lasts 10 seconds. Each second, Soaked and a stack of Seeded on every enemy in it, and 2 health to you while you stand in it. Five petals; each holds its enemy 3 seconds. The burst is about 5 metres in radius: 30 damage and 30% more for each petal closed (75 at five), 40 stagger and a stack of Seeded.


      <b>Works with.</b> Wellspring (the flask heals half again as much), Regrowth, Morning Dew (the flask''s ward), Drowned Roots, Spilled Water, Catch the Rain.


      <b>Example.</b> Light Wellspring, drink in the middle of a pack, then perfect-guard five blows in the lotus: it bursts for 75 on everyone held.'
  - Id: dark.curse
    Title: Curse
    Group: 
    Body: '<b>What it does.</b> Every blow of your weapon that lands curses the enemy. A Cursed enemy hits you more weakly, and killing it heals you.


      <b>When it happens.</b> Always on once learned: every weapon blow that lands, light or heavy, while Dark is your first element. Weapon blows lay only the first element''s affliction; carried second, Dark curses through Grasp, its other spells, the charged blade and its strike.


      <b>The numbers.</b> 2 Shards. Cursed is one deep and lasts 8 seconds; each blow sets its clock back. A Cursed enemy deals 15% less damage, and killing it heals you 6.


      <b>Works with.</b> Long Curse (it lasts half again as long), Heavy Curse (they hit weaker still), Feast, Dread, Fat of the Kill, Devouring Maw, Hunger (every blow curses while it burns), and Wither on the Blight branch.


      <b>Example.</b> Cut the brute first: while it is Cursed every swing of its takes 15% less of your health, and when it falls you get 6 back.'
  - Id: dark.bloodprice
    Title: Blood Price
    Group: 
    Body: '<b>What it does.</b> When a spell asks more mana than you hold, the rest is paid in health. That health is not lost at once: it turns grey, and dealing damage wins it back like any grey health.


      <b>When it happens.</b> Each time you cast a spell paid in mana with too little mana for it: an element''s larger spell or a duo spell. Basic spells run on cooldowns and cost no mana, and Dark''s own spells cost none, so it matters for the spells of your other element and for duo spells.


      <b>The numbers.</b> 3 Shards. Each point of mana you lack costs half a point of health, taken as grey health. It never takes your last point: if the health is not there, the spell is not cast.


      <b>Works with.</b> Borrowed Strength (the grey health it leaves makes you hit harder), Slow Collector (grey health lingers longer), Small Cuts (health prices 20% smaller), Unpaid, and Wasting Grip on the Blight branch.


      <b>Example.</b> At 10 mana, cast Wasting Grip for 40: it goes off, 15 health turns grey, and the blows that follow win it back.'
  - Id: dark.borrowed
    Title: Borrowed Strength
    Group: 
    Body: '<b>What it does.</b> The more grey health you carry, the harder your weapon strikes.


      <b>When it happens.</b> Always on once learned, for as long as any grey health remains: from blocked blows, Blood Price, Pawned Heart or anything else that leaves health owed.


      <b>The numbers.</b> 3 Shards. Each point of grey health adds 0.75% weapon damage, up to 30% at 40 points.


      <b>Works with.</b> Blood Price, Slow Collector and Unpaid (the grey stays longer), Reckless Arm (swings cost 15% less stamina while any is owed), and Pawned Heart (its stopped heart leaves grey health behind).


      <b>Example.</b> Block a brute''s three-blow chain and carry 20 grey health: your answer strikes 15% harder, and each cut wins some of the grey back.'
  - Id: dark.debtscalled
    Title: Debts Called
    Group: 
    Body: '<b>What it does.</b> Everything near is dragged to a point just in front of you, and when it gets there a burst of shadow strikes it all at once as a heavy blow.


      <b>When it happens.</b> From a spell slot: cast it with that slot''s button (hold L2 and a face button, or 1 to 4).


      <b>The numbers.</b> 4 Shards, no mana: it waits 10 seconds after a cast, less with weapon play. The point is 1 metre ahead of you. For half a second everything within 4.5 metres of it is drawn most of the way in; then everything within 4.5 metres takes 18 damage, 35 stagger and a Curse. As built the burst strikes but throws nothing back, and it does not yet grow as your health falls.


      <b>Works with.</b> Curse, Dread, Feast, Easy Prey, Grasp, and the charged blade (it charges your weapon with Dark when it lands).


      <b>Example.</b> Four soldiers spread round you: one cast draws them into a knot at your sword''s point, all Cursed, ready for a wide swing.'
  - Id: dark.pawnedheart
    Title: Pawned Heart
    Group: 
    Body: '<b>What it does.</b> You tear out your heart and set it down behind you. Your health drops to a single point, and while the heart beats your weapon strikes far harder and swings cost no stamina. Walk away from the heart and then back onto it, and all the health you pawned comes back with a share of the damage you dealt meanwhile. If its ring closes first, the heart stops: you keep one point, and half of what you pawned comes back only as grey health.


      <b>When it happens.</b> From a spell slot: cast it with that slot''s button (hold L2 and a face button, or 1 to 4). It cannot be cast at one point of health.


      <b>The numbers.</b> 4 Shards, no mana: the price is health, and it waits 40 seconds after a cast, less with weapon play. The heart lies 1.8 metres behind you and beats for 10 seconds. While it beats: 60% more weapon damage and swings free of stamina. You must step 2.6 metres from it, then come within 1 metre of it again: back come all the health pawned and 30% of the damage you dealt. A blow that lands on you while it beats can kill you.


      <b>Works with.</b> Borrowed Strength (the grey health a stopped heart leaves), Unpaid, Near the Grave (you are below a third the whole time), Hunger, and Small Cuts.


      <b>Example.</b> Pawn the heart beside a staggered brute, cut it down in five free swings, then step back onto the heart and stand up with more health than you pawned.'
  - Id: dark.unpaid
    Title: Unpaid
    Group: 
    Body: '<b>What it does.</b> Grey health lingers twice as long before it fades, and every blow you land heals you a little. The price: flasks heal half as much.


      <b>When it happens.</b> Always on once learned. The healing comes with every weapon blow that lands.


      <b>The numbers.</b> 6 Shards. Grey health fades at half its usual speed, 5 a second where it is 10. Each blow that lands heals 2, at most twice a second. A flask heals 22.5 where it healed 45. As built nothing is yet left wholly grey: every wound still takes health as it always did.


      <b>Works with.</b> Borrowed Strength (the grey stays and keeps you strong), Blood Price, Slow Collector, Pawned Heart, Hunger.


      <b>Example.</b> Block a long chain and keep cutting: the grey health waits longer for you to win it back, and each cut adds 2 besides.'
  - Id: dark.feast
    Title: Feast
    Group: 
    Body: '<b>What it does.</b> A finisher on a Cursed enemy feeds you: it heals, and heals more while Hunger burns.


      <b>When it happens.</b> Every finisher (a heavy blow on a staggered enemy) that lands on a Cursed enemy.


      <b>The numbers.</b> 3 Shards. Heals 12, and 6 more while Hunger lasts: 18 in all.


      <b>Works with.</b> Curse, Grasp and Debts Called (to curse first), Hunger, Long Hunger, Never Sated (20 more on any finisher), and The Reaping on the Blight branch.


      <b>Example.</b> Stagger a Cursed brute with Hunger lit and finish it: 18 health back, and 6 more when it dies.'
  - Id: dark.glut
    Title: Glut
    Group: 
    Body: '<b>What it does.</b> Drinking a flask wraps you in a shade that turns aside one blow. So does a kill, though not more than once in ten seconds.


      <b>When it happens.</b> Every flask you drink, and any kill at most once every ten seconds.


      <b>The numbers.</b> 3 Shards. One ward a flask or a kill, three at most. A kill gives one at most once in 10 seconds. Each ward takes a blow you did not guard, a red attack among them. As built it gives wards; health over a full bar is not yet kept.


      <b>Works with.</b> Near the Grave (kills give wards below a third), Dread, Fat of the Kill (a Cursed kill heals 3 more). Never Sated takes your flasks, so only kills feed it then.


      <b>Example.</b> Drink between two packs and the next soldier''s thrust breaks on the shade instead of on you.'
  - Id: dark.dread
    Title: Dread
    Group: 
    Body: '<b>What it does.</b> When a Cursed enemy dies, every enemy near where it fell loses heart, and its balance buckles.


      <b>When it happens.</b> Each time a Cursed enemy dies, whatever killed it; at most once a second.


      <b>The numbers.</b> 3 Shards. 30 stagger to every enemy within 8 metres of where it fell. No damage.


      <b>Works with.</b> Curse, Debts Called (curse a knot of them), Easy Prey, Feast, Carrion Flies and One Death Feeds on the Blight branch, Unsteady (more stagger from each).


      <b>Example.</b> Kill a Cursed soldier at the front of a pack and the four behind it are 30 nearer a stagger before they reach you.'
  - Id: dark.maw
    Title: Devouring Maw
    Group: 
    Body: '<b>What it does.</b> A great jaw of shadow rises at your shoulder and lunges down a lane before you, striking and carrying what it passes, then closes at the end of its reach. Each Cursed enemy it bites feeds you.


      <b>When it happens.</b> From a spell slot: cast it with that slot''s button (hold L2 and a face button, or 1 to 4).


      <b>The numbers.</b> 4 Shards, no mana: it waits 11 seconds after a cast, less with weapon play. It forms for 0.3 seconds and runs 5 metres along a lane 3.2 metres wide. What it passes takes 15 damage, 15 stagger and a Curse, and is shoved along with it. The jaws close 5 metres ahead: everything within 2.4 metres takes 30 damage and 30 stagger as a heavy blow, and a Curse. Each time it strikes an enemy that is Cursed you heal 5.


      <b>Works with.</b> Curse and Grasp (curse them first, so every strike feeds), Long Shadows (15% harder), Feast, Dread, Hunger, and the charged blade.


      <b>Example.</b> A row of Cursed soldiers in a corridor: the jaw drags them to its end and closes on all of them, and you heal for each.'
  - Id: dark.neversated
    Title: Never Sated
    Group: 
    Body: '<b>What it does.</b> You carry no flasks at all. Instead every blow you land feeds you a little, every Cursed kill a great deal, and every finisher more.


      <b>When it happens.</b> Always on once learned: with every weapon blow that lands, every Cursed enemy killed and every finisher.


      <b>The numbers.</b> 6 Shards. No flasks, and none are earned back. Each blow heals 6% of its damage. A Cursed kill heals 12, on top of Cursed''s own 6. A finisher heals 20.


      <b>Works with.</b> Curse, Feast (a Cursed finisher heals 32, 38 in Hunger), Hunger (its 30% and this 6% together), Fat of the Kill, Grave Appetite.


      <b>Example.</b> Against a long pack, never stop: each kill and finisher keeps you standing where a flask would have.'
  - Id: dark.nearthegrave
    Title: Near the Grave
    Group: 
    Body: '<b>What it does.</b> Below a third of your health you strike harder, and each kill wraps you in a shade that takes the next blow.


      <b>When it happens.</b> Always on once learned, while your health is below a third. The shade comes with each kill made down there.


      <b>The numbers.</b> 3 Shards. Below a third: 20% more weapon damage. Each kill below a third gives one ward, three at most.


      <b>Works with.</b> Hard to Bury (12% less damage taken down there), Pawned Heart (it puts you there), Hollow Strength, Glut, A Life for a Life.


      <b>Example.</b> At 25 health in a pack: cut harder, and each soldier that falls leaves you a shade against the next one''s blow.'
  - Id: dark.hollowstrength
    Title: Hollow Strength
    Group: 
    Body: '<b>What it does.</b> While you are Risen, you strike harder and no blow makes you flinch. Each kill stills the draining of your health for a few breaths.


      <b>When it happens.</b> While Risen: after A Life for a Life stands you up, or for good with Dead Already.


      <b>The numbers.</b> 3 Shards. Risen: 25% more weapon damage, and blows that land do not stop you. Each kill stops the drain for 3 seconds.


      <b>Works with.</b> A Life for a Life, Dead Already, Slow Rot (the drain runs at 70%), Grave Appetite (each blow heals 1 more while Risen), Near the Grave.


      <b>Example.</b> Risen with a sliver of health: swing straight through the soldiers'' blows, and each one you kill gives you three seconds without the drain.'
  - Id: dark.secondshadow
    Title: Second Shadow
    Group: 
    Body: '<b>What it does.</b> Your shadow stands at your shoulder for a while. Every weapon blow you land, it lands again a beat later, for half the damage, and curses.


      <b>When it happens.</b> From a spell slot: cast it with that slot''s button (hold L2 and a face button, or 1 to 4). Then every weapon blow that lands is echoed.


      <b>The numbers.</b> 4 Shards, no mana: it waits 12 seconds after a cast, less with weapon play. It stands for 8 seconds. Each echo lands 0.2 seconds after your blow, for 50% of its damage with no stagger, and lays a Curse. One shadow at a time.


      <b>Works with.</b> Curse, Pawned Heart (half of a much bigger blow), Borrowed Strength, Near the Grave, Hollow Strength, Hunger.


      <b>Example.</b> Cast it as a brute kneels staggered: every cut of the finisher''s opening lands twice.'
  - Id: dark.deadstand
    Title: The Dead Stand
    Group: 
    Body: '<b>What it does.</b> Three shades rise beside you. Each runs at an enemy, a different one while there are enough, and jabs it for a while before going out. With no enemy near they keep at your side.


      <b>When it happens.</b> From a spell slot: cast it with that slot''s button (hold L2 and a face button, or 1 to 4).


      <b>The numbers.</b> 4 Shards, no mana: it waits 12 seconds after a cast, less with weapon play. Three shades for 5 seconds. Each finds an enemy within 16 metres; in reach, it jabs about half a second later and then every 1.6 seconds, for 12 damage, 12 stagger and a Curse each time. As built they rise beside you, not from the dead.


      <b>Works with.</b> Curse, Dread and Feast (the shades keep the pack Cursed), Long Shadows (15% harder), and the charged blade.


      <b>Example.</b> Call them on three archers at the back while you hold the front: each archer is Cursed and pestered until you get there.'
  - Id: dark.deadalready
    Title: Dead Already
    Group: 
    Body: '<b>What it does.</b> You do not wait to die: you are Risen from now on. In every fight your health drains toward its last point, and your blows feed you. You strike far harder. There is no second rising.


      <b>When it happens.</b> Always on once learned. The drain runs while an enemy is within 12 metres of you.


      <b>The numbers.</b> 6 Shards. 25% more weapon damage, and 30% of each blow''s damage comes back as health. The drain takes 2 health a second, never the last point. Every mark that asks for you to be Risen is in force at all times. A Life for a Life can no longer stand you up.


      <b>Works with.</b> Hollow Strength (another 25%, no flinch, and kills still the drain), Slow Rot (drain 70%), Grave Appetite, Hunger (another 30% back), Never Sated.


      <b>Example.</b> Fight without pause: every cut gives back far more than the drain takes, and the moment you stop to wait, it bleeds you down.'
  - Id: dark.lifeforalife
    Title: A Life for a Life
    Group: 
    Body: '<b>What it does.</b> Once, the blow that would kill you does not. You stand again with half your health, and it drains away. A sigil hangs over the enemy that killed you: land a finisher on it and you live again, health returns, and you may rise once more.


      <b>When it happens.</b> The moment a blow would kill you, if you have not risen yet. The finisher on the killer, or on anyone if the killer is already gone, ends it.


      <b>The numbers.</b> A god''s gift, never sold; in the playtest it can be bought. You rise at half your full health. It drains 4 a second, never the last point. The finisher gives back half your full health and readies the rising again. Without it you stay Risen, draining to one point, and a blow that kills you then is a fall; after a fall you may rise again. Dead Already turns it off.


      <b>Works with.</b> Hollow Strength, Slow Rot, Grave Appetite, Near the Grave, Feast.


      <b>Example.</b> A brute''s red overhead kills you: rise, break its balance, finish it, and stand with half your health and your rising ready again.'
  - Id: earth.tremor
    Title: Tremor
    Group: 
    Body: '<b>What it does.</b> Your heavy blows shake the ground under an enemy and lay Tremor, and a finisher lays all of it at once. A shaken enemy is slowed, and its balance does not come back while the shaking lasts.


      <b>When it happens.</b> Every heavy blow that lands adds a stack; every finisher fills it. Like every root, it lays with the weapon only while Earth is your first element; carried second, Earth''s Tremor comes from your spells, the charged blade and the R2 strike.


      <b>The numbers.</b> 2 Shards. One stack a heavy blow, three on a finisher, three at most. Tremor lasts 6 seconds; each stack slows the enemy by 10%, and while it lasts its stagger meter does not drain.


      <b>Works with.</b> Heavy Hand and The Slow Hand (more heavy blows, or every blow shaking), Cairn (it spends Tremor for stones), Left in Rubble, Bedrock (one more stack with every blow), Buckled on the Forge branch, and The Ground Gives when Soaked meets it.


      <b>Not built yet.</b> Earth''s base buff from GAME.md, afflictions laid on you lasting half as long: nothing lays an affliction on the player yet.


      <b>Example.</b> A heavy blow on a brute leaves its balance bar stuck where you left it: step back, guard its swing, and come in again with the bar still waiting.'
  - Id: earth.heavyhand
    Title: Heavy Hand
    Group: 
    Body: '<b>What it does.</b> Nothing stops your heavy blows. Struck while winding one up or swinging it, you still take the blow, but less of it, and yours still lands. Red attacks cannot stop it either.


      <b>When it happens.</b> Always on once learned: any blow that lands on you during a heavy blow''s wind-up or swing.


      <b>The numbers.</b> 3 Shards. You take 35% less from a blow that lands then, and you do not flinch.


      <b>Works with.</b> Tremor, The Slow Hand, Under the Mound and Cairn, which grow from it, Hand of the Mountain, Hammer and Anvil on the Forge branch.


      <b>Example.</b> Two soldiers swing at you as you wind up: you take both, lightly, and your heavy blow lands on the first anyway.'
  - Id: earth.mound
    Title: Under the Mound
    Group: 
    Body: '<b>What it does.</b> Under the Mound, the movement spell of the tree. You sink into the ground and travel as a hump of heaving turf along the stick, out of reach, and burst out in a ring of thrown sod and stones that shakes everything round you.


      <b>When it happens.</b> From a spell slot: cast it with that slot''s button (hold L2 and a face button, or 1 to 4).


      <b>The numbers.</b> 4 Shards, no mana: it waits 9 seconds after a cast, less with weapon play (its Empower: 8, and 10 metres). Up to 8 metres; where you come out, 12 damage, 25 stagger and one Tremor. As built it is a step through the enemy faced (8 metres ahead with none), and if it lands, your next heavy blow within 4 seconds is critical.


      <b>Works with.</b> Heavy Hand, Tremor and Cairn (it shakes what it reaches), The Slow Hand, the charged blade: it charges your weapon with Earth when it lands.


      <b>Not built yet.</b> Going under the ground along the stick, untouchable on the way, and the ring of sod 2.5 metres round where you come up: for now a step through the enemy faced that strikes as you pass.


      <b>Example.</b> An archer behind a line of shields: go under them and come up at its back, shaken and open to your heavy blow.'
  - Id: earth.mound.shape
    Title: 'Under the Mound: Ditch and Bank or Barrow Road'
    Group: 
    Body: '<b>What it does.</b> Opens two shapes of Under the Mound, chosen at any rest fire. <b>Ditch and Bank</b>, the old earthworks: the turf you heave stays up behind you as a bank a metre high along your whole path, nothing walks through it, and what stands on the line as it rises is thrown off it, shaken. You draw a wall as you go. <b>Barrow Road</b>: hold to stay under and steer; come up under an enemy and it is thrown up as by Stone Rise, and you stand behind it.


      <b>When it happens.</b> Whenever you cast Under the Mound, as the shape it wears. Before this is bought, the plain spell is cast.


      <b>The numbers.</b> 3 Shards. Ditch and Bank: a line of six patches 8 metres long from where you went under, 0.6 metres round each, for 5 seconds, biting once a second for 4 damage, 10 stagger and one Tremor. Barrow Road: under for up to 1.5 seconds; what you come up under is thrown up for 0.6 seconds.


      <b>Works with.</b> Ditch and Bank: Quake Step and Cairn on what stands on the bank. Barrow Road: Under the Mound''s own Master, your heavy blows on what hangs in the air.


      <b>Not built yet.</b> The bank blocking bodies, and enemies thrown off it as it rises: for now it is ground along your path that bites and shakes. Barrow Road''s hold and steer: for now the spell goes where it goes, and only the throw is built.


      <b>Example.</b> Ditch and Bank across a doorway: the pack that follows you through it comes out shaken.'
  - Id: earth.mound.master
    Title: 'Under the Mound: Mastered'
    Group: 
    Body: '<b>What it does.</b> Go under in the instant a blow would land on you, as a perfect dodge, and you come up at once behind the attacker. Your next blow lands as a heavy blow, with two Tremor, and breaks half again as much balance.


      <b>When it happens.</b> For now, every cast of Under the Mound. It must be in a slot.


      <b>The numbers.</b> 3 Shards. Each cast gives what a perfect dodge gives: 12 mana and 1.5 seconds off every running spell and strike clock. For 3 seconds, until your next blow lands, your blows break 50% more balance and each lays one stack more.


      <b>Works with.</b> Tremor (the next blow''s extra stack), Heavy Hand and The Slow Hand, Cairn (the mana it gives back).


      <b>Not built yet.</b> The shared movement rule''s timing, started as a blow would land, and coming up behind the attacker; the next blow landing as a heavy blow: for now every cast gives the dodge''s reward and the stronger next blow.


      <b>Example.</b> A brute''s overhead is falling: go under it, come up behind, and the next blow nearly breaks it.'
  - Id: earth.cairn
    Title: Cairn
    Group: 
    Body: '<b>What it does.</b> Cairn, Earth''s larger spell and its detonator. You stamp the weapon''s butt and the Cailleach''s stones fall from her apron onto every shaken enemy near you, one stone for each depth of Tremor it carries. The Tremor is spent, and the stones stay heaped on it, slowing it.


      <b>When it happens.</b> From a spell slot: cast it with that slot''s button (hold L2 and a face button, or 1 to 4). It costs mana, not a wait.


      <b>The numbers.</b> 4 Shards, 40 mana (its Empower: 35). Every enemy within 10 metres carrying Tremor, 0.3 seconds after the cast: a stone falls for each depth, 12 damage and 15 stagger each (three stones on a full Tremor, 36 and 45), and 10 more damage for the heap. The heap stays 4 seconds and slows the enemy by 30%. An enemy with no Tremor is not touched.


      <b>Works with.</b> Tremor and everything that lays it: heavy blows, finishers, Quake Step, The Slow Hand. Unbroken Cairn and your heavy blows, Rooted for its Master.


      <b>Not built yet.</b> The slow as 15% a stone (for now 30% whatever the depth), and the Empower''s 14 a stone (for now 12).


      <b>Example.</b> Three soldiers each shaken three deep: one stamp drops nine stones and leaves all three slowed and with their shaking spent.'
  - Id: earth.cairn.shape
    Title: 'Cairn: Unbroken Cairn or Thrown Stones'
    Group: 
    Body: '<b>What it does.</b> Opens two shapes of Cairn, chosen at any rest fire. <b>Unbroken Cairn</b>: the stones land soft and wait, and your next heavy blow on a heaped enemy breaks its cairn outward into everything near it. The burst waits for your blow. <b>Thrown Stones</b>: the stones do not stay; each enemy''s heap is flung at once at the nearest other enemy, so one shaken enemy shakes the next.


      <b>When it happens.</b> Whenever you cast Cairn, as the shape it wears. Before this is bought, the plain stones fall.


      <b>The numbers.</b> 3 Shards. Unbroken Cairn: a heavy blow on a heaped enemy within 4 seconds bursts 2.5 metres round it, 36 damage and 20 stagger. Thrown Stones: from each heaped enemy a stone flies to the nearest other enemy within 5 metres, 24 damage, 10 stagger and two Tremor.


      <b>Works with.</b> Unbroken Cairn: Heavy Hand and The Slow Hand. Thrown Stones: Cairn cast again on what the stones shook.


      <b>Not built yet.</b> Unbroken Cairn''s stones landing soft (for now they still fall at the cast) and its burst as 18 a stone (for now 36 whatever the depth). Thrown Stones'' heaps flung in place of staying (for now they still fall and heap) and a stone for each depth (for now two stones'' worth).


      <b>Example.</b> Unbroken Cairn on a pack round a brute: one heavy blow on the brute breaks its heap through all of them.'
  - Id: earth.cairn.master
    Title: 'Cairn: Mastered'
    Group: 
    Body: '<b>What it does.</b> Cast it after standing still for a second, and every stone strikes twice and half the mana comes back.


      <b>When it happens.</b> For now, when you cast it while Rooted (no dodge begun for 3 seconds). Cairn must be in a slot.


      <b>The numbers.</b> 3 Shards. 20 mana back. A second fall 0.8 seconds after the cast on each shaken enemy, 24 damage and 30 stagger.


      <b>Works with.</b> Rooted, Immovable, Heavy Hand; Mountain Stance, which keeps you standing.


      <b>Not built yet.</b> Standing still for a second as the moment (for now Rooted, three seconds without a dodge), and every stone striking twice (for now a second fall of two stones'' worth).


      <b>Example.</b> Hold your ground through a soldier''s chain, then stamp: twice the stones, and half the price back for the next.'
  - Id: earth.slowhand
    Title: The Slow Hand
    Group: 
    Body: '<b>What it does.</b> The Slow Hand, a keystone. Every swing is slower and costs more stamina, but your light blows hit like heavy ones, and every blow shakes its enemy.


      <b>When it happens.</b> Always on once learned. The Tremor on every blow comes only while Earth is your first element.


      <b>The numbers.</b> 6 Shards. Swings 22% slower; blows cost 20% more stamina. Light blows deal 35% more damage and 60% more stagger. Every weapon blow lays one stack of Tremor.


      <b>Works with.</b> Tremor, Heavy Hand, Cairn (full Tremor everywhere to spend), Under the Mound''s Master, Bedrock.


      <b>Not built yet.</b> Light blows counting as heavy: for now they pass no guard, force no flinch, and set off nothing that waits on a heavy blow.


      <b>Example.</b> Three light blows on a soldier leave it three deep in Tremor and close to staggered, without a heavy blow thrown.'
  - Id: earth.rooted
    Title: Rooted
    Group: 
    Body: '<b>What it does.</b> Fight for a few breaths without rolling and you are Rooted. Rooted, you take less from every blow and holding your guard costs less stamina. Starting a roll ends it, and the count begins again.


      <b>When it happens.</b> Always on once learned. You are Rooted once no dodge has begun for 3 seconds.


      <b>The numbers.</b> 3 Shards. Rooted: 8% less damage taken, and a blocked blow costs 30% less stamina.


      <b>Works with.</b> Quake Step and Mountain Stance, which grow from it, Immovable, Heavy Hand, the Masters of Stone Rise and Cairn (both ask you to stand your ground), and Bedrock (20% less damage again while it burns).


      <b>Not built yet.</b> Nothing yet stops you being pushed back while Rooted.


      <b>Example.</b> Plant your feet in front of a duellist and block its chain: each blocked blow costs less stamina and the grey it leaves is smaller.'
  - Id: earth.quakestep
    Title: Quake Step
    Group: 
    Body: '<b>What it does.</b> Quake Step, a breaker. You raise a foot and bring it down, and the ground heaves all round you and shakes everything it strikes. What it strikes flinches: the attack it had begun is broken, unless it is steadfast.


      <b>When it happens.</b> From a spell slot: cast it with that slot''s button (hold L2 and a face button, or 1 to 4).


      <b>The numbers.</b> 4 Shards, no mana: it waits 9 seconds after a cast, less with weapon play (its Empower: 8, and 6 metres). It lands 0.45 seconds after the cast, 5 metres round you: 16 damage, 30 stagger and two stacks of Tremor on each enemy, and each flinches for 0.4 seconds.


      <b>Works with.</b> Tremor and Cairn (two stacks on everything round you), Rooted, Standing Stones (a pillar on what it strikes), Buckled on the Forge branch. Landing it charges the blade with Earth.


      <b>Not built yet.</b> The double stagger on an enemy showing an attack, and its attack broken only then: for now everything it strikes flinches, and the stagger is the same for all.


      <b>Example.</b> Four soldiers close round you: stamp, and all four are two deep in Tremor with their balance bars stuck.'
  - Id: earth.quakestep.shape
    Title: 'Quake Step: Struck From Afar or The Second Wave'
    Group: 
    Body: '<b>What it does.</b> Opens two shapes of Quake Step, chosen at any rest fire. <b>Struck From Afar</b>, the Cailleach striking the ground with her staff: the stamp lands not round you but on the shadow of a far enemy, breaking its attack where it stands and holding it a moment. You break the archer''s draw without crossing the room. <b>The Second Wave</b>: one stamp sends out two rings, the quick thin wave of an earthquake and then the slow heavy one; what both catch is thrown off its feet.


      <b>When it happens.</b> Whenever you cast Quake Step, as the shape it wears. Before this is bought, the plain ring is cast.


      <b>The numbers.</b> 3 Shards. Struck From Afar: a ring 2.5 metres round an enemy up to 8 metres off, 0.45 seconds after the cast, 16 damage, 30 stagger and two Tremor, and it is held 0.6 seconds. The Second Wave: a ring to 5 metres, 8 damage and one Tremor, then 0.7 seconds later a ring to 7 metres round where you stamped, 18 damage and 40 stagger; what the first ring strikes is thrown down for 1 second.


      <b>Works with.</b> Struck From Afar: Cairn on the one it shook. The Second Wave: Tremor, Unbroken Cairn and your heavy blows on what lies on the ground.


      <b>Not built yet.</b> Struck From Afar placed on the enemy faced (for now the nearest within 8 metres). The Second Wave throwing down only what the second ring catches too, at that moment (for now what the first ring catches is thrown down at once).


      <b>Example.</b> The Second Wave in a crowd: step back after the first ring so the second catches them all as they come.'
  - Id: earth.quakestep.master
    Title: 'Quake Step: Mastered'
    Group: 
    Body: '<b>What it does.</b> Break an enemy out of its wind-up, and Quake Step is ready again at once.


      <b>When it happens.</b> For now, whenever Quake Step strikes an enemy, at most once in 18 seconds. Quake Step must be in a slot.


      <b>The numbers.</b> 3 Shards. Its own wait ends.


      <b>Works with.</b> The Second Wave (two stamps in a row), Cairn after two stamps.


      <b>Not built yet.</b> An enemy broken out of its wind-up as the moment: nothing yet tells when an enemy begins an attack, so any stamp that lands counts, once in 18 seconds.


      <b>Example.</b> Stamp a soldier out of its swing, then stamp again as its friend closes.'
  - Id: earth.stance
    Title: Mountain Stance
    Group: 
    Body: '<b>What it does.</b> Mountain Stance, a counter (Grey Stone, the Cailleach turning to stone each summer). You go wholly to stone, unable to move. A blow that strikes the stone is turned, red ones too, and it jars its attacker: it is shaken and its next attack comes late. The blows the stone turned load your next heavy blow.


      <b>When it happens.</b> From a spell slot: cast it with that slot''s button (hold L2 and a face button, or 1 to 4), then any blow while you stand.


      <b>The numbers.</b> 4 Shards, no mana: it waits 10 seconds after a cast, less with weapon play (its Empower: 9, and 3 seconds). As built it is the stance of stone: up to 2.5 seconds, and the first blow to land is turned for nothing and answered by a jar of stone 3 metres long and 120 degrees wide toward the one who struck: 6 damage, 10 stagger and two Tremor. Its wind-ups come at 0.7 of their pace for 3 seconds, and for 3.5 seconds your next blow that lands breaks 50% more balance.


      <b>Works with.</b> Rooted (stand, and it counts), Immovable, which grows from it, Heavy Hand, Cairn''s Master, Buckled on the Forge branch.


      <b>Not built yet.</b> Every blow turned for as long as you stand, not only the first; the load counted as 20 stagger for each blow turned (25 with the Empower) and given to the next heavy blow within a second of letting go; the wait of 5 seconds when nothing struck the stone. For now the first blow is turned and the next blow of any kind is loaded.


      <b>Example.</b> A duellist starts its chain: go to stone, take the first cut on the stone, and its next swing comes slow enough to guard.'
  - Id: earth.stance.shape
    Title: 'Mountain Stance: Stone Skin or Fist of Rock'
    Group: 
    Body: '<b>What it does.</b> Opens two shapes of Mountain Stance, chosen at any rest fire. <b>Stone Skin</b>: the blow is turned but not answered; two plates of stone grow on your shoulders instead, each taking most of one blow and stopping its flinch, then breaking in a burst round you. <b>Fist of Rock</b>, the stance as it was first built: stand as stone a short while, and the first blow to land is turned for nothing and a fist of rock rises under the one who struck. One blow, answered at once.


      <b>When it happens.</b> Whenever you cast Mountain Stance, as the shape it wears. Before this is bought, Grey Stone is cast.


      <b>The numbers.</b> 3 Shards. Stone Skin: when the stance turns a blow, two wards, three held at most; each turns one blow and breaks in a burst 3 metres round you, 14 damage, 24 stagger and one Tremor. Fist of Rock: up to 1.5 seconds; the answer is a cone 4 metres long and 90 degrees wide, 30 damage, 60 stagger and two Tremor.


      <b>Works with.</b> Stone Skin: Glaze''s ward if you carry Ice, Heavy Hand, Immovable. Fist of Rock: Tremor and Cairn, Unbroken Cairn''s heavy blow after it.


      <b>Not built yet.</b> Stone Skin''s plates taking 60% of one blow (for now a ward takes the whole of it), and the stance''s jar set aside while it is worn. Fist of Rock''s answer rising under the one who struck: for now it is a cone thrown at it.


      <b>Example.</b> Stone Skin before a pack closes: the first two blows that reach you each throw stone back at the whole ring.'
  - Id: earth.stance.master
    Title: 'Mountain Stance: Mastered'
    Group: 
    Body: '<b>What it does.</b> Turn a red attack, and its attacker is stunned for a second and a half, less for a god or an elite, and Mountain Stance is ready again.


      <b>When it happens.</b> For now, whenever the stance turns any blow. Mountain Stance must be in a slot.


      <b>The numbers.</b> 3 Shards. The attacker is held 1.5 seconds (a god or an elite 0.6, the colossus not at all). The stance''s wait ends, at most once in 20 seconds.


      <b>Works with.</b> Fist of Rock (a full answer on a held enemy), Cairn and your heavy blows on the one held.


      <b>Not built yet.</b> The red attack as the moment: nothing yet tells the blow turned was red, so any blow counts, and the stance comes back once in 20 seconds at most.


      <b>Example.</b> A brute''s red overhead lands on the stone: it stands stunned while you break its balance.'
  - Id: earth.immovable
    Title: Immovable
    Group: 
    Body: '<b>What it does.</b> Immovable, a keystone. You stop rolling away. Your roll hardly moves you, but every blow takes less of you, guarding and dodging cost less stamina, and the moment of a perfect guard is longer.


      <b>When it happens.</b> Always on once learned.


      <b>The numbers.</b> 6 Shards. The roll goes a tenth as far (about half a metre). 16% less damage taken. Dodges and blocked blows cost 30% less stamina. The perfect guard''s moment is 30% longer.


      <b>Works with.</b> Mountain Stance, which it grows from, Rooted (do not roll, and both count), Heavy Hand, Cairn''s and Stone Rise''s Masters (you are always standing your ground), Bedrock.


      <b>Not built yet.</b> The dodge as a brace that moves nowhere, whose first moment turns any blow, red ones too, and Rooted that never ends: for now the roll is still a roll, it lets blows pass through it, and it still ends Rooted.


      <b>Example.</b> Fight a duellist toe to toe: guard everything, perfect-guard what you can, and roll in place through the one red thrust.'
  - Id: earth.standingstones
    Title: Standing Stones
    Group: 
    Body: '<b>What it does.</b> When a spell of yours strikes an enemy, a pillar of stone comes down on it a moment later and shakes it.


      <b>When it happens.</b> Whenever a spell of yours strikes an enemy, Stone Rise or any spell in your slots. At most once every second and a half.


      <b>The numbers.</b> 3 Shards. The pillar falls on a warning ring 0.5 seconds later, 1.5 metres in radius: 20 damage, 35 stagger and one stack of Tremor.


      <b>Works with.</b> Stone Rise, which grows beside it, Left in Rubble and Fissure, Quake Step, Tremor and Cairn.


      <b>Not built yet.</b> The design re-aims it: two of your stones may stand at once, and an enemy driven into one is hurt and breaks it. Nothing yet stands on the field to be driven into, so the falling pillar stands in.


      <b>Example.</b> Stone Rise under an archer, and half a second later a pillar lands on it as well.'
  - Id: earth.base
    Title: Stone Rise
    Group: 
    Body: '<b>What it does.</b> Stone Rise, Earth''s own spell, comes with the element and is never bought. A quarter second after the cast the ground breaks under the enemy faced and throws it up for a moment, and three rocks stand behind it that nothing walks through.


      <b>When it happens.</b> From a spell slot: cast it with that slot''s button (hold L2 and a face button, or 1 to 4). Carrying Earth, it is always yours to put in a slot.


      <b>The numbers.</b> Given with Earth. No mana: it waits 7 seconds after a cast, less with weapon play; its Empower makes that 6. An enemy within 5 metres, 1.3 metres round it: 14 damage, 30 stagger and one Tremor. The rocks stand 4.5 seconds.


      <b>Works with.</b> Its Empower, its two shapes and its Master; Tremor and Cairn; Standing Stones (a pillar on what it strikes); the charged blade, which its landing charges with Earth.


      <b>Not built yet.</b> The Empower''s 18 damage and 36 stagger: the base spell is cast by Earth''s kit, which takes only the Empower''s shorter wait.


      <b>Example.</b> Rise the stone under the archer at the back: it is thrown up, shaken, and walled off from the fight behind it.'
  - Id: earth.base.shape
    Title: 'Stone Rise: Raised Stone or Dropped From the Apron'
    Group: 
    Body: '<b>What it does.</b> Opens two shapes of Stone Rise, chosen at any rest fire. <b>Raised Stone</b>: no rocks behind; the pillar that lifted the enemy stays beside it, blocking bodies and thrown attacks, and a heavy blow of yours on it shatters it into a cone of shards away from you. Raise it, fight round it, break it through them. <b>Dropped From the Apron</b>: a boulder falls from above onto the spot, its shadow growing, and lies there; a heavy blow on it rolls it along the blow, crushing a lane, until it breaks on a wall or a large enemy.


      <b>When it happens.</b> Whenever you cast Stone Rise, as the shape it wears. Before this is bought, the plain stone rises.


      <b>The numbers.</b> 3 Shards. Raised Stone: for 6 seconds, your next heavy blow on the enemy it lifted throws a cone of shards from you through it, 5 metres and 70 degrees, 18 damage, 20 stagger and one Tremor. Dropped From the Apron: the nearest enemy within 5 metres, 0.6 seconds after the cast, 1.5 metres round it: 24 damage, 45 stagger and two Tremor; for 6 seconds a heavy blow on it crushes a lane 8 metres on from it, away from you, 16 damage, 30 stagger and one Tremor to each it strikes.


      <b>Works with.</b> Raised Stone: Heavy Hand, The Slow Hand. Dropped From the Apron: a pack in a corridor, Cairn on the lane it shook.


      <b>Not built yet.</b> Raised Stone''s pillar left standing beside the enemy, blocking and struck itself (for now the kit''s rocks stand behind it, and the heavy blow lands on the enemy). Dropped From the Apron''s boulder falling from above and lying as a thing to strike, breaking on a wall or a large enemy (for now stone rises under the nearest enemy, and the heavy blow on it sends the lane on).


      <b>Example.</b> Dropped From the Apron on the first of three soldiers in a corridor: one heavy blow on it crushes the two behind.'
  - Id: earth.base.master
    Title: 'Stone Rise: Mastered'
    Group: 
    Body: '<b>What it does.</b> Cast it while you stand your ground, Rooted or still for a second, and the stone rises under the enemy''s own feet and throws it three metres away from you, two deep in Tremor, before it stands.


      <b>When it happens.</b> For now, when you cast it while Rooted (no dodge begun for 3 seconds). Stone Rise must be in a slot.


      <b>The numbers.</b> 3 Shards. What it strikes is thrown 3 metres straight away from you and takes one more stack of Tremor (two with the stone''s own).


      <b>Works with.</b> Rooted, Immovable, Mountain Stance; Cairn on the two stacks it leaves.


      <b>Not built yet.</b> Still for a second as the moment (for now Rooted only), and the throw before the rocks stand.


      <b>Example.</b> Stand your ground and rise the stone under a brute that has come too close: it is thrown off you, two deep.'
  - Id: earth.lift
    Title: Left in Rubble
    Group: 
    Body: '<b>What it does.</b> Left in Rubble, Earth''s reaction lift. Every reaction with Tremor in it leaves a knee-high heap of rubble where it happened, a puff of ochre dust and broken stone, which shakes whatever stands in it.


      <b>When it happens.</b> Whenever a reaction with Tremor in it happens, on any enemy.


      <b>The numbers.</b> 3 Shards. A heap 1 metre round for 6 seconds, biting once a second for 3 damage, 8 stagger and one Tremor.


      <b>Works with.</b> Every pair with Tremor in it (The Ground Gives with Soaked, Chokedamp with Poison and the rest), Stone Remembers (it stands three times as long), Fissure and Stone Remembers, which grow from it.


      <b>Not built yet.</b> Every reaction with Tremor in it striking 20% harder; the rubble standing as one of your stones, that heavy blows drive enemies into and that The Circle Speaks casts from.


      <b>Example.</b> Soak and shake a soldier: the ground gives under it, and the rubble left keeps shaking the next one through.'
  - Id: earth.fissure
    Title: Fissure
    Group: 
    Body: '<b>What it does.</b> Fissure, a breaker. You drive your weapon into the ground. A crack runs ahead and breaks open in a row of spikes that strike and shake what they catch, and holds ordinary enemies where they stand.


      <b>When it happens.</b> From a spell slot: cast it with that slot''s button (hold L2 and a face button, or 1 to 4).


      <b>The numbers.</b> 4 Shards, no mana: it waits 10 seconds after a cast, less with weapon play (its Empower: 9, and 26 damage). The crack runs 8 metres at 20 metres a second, a spike every 1.5 metres from 1.3 metres out, each 1 metre in radius. Each enemy is struck once: 20 damage, 35 stagger and one Tremor, and held 1.2 seconds (a god or an elite 0.5).


      <b>Works with.</b> Left in Rubble, which it grows from, Standing Stones, Tremor and Cairn, your heavy blows on what it holds. Landing it charges the blade with Earth.


      <b>Not built yet.</b> The crack glowing for 0.9 seconds before it breaks open: for now it breaks open as it runs.


      <b>Example.</b> Three spearmen in a line down a stair: one crack catches all three and holds them for your blade.'
  - Id: earth.fissure.shape
    Title: 'Fissure: Basalt or Fault Line'
    Group: 
    Body: '<b>What it does.</b> Opens two shapes of Fissure, chosen at any rest fire. <b>Basalt</b>: the spikes come up as a row of six-sided columns, the slow-cooled stone of the causeway, that stand as a wall; a heavy blow on the row topples it away from you column after column, like dominoes. <b>Fault Line</b>: the crack does not break open by itself. It stays open, and a heavy blow you land beside it erupts the whole line. You lay the line, then fight beside it.


      <b>When it happens.</b> Whenever you cast Fissure, as the shape it wears. Before this is bought, the plain crack is cast.


      <b>The numbers.</b> 3 Shards. Basalt: for 4 seconds, a heavy blow on an enemy the spikes struck topples a lane 6 metres on from it, away from you, 20 damage and 30 stagger to each. Fault Line: the crack strikes for nothing; for 6 seconds a heavy blow on an enemy it crossed erupts 2 metres round that enemy, 24 damage, 40 stagger and two Tremor, at most twice a second.


      <b>Works with.</b> Heavy Hand and The Slow Hand, Tremor and Cairn on what the eruption shook.


      <b>Not built yet.</b> Basalt''s columns standing as a wall that blocks, and toppling one after another (for now the heavy blow on a struck enemy sends a lane on). Fault Line''s open crack shown on the ground, erupting along its whole length on a heavy blow within 2 metres of it, twice at most (for now a heavy blow on an enemy the crack crossed erupts under that enemy, as often as twice a second).


      <b>Example.</b> Fault Line under a pack, then fight among them: every heavy blow erupts under the one it lands on.'
  - Id: earth.fissure.master
    Title: 'Fissure: Mastered'
    Group: 
    Body: '<b>What it does.</b> Land a heavy blow on the crack''s line while it glows, and it erupts at once, half as hard again.


      <b>When it happens.</b> For now, a heavy blow on an enemy within 0.9 seconds of the spikes striking it. Fissure must be in a slot.


      <b>The numbers.</b> 3 Shards. A second eruption 1 metre round it, 10 damage, 18 stagger and one Tremor.


      <b>Works with.</b> Heavy Hand (the heavy blow cannot be stopped as it lands), The Slow Hand, Tremor.


      <b>Not built yet.</b> The crack''s glow before it breaks open, and the heavy blow landed on its line then: for now the window opens as the spikes strike, and it adds a second eruption on that enemy.


      <b>Example.</b> Cast the crack at a brute and step in with a heavy blow as it breaks: it erupts again under the brute.'
  - Id: earth.devotion
    Title: Stone Remembers
    Group: 
    Body: '<b>What it does.</b> Stone Remembers, Earth''s Devotion (the rule of the Celtic land, "stone remembers", given to you): all in on Earth only. Nothing you raise falls by itself: stones, boulders, columns and slabs stand until something breaks them. An enemy driven into one takes a heavy blow of stone, and the stone holds. The longer the fight, the more of the floor is yours.


      <b>When it happens.</b> Only while Earth is carried twice (all in). Always on then.


      <b>The numbers.</b> 6 Shards. As built: what you leave on the ground (a spell''s ground, a hazard from your marks, Left in Rubble''s heaps) stands three times as long, and a heavy blow that lands strikes its enemy as if driven into stone, 1 metre round it, 20 damage, 35 stagger and one Tremor, once in 3 seconds. All in, L2 with R2 is the deep strike, Mountain Cleaver.


      <b>Works with.</b> Left in Rubble, which it grows from, Fissure, Stone Rise, Standing Stones, Heavy Hand.


      <b>Not built yet.</b> Stones that never fall by themselves, eight at most with the oldest crumbling, and an enemy driven into one by a heavy blow, a finisher or a quake: nothing yet stands on the field to be driven into, so every heavy blow stands in, once in 3 seconds.


      <b>Example.</b> A long fight in a narrow hall: the rubble of every reaction stays, and every heavy blow lands as if into stone.'
  - Id: earth.hand
    Title: Hand of the Mountain
    Group: 
    Body: '<b>What it does.</b> While Bedrock burns, a hand of stone as tall as a tower hangs over your shoulder. Each heavy blow or finisher you land, it rises over that enemy and comes down on it a moment later, striking everything round it.


      <b>When it happens.</b> Light Bedrock with the surge button. The hand stays until Bedrock ends.


      <b>The numbers.</b> A god''s gift, never sold; in the playtest it can be bought. The hand falls 0.5 seconds after the blow, 3 metres in radius: 70% of the blow''s damage again, 40 stagger, a heavy blow, one stack of Tremor. It answers one blow at a time: a heavy blow landed while it is still falling is not answered.


      <b>Works with.</b> Bedrock, Heavy Hand, The Slow Hand, Tremor, finishers.


      <b>Example.</b> Light Bedrock and finish a staggered soldier: the hand comes down on the finisher''s spot and staggers the two behind it.'
  - Id: eclipse.twilight
    Title: Twilight
    Group: 
    Body: '<b>What it does.</b> The blow that ends a chain both Marks and Curses the enemy it lands on. Critical blows on an enemy that bears both heal you for a share of what they deal.


      <b>When it happens.</b> The last light blow of a chain, or the heavy blow that ends one, lays both. The healing comes with every critical blow on an enemy carrying Marked and Cursed together.


      <b>The numbers.</b> Mix, 3 Shards. One mark of each. Each critical blow on an enemy bearing both heals you 15% of its damage. A Marked enemy takes critical blows for three weapon blows; a Cursed one deals 15% less and heals you 6 when it dies.


      <b>Works with.</b> Light''s root (marks on perfect guards too), Dark''s root or Grasp (curses), Unblemished and Just Cut (more critical blows), The Dividing Line, Totality.


      <b>Example.</b> End a chain on a brute: the three blows after it are critical and each one gives back health, while the brute''s own blows land 15% lighter.'
  - Id: eclipse.daynight
    Title: Day and Night
    Group: 
    Body: '<b>What it does.</b> A perfect dodge heals you a little. For a while after a perfect dodge, a perfect guard gives double mana; for a while after a perfect guard, a perfect dodge gives double mana. Weaving the two pays twice.


      <b>When it happens.</b> Every perfect dodge heals. Each perfect dodge opens a time in which perfect guards pay double; each perfect guard opens a time in which perfect dodges pay double.


      <b>The numbers.</b> Mix, 4 Shards. 5 health for each perfect dodge. Each window lasts 6 seconds. A perfect guard gives 30 mana in it, where it gives 15; a perfect dodge 24, where it gives 12. As built the dodge heals always, not only after a guard.


      <b>Works with.</b> Clarity (perfect moments half again as long), Dazzle, Struck Flint and Bright Evasion (more mana from each), Low Sun, Daybreak and the deep strike to spend it.


      <b>Example.</b> Dodge a duellist''s lunge at the last moment, then perfect-guard its next cut: 5 health and 42 mana from two blows.'
  - Id: eclipse.duskdawn
    Title: Dusk and Dawn
    Group: 
    Body: '<b>What it does.</b> You step through the enemy you face and cut it in passing, coming out on its far side turned back toward it. If the cut lands, your next heavy blow in the moment after is critical. Nothing can strike you in the step; a wall, or something too big to shove, stops you short.


      <b>When it happens.</b> From a spell slot: cast it with that slot''s button (hold L2 and a face button, or 1 to 4). As built it is the step and its critical heavy blow; the stored cut of light that should land with that heavy blow is still to come.


      <b>The numbers.</b> Mix, 4 Shards, 45 mana. Up to 5 metres: to 1.8 metres past the enemy faced, or about 4 metres ahead with none. The cut is 10 damage, 10 stagger and Marked on all on the line. The heavy blow after it is critical if it lands within 3 seconds.


      <b>Works with.</b> Twilight (a critical heavy blow on a Marked and Cursed enemy heals you), Light''s root, Sentence, Hard Light, and the charged blade, which it charges with Light.


      <b>Example.</b> Step through a captain''s guard, turn, and land a critical heavy blow in its back.'
  - Id: eclipse.lowsun
    Title: Low Sun
    Group: 
    Body: '<b>What it does.</b> Your weapon blows give more mana. Each time your health falls below a third, they give far more for a while.


      <b>When it happens.</b> Always on once learned; the greater share comes each time your health drops below a third.


      <b>The numbers.</b> Mix, 3 Shards. Weapon blows give 20% more mana. Falling below a third adds 60% more for 12 seconds, 80% in all. As built it does not yet rise steadily as your health falls.


      <b>Works with.</b> The Dividing Line, Day and Night, Dark''s marks that are paid in health, Rich Mark and Gleaning, and the mana spells it pays for: Dusk and Dawn, Daybreak.


      <b>Example.</b> A brute''s blow leaves you at a quarter of your health: for twelve seconds every cut fills your mana nearly twice as fast, enough for Dusk and Dawn and a way out.'
  - Id: eclipse.blacksun
    Title: Black Sun
    Group: 
    Body: '<b>What it does.</b> You hang a black sun before you. For three seconds it drags everything near it inward, and then it bursts, striking and Marking all it drew in.


      <b>When it happens.</b> From a spell slot: cast it with that slot''s button (hold L2 and a face button, or 1 to 4). It hangs over the enemy you face, or a little ahead of you with none.


      <b>The numbers.</b> Mix, 4 Shards, no mana: it waits 12 seconds after a cast, less with weapon play. It hangs on an enemy within 5 metres, or 5 metres ahead. For 3 seconds it pulls everything within 5 metres most of the way to its middle. Then it bursts, 5 metres in radius: 40 damage and 40 stagger, a heavy blow, and Marked. As built it bursts at one strength; growing with the blows you land under it is still to come.


      <b>Works with.</b> Light''s root and Sentence (all of them Marked at once), Twilight, Two Suns and Returning Light (a spell hit on each), Hard Light, and the charged blade, which it charges with Light.


      <b>Example.</b> Hang it in the middle of a pack, guard on its edge while they are dragged together, then cut into the knot as it bursts.'
  - Id: eclipse.dividingline
    Title: The Dividing Line
    Group: 
    Body: '<b>What it does.</b> Your health sets how you fight. At half your health or more, your critical blows strike harder and your blows give more mana. Below half, every blow Curses and feeds you. Each time your health falls below a third, a burst round you Curses everything near.


      <b>When it happens.</b> Always on once learned. The day half holds at half health or more; the night half below half; the burst each time your health drops below a third.


      <b>The numbers.</b> Mix, 5 Shards. At half or more: critical blows deal 1.7 times their damage, where they deal 1.5, and blows give 20% more mana. Below half: each weapon blow Curses and heals you 8% of its damage. Below a third: a burst 3.5 metres round you, 16 damage, 25 stagger and Cursed, at most once every 4 seconds. As built the burst does not come when you cross half the other way.


      <b>Works with.</b> Twilight, Low Sun, Light''s root and Unblemished on the day side, Dark''s Cursed kills on the night side, Totality.


      <b>Example.</b> A brute drives you under half: each cut now curses and heals you, and when the next blow drops you below a third the burst curses the pack round you.'
  - Id: eclipse.totality
    Title: Totality
    Group: 
    Body: '<b>What it does.</b> When your surge begins, the sun is covered. While the dark lasts every enemy near you is kept Marked and Cursed, and every weapon blow you land is critical and heals you. What each enemy loses to your weapon in the dark is remembered. When the surge ends the light returns, and a column of it strikes every enemy you wounded for a share of what it lost.


      <b>When it happens.</b> Light your surge with the surge button (either element''s surge you wear); the light returns when it ends.


      <b>The numbers.</b> A god''s gift, never sold; in the playtest it can be bought. Each second, Marked and Cursed on every enemy within 14 metres. Every weapon blow critical; each heals 1, at most five times a second. The returning column deals half of what that enemy lost to your weapon, 80 at most, with 30 stagger.


      <b>Works with.</b> Clarity (eight seconds of dark that also marks with every blow) or Hunger (feeding you while it drains), Twilight (critical blows on the Marked and Cursed heal you more), Weighed, Sentence, The Dividing Line.


      <b>Example.</b> Light the surge among four soldiers, cut each of them hard while the dark lasts, and watch the light come back down on all four as it ends.'
  - Id: fire.cinder
    Title: Cinder
    Group: 
    Body: '<b>What it does.</b> Every blow of your weapon that lands sets the enemy burning and lays one stack of Burn. Each further blow adds another stack, up to five. A burning enemy takes damage every second, more for each stack.


      <b>When it happens.</b> Always on once learned, while Fire is your first element: every weapon blow that lands, light or heavy. Carried as the second element, it lays nothing with the weapon; Burn then comes from your Fire spells, the charged blade and the R2 strike.


      <b>The numbers.</b> 2 Shards. One stack a blow, five at most. A burn deals 5 damage a second and each stack adds 30%, so 12.5 a second at five. Each blow sets its clock back to 4 seconds; when it runs out the stacks go with it. A burn set off by another mark deals 10 damage and 10 more for each stack: 60 at five.


      <b>Works with.</b> Heat, Breath of the Lioness (its cone sets a burn off), Catching Fire, Meteor Leap''s Master, and Kindle.


      <b>Example.</b> Five quick light blows on a soldier leave it five deep, burning for 12.5 a second while you step back and raise your guard.'
  - Id: fire.heat
    Title: Heat
    Group: 
    Body: '<b>What it does.</b> Landing blows without being struck builds Heat, a level at a time, up to five. Each level makes your weapon hit harder. A blow that lands on you puts it out, and standing off too long cools it a level at a time.


      <b>When it happens.</b> Always on once learned. Every weapon blow that lands counts; lighting Kindle with the surge button fills it at once.


      <b>The numbers.</b> 3 Shards. Three blows a level, five levels. Each level adds 6% weapon damage, 30% at five. Six seconds without landing a blow loses a level. A blow that lands on you drops it to nothing.


      <b>Works with.</b> White Heat, Wildfire Rush (a level for each enemy passed), Kindle, and the two spells that grow from it, Uraeus and Meteor Leap.


      <b>Example.</b> Fifteen blows in, every cut is 30% heavier. One careless swing from a brute and you are back to nothing.'
  - Id: fire.base
    Title: Flame Wave
    Group: 
    Body: '<b>What it does.</b> Flame Wave, Fire''s own spell, comes with the element and is never bought. Fire runs out along the ground in a cone ahead of you, striking everything in it and setting it burning, and three patches of fire burn on where it ran.


      <b>When it happens.</b> From a spell slot: cast it with that slot''s button (hold L2 and a face button, or 1 to 4). Carrying Fire, it is always yours to put in a slot.


      <b>The numbers.</b> Given with Fire. No mana: it waits 7 seconds after a cast, less with weapon play; its Empower makes that 5.5. The cone is 5.5 metres long and 70 degrees wide: 20 damage, 24 stagger and a stack of Burn. Three patches burn on for 3 seconds.


      <b>Works with.</b> Its Empower, its two shapes and its Master; Cinder to deepen what it lit; the charged blade, which its landing charges with Fire.


      <b>Not built yet.</b> The Empower''s longer patches (5 seconds): the base spell is cast by Fire''s kit, which takes only the Empower''s shorter wait.


      <b>Example.</b> Open a fight with it across a line of soldiers: every one of them burning before your first blow.'
  - Id: fire.base.shape
    Title: 'Flame Wave: Cinder Fan or Running Fire'
    Group: 
    Body: '<b>What it does.</b> Opens two shapes of Flame Wave. Choose which it wears at any rest fire, in the Hand. <b>Cinder Fan</b>: close and wide, the shape for being surrounded; what it touches burns two deep and is thrown back. <b>Running Fire</b>: one narrow tongue of flame runs far along the ground, and a low burning line stays behind it; whatever crosses it takes two Burn.


      <b>When it happens.</b> Whenever you cast Flame Wave, as the shape it wears. Before this is bought, the plain wave is cast.


      <b>The numbers.</b> 3 Shards. Cinder Fan: 3 metres and 150 degrees, 22 damage, 20 stagger, two Burn, and a throw of 1.5 metres. Running Fire: 12 metres in under a second, 12 damage and 10 stagger with two Burn on what the tongue touches, and the line burns 4 seconds, biting 3 every half second with two Burn.


      <b>Works with.</b> Catching Fire and Black Pitch in a crowd (Cinder Fan); Breath of the Lioness and Kiln Stance against a pack that closes in; Fuel to It on wet ground (Running Fire across a river makes steam).


      <b>Example.</b> Surrounded by four soldiers, Cinder Fan throws them all back burning two deep. Facing an archer behind a wall of shields, Running Fire reaches it.'
  - Id: fire.base.master
    Title: 'Flame Wave: Mastered'
    Group: 
    Body: '<b>What it does.</b> Cast Flame Wave in the same instant as the charged blade''s third blow lands, and its cooldown does not start.


      <b>When it happens.</b> The third blow of a charged blade lands: for half a second after it, your next Flame Wave starts no wait. Flame Wave must be in a slot.


      <b>The numbers.</b> 3 Shards. A window of 0.5 seconds after the third charged blow. Then the wave lands, charges the blade again, and the dance goes on.


      <b>Works with.</b> The charged blade above all; Cinder and Heat, which pay for staying in.


      <b>Not built yet.</b> The wave leaving from the blade along the swing; for now it leaves from you as always.


      <b>Example.</b> Wave, three blows, wave again at once: a burning crowd that never gets its feet.'
  - Id: fire.uraeus
    Title: Uraeus
    Group: 
    Body: '<b>What it does.</b> A cobra of flame rises from your shoulder and stands for a while, spitting burning venom at enemies near you.


      <b>When it happens.</b> From a spell slot: cast it with that slot''s button. It spits by itself while it stands.


      <b>The numbers.</b> 4 Shards, no mana: it waits 10 seconds (its Empower: 8). It stands 8 seconds and spits at enemies within 8 metres, six spits at most (its Empower: eight), each 8 damage, 6 stagger and two Burn.


      <b>Works with.</b> Heat, which it grows from; Cinder; its Master on what already burns.


      <b>Not built yet.</b> The spit answering an enemy that begins an attack (it needs a trigger on an enemy''s wind-up), and the venom burning at the target''s feet. For now the cobra spits on its own, like a phalanx of fire.


      <b>Example.</b> Cast it before a pack closes in, and every one that comes near takes venom while you fight the first.'
  - Id: fire.uraeus.shape
    Title: 'Uraeus: Coiled or Set Down'
    Group: 
    Body: '<b>What it does.</b> Opens two shapes of Uraeus, chosen at any rest fire. <b>Coiled</b>: it stays close and spits only at what is within 3 metres, each spit laying three Burn. <b>Set Down</b>: it is planted where you cast it and guards a circle of 9 metres round itself whether you stay or not: leave it on a door.


      <b>When it happens.</b> Whenever you cast Uraeus, as the shape it wears.


      <b>The numbers.</b> 3 Shards. Coiled: reach 3 metres, three Burn a spit. Set Down: a spit every 1.2 seconds at an enemy within 9 metres of the cobra, 8 damage and two Burn, for 8 seconds.


      <b>Works with.</b> Kiln Stance and Breath of the Lioness (Coiled, for fighting close); Black Pitch and Catching Fire (Set Down by a crowd).


      <b>Not built yet.</b> Coiled''s spit holding the enemy''s wind-up for a moment.


      <b>Example.</b> Set it down at a gate and fight the brute on the far side of the yard while the cobra keeps the soldiers burning.'
  - Id: fire.uraeus.master
    Title: 'Uraeus: Mastered'
    Group: 
    Body: '<b>What it does.</b> Each spit that lands on an enemy already burning lays twice the Burn: the fire is fed.


      <b>When it happens.</b> A spit of your Uraeus strikes an enemy that is already burning. Uraeus must be in a slot.


      <b>The numbers.</b> 3 Shards. Two more stacks of Burn on top of the spit''s own.


      <b>Works with.</b> Cinder and Flame Wave, which light them first.


      <b>Not built yet.</b> The cobra standing a second longer for each spit fed.


      <b>Example.</b> Light a pack with Flame Wave, then cast Uraeus: every spit takes them a step nearer to five.'
  - Id: fire.meteor
    Title: Meteor Leap
    Group: 
    Body: '<b>What it does.</b> You leap out of the fight and come down beside the enemy you face as a falling stone, a heavy blow that leaves a burning crater. Nothing can strike you in the air.


      <b>When it happens.</b> From a spell slot: cast it with that slot''s button (hold L2 and a face button, or 1 to 4).


      <b>The numbers.</b> 4 Shards, 45 mana (its Empower: 35). It finds an enemy faced within 9 metres and lands you 1 metre short of it; with none, 5 metres ahead. The leap takes 0.62 seconds. The landing strikes everything within 3.2 metres for 46 damage and 55 stagger. The crater burns for 4 seconds and bites for 5 every half second.


      <b>Works with.</b> Heat, which it grows from; Catching Fire; its Master on an enemy at five Burn.


      <b>Not built yet.</b> The Empower''s longer crater (6 seconds).


      <b>Example.</b> An archer stands behind two shield-bearers: leap over them and land on it.'
  - Id: fire.meteor.shape
    Title: 'Meteor Leap: Falling Star or Ash Fall'
    Group: 
    Body: '<b>What it does.</b> Opens two shapes of Meteor Leap, chosen at any rest fire. <b>Falling Star</b>: you do not leap; a burning stone falls on the aim point after a breath and you go on fighting. <b>Ash Fall</b>: the landing throws hot ash round you, and enemies in it keep catching fire.


      <b>When it happens.</b> Whenever you cast Meteor Leap, as the shape it wears.


      <b>The numbers.</b> 3 Shards. Falling Star: it falls 0.8 seconds after the cast, within 9 metres, 46 damage and 60 stagger in 3.2 metres, a stack of Burn, and a burning patch for 4 seconds. Ash Fall: ash 3 metres round where you land for 5 seconds, a Burn and 2 damage a second to all in it.


      <b>Works with.</b> Cinder and Catching Fire (Ash Fall in a crowd); Kiln Stance and Breath of the Lioness (Falling Star while you hold your ground).


      <b>Not built yet.</b> Falling Star''s own stone and growing shadow (it uses the thrown sphere for now), and balance not recovering in Ash Fall.


      <b>Example.</b> Hold the line with your guard and call the stone down on the brute behind it.'
  - Id: fire.meteor.master
    Title: 'Meteor Leap: Mastered'
    Group: 
    Body: '<b>What it does.</b> Land Meteor Leap on an enemy at five Burn and its burn goes off with the blow, and half the mana comes back.


      <b>When it happens.</b> The leap''s landing strikes an enemy at full Burn. Meteor Leap must be in a slot.


      <b>The numbers.</b> 3 Shards. The burn is set off for 10 damage a stack (50 at five). 22 mana comes back, once a landing.


      <b>Works with.</b> Cinder and Uraeus, to bring an enemy to five; Heat for the weight behind it.


      <b>Example.</b> Five quick blows on the brute, step back, leap: its burn goes off under the stone and your mana is half full again.'
  - Id: fire.lift
    Title: Fuel to It
    Group: 
    Body: '<b>What it does.</b> Fuel to It: every reaction with Burn in it leaves the ground where it happened burning.


      <b>When it happens.</b> Whenever Burn reacts on an enemy with the other affliction it carries (Steam with Soaked, Flashover with Static and the rest).


      <b>The numbers.</b> 3 Shards. A burning patch 1.5 metres in radius for 3 seconds, biting 3 every half second with a stack of Burn.


      <b>Works with.</b> Carrying a second element: every reaction of Fire''s ten.


      <b>Not built yet.</b> The reactions themselves striking 25% harder (it needs a stat for reaction damage).


      <b>Example.</b> Fire and Water on one enemy: Steam bursts, and the ground under it keeps burning.'
  - Id: fire.whiteheat
    Title: White Heat
    Group: 
    Body: '<b>What it does.</b> Heat can rise to eight. Every level above five also quickens your swing. But struck while above five, you catch fire yourself for a while.


      <b>When it happens.</b> Always on once learned. The speed comes with each level above five; the burn comes when a blow lands on you up there.


      <b>The numbers.</b> 6 Shards. Heat to eight, 48% weapon damage at the top. Each level above five adds 5% swing speed, 15% at eight. Struck above five, you burn for 4 seconds at 4 damage a second; it never takes your last point. The blow still puts your Heat out, as always.


      <b>Works with.</b> Heat, Wildfire Rush, and Kindle, which now fills Heat to eight at once.


      <b>Example.</b> Light Kindle at the start of a fight: you are at eight Heat straight away, swinging 15% faster for 48% more, as long as nothing touches you.'
  - Id: fire.devotion
    Title: Fire Without End
    Group: 
    Body: '<b>What it does.</b> Fire Without End, Fire''s Devotion: all in on Fire only. Burns last far longer, and a burn left alone deepens by itself. Light everything once, then fight the one in front of you while the rest of the room cooks.


      <b>When it happens.</b> Only while Fire is carried twice (all in). Then always.


      <b>The numbers.</b> 6 Shards. Burns last twice as long. Every 4 seconds, the burning enemy you face gains a stack of Burn, up to five. All in, L2 with R2 is the deep strike, Burnt Offering.


      <b>Works with.</b> Cinder, Flame Wave, Catching Fire, and the deep strike.


      <b>Not built yet.</b> Burns that never go out by themselves, and every burn near you deepening, not only the one faced.


      <b>Example.</b> Flame Wave across a room, then a duel with one soldier: the rest are at five when you turn round.'
  - Id: fire.backdraft
    Title: Breath of the Lioness
    Group: 
    Body: '<b>What it does.</b> Breath of the Lioness (once Backdraft): a perfect guard throws a cone of fire back at the one who struck, as Sekhmet''s breath was the desert wind. Against a burning enemy, its burn goes off too.


      <b>When it happens.</b> A perfect guard: press the guard button just before a blow lands.


      <b>The numbers.</b> 3 Shards. A cone 4.5 metres long and 100 degrees wide. 16 damage and 18 stagger to all in it, and each burns for 3 seconds. Two stacks of Burn on the attacker. A burning attacker''s burn goes off for 10 damage and 10 more for each stack.


      <b>Works with.</b> Cinder to build the burn it sets off, Kiln Stance (whose turned blows count as perfect guards), Flame Trail.


      <b>Example.</b> Against a soldier''s thrust, guard just before it lands: the fire throws it off balance; at five Burn, its burn goes off in the same breath.'
  - Id: fire.kiln
    Title: Kiln Stance
    Group: 
    Body: '<b>What it does.</b> You stand ready in flame. The first blow that reaches you, from any side, red attack or not, is turned for nothing and answered with fire. The caught blow counts as a perfect guard, so it gives that mana and sets off every mark that waits on one. If nothing comes, the stance goes out and the cast is spent.


      <b>When it happens.</b> From a spell slot: cast it with that slot''s button, then any blow in the next 1.2 seconds.


      <b>The numbers.</b> 4 Shards, no mana: it waits 9 seconds (its Empower: 7, and four Burn). Ready for 1.2 seconds. The answer is a pillar of fire 1.7 metres in radius under the attacker: 30 damage, 50 stagger, a heavy blow, three stacks of Burn.


      <b>Works with.</b> Breath of the Lioness, which it grows from; its Master on a burning attacker.


      <b>Not built yet.</b> Shut Door as designed: held up to 3 seconds, every blow turned banked as smoke under a hood (three at most), and the door opened in a cone of flame when you let go, 20 damage and 15 more for each blow banked. It needs a spell held on its button. For now the Learn is the stance as it was built, The Kiln.


      <b>Example.</b> A brute winds up a red overhead you cannot guard: cast just before it falls, and the pillar answers it.'
  - Id: fire.kiln.shape
    Title: 'Kiln Stance: The Kiln or Firewalker'
    Group: 
    Body: '<b>What it does.</b> Opens two shapes of Kiln Stance, chosen at any rest fire. <b>The Kiln</b>: the stance as it was, the first blow answered at once by a pillar of fire, for single blows. <b>Firewalker</b>: a stance you walk in, for a shorter time: walk into the swing.


      <b>When it happens.</b> Whenever you cast Kiln Stance, as the shape it wears.


      <b>The numbers.</b> 3 Shards. The Kiln: ready 1.2 seconds, the pillar 30 damage, 50 stagger, three Burn. Firewalker: ready 0.6 seconds.


      <b>Works with.</b> Breath of the Lioness; Uraeus Coiled.


      <b>Not built yet.</b> Walking at half speed in Firewalker (for now it is the stance held a shorter time).


      <b>Example.</b> Against a quick double cut, The Kiln answers the first; against a slow brute, Firewalker meets the swing.'
  - Id: fire.kiln.master
    Title: 'Kiln Stance: Mastered'
    Group: 
    Body: '<b>What it does.</b> Turn a blow from an attacker already burning, and a pillar of fire rises under it with the answer: its burn goes off and it is thrown down.


      <b>When it happens.</b> Kiln Stance''s answer strikes a burning enemy. Kiln Stance must be in a slot.


      <b>The numbers.</b> 3 Shards. Its burn goes off for 10 damage a stack, and it lies knocked down for 1.2 seconds (elites and gods less).


      <b>Works with.</b> Cinder and Flame Wave to light the attacker first.


      <b>Example.</b> Light the brute, wait for its overhead, answer it: it goes up and down at once.'
  - Id: fire.trail
    Title: Flame Trail
    Group: 
    Body: '<b>What it does.</b> Your dodge leaves a line of fire on the ground behind it that burns whatever walks through.


      <b>When it happens.</b> Every dodge.


      <b>The numbers.</b> 3 Shards. Four patches along the dodge''s path, each 0.95 metres in radius, laid as you roll. Each burns for 2.6 seconds and bites for 4 damage every half second, setting what it touches burning for 2 seconds.


      <b>Works with.</b> Wildfire Rush, which grows from it, for a second line; Breath of the Lioness.


      <b>Example.</b> Roll back from a charging brute: it runs through all four patches to reach you and arrives burning.'
  - Id: fire.rush
    Title: Wildfire Rush
    Group: 
    Body: '<b>What it does.</b> You become a point of fire and drive straight through every enemy in your path, coming out the far side facing back. Each enemy passed is struck, set burning and raises your Heat a level. Then a second cut lands on everyone on the line, and the line burns. Nothing can strike you while you drive; a wall, or something too big to shove, stops you.


      <b>When it happens.</b> From a spell slot: cast it with that slot''s button (hold L2 and a face button, or 1 to 4).


      <b>The numbers.</b> 4 Shards, no mana: it waits 8 seconds after a cast (its Empower: 6, and the line burns 4 seconds). Up to 7 metres, along a lane 2 metres wide. Passing: 14 damage, 20 stagger and two stacks of Burn. The cut after: 14 damage, 20 stagger and two stacks more. The line burns 2.6 seconds, biting for 4 every half second. One Heat level for each enemy passed.


      <b>Works with.</b> Flame Trail, which it grows from; Heat and White Heat; Cinder; Catching Fire.


      <b>Example.</b> Drive through three soldiers in a row: Heat goes from none to three, and each is four deep in Burn.'
  - Id: fire.rush.shape
    Title: 'Wildfire Rush: Fire Front or Smoke Road'
    Group: 
    Body: '<b>What it does.</b> Opens two shapes of Wildfire Rush, chosen at any rest fire. <b>Fire Front</b>: you go as the front of a grass fire, a wall of flame, slower, and what it meets is thrown down at the end; the drive that pushes a crowd instead of passing through it. <b>Smoke Road</b>: the escape, the line of fire left between you and them.


      <b>When it happens.</b> Whenever you cast Wildfire Rush, as the shape it wears.


      <b>The numbers.</b> 3 Shards. Fire Front: 5 metres, 4 metres wide, a third of the speed; each enemy struck is knocked down for 0.6 seconds. Smoke Road: 6 metres, the passing cut lighter (4 damage).


      <b>Works with.</b> Catching Fire and Black Pitch (Fire Front into a crowd); Flame Trail (Smoke Road out of one).


      <b>Not built yet.</b> Fire Front carrying the enemies before you, and Smoke Road going back out of the fight: for now both drive forward.


      <b>Example.</b> Fire Front through a doorway packed with soldiers: they go down burning in a heap on the far side.'
  - Id: fire.rush.master
    Title: 'Wildfire Rush: Mastered'
    Group: 
    Body: '<b>What it does.</b> Started in the instant a blow would land on you, Wildfire Rush counts as a perfect dodge, and your Heat goes to five.


      <b>When it happens.</b> You cast Wildfire Rush. Wildfire Rush must be in a slot.


      <b>The numbers.</b> 3 Shards. For now every cast gives what a perfect dodge gives: 12 mana and 1.5 seconds off every running cooldown.


      <b>Works with.</b> Heat and White Heat.


      <b>Not built yet.</b> The timing (started as a blow would land) and Heat going to five: both need the enemy''s blow as a moment.


      <b>Example.</b> Drive out of a brute''s swing and through its friends, and every other spell is that much nearer.'
  - Id: fire.firebomb
    Title: Firebomb Flask
    Group: 
    Body: '<b>What it does.</b> Holding the flask button throws the flask instead of drinking it. It heals nothing: it bursts in fire where it lands, leaves flames on the ground there, and lays three stacks of Burn on everything near. A short press still drinks.


      <b>When it happens.</b> Hold the flask button. Each throw uses a flask.


      <b>The numbers.</b> 3 Shards. Hold 0.3 seconds to throw. It flies at the enemy ahead within 9 metres, or 5 metres ahead, and lands 0.4 seconds later. The burst is 2.6 metres in radius: 36 damage, 30 stagger, three stacks of Burn and 4 seconds of burning. The flames left are 2.2 metres in radius and bite for 5 every half second for 3.5 seconds.


      <b>Works with.</b> Catching Fire, Black Pitch, Flame Wave (all on the Ruin bough).


      <b>Example.</b> Three soldiers bunch at a gate: one flask leaves all three three deep and standing in fire.'
  - Id: fire.catch
    Title: Catching Fire
    Group: 
    Body: '<b>What it does.</b> When a burning enemy dies, its burn is thrown onto everyone standing near it, as deep as it was.


      <b>When it happens.</b> The moment a burning enemy dies, whatever killed it.


      <b>The numbers.</b> 3 Shards. Every enemy within 4 metres of the one that died takes as many stacks of Burn as it carried, up to five. It can happen at most five times a second.


      <b>Works with.</b> Cinder to build the depth first, Black Pitch (which grows from it), Firebomb Flask, and Breath of the Lioness to set the new burns off.


      <b>Example.</b> Kill a soldier at five Burn in the middle of a pack, and the two beside it are five deep at once without a blow from you.'
  - Id: fire.pitch
    Title: Black Pitch
    Group: 
    Body: '<b>What it does.</b> You throw a jar of embalmer''s pitch at the enemy faced. Your next blows on it splash fire over everyone near it.


      <b>When it happens.</b> From a spell slot: cast it with that slot''s button. Then the next three blows of your weapon on the coated enemy, within 8 seconds.


      <b>The numbers.</b> 4 Shards, no mana: it waits 11 seconds (its Empower: 9, and the coat lasts 10 seconds). Thrown up to 7 metres. Each of three blows on it sets off a burst 2 metres round it: 16 damage, 35 stagger and three Burn.


      <b>Works with.</b> Catching Fire, which it grows from; Cinder; Firebomb Flask.


      <b>Not built yet.</b> The pitch as designed: blows spread a coat from enemy to enemy without fire, and the first fire that touches any coated enemy (a Burn laid, a burning patch, a reaction) takes all of them at once, 16 damage and 8 more for each blow that spread it, up to 70, and the floor under each burns. For now the coat is a brand that the next blows set off round the one coated.


      <b>Example.</b> Coat the soldier in the middle of a pack and cut it three times: the pack burns three deep.'
  - Id: fire.pitch.shape
    Title: 'Black Pitch: Pitch Pool or The Torch'
    Group: 
    Body: '<b>What it does.</b> Opens two shapes of Black Pitch, chosen at any rest fire. <b>Pitch Pool</b>: thrown on the floor, a pool of burning pitch. <b>The Torch</b>: one enemy coated deep, and nothing splashes; it burns and sets alight everyone near it each second as it walks.


      <b>When it happens.</b> Whenever you cast Black Pitch, as the shape it wears.


      <b>The numbers.</b> 3 Shards. Pitch Pool: 3 metres across, 8 seconds, biting 3 every half second with a stack of Burn. The Torch: for 8 seconds, every second, a stack of Burn on everyone within 2 metres of the torch; its blows set off a burst of 0.8 metres.


      <b>Works with.</b> Catching Fire (The Torch into a crowd); Flame Wave''s Running Fire across the pool.


      <b>Not built yet.</b> The pool coating whoever walks through it, and The Torch lit only when fire touches it (for now it is lit at once).


      <b>Example.</b> Make the brute The Torch and let it walk into its friends.'
  - Id: fire.pitch.master
    Title: 'Black Pitch: Mastered'
    Group: 
    Body: '<b>What it does.</b> Light it with a finisher, and every other burning enemy near goes up with the coated, at half.


      <b>When it happens.</b> A finisher lands on a burning enemy. Black Pitch must be in a slot.


      <b>The numbers.</b> 3 Shards. The finished enemy''s burn is set off for 5 damage a stack in 4 metres.


      <b>Works with.</b> Cinder, Catching Fire.


      <b>Not built yet.</b> Every other burning enemy within 10 metres going up at half, and only when the finisher lights the coat.


      <b>Example.</b> End a coated soldier''s chain with a finisher, and the fire runs on to the next.'
  - Id: fire.sun
    Title: Falling Sun
    Group: 
    Body: '<b>What it does.</b> Lighting Kindle starts the sun on its road. At dawn it is rolled to the enemy you face, and the ground it crosses burns. At noon it hangs over that enemy, and burns near you deepen by themselves. At dusk it sets on the enemy below, heavier for every burn it finds. A blow on you sends it under, to rise again.


      <b>When it happens.</b> Light Kindle with the surge button. It sets when Kindle ends, or when you press the surge button again.


      <b>The numbers.</b> A god''s gift, never sold; in the playtest it can be bought. Dawn: up to 9 metres; the first enemy met takes 14 damage, 20 stagger, two Burn. Noon: each second, a stack of Burn on all within 6 metres of you. Dusk: 60 damage, 80 stagger in 4 metres, 8% more a Burn stack found, up to double; half if called while rolling. Sent under, it rises in 1.5 seconds if Kindle has 3 left.


      <b>Works with.</b> Cinder, Heat.


      <b>Example.</b> Press again over a crowd at five Burn.'
  - Id: forge.hammeranvil
    Title: Hammer and Anvil
    Group: 
    Body: '<b>What it does.</b> A heavy blow on a shaken enemy strikes twice: once from your weapon, and once more a moment later as the stone answers. Heavy blows also lay Tremor and Sundered together, whichever of the two you carry first. As built, the second strike asks for Tremor on the enemy, not stone at its back, and it bursts round you rather than behind the enemy.


      <b>When it happens.</b> Every heavy blow that lands. The second strike needs the enemy to carry Tremor already.


      <b>The numbers.</b> Mix, 3 Shards. The second strike lands 0.15 seconds later, 2.3 metres round you: 60% of the heavy blow''s damage and 20 stagger, at most twice a second. Each heavy blow also adds a stack of Tremor and a notch of Sundered; your first element''s own is not laid twice when its root already lays it with heavy blows.


      <b>Works with.</b> Tremor, Heavy Hand, Buckled, Mountain Stance and Quake Step (Tremor to start it), Metal''s root.


      <b>Example.</b> Shake a brute with Quake Step, then land two heavy blows: each one lands again for 60% as the stone answers.'
  - Id: forge.struckore
    Title: Struck Ore
    Group: 
    Body: '<b>What it does.</b> A perfect guard strikes a spike of ore up from the ground under the one who struck and shakes it, and three blades fly from you toward it, notching what they pass.


      <b>When it happens.</b> A perfect guard: press the guard button just before a blow lands.


      <b>The numbers.</b> Mix, 3 Shards. The spike falls 0.2 seconds later, 1.2 metres in radius: 10 damage, 20 stagger and one stack of Tremor. The three blades fly in a narrow fan at 10 metres a second for 1.2 seconds; each strikes the first enemy it meets for 9 damage, 4 stagger and one notch of Sundered. As built the spike strikes and is gone; a pillar that stands to be broken is to come.


      <b>Works with.</b> Buckled (both afflictions from one guard), Toppling and Stone Skin on the Earth tree, Immovable, Hammer and Anvil.


      <b>Example.</b> Perfect-guard a soldier''s swing: it is shaken and notched at once, and the soldier behind it takes a blade too.'
  - Id: forge.buckled
    Title: Buckled
    Group: 
    Body: '<b>What it does.</b> An enemy that is both shaken and notched loses its balance far sooner, from everything that strikes it.


      <b>When it happens.</b> Always on once learned, on any enemy carrying Tremor and Sundered together.


      <b>The numbers.</b> Mix, 3 Shards. 40% more stagger from every source while it carries both. Tremor also stops its balance draining, so what you put in stays.


      <b>Works with.</b> Hammer and Anvil, Struck Ore, World Anvil (lays both), Mountain Stance, Quake Step, Earth''s and Metal''s roots, the charged blade of whichever element you carry second.


      <b>Example.</b> Notch a brute with Metal blows, shake it with Quake Step, and its balance bar fills almost half again as fast.'
  - Id: forge.triphammer
    Title: Trip Hammer
    Group: 
    Body: '<b>What it does.</b> A great hammer forms over the enemy you face, follows it for a moment, then falls on it as a heavy blow and leaves a crack in the ground that bites for a second. As built it is a hammer that falls; landing a heavy blow of your own at the same instant does not yet double it.


      <b>When it happens.</b> From a spell slot: cast it with that slot''s button (hold L2 and a face button, or 1 to 4). With no enemy faced it falls 10 metres ahead, and the slot still waits.


      <b>The numbers.</b> Mix, 4 Shards, no mana: it waits 12 seconds after a cast, less with weapon play. An enemy within 10 metres. It falls 1 second after the cast, 2.5 metres in radius: 30 damage, 50 stagger, a heavy blow, one stack of Tremor. The crack is about 1.9 metres in radius for 1 second, biting for 2 every half second with a stack of Tremor.


      <b>Works with.</b> Buckled, Hammer and Anvil (the Tremor it lays opens the second strike), Standing Stones. Landing it charges the blade with Earth.


      <b>Example.</b> Cast it on a brute, then close in: by the time you reach it the hammer has fallen and it is shaken for your heavy blow.'
  - Id: forge.drawnfromstone
    Title: Drawn From Stone
    Group: 
    Body: '<b>What it does.</b> You draw a sword of stone and iron from the ground and give one great swing through a half circle before you. As built it is that one swing; holding the great sword for three swings is to come.


      <b>When it happens.</b> From a spell slot: cast it with that slot''s button (hold L2 and a face button, or 1 to 4).


      <b>The numbers.</b> Mix, 5 Shards, 50 mana. A half circle 4 metres deep: 40 damage, 60 stagger and one stack of Tremor to everything in it.


      <b>Works with.</b> Buckled, Hammer and Anvil, Standing Stones, Hard Stone. Landing it charges the blade with Earth.


      <b>Example.</b> Ringed by soldiers in front of you: one swing shakes them all and leaves each well on its way to staggered.'
  - Id: forge.foldedsteel
    Title: Folded Steel
    Group: 
    Body: '<b>What it does.</b> Every finisher you land folds your blade once more. Each fold makes every blow of the weapon a little harder, and a little heavier to swing. The count shows on the screen as Folds, and it is kept for the run.


      <b>When it happens.</b> Each finisher that lands (a heavy blow on a staggered enemy) adds a fold.


      <b>The numbers.</b> Mix, 5 Shards. Ten folds at most. Each fold: 3% more weapon damage and 1% more stamina for each blow. At ten: 30% more damage, 10% more stamina.


      <b>Works with.</b> Buckled and Tremor (more staggers, more finishers), World Anvil, Hammer and Anvil.


      <b>Example.</b> Ten finishers into a land, every cut you make is 30% heavier than when you began.'
  - Id: forge.worldanvil
    Title: World Anvil
    Group: 
    Body: '<b>What it does.</b> Your finisher is struck on an anvil that rises out of the ground. Its ring runs out and strikes every other enemy near, shaking it and breaking its armour, and a blade is forged for each one it reaches. The blades hang at your shoulders and fly with your next heavy blow, each at an enemy near.


      <b>When it happens.</b> Every finisher that lands. The blades wait for your next heavy swing.


      <b>The numbers.</b> A god''s gift, never sold; in the playtest it can be bought. The ring reaches 6 metres from the finished enemy: 15 damage, 30 stagger, three stacks of Tremor and three notches of Sundered to each other enemy in it. One blade for each enemy reached, six at most, kept up to 14 seconds. Each flies at an enemy within 10 metres for 10 damage, 12 stagger and one notch of Sundered.


      <b>Works with.</b> Buckled (every enemy it reaches is left shaken and notched), Folded Steel, Hammer and Anvil.


      <b>Example.</b> Finish a soldier in a pack of four: the other three are shaken and notched three deep, and your next heavy blow throws three blades.'
  - Id: glacier.coldwater
    Title: Cold Water
    Group: 
    Body: '<b>What it does.</b> Your blows lay Chill and Soaked together. A Soaked enemy passes any Chill laid on it to everyone within 4 metres, so from the second blow on, your cold spreads through a crowd.


      <b>When it happens.</b> Every weapon blow that lands, light or heavy. It needs Ice and Water both carried.


      <b>The numbers.</b> Mix, 3 Shards. One stack of Chill and one of Soaked on each blow, whichever of the two you carry first. Your first element''s own is not laid twice: with Ice first and Chill learned, a blow lays the root''s one Chill and this mark''s Soaked. Soaked lasts 8 seconds and makes spells deal the enemy 25% more damage.


      <b>Works with.</b> Chill or Soaked, Flash Freeze, Cold in the Bones, Icebreaker, Creeping Ice, The Wave Stands Still, Riptide.


      <b>Example.</b> Holding Ice first, two blows on a soldier in a pack leave it two deep in Chill and Soaked, and the Chill has run into the two beside it as well.'
  - Id: glacier.flash
    Title: Flash Freeze
    Group: 
    Body: '<b>What it does.</b> A Soaked enemy freezes at three Chill, not five. The water goes into the ice: the freeze spends the Soaked.


      <b>When it happens.</b> Always on once learned, the moment a Soaked enemy reaches three stacks of Chill.


      <b>The numbers.</b> Mix, 3 Shards. Frozen at three for the usual 2.5 seconds (elites and gods 1 second). A heavy blow then shatters it for 45 more damage, as always.


      <b>Works with.</b> Cold Water (both on every blow), Chill, Cold Read, Riptide, Icebreaker, All at Once, Brittle.


      <b>Example.</b> With Cold Water and Chill learned, a soldier is frozen after its second blow; the heavy blow that follows shatters it.'
  - Id: glacier.creeping
    Title: Creeping Ice
    Group: 
    Body: '<b>What it does.</b> You send a line of ice spikes along the ground ahead of you. Each enemy on the line is struck once and chilled.


      <b>When it happens.</b> From a spell slot: cast it with that slot''s button (hold L2 and a face button, or 1 to 4).


      <b>The numbers.</b> Mix, 4 Shards, no mana: it waits 12 seconds after a cast, less with weapon play. The spikes run 8 metres from 1.3 metres ahead of you, at 20 metres a second, each 0.6 metres in radius. 8 damage, 10 stagger and two stacks of Chill to each enemy. As built it does not hold enemies by the feet.


      <b>Works with.</b> Cold Water (Soaked enemies pass the Chill on), Flash Freeze (two stacks and one blow freeze a Soaked enemy), Bitter Cold, Chill.


      <b>Example.</b> Send it down a line of Soaked soldiers: each is two deep, and one more blow on any of them freezes it.'
  - Id: glacier.breaker
    Title: Icebreaker
    Group: 
    Body: '<b>What it does.</b> Shattering an enemy gives you mana and fills part of a flask you have used.


      <b>When it happens.</b> Each time a frozen enemy is shattered.


      <b>The numbers.</b> Mix, 3 Shards. 12 mana and a third of a flask a shatter, while you carry fewer flasks than your most. Three shatters leave it a hair short; the fourth fills it.


      <b>Works with.</b> Flash Freeze, Cold Water, Flying Shards, All at Once, The Wave Stands Still (one heavy blow shatters all it holds), The World Holds Still.


      <b>Example.</b> Shatter four frozen soldiers in one fight and a spent flask is back on your belt.'
  - Id: glacier.bones
    Title: Cold in the Bones
    Group: 
    Body: '<b>What it does.</b> Striking a Soaked enemy makes your perfect guard easier for a few seconds: the moment for it is a quarter longer.


      <b>When it happens.</b> Each time a weapon blow or a spell of yours strikes a Soaked enemy, at most twice a second.


      <b>The numbers.</b> Mix, 4 Shards. The perfect-guard moment is 25% longer for 4 seconds: about 0.23 seconds where it is 0.18. As built it lengthens your own moment to guard; it does not slow the enemy''s wind-up.


      <b>Works with.</b> Cold Water (every blow soaks), Cold Read, Gathering Frost, Patient Guard, Weight of Ice.


      <b>Example.</b> Cut a Soaked duellist twice, then meet its answer with a perfect guard you would have missed.'
  - Id: glacier.wave
    Title: The Wave Stands Still
    Group: 
    Body: '<b>What it does.</b> You throw a great wave that rolls ahead while you hold the button, soaking and carrying what it meets. Let go, and it freezes where it stands with everything in it Frozen. One heavy blow beside the wall shatters it and all it holds.


      <b>When it happens.</b> From a spell slot: cast it with that slot''s button (hold L2 and a face button, or 1 to 4), and keep holding it. Letting go, or the wave reaching its end, freezes it.


      <b>The numbers.</b> Mix, 5 Shards, 50 mana. The wave rolls from 1 metre ahead at 6 metres a second, at least 2.5 metres and at most 9, 6 metres wide. What it meets takes 10 damage and is Soaked, and is pushed along. Frozen, it is a wall nothing walks through, and everything within about 3 metres behind it is chilled to full depth. It stands 4 seconds. A heavy blow swung beside it shatters it: 45 damage and 60 stagger to everything in it, as a heavy blow, so each frozen enemy also shatters for 45.


      <b>Works with.</b> Icebreaker (mana and flask for every enemy shattered), Flying Shards and Clean Break on the Ice tree, All at Once (each shatter three times as hard), Brittle.


      <b>Example.</b> Roll the wave over a pack, let go as it reaches them, then walk up and break it: every one of them shatters at once.'
  - Id: glacier.weight
    Title: Weight of Ice
    Group: 
    Body: '<b>What it does.</b> Each blow you catch on your guard lays a plate of ice on you, up to five; a perfect guard lays two. Each plate turns a little of every wound. Your next heavy blow spends them all in one great edge of ice along its line, longer and harder for every plate.


      <b>When it happens.</b> Plates come with each blocked blow and each perfect guard. They are spent by your next heavy swing, whether or not it lands, or fall away 30 seconds after the last was laid.


      <b>The numbers.</b> A god''s gift, never sold; in the playtest it can be bought. Each plate takes 6% off the damage you take, 30% at five. The edge reaches 2.5 metres and 1.2 more a plate (8.5 at five), 1.3 metres to each side: 12 damage, 12 stagger and one stack of Chill a plate, as a heavy blow. Five plates: 60 damage, 60 stagger and five Chill, enough to freeze.


      <b>Works with.</b> Cold Read, Gathering Frost, Cold in the Bones, Braced, Unmoved, Chill.


      <b>Example.</b> Guard a brute''s three-blow chain, the last perfectly: four plates. Your heavy blow throws an edge 7 metres long through it and the soldier behind.'
  - Id: halo.brightsteel
    Title: Bright Steel
    Group: 
    Body: '<b>What it does.</b> A perfect guard flashes off your blade. The attacker is Marked, and its armour is notched.


      <b>When it happens.</b> Every perfect guard: press the guard button just before a blow lands.


      <b>The numbers.</b> Mix, 3 Shards. One stack of Marked and one notch of Sundered on the attacker. Where your first element''s root mark already lays its own with a perfect guard (Sunder''s notch, or Marked''s), that one is not laid twice: the guard leaves one of each.


      <b>Works with.</b> Sunder, Halo of Blades (the three Marked blows that follow are critical, and each forges a blade), Counter Cut, Open Line, Edge Guard, Mirror Edge.


      <b>Example.</b> Perfect-guard a soldier''s swing and answer with three light blows: all three are critical, and land on notched armour.'
  - Id: halo.haloofblades
    Title: Halo of Blades
    Group: 
    Body: '<b>What it does.</b> Every critical blow you land forges a blade of light in a ring behind your shoulders, up to six. A perfect guard looses them all at the one who struck.


      <b>When it happens.</b> Each critical weapon blow forges one; a perfect guard looses every one that hangs. The count shows on the screen as Blades.


      <b>The numbers.</b> Mix, 4 Shards. Six blades at most. Each flies at 16 metres a second, turning after the attacker, and strikes for 9 damage and 8 stagger with one notch of Sundered.


      <b>Works with.</b> Bright Steel and Marked enemies (every blow on them is critical), Counter Cut, Answering Draw, Clean Edge, Edge Guard, Blinding Guard.


      <b>Example.</b> Land three critical blows on a Marked soldier, then perfect-guard the brute behind it: three blades fly into the brute.'
  - Id: halo.answeringdraw
    Title: Answering Draw
    Group: 
    Body: '<b>What it does.</b> After any perfect guard, every blow you land for a moment is critical. The Iaido Slash also Marks what it cuts and notches its armour.


      <b>When it happens.</b> The mark and notch when the Iaido Slash, the Katana''s weapon skill (Q, Triangle or Y), strikes. It needs the Katana. The critical moment opens with each perfect guard.


      <b>The numbers.</b> Mix, 4 Shards. One stack of Marked and one notch of Sundered from the slash. For 1.5 seconds after a perfect guard, every weapon blow is critical (one and a half times damage). Where your first element''s root mark already lays its own with the slash, that one is not laid twice.


      <b>Works with.</b> Master''s Answer (after a perfect guard the slash comes at once, free, and critical), Halo of Blades, Bright Steel, Counter Cut, Clean Edge.


      <b>Example.</b> Perfect-guard a thrust and loose the Iaido Slash straight away: it lands critical on everything it cuts.'
  - Id: halo.mirroredge
    Title: Mirror Edge
    Group: 
    Body: '<b>What it does.</b> A perfect guard throws a bolt of light straight back at the attacker. It strikes hard and Marks what it hits.


      <b>When it happens.</b> Every perfect guard. As built it answers any perfect guard, not only one against a thrown attack, and the bolt carries its own damage, not the turned blow''s.


      <b>The numbers.</b> Mix, 3 Shards. The bolt flies straight at 18 metres a second for 1.5 seconds, passing through: 20 damage, 30 stagger and one stack of Marked to each enemy it strikes.


      <b>Works with.</b> Bright Steel, Halo of Blades, Blinding Guard, Open Line, Edge Guard.


      <b>Example.</b> An archer looses and you perfect-guard the arrow: the bolt runs back down the line and Marks it.'
  - Id: halo.sunwheels
    Title: Sun Wheels
    Group: 
    Body: '<b>What it does.</b> Two wheels of bright steel turn round you for a while, cutting and notching whatever they pass.


      <b>When it happens.</b> From a spell slot: cast it with that slot''s button (hold L2 and a face button, or 1 to 4). As built the wheels do not yet fly out on a perfect guard.


      <b>The numbers.</b> Mix, 4 Shards, no mana: it waits 12 seconds after a cast, less with weapon play. Two wheels 2.5 metres out from you for 9 seconds. Every half second each strikes what is within a metre of it for 5 damage, 4 stagger and a notch of Sundered; an enemy is struck once in each half second however many wheels pass it.


      <b>Works with.</b> Ricochet (every strike is a spell striking), Sunder, the charged blade (it charges your weapon with Metal), True Flight.


      <b>Example.</b> Cast it before stepping into a ring of small enemies: nine seconds later each is notched three deep.'
  - Id: halo.blindingguard
    Title: Blinding Guard
    Group: 
    Body: '<b>What it does.</b> A perfect guard blinds those before you: they are Marked and their balance is shaken. Everyone near you, on any side, is held still for a breath. The price: a blow held on a plain guard costs more stamina.


      <b>When it happens.</b> Always on once learned: the flash with every perfect guard, the price with every blocked blow.


      <b>The numbers.</b> Mix, 5 Shards. You turn to the attacker; a cone 6 metres long and 120 degrees wide gives 15 stagger and one stack of Marked to all in it. Everyone within 6 metres is held for 1.5 seconds (elites for less; what cannot be frozen, not at all). A blocked blow costs a fifth more stamina: 1.08 a point of damage where it cost 0.9.


      <b>Works with.</b> Bright Steel, Halo of Blades, Mirror Edge, Open Line, Edge Guard.


      <b>Example.</b> Three soldiers press you; perfect-guard the first: all three stand still and Marked, and your next blows are critical.'
  - Id: halo.sixmirrors
    Title: Six Mirrors
    Group: 
    Body: '<b>What it does.</b> Six mirrors of steel stand in a ring round the enemy you face. You vanish and cross the ring from each mirror in turn, faster than can be followed, then stand again where you began, and every cut lands at once. Nothing can strike you from the vanishing to the landing.


      <b>When it happens.</b> From a spell slot: cast it with that slot''s button (hold L2 and a face button, or 1 to 4).


      <b>The numbers.</b> A god''s gift, never sold; in the playtest it can be bought. 60 mana. An enemy within 8 metres; the ring is 3 metres in radius. Six crossings 0.13 seconds apart, then 0.3 seconds still. Each cut deals 14 damage and 12 stagger to the enemy (84 and 72 in all), and half to anything else its line crossed. Then everything within 1.2 metres of the ring''s middle is Marked and notched three deep.


      <b>Works with.</b> Bright Steel, Halo of Blades (the Marked blows after are critical), Sunder, Counter Cut, the charged blade (it charges your weapon with Metal).


      <b>Example.</b> Against a lone duellist: cast, and it takes 84, is Marked and notched three deep, and your next three blows are critical on broken armour.'
  - Id: ice.chill
    Title: Chill
    Group: 
    Body: '<b>What it does.</b> Every blow of your weapon that lands chills the enemy, a stack at a time, up to five. Each stack slows it. At five it is Frozen: held still in ice until it thaws, or until a heavy blow shatters it for a burst of damage.


      <b>When it happens.</b> Always on once learned: every weapon blow that lands, light or heavy, while Ice is your first element (or all in). With Ice second, your weapon lays the first element''s affliction and Chill comes from your Ice spells, the charged blade and the R2 strike.


      <b>The numbers.</b> 2 Shards. One stack a blow, five at most, lasting 6 seconds. Each stack slows the enemy by 7%. At five it freezes for 2.5 seconds; elites and gods thaw after 1 second, and some great forms cannot be frozen. A heavy blow on a frozen enemy shatters it for 45 more damage, and the Chill ends. Nothing chills a frozen enemy further.


      <b>Works with.</b> Glaze (one more Chill a blow), Hoarfrost, Cold Read, Flying Shards, Brittle, All at Once, Cold Settles, Deep Winter, and Soaked, which carries Chill to everyone within 4 metres.


      <b>Example.</b> Four quick light blows slow a soldier to a crawl; the fifth freezes it, and a heavy blow breaks it for 45 on top of the cut.'
  - Id: ice.shards
    Title: Flying Shards
    Group: 
    Body: '<b>What it does.</b> A shattered enemy throws its ice wide. Everyone the shards reach is struck and chilled two deep, the one that shattered among them.


      <b>When it happens.</b> Each time a frozen enemy is shattered, by your heavy blow or anything else that shatters.


      <b>The numbers.</b> 3 Shards. A burst 4.5 metres round the shattered enemy: 14 damage, 10 stagger and two stacks of Chill to each.


      <b>Works with.</b> Chill, Brittle, All at Once, Eight Points and Hanging Ice, which grow from it, Cold Settles, Icebreaker on the Glacier branch, and The World Holds Still, whose chain of shatters throws the shards again at each link.


      <b>Example.</b> Shatter one frozen soldier in a pack of four: the other three are two deep at once, three light blows from freezing.'
  - Id: ice.eight
    Title: Eight Points
    Group: 
    Body: '<b>What it does.</b> Eight shards stand on a ring round the enemy you face for a breath, then fly in together. Each lays a stack of Chill, and as they close they spend the Chill it carries for more damage: the detonator of the tree.


      <b>When it happens.</b> From a spell slot: cast it with that slot''s button (hold L2 and a face button, or 1 to 4). With no enemy faced the shards close on a spot 6 metres ahead, and the slot still waits.


      <b>The numbers.</b> 4 Shards, no mana: it waits 11 seconds after a cast, less with weapon play (its Empower: 9, and the shards close after 0.9 seconds). An enemy within 6 metres. The ring is 3.5 metres round it and closes after 1.2 seconds. Each shard deals 5 damage, 4 stagger and one stack of Chill; each that lands on a chilled enemy then spends its Chill in a small burst, 5 damage and 2 stagger a stack.


      <b>Works with.</b> Flying Shards, which it grows from; Chill and Cold Read to lay the stacks first; Hanging Ice; All at Once; Cold Settles when a second element''s affliction is on the enemy too.


      <b>Not built yet.</b> A Frozen enemy shattered by the shards: a spell''s blow does not shatter, so a frozen enemy''s Chill is spent like any other''s.


      <b>Example.</b> Chill a brute four deep with your blade, then close the ring on it: the first shard spends all four for 25 on top of its own.'
  - Id: ice.eight.shape
    Title: 'Eight Points: Wolf''s Jaws or Eight on Eight'
    Group: 
    Body: '<b>What it does.</b> Opens two shapes of Eight Points, chosen at any rest fire. <b>Wolf''s Jaws</b>: two rows of four close from in front and behind in half a second, too fast to walk out of; one target only. <b>Eight on Eight</b>: one shard comes down on each of up to eight enemies within 8 metres, each spending that enemy''s Chill; for crowds.


      <b>When it happens.</b> Whenever you cast Eight Points, as the shape it wears.


      <b>The numbers.</b> 3 Shards. Wolf''s Jaws: the ring 2 metres round the enemy, closing after 0.5 seconds. Eight on Eight: up to eight enemies within 8 metres, each struck 0.5 seconds after the cast for 8 damage, 10 stagger and a stack of Chill, then its Chill spent as above.


      <b>Works with.</b> Hanging Ice (Wolf''s Jaws on its enemy while it falls); Flying Shards and Cold Settles in a crowd (Eight on Eight).


      <b>Not built yet.</b> Wolf''s Jaws as two rows closing from front and back (for now a tighter, faster ring), and Eight on Eight''s shards falling from above (for now they rise under each enemy as pillars).


      <b>Example.</b> A duellist that steps out of the plain ring cannot step out of Wolf''s Jaws. Six soldiers two deep: Eight on Eight spends all of them at once.'
  - Id: ice.eight.master
    Title: 'Eight Points: Mastered'
    Group: 
    Body: '<b>What it does.</b> Land a heavy blow on the enemy as the shards close, and every shard counts as a shatter.


      <b>When it happens.</b> A heavy blow (a finisher counts) on an enemy within 0.3 seconds of an Eight Points shard landing on it. Eight Points must be in a slot.


      <b>The numbers.</b> 3 Shards. The heavy blow strikes once more as a shatter does: 45 damage, 30 stagger and a stack of Chill within a metre.


      <b>Works with.</b> Hanging Ice and Flying Shards; All at Once; the heavy weapons, whose heavy is slow to time.


      <b>Not built yet.</b> Every shard counting as a shatter, eight shatters with Flying Shards from each: for now the timed heavy strikes once more, as one shatter.


      <b>Example.</b> Start the heavy as the ring tightens: it lands with the shards, and the enemy takes a second break on top.'
  - Id: ice.hanging
    Title: Hanging Ice
    Group: 
    Body: '<b>What it does.</b> A great icicle hangs over the enemy you face and follows it while its shadow grows. Then it falls as a heavy blow that chills what it strikes, and leaves cracked ground that bites for a moment. On a Frozen enemy it shatters it.


      <b>When it happens.</b> From a spell slot: cast it with that slot''s button (hold L2 and a face button, or 1 to 4). With no enemy faced the slot is still spent and waits.


      <b>The numbers.</b> 4 Shards, no mana: it waits 10 seconds after a cast, less with weapon play (its Empower: 8, and it falls after 2.4 seconds). An enemy within 7 metres; with none, 7 metres ahead. It falls after 3 seconds, following its enemy until a moment before. The fall strikes everything within 2 metres for 30 damage, 60 stagger and three stacks of Chill, as a heavy blow. The crack, 1.5 metres round, bites every half second for 2 seconds for 2 damage and a stack of Chill.


      <b>Works with.</b> Chill (freeze it during the wait and the icicle shatters it), Flying Shards, which it grows from, Eight Points, Brittle, All at Once.


      <b>Not built yet.</b> The shatter of a Frozen enemy for 90: for now the fall shatters it as any heavy blow does, for 45.


      <b>Example.</b> Hang it over a brute and chill it to five with your blade as it falls: the icicle comes down on a frozen body and breaks it.'
  - Id: ice.hanging.shape
    Title: 'Hanging Ice: Icicles or Held by a Thread'
    Group: 
    Body: '<b>What it does.</b> Opens two shapes of Hanging Ice, chosen at any rest fire. <b>Icicles</b>: three smaller icicles fall a second apart along where the enemy moves; it punishes running. <b>Held by a Thread</b>: it does not fall by itself, but hangs up to eight seconds and falls with your next heavy blow on its enemy, woven into the heavy.


      <b>When it happens.</b> Whenever you cast Hanging Ice, as the shape it wears.


      <b>The numbers.</b> 3 Shards. Icicles: three falls a second apart, each 1.5 metres round, 12 damage, 25 stagger and a stack of Chill. Held by a Thread: a sign on the enemy within 7 metres for 8 seconds; the next weapon blow on it brings down the full icicle, 30 damage, 60 stagger and three Chill in 2 metres.


      <b>Works with.</b> Chill and the heavy blow (Held by a Thread: the icicle and the heavy land together); Flying Shards.


      <b>Not built yet.</b> Only a heavy blow bringing Held by a Thread down, and the icicle seen hanging (for now any weapon blow on its enemy sets it off, as a sign).


      <b>Example.</b> An archer that keeps running from you: Icicles, and every step it takes is under ice.'
  - Id: ice.hanging.master
    Title: 'Hanging Ice: Mastered'
    Group: 
    Body: '<b>What it does.</b> Let Hanging Ice land in the moment its enemy freezes, and it shatters it four times over and its cooldown comes back.


      <b>When it happens.</b> For now, when the fall itself freezes what it strikes. Hanging Ice must be in a slot.


      <b>The numbers.</b> 3 Shards. The slot''s wait is ended at once.


      <b>Works with.</b> Chill and Cold Read to bring the enemy to two before it lands; Eight Points; Rime Guard.


      <b>Not built yet.</b> The timing (within 0.3 seconds of the enemy becoming Frozen, by any hand) and the shatter four times over; for now a fall that brings its enemy to five freezes it and gives the cooldown back.


      <b>Example.</b> Two Chill on a brute, then the icicle''s three: it freezes under the fall, and a second icicle is ready to hang over it.'
  - Id: ice.lift
    Title: Cold Settles
    Group: 
    Body: '<b>What it does.</b> Cold Settles, Ice''s reaction lift: every reaction with Chill in it leaves frozen ground where it happened, and what it struck is slowed.


      <b>When it happens.</b> Whenever Chill reacts on an enemy with the other affliction it carries (Steam with Burn, Supercooled with Static, and the rest).


      <b>The numbers.</b> 3 Shards. A patch of frozen ground 1.5 metres round the reaction for 4 seconds, biting once a second for 1 damage and a stack of Chill. The enemy it happened on keeps 60% of its speed for 2 seconds (elites half the slowing, gods none).


      <b>Works with.</b> Carrying a second element: every reaction of Ice''s ten; Flying Shards, which it grows from; All at Once and Deep Winter above it.


      <b>Not built yet.</b> The slow on everything the reaction struck: for now only the enemy it happened on.


      <b>Example.</b> Ice and Water on a soldier in a crowd: the reaction goes off, the floor freezes round it, and the soldiers walking in take Chill.'
  - Id: ice.allatonce
    Title: All at Once
    Group: 
    Body: '<b>What it does.</b> Shattering strikes three times as hard. The price: Chill no longer slows anyone. It still freezes at five.


      <b>When it happens.</b> Always on once learned.


      <b>The numbers.</b> 6 Shards. A shatter deals 135 where it dealt 45. Chill''s slowing is gone, at every depth.


      <b>Works with.</b> Eight Points, Hanging Ice, Flying Shards, Brittle, Cold Settles, Flash Freeze on the Glacier branch.


      <b>Example.</b> Freeze an elite and shatter it with one heavy blow: 135 from the ice alone, on top of the blow.'
  - Id: ice.devotion
    Title: Deep Winter
    Group: 
    Body: '<b>What it does.</b> Deep Winter, Ice''s Devotion: all in on Ice only. Chill never fades, and lighting Glaze freezes every enemy within four metres at once. No Chill is ever wasted, so you can spread it over a whole room and come back for each in turn.


      <b>When it happens.</b> Only while Ice is carried twice (all in). The freeze comes each time Glaze is lit.


      <b>The numbers.</b> 6 Shards. Chill lasts three times as long (18 seconds where it lasted 6). Lighting Glaze lays Chill to full depth on everything within 4 metres of you, which freezes what can be frozen. All in, L2 with R2 is the deep strike, Ice Through: the spike freezes the enemy at once if it carries three Chill or more.


      <b>Works with.</b> Every spell of the tree; Splinter Ward and The World Holds Still, which answer Glaze too; Flying Shards, for the room frozen at once.


      <b>Not built yet.</b> Chill that never fades by itself: for now it lasts three times as long.


      <b>Example.</b> Chill four soldiers two deep each, step into the middle and light Glaze: all four are Frozen, and every heavy blow breaks one.'
  - Id: ice.coldread
    Title: Cold Read
    Group: 
    Body: '<b>What it does.</b> A perfect guard chills the one who struck, two stacks at once.


      <b>When it happens.</b> A perfect guard: press the guard button just before a blow lands.


      <b>The numbers.</b> 3 Shards. Two stacks of Chill on the attacker.


      <b>Works with.</b> Chill (three blows after the guard freeze it), Rime Guard and Splinter Ward, which grow from it, Flash Freeze on the Glacier branch.


      <b>Example.</b> A soldier already three deep swings at you: guard it perfectly and it freezes on the spot, ready for a heavy blow.'
  - Id: ice.rime
    Title: Rime Guard
    Group: 
    Body: '<b>What it does.</b> You breathe out a low, thin freezing fog round you. An enemy that strikes at you is chilled two deep, rime grows on its weapon arm, and its next wind-up comes half again as slowly. A perfect guard freezes the attacker at once.


      <b>When it happens.</b> From a spell slot: cast it with that slot''s button (hold L2 and a face button, or 1 to 4). The answers come from the next blows that come at you.


      <b>The numbers.</b> 4 Shards, no mana: it waits 9 seconds after a cast, less with weapon play (its Empower: 7, and the fog 4 metres round). The fog is 3 metres round where you breathed it and stands 6 seconds; it does no harm itself. Each cast holds three answers: a blow that lands on you or on your guard lays two Chill on its attacker, and a perfect guard lays five, which freezes it. Every enemy standing in the fog winds up its attacks half again as slowly while it stays there.


      <b>Works with.</b> Cold Read, which it grows from (a perfect guard in the fog: Cold Read''s two and the freeze); Hanging Ice; Splinter Ward.


      <b>Not built yet.</b> The fog''s six seconds as the window for the answers (for now the three answers wait for the next blows, fog or not, and are spent by them), the rime on the attacker''s weapon arm, and only the attacker''s next wind-up slowed (for now everything standing in the fog winds up slowly).


      <b>Example.</b> Breathe the fog at a duellist and let it come: its first thrust lands you two Chill on it, its next comes slow enough to guard perfectly, and it freezes.'
  - Id: ice.rime.shape
    Title: 'Rime Guard: Freezing Fog or Breath on the Steel'
    Group: 
    Body: '<b>What it does.</b> Opens two shapes of Rime Guard, chosen at any rest fire. <b>Freezing Fog</b>: the fog stays where it was breathed, five metres wide, and everything in it gains a Chill a second; hold a door with it. <b>Breath on the Steel</b>: no fog; the rime goes on your guard, and every blow guarded lays two Chill on the attacker and every perfect guard freezes it.


      <b>When it happens.</b> Whenever you cast Rime Guard, as the shape it wears. Breath on the Steel''s guard answers come while the shape is worn.


      <b>The numbers.</b> 3 Shards. Freezing Fog: 2.5 metres round, a stack of Chill on all in it each second for 6 seconds. Breath on the Steel: two Chill for each blow guarded, five (a freeze) for each perfect guard.


      <b>Works with.</b> Cold Read and Splinter Ward (Breath on the Steel); Winter Wall and Hanging Ice to keep them in the fog (Freezing Fog).


      <b>Not built yet.</b> Breath on the Steel''s six seconds after a cast: for now every guard chills and every perfect guard freezes while it is worn, cast or not. Freezing Fog empowered reaches 4 metres round, past its own 2.5 (an Empower''s numbers are set after the shape''s).


      <b>Example.</b> A corridor and a pack: Freezing Fog in the doorway, and they arrive at you three or four deep.'
  - Id: ice.rime.master
    Title: 'Rime Guard: Mastered'
    Group: 
    Body: '<b>What it does.</b> A perfect guard in the fog''s first second freezes everything in the fog, not only the attacker.


      <b>When it happens.</b> For now, any perfect guard while Rime Guard is in a slot, once in nine seconds.


      <b>The numbers.</b> 3 Shards. Chill to full depth on everything within 3 metres of you, which freezes what can be frozen.


      <b>Works with.</b> Cold Read, Flying Shards (a crowd frozen, then broken one by one), All at Once.


      <b>Not built yet.</b> Only in the fog''s first second, and only what stands in the fog; for now any perfect guard, fog or not, once in nine seconds.


      <b>Example.</b> Three soldiers swing at once into the fresh fog: guard the first perfectly and all three stand frozen round you.'
  - Id: ice.splinter
    Title: Splinter Ward
    Group: 
    Body: '<b>What it does.</b> When a ward turns a blow, it bursts round you, striking and chilling everything near, and gives you what a perfect guard gives: its mana and its cut to every cooldown.


      <b>When it happens.</b> Each time a ward is spent: Glaze''s ward, or any other.


      <b>The numbers.</b> 3 Shards. A burst 3.5 metres round you: 12 damage, 30 stagger and three stacks of Chill. 15 mana, and 2 seconds off every running cooldown.


      <b>Works with.</b> Glaze (one ward when lit), Cold Read, which it grows from, Winter Wall and Sent Sliding above it, Deep Winter, Chill.


      <b>Not built yet.</b> The turned blow counting as a perfect guard for other marks (Cold Read, Rime Guard): for now it gives a perfect guard''s mana and cut alone.


      <b>Example.</b> Light Glaze and let a brute''s red attack land on the ward: everything round you is three deep and staggered, and your spells are two seconds nearer.'
  - Id: ice.wall
    Title: Winter Wall
    Group: 
    Body: '<b>What it does.</b> You raise a wall of ice before you. Nothing walks through it and blows from its far side do not reach you. When its time ends, or when you strike it with a heavy blow, it bursts and chills everything near it.


      <b>When it happens.</b> From a spell slot: cast it with that slot''s button (hold L2 and a face button, or 1 to 4). A heavy blow swung within reach of it bursts it early.


      <b>The numbers.</b> 4 Shards, 35 mana (its Empower: 30, and a burst of 36). The wall rises 2 metres ahead, 5 metres wide, and stands 6 seconds. The burst reaches 4 metres round it: 30 damage, 50 stagger and three stacks of Chill; burst by your heavy blow, it lands as a heavy blow. One wall of ice stands at a time.


      <b>Works with.</b> Splinter Ward, which it grows from, Sent Sliding, Rime Guard''s Freezing Fog, Chill.


      <b>Not built yet.</b> Its 60 health, the touch that chills, and the burst thrown forward as a cone of 6 metres: for now it chills only when it bursts, round where it stands.


      <b>Example.</b> Archers loose at you across a yard: raise the wall, wait behind it for the soldiers to come round, then cut it as they gather.'
  - Id: ice.wall.shape
    Title: 'Winter Wall: Shield Wall or Cracked Wall'
    Group: 
    Body: '<b>What it does.</b> Opens two shapes of Winter Wall, chosen at any rest fire. <b>Shield Wall</b>: a shorter wall that moves ahead of you at walking pace; advance behind it. <b>Cracked Wall</b>: it bursts by itself a moment after an enemy first strikes it, a trap that answers the enemy, not you.


      <b>When it happens.</b> Whenever you cast Winter Wall, as the shape it wears.


      <b>The numbers.</b> 3 Shards. Shield Wall: 3 metres wide, standing 4 seconds. Cracked Wall: it bursts by itself 3 seconds after it rises, with the Learn''s burst.


      <b>Works with.</b> Rime Guard and Hanging Ice behind a Shield Wall; Flying Shards at a Cracked Wall in a doorway.


      <b>Not built yet.</b> Shield Wall moving with you (for now it stands where it rose, shorter), and Cracked Wall bursting 1.5 seconds after an enemy first strikes it (for now on a clock).


      <b>Example.</b> A god''s charge across the arena: a Cracked Wall in its road, and it runs into the burst.'
  - Id: ice.wall.master
    Title: 'Winter Wall: Mastered'
    Group: 
    Body: '<b>What it does.</b> Burst Winter Wall with a heavy blow in the instant after an enemy strikes it, and the cone freezes everything it reaches.


      <b>When it happens.</b> For now, every burst of the wall. Winter Wall must be in a slot.


      <b>The numbers.</b> 3 Shards. Chill to full depth on everything the burst strikes, which freezes what can be frozen.


      <b>Works with.</b> Flying Shards and All at Once (a frozen crowd to break), Sent Sliding.


      <b>Not built yet.</b> The timing (a heavy blow within 0.3 seconds of an enemy striking the wall): for now every burst freezes what it reaches.


      <b>Example.</b> Soldiers hacking at the wall: cut it as one strikes, and all of them stand frozen in its shards.'
  - Id: ice.sliding
    Title: Sent Sliding
    Group: 
    Body: '<b>What it does.</b> Your heavy blow no longer shatters a Frozen enemy where it stands. It sends it sliding along the blow as a block of ice, striking all it meets, and it shatters at the end or on a wall. Freeze one, then bowl it into the rest.


      <b>When it happens.</b> Always on once learned: each time a frozen enemy is shattered.


      <b>The numbers.</b> 6 Shards. A lane of ice 10 metres long and 2 wide runs on from the shattered enemy along the blow: everything on it takes 30 damage, 30 stagger and two stacks of Chill. At most twice a second.


      <b>Works with.</b> Flying Shards and Chill (each one struck is two nearer its own freeze), Winter Wall, All at Once, The World Holds Still.


      <b>Not built yet.</b> The heavy blow sending the frozen body sliding as a block, throwing aside what it meets and shattering at its end or on a wall: for now it shatters where it stands as before, and the lane of ice runs on from it.


      <b>Example.</b> Freeze the soldier at the head of a line and break it toward the rest: the ice runs through all of them.'
  - Id: ice.brittle
    Title: Brittle
    Group: 
    Body: '<b>What it does.</b> An enemy whose ice is gone, by a thaw or a shatter, stays brittle for a while. Your weapon cuts deeper into it and its balance breaks sooner.


      <b>When it happens.</b> Always on once learned, on every enemy that has been Frozen and is no longer.


      <b>The numbers.</b> 3 Shards. For 5 seconds after its ice is gone the enemy takes 20% more damage from weapon blows and 20% more stagger from everything. Spells do not cut deeper.


      <b>Works with.</b> Chill, Flying Shards, All at Once, Ski Run, which grows from it, and the finisher: a shatter and a few brittle blows often stagger it.


      <b>Example.</b> Shatter a brute, then keep cutting: for five seconds every blow bites a fifth harder and its balance bar fills fast.'
  - Id: ice.base
    Title: Hoarfrost
    Group: 
    Body: '<b>What it does.</b> Hoarfrost, Ice''s own spell, comes with the element and is never bought. Crystals grow out along the ground in a fan and the cold strikes as they come. They stand a while, and a blow of your weapon among them shatters them all.


      <b>When it happens.</b> From a spell slot: cast it with that slot''s button (hold L2 and a face button, or 1 to 4). Carrying Ice, it is always yours to put in a slot.


      <b>The numbers.</b> Given with Ice. No mana: it waits 7 seconds after a cast, less with weapon play; its Empower makes that 5.5. Thirteen crystals over a fan 4.5 metres long and 110 degrees wide: 10 damage, 15 stagger and two stacks of Chill. They stand 4 seconds; a weapon blow among them shatters them all, 5 damage, 8 stagger and one more Chill to everything near.


      <b>Works with.</b> Its Empower, its two shapes and its Master; Chill; Brittle; the charged blade, which its landing charges with Ice.


      <b>Not built yet.</b> The Empower''s third stack of Chill: the base spell is cast by Ice''s kit, which takes only the Empower''s shorter wait.


      <b>Example.</b> Cast it at three soldiers, then cut into the crystals: every one of them is three deep before your second blow.'
  - Id: ice.base.shape
    Title: 'Hoarfrost: Black Ice or Frost Line'
    Group: 
    Body: '<b>What it does.</b> Opens two shapes of Hoarfrost, chosen at any rest fire. <b>Black Ice</b>: no crystals; a sheet of clear ice covers the ground ahead and chills what stands on it. <b>Frost Line</b>: one branching line of frost creeps far along the floor, chilling all it crosses; it reaches the archer behind the shield.


      <b>When it happens.</b> Whenever you cast Hoarfrost, as the shape it wears. Before this is bought, the crystals are cast.


      <b>The numbers.</b> 3 Shards. Black Ice: a sheet 2.3 metres round, 2.5 metres ahead, for 5 seconds; each second it bites what stands on it for 1 damage and a stack of Chill. Frost Line: a line 10 metres long, 1.4 metres wide, run out in a moment: 8 damage, 10 stagger and two stacks of Chill.


      <b>Works with.</b> Winter Wall and Rime Guard to keep enemies on the ice (Black Ice); Eight Points and Hanging Ice on the archer it reaches (Frost Line).


      <b>Not built yet.</b> Black Ice throwing enemies on it half again as far and a dodge on it sliding twice as far.


      <b>Example.</b> Black Ice down a corridor: the soldiers who walk in arrive two or three deep before you have swung.'
  - Id: ice.base.master
    Title: 'Hoarfrost: Mastered'
    Group: 
    Body: '<b>What it does.</b> Cast Hoarfrost within half a second after a shatter, and the crystals grow out from the shattered spot, Chill four deep.


      <b>When it happens.</b> For now, in the moment after any shatter. Hoarfrost must be in a slot.


      <b>The numbers.</b> 3 Shards. For 0.8 seconds after a shatter, every enemy within 6 metres of it is marked; the next blow or spell on each lays two more stacks of Chill.


      <b>Works with.</b> Flying Shards (its burst is the blow that spends the mark); Chill; All at Once.


      <b>Not built yet.</b> Only Hoarfrost cast in the half second after a shatter, its crystals grown from the shattered spot: for now anything that strikes them in that moment lays the two more.


      <b>Example.</b> Shatter one soldier and cast at once into the rest: they take the crystals'' Chill and two more, one blow from freezing.'
  - Id: ice.ski
    Title: Ski Run
    Group: 
    Body: '<b>What it does.</b> A lane of clear ice runs out ahead and you slide down it at once, throwing snow, through whatever stands on it. Enemies on the lane are chilled two deep, and the lane stays.


      <b>When it happens.</b> From a spell slot: cast it with that slot''s button (hold L2 and a face button, or 1 to 4). A wall, or anything too big to be shoved, stops the slide.


      <b>The numbers.</b> 4 Shards, no mana: it waits 8 seconds after a cast, less with weapon play (its Empower: 6, and a lane of 12 metres). You go 9 metres; each enemy passed takes 6 damage, 10 stagger and two stacks of Chill. The lane stays 5 seconds and bites what stands on it for 1 damage every half second. Nothing can strike you while you slide.


      <b>Works with.</b> Brittle, which it grows from; Chill; Hanging Ice and Eight Points on those you leave behind.


      <b>Not built yet.</b> The untouchable time only for the first 0.2 seconds (for now the whole slide), and a dodge along the lane carrying twice as far.


      <b>Example.</b> Ringed in, slide out through the thinnest side: everyone you pass is two deep and the ice lies between you.'
  - Id: ice.ski.shape
    Title: 'Ski Run: Thin Ice or Shooting Run'
    Group: 
    Body: '<b>What it does.</b> Opens two shapes of Ski Run, chosen at any rest fire. <b>Thin Ice</b>: the lane is lake ice over black water; whoever steps onto it cracks through to the knees and is held, and a heavy blow on it then freezes the water round it. <b>Shooting Run</b>: as you slide you loose three shards of ice at the nearest enemy, as she shoots from her skis.


      <b>When it happens.</b> Whenever you cast Ski Run, as the shape it wears.


      <b>The numbers.</b> 3 Shards. Thin Ice: each enemy the slide passes is held for 1.2 seconds (elites less) and is three deep in Chill; a heavy blow on it within those 1.2 seconds lays Chill to full depth, and it is Frozen. Shooting Run: three homing shards, each 8 damage, 6 stagger and a stack of Chill.


      <b>Works with.</b> Brittle and Flying Shards (Thin Ice: a held enemy frozen and broken); Hanging Ice (Shooting Run brings an archer''s Chill up).


      <b>Not built yet.</b> Thin Ice taking whoever steps onto the lane within 5 seconds after (for now those the slide passes), and a god slowed by 30% rather than held; Shooting Run''s shards loosed through the slide (for now all three as it starts).


      <b>Example.</b> Slide past two soldiers on Thin Ice and turn: both are held to the knees, and one heavy blow freezes the first.'
  - Id: ice.ski.master
    Title: 'Ski Run: Mastered'
    Group: 
    Body: '<b>What it does.</b> Started in the instant a blow would land on you, Ski Run counts as a perfect dodge. And slide through an enemy in the moment it shatters, and the lane freezes everything standing on it.


      <b>When it happens.</b> For now, every cast of Ski Run, and every slide through a Frozen enemy. Ski Run must be in a slot.


      <b>The numbers.</b> 3 Shards. What a perfect dodge gives: 12 mana and 1.5 seconds off every running cooldown. Sliding through a Frozen enemy runs a lane 9 metres on from it, 2 metres wide, laying Chill to full depth on all on it, once a second at most.


      <b>Works with.</b> Rime Guard''s and Cold Read''s freezes to slide through; Flying Shards; All at Once.


      <b>Not built yet.</b> The timing (started as a blow would land), and the moment of a shatter: for now every cast gives the dodge''s mana and cuts, and any Frozen enemy slid through freezes the lane on from it.


      <b>Example.</b> Freeze the front soldier, slide through it at the line behind: the line stands frozen in your wake.'
  - Id: ice.stillworld
    Title: The World Holds Still
    Group: 
    Body: '<b>What it does.</b> Lighting Glaze raises a shell of ice round you. Press the surge button again while Glaze lasts and the shell breaks outward as a ring that freezes everything it crosses, while the world is slowed. And whenever you shatter a frozen enemy, a line of breaking ice runs to the nearest one still Frozen and shatters that one too, which sends the line on again.


      <b>When it happens.</b> The shell comes when you light the surge, and stands while it lasts; the break comes when you press the surge button again, once each time you light it. As built it answers whichever surge you light. The chain of shatters comes with every shatter, Glaze or not.


      <b>The numbers.</b> A god''s gift, never sold; in the playtest it can be bought. The ring runs out to 9 metres in half a second: 10 damage, 30 stagger and Chill to full depth, so it freezes what can be frozen. Enemies are slowed to a fifth of their speed for 1.5 seconds. Glaze and its ward stay. The chain looks for a Frozen enemy within 7 metres of the one that shattered and strikes it 0.2 seconds later for 20 damage and 30 stagger as a heavy blow, which shatters it for 45 more.


      <b>Works with.</b> Glaze, Flying Shards (the shards fly at every link), All at Once, Brittle, Sent Sliding, Deep Winter.


      <b>Example.</b> Light Glaze in a crowd, break it outward, and shatter the nearest: the ice runs from one to the next until every frozen body has broken.'
  - Id: life.seed
    Title: Seeded
    Group: 
    Body: '<b>What it does.</b> Every blow of your weapon that lands plants a seed in the enemy: one stack of Seeded, up to three. Each further weapon blow on a Seeded enemy mends you a little, more for each stack. When a Seeded enemy dies, it bursts into thorns that strike everyone near it.


      <b>When it happens.</b> Always on once learned: every weapon blow that lands, light or heavy, while Life is your first element (or all in). With Life second, Seeded comes from your spells, the charged blade and the R2 strike instead.


      <b>The numbers.</b> 2 Shards. One stack a blow, three at most, lasting 8 seconds. Each weapon blow on a Seeded enemy mends 1 health for each stack, 3 at full depth. Its death throws 12 damage a stack at everyone within 3 metres, 36 at three.


      <b>Works with.</b> Ripening, Fallen Seeds, Reap What Is Sown (it bursts every seed it reaches), Root and Branch, Regrowth (one more stack a blow), Briar Patch, and Rot Roots when Poison meets the seed.


      <b>Example.</b> With the Twin Knives, three quick cuts seed a soldier three deep; every cut after that gives back 3 health while you keep pressing it.'
  - Id: life.fallen
    Title: Fallen Seeds
    Group: 
    Body: '<b>What it does.</b> Where a Seeded enemy dies, a thornbush grows and stands for a while. It lashes and seeds whatever stands in it. The bush is something grown.


      <b>When it happens.</b> Whenever an enemy carrying Seeded dies, whatever killed it.


      <b>The numbers.</b> 3 Shards. A bush 2 metres in radius for 8 seconds. It bites every half second for 4 damage and one stack of Seeded. Four stand at once at most; a fifth takes the place of the oldest.


      <b>Works with.</b> Seeded (its death burst comes too), Reap What Is Sown and Elder Tree, which grow from it, Root and Branch above them, Drawn From the Wood (the bushes are its price), Root Walk (a place to come up), Wildwood.


      <b>Example.</b> Kill a seeded soldier in a doorway: the bush where it fell seeds everyone who follows it through.'
  - Id: life.reap
    Title: Reap What Is Sown
    Group: 
    Body: '<b>What it does.</b> Reap What Is Sown, the detonator of the tree. You call in the harvest: everything you have grown bursts where it stands, the seeds in the enemies near you burst now and are spent, and you mend for each burst.


      <b>When it happens.</b> From a spell slot: cast it with that slot''s button (hold L2 and a face button, or 1 to 4).


      <b>The numbers.</b> 4 Shards, no mana: it waits 12 seconds after a cast, less with weapon play (its Empower: 10). Each grown thing, wherever it stands, bursts 3 metres round for 16 damage and 25 stagger and is gone, and mends you 5. A call 6 metres round you lands 0.2 seconds after the cast: 16 damage and 25 stagger; every Seeded enemy it strikes has its seed burst at once, 11 damage and 5 stagger a stack to everyone within 3 metres, and mends you 5.


      <b>Works with.</b> Fallen Seeds and Sapling (the things it bursts), Briar Patch, Seeded and Ripening, Wood Grows Back (the garden comes again), Wildwood (more to burst), and the charged blade: it charges your weapon with Life when it lands.


      <b>Not built yet.</b> Every Seeded enemy in the fight bursting, not only those within the call''s 6 metres; the Empower''s 7 mending a burst (for now 5).


      <b>Example.</b> Three saplings stand round you and a pack closes in: reap, and four bursts go off at once while you mend 20.'
  - Id: life.reap.shape
    Title: 'Reap What Is Sown: Golden Sickle or Second Sowing'
    Group: 
    Body: '<b>What it does.</b> Opens two shapes of Reap What Is Sown, chosen at any rest fire. <b>Golden Sickle</b>, the druids'' sickle: only the Seeded within eight metres are reaped, each cut once by one sweep of gold, and the garden is kept standing. <b>Second Sowing</b>: everything bursts as before, and each burst sows a new seed in all it reaches, so the loop keeps going.


      <b>When it happens.</b> Whenever you cast Reap What Is Sown, as the shape it wears. Before this is bought, the plain call is cast.


      <b>The numbers.</b> 3 Shards. Golden Sickle: one sweep 8 metres all round you, 16 damage and 25 stagger, and each Seeded enemy it cuts has its seed burst as the Learn''s. Second Sowing: each seed set off (by Reap, Ripening or anything else) lays one Seeded on every enemy within 3 metres of it.


      <b>Works with.</b> Ripening (its bursts sow too, while Second Sowing is worn); Fallen Seeds and Sapling for the garden Golden Sickle should keep.


      <b>Not built yet.</b> Golden Sickle keeping the garden standing: for now the grown things still burst. Second Sowing''s grown things sowing as they burst: for now only the seeds set off sow.


      <b>Example.</b> Second Sowing in a crowd: reap once to seed the whole pack again, cut, reap again.'
  - Id: life.reap.master
    Title: 'Reap What Is Sown: Mastered'
    Group: 
    Body: '<b>What it does.</b> Cast it within half a second of a Seeded enemy dying, and every burst counts twice.


      <b>When it happens.</b> For now, for half a second after any Seeded enemy dies. Reap What Is Sown must be in a slot.


      <b>The numbers.</b> 3 Shards. For half a second every seed set off bursts twice as hard (bursts of seeds 100% stronger).


      <b>Works with.</b> Seeded''s own death burst (kill one, then reap the rest); Ripening''s heavy blow in the same half second.


      <b>Not built yet.</b> The garden''s bursts and the mending counted twice too, and the window tied to the cast: for now any seed set off in that half second is doubled.


      <b>Example.</b> Finish the seeded soldier and reap as it falls: the seeds in its friends burst for twice their thorns.'
  - Id: life.tree
    Title: Elder Tree
    Group: 
    Body: '<b>What it does.</b> Elder Tree, the larger spell of the tree. A tree grows where you stand, shoot, sapling and oak, in three seconds. Grown, for fifteen seconds a ring lies under its crown: enemies inside stay Seeded, you mend, and every few seconds a root comes up under the enemies inside.


      <b>When it happens.</b> From a spell slot: cast it with that slot''s button (hold L2 and a face button, or 1 to 4).


      <b>The numbers.</b> 4 Shards, 40 mana (its Empower: 32, and it grows in 2 seconds). The ring is 3 metres in radius and lies 18 seconds from the cast, biting once a second for 1 damage and Seeded. The roots first strike 3 seconds after planting, then every 3 seconds for 15 seconds: 16 damage, 45 stagger and one Seeded. The cast holds 15 seconds of shade: each second in a fight spends one and mends you 3. The tree is not one of your grown things: Reap What Is Sown and Drawn From the Wood leave it be.


      <b>Works with.</b> Seeded, Ripening (heavy blows on what it seeded), Fallen Seeds, which it grows from, Sapling''s Master (a small tree of the same kind), and the charged blade: its first strike charges your weapon with Life.


      <b>Not built yet.</b> The tree''s 40 health while it grows and the enemies turning on it; each root under one enemy, a staggered one first (for now the roots strike everything in the ring); the mending only inside the ring while the tree stands (for now 3 a second for 15 seconds of fighting, anywhere).


      <b>Example.</b> Plant it where a pack must come to you and fight at its foot: every three seconds the roots stagger and seed them while you mend.'
  - Id: life.tree.shape
    Title: 'Elder Tree: Walking Tree or Grown at Once'
    Group: 
    Body: '<b>What it does.</b> Opens two shapes of Elder Tree, chosen at any rest fire. <b>Walking Tree</b>: the tree pulls up its roots and follows you at walking pace, with a smaller ring; the stag grown through with forest. <b>Grown at Once</b>: no growing; it comes up full in an instant and stands only six seconds, so setup becomes burst.


      <b>When it happens.</b> Whenever you cast Elder Tree, as the shape it wears. Before this is bought, the growing tree is cast.


      <b>The numbers.</b> 3 Shards. Walking Tree: the roots strike 2 metres round it. Grown at Once: the roots strike at once and then every 3 seconds for 6 seconds, 3 metres round: 16 damage, 45 stagger and Seeded.


      <b>Works with.</b> Root Walk (go where the tree is); The Garden Holds You and Wildwood near the ring.


      <b>Not built yet.</b> Walking Tree following you: for now it stands where it was planted, with the smaller ring. With either shape the shade ring and the mending keep the Learn''s times.


      <b>Example.</b> Grown at Once on a staggered brute: the first root lands before it stands up.'
  - Id: life.tree.master
    Title: 'Elder Tree: Mastered'
    Group: 
    Body: '<b>What it does.</b> Plant it on something you grew, and it grows at once.


      <b>When it happens.</b> For now, when you cast it within 4 metres of something you grew. Elder Tree must be in a slot.


      <b>The numbers.</b> 3 Shards. For now a root bursts up at once 3 metres round you, 16 damage, 45 stagger and Seeded, before the tree''s own first root.


      <b>Works with.</b> Fallen Seeds and Sapling for something to plant on; Briar Patch''s bed; Wildwood.


      <b>Not built yet.</b> The whole tree grown at once on the grown thing: for now the first root comes at once and the tree still grows.


      <b>Example.</b> Cast Briar Patch, step into the bed and plant the tree on it: the roots answer at once.'
  - Id: life.lift
    Title: Root and Branch
    Group: 
    Body: '<b>What it does.</b> Root and Branch, Life''s reaction lift: every reaction with Seeded in it mends you and sows a seed in everything it reaches.


      <b>When it happens.</b> Whenever Seeded reacts on an enemy with the other affliction it carries (Rot Roots with Poison, and the rest).


      <b>The numbers.</b> 3 Shards. Each such reaction mends you 4 and lays one Seeded on every enemy within 3 metres of where it happened.


      <b>Works with.</b> Carrying a second element: every reaction of Life''s ten; Seeded; Fallen Seeds, which it grows from; Wood Grows Back above it.


      <b>Not built yet.</b> The seed sown in exactly what the reaction struck: for now everything within 3 metres.


      <b>Example.</b> Life and Poison on a huddle: Rot Roots goes off on one, you mend 4, and its neighbours are seeded for the next.'
  - Id: life.devotion
    Title: Wood Grows Back
    Group: 
    Body: '<b>What it does.</b> Wood Grows Back, Life''s Devotion (the land''s rule, "wood forgets"): all in on Life only. Whatever you grow grows back where it stood after it is spent, burst or cut down, and every spell you cast sows a sapling where it lands. The garden never runs out, so Reap What Is Sown and Root Walk can be spent freely, and every fight becomes a forest.


      <b>When it happens.</b> Only while Life is carried twice (all in). A sapling is sown each time a spell strikes.


      <b>The numbers.</b> 6 Shards. A sapling where a spell strikes, at most one every 2 seconds: it reaches 3.5 metres, stands 12 seconds, and every 1.5 seconds strikes for 6 damage, 8 stagger and Seeded; four stand at once at most. All in, L2 with R2 is the deep strike, Briar Root: the cutting grows into a briar round the enemy''s feet and roots it for a second.


      <b>Works with.</b> Every spell of the tree; Reap What Is Sown and Drawn From the Wood, which spend the garden; Root Walk, which goes to it.


      <b>Not built yet.</b> Whatever is spent growing back where it stood 6 seconds later: for now only the saplings each spell sows. Briar Root''s briar staying as something grown.


      <b>Example.</b> Briar Patch, Reap What Is Sown, Briar Patch again: every cast leaves a sapling, so the reaping always has something to burst.'
  - Id: life.ripen
    Title: Ripening
    Group: 
    Body: '<b>What it does.</b> A heavy blow on a Seeded enemy bursts its seed at once, without waiting for it to die. The thorns strike everyone near it, and you mend.


      <b>When it happens.</b> Every heavy blow or finisher that lands on a Seeded enemy, at most once a second.


      <b>The numbers.</b> 3 Shards. The burst is 3 metres in radius: 11 damage and 5 stagger for each stack, 33 and 15 at three. The seed is spent, so it will not burst again at death. You mend 10.


      <b>Works with.</b> Seeded, Drawn From the Wood and The Garden Holds You, which grow from it, Bitter Rind (a rooted enemy is an easy heavy blow), Elder Tree (it seeds for you), Reap What Is Sown''s Second Sowing.


      <b>Example.</b> Two light blows and a heavy on a soldier in a crowd: the heavy bursts its seed through the pack and gives you 10.'
  - Id: life.harvest
    Title: Drawn From the Wood
    Group: 
    Body: '<b>What it does.</b> Drawn From the Wood. You kneel, and every grown thing of yours withers into you, bursting in thorns as it goes. In return you get a window of green blood: every weapon blow is critical and mends a fifth of its damage. The garden you grew is the price, not your health.


      <b>When it happens.</b> From a spell slot: cast it with that slot''s button (hold L2 and a face button, or 1 to 4). It wants something grown near you.


      <b>The numbers.</b> 4 Shards, no mana: it waits 12 seconds after a cast, less with weapon play (its Empower: 10). Each grown thing, wherever it stands, bursts 2 metres round for 12 damage and Seeded and is gone. For now, cast within 4 metres of something you grew, the window is 6 seconds: every weapon blow critical, and 20% of its damage back as health.


      <b>Works with.</b> Fallen Seeds, Sapling, Briar Patch and Root Walk for the garden it spends; Wood Grows Back to have it again; Ripening, which it grows from; Seeded mending on top.


      <b>Not built yet.</b> The window as a second and a half for each grown thing withered, ten seconds at most, and only those within 12 metres; the half-second kneel; the Empower''s 16-damage thorns (for now 12).


      <b>Example.</b> Three bushes stand round a brute: draw them in, and cut it with six seconds of critical, mending blows.'
  - Id: life.harvest.shape
    Title: 'Drawn From the Wood: Blood in the Furrow or Feed the Ground'
    Group: 
    Body: '<b>What it does.</b> Opens two shapes of Drawn From the Wood, chosen at any rest fire. <b>Blood in the Furrow</b>: the green blood soaks into the ground where you knelt, a ring that seeds everything in it each second; fight in a place, not round yourself. <b>Feed the Ground</b>: the one place Life pays in blood; nothing withers, you give a quarter of your health to your garden, and for a while everything you have grown strikes twice as hard and twice as often.


      <b>When it happens.</b> Whenever you cast Drawn From the Wood, as the shape it wears. Before this is bought, the withering is cast.


      <b>The numbers.</b> 3 Shards. Blood in the Furrow: a ring 8 metres across where you knelt for 6 seconds, biting once a second for 1 damage and Seeded. Feed the Ground: it costs 25 health, left grey to be won back by blows; with 25 health or less it cannot be cast. For 8 seconds what you grow strikes twice as hard.


      <b>Works with.</b> Blood in the Furrow: Bitter Rind and Briar Coat, which hold the fight in place. Feed the Ground: Fallen Seeds, Sapling and Wildwood for a garden worth feeding; the Master for a price paid in grey.


      <b>Not built yet.</b> Blood in the Furrow''s window held only while you stand in the ring. Feed the Ground taking a quarter of your present health (for now 25), sparing the garden (for now it still withers as the Learn''s does) and doubling what already stands and how often it strikes (for now only what you grow in the 8 seconds strikes harder).


      <b>Example.</b> Blood in the Furrow at a choke point: wait in the ring and let them come to you, seeded on every step.'
  - Id: life.harvest.master
    Title: 'Drawn From the Wood: Mastered'
    Group: 
    Body: '<b>What it does.</b> Cast it within a second of being struck, and the price comes from the grey health that blow left: nothing withers, each grown thing still gives its time, and Feed the Ground takes no real health.


      <b>When it happens.</b> For now, for one second after any blow lands on you. Drawn From the Wood must be in a slot.


      <b>The numbers.</b> 3 Shards. For that second, prices in health cost nothing: Feed the Ground''s 25 is not taken.


      <b>Works with.</b> Feed the Ground; Briar Coat (the blow that lands cuts the attacker too); Seeded''s mending to win the grey back.


      <b>Not built yet.</b> The garden kept on such a cast while each grown thing still gives its time, and the price drawn from that blow''s grey: for now only the health price is waived.


      <b>Example.</b> Take a soldier''s blow, then Feed the Ground at once: the garden strikes twice as hard and you pay nothing.'
  - Id: life.garden
    Title: The Garden Holds You
    Group: 
    Body: '<b>What it does.</b> The Garden Holds You. Near anything you grew, you cannot be thrown, pulled or knocked down, and plain blows do not make you flinch. Roots run from the nearest plant to your heels. Fight in the garden.


      <b>When it happens.</b> Always on once learned, while something you grew stands within 4 metres of you.


      <b>The numbers.</b> 3 Shards. For now, wounds take 20% less while something you grew stands within 4 metres.


      <b>Works with.</b> Briar Patch and Fallen Seeds for a garden to stand in, Root Walk and Wildwood, which grow from it, Ripening.


      <b>Not built yet.</b> The footing itself (never thrown, pulled or knocked down, no flinch from plain blows) and the roots drawn to your heels: for now it is less damage taken in the garden.


      <b>Example.</b> Stand in your own bed of briars against a brute: its blows land for a fifth less while you trade.'
  - Id: life.walk
    Title: Root Walk
    Group: 
    Body: '<b>What it does.</b> Root Walk, the movement spell of the tree. You sink into the ground in a swirl of leaves and come up at a grown thing of yours, or ahead if there is none. Nothing can touch you under the ground. A sapling sprouts where you went down, and roots burst round you as you come up.


      <b>When it happens.</b> From a spell slot: cast it with that slot''s button (hold L2 and a face button, or 1 to 4).


      <b>The numbers.</b> 4 Shards, no mana: it waits 8 seconds after a cast, less with weapon play (its Empower: 6, and two Seeded). For now it is a step: up to 8 metres toward and past the enemy you face, 6 metres ahead with none, untouchable for it; what it passes takes 10 damage, 15 stagger and Seeded, and your next heavy blow within half a second is critical. The sapling where you went down reaches 3.5 metres, stands 6 seconds and every 1.5 seconds strikes for 6 damage, 8 stagger and Seeded.


      <b>Works with.</b> Fallen Seeds, Sapling and Briar Patch for places to come up; The Garden Holds You, which it grows from; Wood Grows Back (spend the garden, it returns).


      <b>Not built yet.</b> Going under the ground to a grown thing within 12 metres, the one nearest where you aim, and coming up half a second later; the roots bursting round you as you come up rather than along the way.


      <b>Example.</b> Surrounded, walk out through the soldier in front: the sapling you leave keeps the rest busy.'
  - Id: life.walk.shape
    Title: 'Root Walk: Up Through Them or Changeling'
    Group: 
    Body: '<b>What it does.</b> Opens two shapes of Root Walk, chosen at any rest fire. <b>Up Through Them</b>: you go to a Seeded enemy instead, and come up under it, lifting it on roots. <b>Changeling</b>: you change places with the grown thing, so it stands where you stood, in the path of the blow aimed at you.


      <b>When it happens.</b> Whenever you cast Root Walk, as the shape it wears. Before this is bought, the plain walk is cast.


      <b>The numbers.</b> 3 Shards. Up Through Them: a Seeded enemy the walk strikes is thrown up for 0.6 seconds (elites and gods for less). Changeling: a thornbush 2 metres round rises where you stood for 8 seconds, biting every half second for 4 and Seeded, and the enemies within 2.5 metres lose track of you for 1.5 seconds.


      <b>Works with.</b> Up Through Them: Seeded, the charged blade and every mark that answers a lifted enemy. Changeling: Fallen Seeds'' bushes, Reap What Is Sown to burst what you left behind.


      <b>Not built yet.</b> Up Through Them going to the nearest Seeded enemy rather than the one faced. Changeling changing places with a grown thing: for now a bush rises where you stood and those near it strike at it.


      <b>Example.</b> Changeling out of a pincer: both soldiers swing at the bush you leave.'
  - Id: life.walk.master
    Title: 'Root Walk: Mastered'
    Group: 
    Body: '<b>What it does.</b> Started in the instant a blow would land on you, it counts as a perfect dodge, and the sapling left behind is a full thornbush.


      <b>When it happens.</b> For now, every cast. Root Walk must be in a slot.


      <b>The numbers.</b> 3 Shards. Each cast gives a perfect dodge''s mana (12) and takes 1.5 seconds off every running spell and strike clock. A thornbush 2 metres round grows where you went down for 8 seconds, biting every half second for 4 and Seeded.


      <b>Works with.</b> Every mark that answers mana; Reap What Is Sown (one more thing to burst); The Garden Holds You.


      <b>Not built yet.</b> The timing (started as a blow would land), and the thornbush in place of the sapling: for now it grows beside it.


      <b>Example.</b> Walk out of a brute''s swing, then walk again sooner: each walk leaves a bush and a sapling behind.'
  - Id: life.wildwood
    Title: Wildwood
    Group: 
    Body: '<b>What it does.</b> What you grow stands three times as long, and you may keep three more of each kind. The price: far from your garden, your weapon is a fifth weaker.


      <b>When it happens.</b> Always on once learned. The price holds whenever nothing you have grown stands within 7 metres of you.


      <b>The numbers.</b> 6 Shards. Grown things stand three times as long (thornbushes 24 seconds, saplings 36). Three more of each kind may stand at once. Weapon damage down 20% with nothing grown within 7 metres.


      <b>Works with.</b> Fallen Seeds, Sapling, Briar Patch, The Garden Holds You, which it grows from, Reap What Is Sown and Drawn From the Wood (more to spend).


      <b>Not built yet.</b> Grown things standing for ever: for now three times as long.


      <b>Example.</b> Plant a ring of saplings at the top of a stair and hold it: the garden lasts the whole fight, and you never leave it.'
  - Id: life.rind
    Title: Bitter Rind
    Group: 
    Body: '<b>What it does.</b> A plain guard seeds the attacker. A perfect guard roots it where it stands for a moment.


      <b>When it happens.</b> Each blow you block, and each perfect guard.


      <b>The numbers.</b> 3 Shards. One stack of Seeded on the attacker for each blocked blow. A perfect guard holds it still for 1 second (elites and gods for less; a few great forms cannot be held).


      <b>Works with.</b> Briar Coat, which grows from it, Sapling (perfect guards plant), Seeded, Ripening (a held enemy is an easy heavy blow).


      <b>Example.</b> Perfect-guard a brute''s swing: it stands rooted for a second, long enough for a heavy blow that bursts its seed.'
  - Id: life.base
    Title: Briar Patch
    Group: 
    Body: '<b>What it does.</b> Briar Patch, Life''s own spell, comes with the element and is never bought. A bed of thorned vines grows ahead of you and stands, lashing, seeding and slowing whatever stands in it. The bed counts as grown.


      <b>When it happens.</b> From a spell slot: cast it with that slot''s button (hold L2 and a face button, or 1 to 4). Carrying Life, it is always yours to put in a slot.


      <b>The numbers.</b> Given with Life. No mana: it waits 7 seconds after a cast, less with weapon play; its Empower makes that 5.5. The bed is 2.5 metres across, 3 metres ahead, and stands 6 seconds: it lashes twice a second for 4 damage and Seeded, and slows what stands in it by a fifth.


      <b>Works with.</b> Its Empower, its two shapes and its Master; Seeded; Reap What Is Sown and Drawn From the Wood, which spend the bed; The Garden Holds You and Root Walk; the charged blade, which its landing charges with Life.


      <b>Not built yet.</b> The Empower''s bed 3.3 metres across: the base spell is cast by Life''s kit, which takes only the Empower''s shorter wait.


      <b>Example.</b> Lay the bed in a doorway and fight on its edge: everything that comes through is seeded and slow.'
  - Id: life.base.shape
    Title: 'Briar Patch: Burrs or Seed Pods'
    Group: 
    Body: '<b>What it does.</b> Opens two shapes of Briar Patch, chosen at any rest fire. <b>Burrs</b>: no bed; a spray of hooked burrs over a fan ahead, and every enemy hit carries them, dropping seeds that sprout tufts of briar as it goes; your blows on a burred enemy shake burrs onto its neighbours. The enemy plants your garden for you, as burdock rides on animals. <b>Seed Pods</b>: no bed; three pods are thrown, swell, and burst a second later in a spray of seeds, each leaving a small bush.


      <b>When it happens.</b> Whenever you cast Briar Patch, as the shape it wears. Before this is bought, the bed is cast.


      <b>The numbers.</b> 3 Shards. Burrs: a cone 4 metres long and 90 degrees wide, 4 damage, 5 stagger and Seeded. A burred enemy carries them 6 seconds and drops a tuft every 1.5 seconds: 0.8 metres round, 4 seconds, biting every half second for 4 and Seeded, grown, six at most. Your weapon blows on it seed and burr every enemy within 2 metres, at most twice a second. Seed Pods: three pods under the nearest enemies within 6 metres, bursting 1 second later 1.5 metres round: 12 damage, 10 stagger and two Seeded; each that strikes leaves a bush 1 metre round for 6 seconds, biting every half second for 4 and Seeded, grown, three at most.


      <b>Works with.</b> Burrs: Root Walk (a place to come up wherever they went), Reap What Is Sown on a room full of tufts. Seed Pods: Fallen Seeds'' bushes, Drawn From the Wood.


      <b>Not built yet.</b> Burrs dropping a seed for every 1.5 metres the enemy moves (for now every 1.5 seconds, moving or not). Seed Pods thrown in a fan, each leaving its bush where it bursts whether it strikes or not (for now under the nearest enemies, a bush under each it strikes).


      <b>Example.</b> Burr a pack and back away: they bring your garden to you.'
  - Id: life.base.master
    Title: 'Briar Patch: Mastered'
    Group: 
    Body: '<b>What it does.</b> Cast it on something you grew, within a metre of it, and the bed grows into a thicket round it, larger and longer, and whatever stands in it as it grows is rooted.


      <b>When it happens.</b> For now, when you cast it within 4 metres of something you grew. Briar Patch must be in a slot.


      <b>The numbers.</b> 3 Shards. A thicket 4 metres across where the bed lands, for 10 seconds, biting every half second for 4 and Seeded; it is grown, two at most. Every enemy within 2 metres of it as it grows is rooted for 1 second: it cannot walk, but it still strikes what comes into reach.


      <b>Works with.</b> Fallen Seeds, Sapling and the bed itself for something to cast on; Ripening on what the thicket roots; Wildwood.


      <b>Not built yet.</b> The thicket grown round the grown thing it was cast on: for now it grows where the bed lands while you stand near something grown.


      <b>Example.</b> Two beds in a row: the second grows into a thicket and roots the soldiers in it.'
  - Id: life.coat
    Title: Briar Coat
    Group: 
    Body: '<b>What it does.</b> Thorns grow on you. An enemy that strikes you, or whose blow you block, is cut and seeded.


      <b>When it happens.</b> Each blow that lands on you, and each blow you block with a plain guard, at most twice a second for each.


      <b>The numbers.</b> 3 Shards. A burst 1.2 metres round the attacker: 8 damage and one stack of Seeded. As built any attacker is cut, even one striking from afar: the thorns land where the blow came from.


      <b>Works with.</b> Seeded (your next blows on it mend you), Bitter Rind, which it grows from, Sapling, which grows from it, Drawn From the Wood''s Master (a blow taken).


      <b>Example.</b> Block a soldier''s chain of three: it is cut and seeded on the way in, and your answer mends you.'
  - Id: life.sapling
    Title: Sapling
    Group: 
    Body: '<b>What it does.</b> Sapling, the counter of the tree. For a while after the cast, each perfect guard or perfect dodge plants a sapling where the attacker stands. Each lashes the enemies near it again and again, seeding them. They count as grown.


      <b>When it happens.</b> From a spell slot: cast it with that slot''s button (hold L2 and a face button, or 1 to 4). Then guard or dodge perfectly: press the guard button just before a blow lands, or dodge just before it.


      <b>The numbers.</b> 4 Shards, no mana: it waits 9 seconds after a cast, less with weapon play (its Empower: 7). A cast holds three saplings, spent by the next perfect guards and perfect dodges. Each sapling reaches 3.5 metres and stands 12 seconds. Every 1.5 seconds it strikes everything in reach for 6 damage, 8 stagger and one stack of Seeded. Three stand at once from guards and three from dodges; one more takes the place of the oldest. On a dodge it is planted at the enemy you face.


      <b>Works with.</b> Bitter Rind and Briar Coat (they answer the same guard), Briar Coat, which it grows from, Reap What Is Sown and Drawn From the Wood (they spend the saplings), Root Walk, Wildwood, Seeded.


      <b>Not built yet.</b> The window as eight seconds after the cast (for now the three wait until spent); three at most between guards and dodges; the Empower''s fourth sapling; each lashing only the nearest enemy (for now everything within its reach).


      <b>Example.</b> Cast it as a pack closes in and perfect-guard three blows: three saplings stand among them, seeding everything that comes.'
  - Id: life.sapling.shape
    Title: 'Sapling: Strangler or Dodder'
    Group: 
    Body: '<b>What it does.</b> Opens two shapes of Sapling, chosen at any rest fire. <b>Strangler</b>: each one climbs the attacker instead, as a strangler fig climbs its host; it is rooted and seeded deep, and nothing stands after. <b>Dodder</b>: the seed grows on the attacker itself, pale threads that drink from it; each of your blows on it mends you more, and its balance breaks sooner.


      <b>When it happens.</b> For now, on every perfect guard and perfect dodge while the shape is worn, beside the saplings. Before this is bought, the saplings alone are planted.


      <b>The numbers.</b> 3 Shards. Strangler: the attacker is rooted for 1 second (it cannot walk, but still strikes what comes into reach) and Seeded two deep. Dodder: for 6 seconds each of your weapon blows on it mends you 3, and it takes a quarter more stagger.


      <b>Works with.</b> Strangler: Ripening on the rooted enemy. Dodder: Seeded''s own mending; Bitter Rind and Briar Coat on the same attacker.


      <b>Not built yet.</b> Each in place of the sapling, and only within the cast''s window: for now they answer every perfect guard and dodge while worn, and the saplings are still planted.


      <b>Example.</b> Dodder on a brute''s perfect-guarded swing: six seconds of cuts that mend 3 more each and break it a quarter sooner.'
  - Id: life.sapling.master
    Title: 'Sapling: Mastered'
    Group: 
    Body: '<b>What it does.</b> Plant all three within three seconds, and the third comes up as a full Elder Tree for six seconds.


      <b>When it happens.</b> For now, on a perfect guard, at most once every 15 seconds. Sapling must be in a slot.


      <b>The numbers.</b> 3 Shards. A small Elder Tree rises at the attacker: its roots strike 3 metres round 0.3 seconds after, then every 3 seconds for 6 seconds, 16 damage, 45 stagger and Seeded each time.


      <b>Works with.</b> Elder Tree; Bitter Rind on the same perfect guard; Ripening on what the roots seed.


      <b>Not built yet.</b> The three planted within three seconds as its condition: for now any perfect guard, once in fifteen seconds.


      <b>Example.</b> Perfect-guard a soldier''s swing: a tree rises under it and the roots break the crowd behind.'
  - Id: life.spring
    Title: First Spring
    Group: 
    Body: '<b>What it does.</b> While your surge burns, press the surge button again and give half your health to the ground. A stand of trees comes up through every Seeded enemy near, strikes it and holds it. Strike what the forest holds, and the health you gave comes back.


      <b>When it happens.</b> Light the surge (Regrowth, or the other element''s surge if you wear that), then press the surge button again while it lasts. Once each time the surge is lit. With nothing Seeded near, it says so and you may press again.


      <b>The numbers.</b> A god''s gift, never sold; in the playtest it can be bought. Up to eight Seeded enemies within 12 metres. Each takes 30 damage and 60 stagger and is held for 4 seconds (elites and gods for less). Half your present health is taken and turns grey. Each blow on a held enemy wins back half its damage as health, never more than you gave.


      <b>Works with.</b> Seeded, Regrowth (4 health a second while it lasts), Briar Patch''s Burrs and Seed Pods to seed a crowd, Root and Branch.


      <b>Example.</b> Seed a pack with Briar Patch, light Regrowth, press again: the whole pack stands held while you cut your health back out of them.'
  - Id: light.mark
    Title: Marked
    Group: 
    Body: '<b>What it does.</b> The last blow of a chain, and every perfect guard, leave a mark of light on the enemy: it is Marked. Your next three weapon blows on a Marked enemy are critical and each gives more mana; then the mark is spent.


      <b>When it happens.</b> Always on once learned. The last light blow of a chain, or the heavy blow that ends one, marks the enemy it lands on; a perfect guard marks the one who struck. It marks whether Light is your first element or your second, since it is the mark''s own doing and not the weapon''s.


      <b>The numbers.</b> 2 Shards. A mark lasts 8 seconds or three weapon blows, whichever ends first. Each of those blows is critical, one and a half times its damage, and gives 2 more mana. Marking again refills the three blows.


      <b>Works with.</b> Glare, which marks what its ray strikes; Clarity, which marks with every blow; Lasting Mark (a fourth blow), Sharp Light (critical blows 15% harder), Plain Guilt, Rich Mark, Weighed and Sentence, and the charged blade, whose third Light blow throws a ray that marks.


      <b>Example.</b> Three light blows on a soldier mark it with the third; a heavy blow, then two more light blows, all land critical.'
  - Id: light.justcut
    Title: Just Cut
    Group: 
    Body: '<b>What it does.</b> A blow that lands may flash. For a moment after a flash every blow you land is critical. A blow that lands may also give you a little stamina back.


      <b>When it happens.</b> Any weapon blow that lands, one time in four, at most once every 1.5 seconds. The flash and the stamina are each their own roll. As built the flash comes by chance; a blow pressed at the exact moment the last one lands does not yet make it.


      <b>The numbers.</b> 3 Shards. One chance in four of a flash: every blow critical for 0.8 seconds. One chance in four of 6 stamina back. Each can come at most once every 1.5 seconds.


      <b>Works with.</b> Sharp Light (critical blows strike 15% harder), Bowed Head (critical blows break balance 20% sooner), Weighed, and quick weapons such as the Twin Knives, which fit more blows into the moment.


      <b>Example.</b> In a flurry on a duellist, one cut flashes and the two after it land critical without a mark.'
  - Id: light.dazzle
    Title: Dazzle
    Group: 
    Body: '<b>What it does.</b> A perfect dodge flashes in the attacker''s eyes. It, and every enemy standing close to it, is Marked and held still for a moment.


      <b>When it happens.</b> A perfect dodge: a blow passes through the very start of your roll.


      <b>The numbers.</b> 3 Shards. Everything within 2 metres of the attacker is Marked and held still for 1 second (shorter on elites and gods, and not at all on what cannot be held).


      <b>Works with.</b> Narrow Escape (the perfect moment 23% longer), Bright Evasion (perfect dodges give 42% more mana), Clarity (dodges safe half again as long), Step Into Light, and the root''s three critical blows.


      <b>Example.</b> Roll through a brute''s swing at the last moment: it stands frozen and Marked while you turn and land three critical blows.'
  - Id: light.step
    Title: Step Into Light
    Group: 
    Body: '<b>What it does.</b> You step through the enemy you face in a line of light and come out on its far side, turned back toward it, cutting and Marking everything on the line. If the cut lands, your next heavy blow in the moment after is critical. Nothing can strike you in the step; a wall, or something too big to shove, stops you short.


      <b>When it happens.</b> From a spell slot: cast it with that slot''s button (hold L2 and a face button, or 1 to 4). With no enemy faced you step ahead anyway, and the slot still waits.


      <b>The numbers.</b> 4 Shards, no mana: it waits 8 seconds after a cast, less with weapon play. Up to 7 metres: to 1.8 metres past the enemy faced, or about 5 metres ahead with none. The cut is 10 damage, 10 stagger and Marked on all on the line. The heavy blow after it is critical if it lands within 1.5 seconds.


      <b>Works with.</b> The root (the mark it lays gives the heavy blow and two more their critical), Sharp Light, Long Rays (the step reaches 25% further), Dazzle, and the charged blade: the cut is a spell, so it charges your weapon with Light for the next three moves.


      <b>Example.</b> Step through an archer behind its shield-bearer, turn, and land a critical heavy blow in its back.'
  - Id: light.unblemished
    Title: Unblemished
    Group: 
    Body: '<b>What it does.</b> Fight a while without a wound and every weapon blow you land is critical, and gives more mana. A blow that lands on you ends it, and until you have gone a while unwounded again you take more from every blow.


      <b>When it happens.</b> Always on once learned. You are unwounded once no blow has landed on you for 8 seconds; the gift lasts until the next one does.


      <b>The numbers.</b> 6 Shards. Unwounded: every weapon blow critical, and 25% more mana from blows. After a wound, for 8 seconds or longer, you take 15% more damage. A blocked blow, a perfect guard or a perfect dodge is not a wound.


      <b>Works with.</b> Sharp Light, Weighed (critical blows 30% harder), Bowed Head, Clarity''s longer perfect moments, Measured Guard and Narrow Escape: every blow you turn keeps you clean.


      <b>Example.</b> Guard and dodge a duellist''s whole chain without a scratch, and every answer you give it lands critical.'
  - Id: light.weighed
    Title: Weighed
    Group: 
    Body: '<b>What it does.</b> Marks deepen, up to three. When an affliction on an enemy reaches its full depth, a mark at three among them, your critical blows strike harder for a while.


      <b>When it happens.</b> Always on once learned. The deeper marks need Light to be your first element; with Light second, a mark stays one deep. The harder critical comes each time any affliction you lay fills on an enemy.


      <b>The numbers.</b> 3 Shards. Marked up to three deep, each mark laid adding one. A full affliction makes critical blows deal 1.8 times their damage, where they deal 1.5, for 6 seconds.


      <b>Works with.</b> The root, Sentence (which needs three marks), Plain Guilt, Lasting Mark, Brimming and Two Suns (more marks laid), Unblemished and Just Cut (more critical blows to spend it on).


      <b>Example.</b> End three chains on a brute: it is three deep, and for six seconds every critical blow hits for 1.8 times.'
  - Id: light.sentence
    Title: Sentence
    Group: 
    Body: '<b>What it does.</b> A heavy blow on an enemy marked three deep passes sentence. Its marks are spent at once, and a moment later a blade of light falls on it, striking everything where it lands.


      <b>When it happens.</b> A heavy blow or finisher that lands on an enemy carrying Marked at full depth: three, with Weighed and Light as your first element; with Light second, any mark will do.


      <b>The numbers.</b> 3 Shards. The blade falls 0.8 seconds later, warned by a ring, 1.8 metres in radius: 36 damage and 45 stagger. At most once a second.


      <b>Works with.</b> Weighed, the root, Ring of Spears and Brimming to lay the marks fast, Bowed Head (the heavy blow itself is critical), and finishers: a finisher that passes sentence lands the blade on a kneeling enemy.


      <b>Example.</b> Mark a captain three deep, land a heavy blow, and step back as the blade falls on it and the soldier at its side.'
  - Id: light.spears
    Title: Ring of Spears
    Group: 
    Body: '<b>What it does.</b> Six spears of light stand in the air round the enemy you face, wait a breath, and drive in together, Marking it.


      <b>When it happens.</b> From a spell slot: cast it with that slot''s button (hold L2 and a face button, or 1 to 4). With no enemy faced they close on a spot ahead of you, and the slot still waits.


      <b>The numbers.</b> 4 Shards, no mana: it waits 10 seconds after a cast, less with weapon play. It finds an enemy within 10 metres. The ring is 3 metres in radius and closes after 0.6 seconds. Each spear deals 6 damage and 5 stagger and Marks: 36 damage and 30 stagger in all. As built the spears do not hold the enemy still while they wait.


      <b>Works with.</b> Sentence and Weighed (each spear lays a mark), Returning Light and Two Suns (six spell hits), Heavy Verdict, Hard Light, and the charged blade, which it charges with Light.


      <b>Example.</b> Cast on a brute, land your three critical blows while the spears are still closing, then a heavy blow for Sentence.'
  - Id: light.whatitowes
    Title: What It Owes
    Group: 
    Body: '<b>What it does.</b> An enemy that wounds you is Marked.


      <b>When it happens.</b> Each time a blow lands on you; the mark goes on the enemy that struck.


      <b>The numbers.</b> 3 Shards. One mark on the one who struck.


      <b>Works with.</b> The root (the next three blows you return are critical), Weighed and Sentence, Reckoning, and Unblemished''s price: a wound marks your answer.


      <b>Example.</b> A soldier''s spear catches you: it is Marked, and the three blows you give back are all critical.'
  - Id: light.reckoning
    Title: Reckoning
    Group: 
    Body: '<b>What it does.</b> You set a seal on the enemy you face. Each of your next six weapon blows on it sets off a burst of light round it that strikes and Marks everything near. With no enemy faced nothing is sealed and the slot still waits.


      <b>When it happens.</b> From a spell slot: cast it with that slot''s button (hold L2 and a face button, or 1 to 4). Then land weapon blows on that enemy. As built it is a burst with each blow; the seal that counts every wound and pays it back at once is still to come.


      <b>The numbers.</b> 4 Shards, no mana: it waits 12 seconds after a cast, less with weapon play. An enemy within 10 metres; the seal lasts 6 seconds or six bursts. Each burst is 2 metres in radius: 12 damage, 7 stagger and Marked.


      <b>Works with.</b> The root and Lasting Mark (each burst marks again after the blow that spent it), Weighed and Sentence, Heavy Verdict and Hard Light (the bursts are spells), Returning Light, Two Suns, Condemned.


      <b>Example.</b> Seal a captain in its guard and cut it six times: every burst marks it and the soldiers beside it, and every cut after the first lands critical.'
  - Id: light.condemned
    Title: Condemned
    Group: 
    Body: '<b>What it does.</b> When an affliction on an enemy reaches its full depth, its balance takes a great blow. The price: your weapon deals less to an enemy that carries nothing, though blows and spells on any afflicted enemy strike a little harder.


      <b>When it happens.</b> Always on once learned. The blow to balance comes each time any affliction you lay fills on an enemy, a third mark among them. As built it breaks balance; finishing a marked enemy below a quarter of its health as if it were staggered is still to come.


      <b>The numbers.</b> 6 Shards. A burst 1.2 metres round the enemy: no damage, 60 stagger, at most once every 4 seconds. Weapon damage 15% less; damage on an afflicted enemy 15% more, so against those the two nearly cancel.


      <b>Works with.</b> Weighed, Sentence, Reckoning and Ring of Spears to fill marks, and a second element''s affliction, which fills on its own.


      <b>Example.</b> Bring a brute''s mark to three: the burst all but staggers it, and a heavy blow finishes the work.'
  - Id: light.brimming
    Title: Brimming
    Group: 
    Body: '<b>What it does.</b> While your mana is full, every heavy blow throws a wave of light ahead of it that strikes and Marks everything in front of you.


      <b>When it happens.</b> Each heavy blow or finisher that lands while your mana bar is full.


      <b>The numbers.</b> 3 Shards. A cone 5 metres long and 70 degrees wide: 12 damage, 12 stagger and Marked.


      <b>Works with.</b> Gleaning (blows give 10% more mana), Rich Mark, Struck Flint and perfect guards to fill the bar, Weighed and Sentence, and the root. Spending mana on Daybreak or the surge ends it until the bar is full again.


      <b>Example.</b> Full of mana before a pack: every heavy blow marks the three in front of you.'
  - Id: light.returninglight
    Title: Returning Light
    Group: 
    Body: '<b>What it does.</b> A spell that strikes a Marked enemy gives you mana back.


      <b>When it happens.</b> Each time a spell from your slots strikes an enemy carrying Marked.


      <b>The numbers.</b> 3 Shards. 9 mana, at most once a second.


      <b>Works with.</b> Glare and Ring of Spears (cast on a marked enemy), Standing Light (its glow marks, then strikes again), Reckoning, Two Suns. Basic spells cost no mana now, so the mana goes to Daybreak, Clarity or a deep strike.


      <b>Example.</b> Mark a soldier with a chain, then Glare it: 9 mana back toward your Daybreak.'
  - Id: light.lantern
    Title: Standing Light
    Group: 
    Body: '<b>What it does.</b> You plant a lantern of light a little ahead of you. Enemies in its glow are struck lightly and Marked again and again while it stands.


      <b>When it happens.</b> From a spell slot: cast it with that slot''s button (hold L2 and a face button, or 1 to 4).


      <b>The numbers.</b> 4 Shards, no mana: it waits 12 seconds after a cast, less with weapon play. Planted 2.5 metres ahead; the glow is 5 metres in radius and lasts 10 seconds. It strikes 0.2 seconds after planting and then every 2.5 seconds: 2 damage and Marked each time. As built a perfect guard inside the glow does nothing more.


      <b>Works with.</b> The root (a fresh mark, and three fresh critical blows, every 2.5 seconds), Returning Light and Two Suns (each strike is a spell hit), Weighed and Sentence, Condemned.


      <b>Example.</b> Plant it in a doorway and fight on its edge: everything that comes through arrives Marked, and is Marked again as you spend it.'
  - Id: light.daybreak
    Title: Daybreak
    Group: 
    Body: '<b>What it does.</b> You brace and loose a beam of light down one long line. It bites everything in it four times and Marks it. The stick, or the cursor, turns it slowly while it burns.


      <b>When it happens.</b> From a spell slot: cast it with that slot''s button (hold L2 and a face button, or 1 to 4). As built the beam is loosed at once; gathering it blow by blow before you loose it is still to come.


      <b>The numbers.</b> 4 Shards, 45 mana. A 0.3-second brace, then a beam 12 metres long and 1.6 metres wide for 0.4 seconds. It bites every 0.1 seconds: 12 damage, 9 stagger and Marked each time, 48 damage on what stays in it.


      <b>Works with.</b> Long Rays (25% further), Hard Light and Heavy Verdict, Returning Light, Two Suns, Weighed and Sentence, and the charged blade, which it charges with Light.


      <b>Example.</b> A line of spearmen coming up a stair: one beam down the stair marks them all and leaves them reeling.'
  - Id: light.twosuns
    Title: Two Suns
    Group: 
    Body: '<b>What it does.</b> Each enemy your spells strike is struck again by a burst of light a moment later, and Marked. The price: spells paid in mana cost a quarter more.


      <b>When it happens.</b> Always on once learned: each time a spell from your slots strikes an enemy. As built it is a burst on each enemy struck; the second casting of your spell from the far side is still to come.


      <b>The numbers.</b> 6 Shards. A burst 2.5 metres in radius on the enemy struck, 0.4 seconds later: 12 damage, 10 stagger and Marked; at most five times a second. Daybreak costs 56 mana where it cost 45. Spells on a cooldown still cost nothing.


      <b>Works with.</b> Ring of Spears, Reckoning, Standing Light, Daybreak and Glare, Weighed and Sentence, Condemned.


      <b>Example.</b> Glare a pack: the ray strikes three, and a burst follows on each, marking the ones beside them too.'
  - Id: light.scales
    Title: The Scales
    Group: 
    Body: '<b>What it does.</b> While your surge lasts, the wounds you deal with your weapon and the wounds you take are weighed. If yours are the heavier when it ends, a sword of light falls on every Marked enemy near you. If not, the light leaves you, and your mana with it.


      <b>When it happens.</b> Light your surge with the surge button (Clarity, or the other element''s surge if you wear that); the scales are read when it ends.


      <b>The numbers.</b> A god''s gift, never sold; in the playtest it can be bought. Each sword deals 60% of how much more you dealt than you took, 120 at most, with 80 stagger, as a heavy blow, to each Marked enemy within 12 metres. Taken more than you dealt, or as much: your mana empties.


      <b>Works with.</b> Clarity (it marks with every blow and makes the perfect moments half again as long, so you take less), Unblemished, the root, Standing Light and Brimming to have them Marked when it ends.


      <b>Example.</b> Light Clarity, guard and cut for eight seconds without being touched: 200 dealt to none taken, and a sword falls for 120 on every Marked enemy.'
  - Id: lightning.static
    Title: Static
    Group: 
    Body: '<b>What it does.</b> Light blows build Static on an enemy, a stack at a time, up to five. Static does nothing by itself: a heavy blow or a finisher discharges it all at once, into the one struck and everyone standing near it.


      <b>When it happens.</b> Always on once learned. While Lightning is your first element, every light blow that lands adds a stack. Carried as the second element, the weapon lays none; Static then comes from your Lightning spells, the charged blade and the R2 strike. Either way, a heavy blow or a finisher on an enemy carrying Static discharges it.


      <b>The numbers.</b> 2 Shards. One stack a light blow, five at most, lasting 6 seconds. A discharge deals 7 damage and 5 stagger for each stack to everything within 4 metres: 35 damage and 25 stagger at five.


      <b>Works with.</b> Single Stroke, Waiting Thunder, Chain Lance, Seven Flashes, Overdrive''s quicker swings, and Arc Fire or Thunder Lift on the mixed branches.


      <b>Example.</b> Four light blows on a soldier, then a heavy: 28 damage leaps out of it into the two beside it as well.'
  - Id: lightning.lift
    Title: Strikes Twice
    Group: 
    Body: '<b>What it does.</b> Strikes Twice: every reaction with Static in it strikes again half a second later where it happened, as lightning comes back down its own channel.


      <b>When it happens.</b> Whenever Static reacts on an enemy with the other affliction it carries (Flashover with Burn and the rest).


      <b>The numbers.</b> 3 Shards. Half a second after the reaction, a bolt in 2 metres round the enemy: 10 damage, 10 stagger and a stack of Static.


      <b>Works with.</b> Carrying a second element: every reaction of Lightning''s ten. Chain Lance and Waiting Thunder, which grow from it.


      <b>Not built yet.</b> The reaction itself striking again at half strength: for now a bolt falls there.


      <b>Example.</b> Burn and Static meet on a soldier: Flashover goes, and a breath later the bolt follows it down.'
  - Id: lightning.lance
    Title: Chain Lance
    Group: 
    Body: '<b>What it does.</b> You throw a bolt ahead that leaps through up to five enemies, leaving Static on each.


      <b>When it happens.</b> From a spell slot: cast it with that slot''s button (hold L2 and a face button, or 1 to 4).


      <b>The numbers.</b> 4 Shards, no mana: it waits 7 seconds after a cast (its Empower: 5.5, and six leaps). Reaches 12 metres to the first enemy, then leaps up to 5 metres from one to the next. 10 damage, 15 stagger and two stacks of Static to each.


      <b>Works with.</b> Strikes Twice, which it grows from; Static; Waiting Thunder''s heavy that discharges what it laid.


      <b>Example.</b> Open on a pack of five archers from range: each takes two Static before they draw.'
  - Id: lightning.lance.shape
    Title: 'Chain Lance: Stepped Leader or Return Stroke'
    Group: 
    Body: '<b>What it does.</b> Opens two shapes of Chain Lance, chosen at any rest fire. <b>Stepped Leader</b>: the lance is not thrown; a bolt steps out along the ground one bright step at a time, laying Static on what is near, then the return stroke lights the whole path at once. <b>Return Stroke</b>: after its last leap it comes back along the same path, striking each enemy again for half.


      <b>When it happens.</b> Whenever you cast Chain Lance, as the shape it wears.


      <b>The numbers.</b> 3 Shards. Stepped Leader: up to 12 metres, a step every 0.15 seconds, 4 damage and a Static on each step; 1.2 seconds after the cast the return stroke strikes the whole path, 14 damage, 10 stagger and a Static. Return Stroke: 5 damage and 5 stagger again on each enemy struck, 0.6 seconds later.


      <b>Works with.</b> Static and Single Stroke (the return stroke''s Static, then a heavy).


      <b>Not built yet.</b> Steering Stepped Leader with the stick while you fight, the heavy blow calling the return stroke, and Return Stroke charging the blade for five blows.


      <b>Example.</b> Stepped Leader down a corridor of soldiers: they all carry Static when the return stroke lights.'
  - Id: lightning.lance.master
    Title: 'Chain Lance: Mastered'
    Group: 
    Body: '<b>What it does.</b> Thrown within half a second after a finisher, Chain Lance leaps to every enemy within twelve metres.


      <b>When it happens.</b> A finisher lands. Chain Lance must be in a slot.


      <b>The numbers.</b> 3 Shards. For now the finisher itself throws the arc: 10 damage, 10 stagger and two Static, leaping to eight enemies within 12 metres, once every 7 seconds.


      <b>Works with.</b> Static, Waiting Thunder.


      <b>Not built yet.</b> Only when the lance is thrown within half a second of the finisher.


      <b>Example.</b> End a chain on the captain and every soldier in the yard carries Static.'
  - Id: lightning.waiting
    Title: Waiting Thunder
    Group: 
    Body: '<b>What it does.</b> Five bolts hang at your shoulder, crackling. Each light blow you land sends one down onto the enemy struck. A heavy blow sends every one that is left. Those not sent when the time runs out go out.


      <b>When it happens.</b> From a spell slot: cast it with that slot''s button (hold L2 and a face button, or 1 to 4). Then your blows send the bolts.


      <b>The numbers.</b> 4 Shards, no mana: it waits 10 seconds after a cast (its Empower: 8, and seven bolts). Five bolts, for 10 seconds. Each deals 8 damage and 6 stagger and lays one stack of Static.


      <b>Works with.</b> Strikes Twice, which it grows from; Static (the bolts build it as you cut); Single Stroke.


      <b>Example.</b> Cast, land two light blows, then a heavy: the last three bolts fall with it and the heavy discharges what they laid.'
  - Id: lightning.waiting.shape
    Title: 'Waiting Thunder: Hanging Cloud or Hammer Fall'
    Group: 
    Body: '<b>What it does.</b> Opens two shapes of Waiting Thunder, chosen at any rest fire. <b>Hanging Cloud</b>: the bolts hang in a small black cloud over the enemy faced and fall on it while you fight. <b>Hammer Fall</b>: light blows send nothing; your heavy blow brings all of it as one bolt.


      <b>When it happens.</b> Whenever you cast Waiting Thunder, as the shape it wears.


      <b>The numbers.</b> 3 Shards. Hanging Cloud: over the enemy faced within 8 metres, a bolt every 0.9 seconds in 1.5 metres for 10 seconds, 8 damage, 6 stagger and a Static each. Hammer Fall: the enemy faced is marked for 10 seconds, and your next blow on it brings one bolt in 3 metres, 40 damage, 60 stagger and two Static.


      <b>Works with.</b> Static and Single Stroke (Hammer Fall into a heavy that discharges).


      <b>Not built yet.</b> Hanging Cloud''s bolts falling as you strike anyone (for now they fall by themselves), and Hammer Fall waiting for a heavy blow only.


      <b>Example.</b> Hang the cloud over the archer and fight the soldier beside you.'
  - Id: lightning.waiting.master
    Title: 'Waiting Thunder: Mastered'
    Group: 
    Body: '<b>What it does.</b> Land the heavy blow within a second of the last bolt falling with a light blow, and all five come back for a second round.


      <b>When it happens.</b> A heavy blow lands. Waiting Thunder must be in a slot.


      <b>The numbers.</b> 3 Shards. For now every heavy blow brings five bolts down round the enemy struck, 8 damage, 6 stagger and a Static each, once every 10 seconds.


      <b>Works with.</b> Static, Single Stroke.


      <b>Not built yet.</b> Only within a second of the last bolt falling with a light blow.


      <b>Example.</b> Light, light, light, light, light, heavy: and the sky goes round again.'
  - Id: lightning.devotion
    Title: In One Breath
    Group: 
    Body: '<b>What it does.</b> In One Breath, Lightning''s Devotion: all in on Lightning only. After a perfect guard or a perfect dodge, your spells have no cooldown for a breath. Cast everything you hold in it; then the cooldowns start from full.


      <b>When it happens.</b> Only while Lightning is carried twice (all in). Every perfect guard and perfect dodge.


      <b>The numbers.</b> 6 Shards. For now a perfect guard or dodge ends every running cooldown at once. All in, L2 with R2 is the deep strike, Down the Channel.


      <b>Works with.</b> Ring of Drums and Thunderclap''s Master, which also live on the perfect guard.


      <b>Not built yet.</b> No cooldown at all for 2.5 seconds after the perfect guard or dodge (the first rule switch, in the next task).


      <b>Example.</b> Wait for the brute''s swing, guard it perfectly, and spend the whole Hand on it.'
  - Id: lightning.charge
    Title: Stored Charge
    Group: 
    Body: '<b>What it does.</b> Perfect guards bank charges, up to three. Each blow you land spends one for double damage and double stagger.


      <b>When it happens.</b> A perfect guard (press the guard button just before a blow lands) banks one; your next weapon blow that lands spends it, and the next charge is ready for the blow after.


      <b>The numbers.</b> 3 Shards. Three charges at most, shown on the HUD. A charged blow deals twice its damage and twice its stagger.


      <b>Works with.</b> Ring of Drums and Thunderclap''s Master on the same perfect guard; a heavy blow that also discharges Static; Single Stroke.


      <b>Example.</b> Perfect-guard three blows of a duellist''s chain, then answer with three doubled blows.'
  - Id: lightning.base
    Title: Thunderclap
    Group: 
    Body: '<b>What it does.</b> Thunderclap, Lightning''s own spell, comes with the element and is never bought. A bolt falls on the enemy you face and forks to two more.


      <b>When it happens.</b> From a spell slot: cast it with that slot''s button. Carrying Lightning, it is always yours to put in a slot.


      <b>The numbers.</b> Given with Lightning. No mana: it waits 9 seconds after a cast (its Empower: 7). Up to 10 metres: 16 damage and 45 stagger, forking to two more. It lays no Static of its own.


      <b>Works with.</b> Static (a heavy right after discharges what is there); its Master on a perfect guard; Stored Charge.


      <b>Not built yet.</b> The Empower''s harder clap (55 stagger): the base spell is cast by Lightning''s kit, which takes only the Empower''s shorter wait.


      <b>Example.</b> A shield-bearer will not open: the clap breaks its balance, and your next blow lands.'
  - Id: lightning.base.shape
    Title: 'Thunderclap: Rolling Thunder or Held Thunder'
    Group: 
    Body: '<b>What it does.</b> Opens two shapes of Thunderclap, chosen at any rest fire. <b>Rolling Thunder</b>: three claps march out in a line. <b>Held Thunder</b>: one huge clap with no forks.


      <b>When it happens.</b> Whenever you cast Thunderclap, as the shape it wears.


      <b>The numbers.</b> 3 Shards. Rolling Thunder: three claps 3 metres apart over 9 metres, 16 damage, 30 stagger and a Static each. Held Thunder: one bolt on the enemy faced within 10 metres, 20 damage and 90 stagger, no forks.


      <b>Works with.</b> Static and Chain Lance (Rolling Thunder down a line); Stored Charge (Held Thunder, then a doubled blow).


      <b>Not built yet.</b> Held Thunder held on its button and growing with the hold: for now it is always the full hold.


      <b>Example.</b> Held Thunder on the captain staggers it outright.'
  - Id: lightning.base.master
    Title: 'Thunderclap: Mastered'
    Group: 
    Body: '<b>What it does.</b> A perfect guard makes the next Thunderclap instant and ends its wait.


      <b>When it happens.</b> A perfect guard. Thunderclap must be in a slot.


      <b>The numbers.</b> 3 Shards. Its cooldown ends at once, and the next cast starts none.


      <b>Works with.</b> Stored Charge and Ring of Drums on the same guard; In One Breath.


      <b>Not built yet.</b> The cast also losing its wind-up.


      <b>Example.</b> Guard the thrust perfectly and clap at once: guard, clap, guard, clap.'
  - Id: lightning.drums
    Title: Ring of Drums
    Group: 
    Body: '<b>What it does.</b> Three drums of cloud and lightning turn behind your shoulders. Each perfect guard or perfect dodge beats one, and a bolt falls on the attacker.


      <b>When it happens.</b> From a spell slot: cast it with that slot''s button, then each perfect guard or perfect dodge until the three drums are beaten.


      <b>The numbers.</b> 4 Shards, no mana: it waits 10 seconds (its Empower: 8). Three beats, each a bolt 1.2 metres round the enemy: 18 damage, 35 stagger and two Static. The drums are shown on the HUD as a count.


      <b>Works with.</b> Stored Charge, which it grows from; Thunderclap''s Master; In One Breath.


      <b>Not built yet.</b> The ring standing 8 seconds (for now the drums wait until beaten), and the third beat''s great clap in 4 metres (30 damage, 60 stagger) that discharges everything in it.


      <b>Example.</b> Cast it before the duellist''s chain: three perfect guards, three bolts on it.'
  - Id: lightning.drums.shape
    Title: 'Ring of Drums: Drum Roll or Silent Drum'
    Group: 
    Body: '<b>What it does.</b> Opens two shapes of Ring of Drums, chosen at any rest fire. <b>Drum Roll</b>: plain guards beat them too, for a small clap. <b>Silent Drum</b>: the beats are saved, and your next heavy blow carries them.


      <b>When it happens.</b> While Ring of Drums is in a slot: Drum Roll on every plain guard, Silent Drum on a heavy blow.


      <b>The numbers.</b> 3 Shards. Drum Roll: a clap 1.5 metres round the attacker, 8 damage, 15 stagger and a Static, at most every half second. Silent Drum: a heavy blow strikes 1.2 metres round its target for 18 more damage, 40 stagger and two Static, once every 3 seconds.


      <b>Works with.</b> Stored Charge (Silent Drum on the doubled heavy).


      <b>Not built yet.</b> A perfect guard beating two drums at once in Drum Roll; in Silent Drum, nothing falling on a beat and the heavy carrying exactly the beats banked.


      <b>Example.</b> Drum Roll for a player who guards rather than dodges.'
  - Id: lightning.drums.master
    Title: 'Ring of Drums: Mastered'
    Group: 
    Body: '<b>What it does.</b> Beat all three within three seconds and the ring stays for another round.


      <b>When it happens.</b> For now: a perfect dodge beats one more drum. Ring of Drums must be in a slot.


      <b>The numbers.</b> 3 Shards. One more bolt, 18 damage, 35 stagger and two Static, at most every 9 seconds.


      <b>Not built yet.</b> The three beats within 3 seconds keeping the ring.


      <b>Example.</b> Dodge, guard, guard: the ring goes round again.'
  - Id: lightning.stroke
    Title: Single Stroke
    Group: 
    Body: '<b>What it does.</b> Static builds to ten. A discharge no longer arcs to anyone else: all of it lands on the one struck, twice as hard.


      <b>When it happens.</b> Always on once learned, while you hold Lightning.


      <b>The numbers.</b> 6 Shards. Static up to ten stacks. A discharge deals 14 damage and 10 stagger for each stack to the one struck alone: 140 damage and 100 stagger at ten.


      <b>Works with.</b> Static, Waiting Thunder, Ring of Drums (which it grows from), Stored Charge (a charged heavy blow that also discharges).


      <b>Example.</b> Against the Gate Captain, keep cutting until it carries ten Static, then land one heavy blow for 140.'
  - Id: lightning.blink
    Title: Blink
    Group: 
    Body: '<b>What it does.</b> Each dodge sends a line of lightning down its path that shocks whatever it crosses.


      <b>When it happens.</b> Every dodge.


      <b>The numbers.</b> 3 Shards. The shock is 1.1 metres in radius and travels with you for the length of the dodge, striking each enemy once for 10 damage and 14 stagger.


      <b>Works with.</b> Afterimage, Lightning Rod, Never There, Storm Step.


      <b>Example.</b> Roll through a gap between two soldiers and both are shocked as you pass.'
  - Id: lightning.rod
    Title: Lightning Rod
    Group: 
    Body: '<b>What it does.</b> You plant a sword point-up a little ahead of you. For eight seconds bolts fall inside a circle round it, again and again, striking whatever stands there and laying Static.


      <b>When it happens.</b> From a spell slot: cast it with that slot''s button (hold L2 and a face button, or 1 to 4).


      <b>The numbers.</b> 4 Shards, no mana: it waits 10 seconds after a cast (its Empower: 8, and the circle reaches 4.5 metres). Planted 2 metres ahead; the circle is 3.5 metres in radius. It strikes 0.2 seconds after planting and then every 0.9 seconds for 8 seconds: 12 damage, 12 stagger and one stack of Static each time.


      <b>Works with.</b> Blink, which it grows from; Static (heavy blows on enemies inside discharge it).


      <b>Not built yet.</b> A second press while the rod stands stepping you to it in a flash, landing with a shock.


      <b>Example.</b> Plant it in a doorway and fight on its edge: everything that comes through it arrives already carrying Static.'
  - Id: lightning.rod.shape
    Title: 'Lightning Rod: Lodestone or Thrown Rod'
    Group: 
    Body: '<b>What it does.</b> Opens two shapes of Lightning Rod, chosen at any rest fire. <b>Lodestone</b>: the rod draws every enemy near in, further for each Static they carry, then discharges all of them. <b>Thrown Rod</b>: the rod is thrown far, into a distant enemy or the ground.


      <b>When it happens.</b> Whenever you cast Lightning Rod, as the shape it wears.


      <b>The numbers.</b> 3 Shards. Lodestone: everything within 7 metres drawn in, then a burst of 14 damage and 30 stagger that sets off all their Static. Thrown Rod: planted up to 10 metres away.


      <b>Works with.</b> Chain Lance and Waiting Thunder to lay the Static first (Lodestone).


      <b>Not built yet.</b> Lodestone pulling toward the rod (for now toward you), and the step to the rod that makes Thrown Rod worth its reach.


      <b>Example.</b> Lance a pack, then Lodestone: they come together and go off at once.'
  - Id: lightning.rod.master
    Title: 'Lightning Rod: Mastered'
    Group: 
    Body: '<b>What it does.</b> Cast in the instant a blow would land on you, Lightning Rod counts as a perfect dodge, and the rod is not spent by the step.


      <b>When it happens.</b> You cast Lightning Rod. Lightning Rod must be in a slot.


      <b>The numbers.</b> 3 Shards. For now every cast gives what a perfect dodge gives: 12 mana and 1.5 seconds off every running cooldown.


      <b>Not built yet.</b> The timing (cast as a blow would land) and the step that would spend the rod.


      <b>Example.</b> Plant the rod in the brute''s face as it swings.'
  - Id: lightning.afterimage
    Title: Afterimage
    Group: 
    Body: '<b>What it does.</b> A dodge at the last moment leaves a copy of you that strikes where you stood a moment later.


      <b>When it happens.</b> A perfect dodge: a blow passes through the very start of your roll.


      <b>The numbers.</b> 3 Shards. The strike lands 0.3 seconds later where your dodge began, 2.3 metres in radius: 26 damage and 28 stagger.


      <b>Works with.</b> Blink, Seven Flashes and Never There, which grow from it.


      <b>Example.</b> A brute''s overhead: roll through it at the last moment, and the copy left behind hits it as the blow lands.'
  - Id: lightning.flashes
    Title: Seven Flashes
    Group: 
    Body: '<b>What it does.</b> You vanish and cut from enemy to enemy in one breath, then stand again where you began with your back to the fight. The cuts land together once you are still, and any enemy left at full Static discharges. You cannot be struck while gone; if you are struck while standing still, the cuts land at half and nothing discharges.


      <b>When it happens.</b> From a spell slot: cast it with that slot''s button (hold L2 and a face button, or 1 to 4).


      <b>The numbers.</b> 4 Shards, 45 mana (its Empower: 35, and 11 a cut). Seven cuts among enemies within 8 metres (against one enemy, seven from all sides), 0.1 seconds apart, then half a second still. Each cut deals 9 damage, 8 stagger and one stack of Static. A full enemy discharges for 7 damage and 5 stagger a stack within 4 metres.


      <b>Works with.</b> Afterimage, which it grows from; Static; Never There.


      <b>Example.</b> Against one duellist at three Static: seven cuts bring it to full and it discharges as you turn.'
  - Id: lightning.flashes.shape
    Title: 'Seven Flashes: One Flash or Left Behind'
    Group: 
    Body: '<b>What it does.</b> Opens two shapes of Seven Flashes, chosen at any rest fire. <b>One Flash</b>: against the enemy faced only, its Static discharged again. <b>Left Behind</b>: you do not stand still so long, ending in the crowd.


      <b>When it happens.</b> Whenever you cast Seven Flashes, as the shape it wears.


      <b>The numbers.</b> 3 Shards. One Flash: the cuts reach only 3 metres, and each that lands on Static sets it off for 4 damage a stack, at most every half second. Left Behind: the still moment after is a tenth of a second.


      <b>Works with.</b> Static, Single Stroke (One Flash on the one carrying ten).


      <b>Not built yet.</b> One Flash''s seven cuts on one line as one blow, and Left Behind ending behind the last enemy with a shape of light left to be struck.


      <b>Example.</b> One Flash on the duellist who carries five Static.'
  - Id: lightning.flashes.master
    Title: 'Seven Flashes: Mastered'
    Group: 
    Body: '<b>What it does.</b> Cast within a third of a second of a perfect dodge, and you do not stand still afterwards: the cuts land at once.


      <b>When it happens.</b> Not yet: see below.


      <b>The numbers.</b> 3 Shards.


      <b>Not built yet.</b> All of it: it needs a cast''s window after a perfect dodge and a Seven Flashes without its still moment. Buying it now does nothing.'
  - Id: lightning.neverthere
    Title: Never There
    Group: 
    Body: '<b>What it does.</b> Every dodge carries you further and a perfect dodge costs nothing. The price: a blow held on your guard costs twice the stamina.


      <b>When it happens.</b> Always on once learned. The free dodge comes with each perfect dodge; the price with each blow you block.


      <b>The numbers.</b> 6 Shards. Dodges go 30% further. A perfect dodge gives back 25 stamina, the dodge''s usual cost. A blocked blow costs twice the stamina for each point caught.


      <b>Works with.</b> Blink, Afterimage (which it grows from), Seven Flashes, Lightning Rod.


      <b>Example.</b> Fight a fast duellist by dodging every swing at the last moment and never raising your guard.'
  - Id: lightning.stormstep
    Title: Storm Step
    Group: 
    Body: '<b>What it does.</b> While Overdrive lasts, every dodge costs nothing and shocks what it passes through, whether or not you learned Blink. A shape of light is left where you stood.


      <b>When it happens.</b> Every dodge while Overdrive, lit with the surge button, is running.


      <b>The numbers.</b> A god''s gift, never sold; in the playtest it can be bought. Each dodge gives back its whole stamina cost. The shock is Blink''s: 10 damage and 14 stagger, 1.1 metres in radius along the dodge.


      <b>Works with.</b> Blink, Afterimage, Never There.


      <b>Example.</b> Light Overdrive in a crowd and roll back and forth through them: no stamina spent, and every pass shocks.'
  - Id: metal.sunder
    Title: Sunder
    Group: 
    Body: '<b>What it does.</b> Heavy blows and perfect guards notch an enemy''s armour, and a finisher notches it three deep at once. Each notch is a stack of Sundered, and each lets your weapon bite deeper.


      <b>When it happens.</b> Always on once learned: every heavy blow that lands, every perfect guard (on the one who struck), every finisher. Light blows notch nothing. A weapon blow lays only your first element''s affliction, so the heavy blow''s and the finisher''s notches come only while Metal is your first element (or your only one); the perfect guard''s notch comes either way.


      <b>The numbers.</b> 2 Shards. One notch a heavy blow or perfect guard, three for a finisher, three at most. Sundered lasts 8 seconds; each notch adds 8% to your weapon''s damage on that enemy, 24% at three. Spells are not made stronger by it.


      <b>Works with.</b> Deep Bite (each notch bites 25% harder), Slow Mending (notches last half again as long), Splinter, Buried Blades, Shatter Point, Counter Cut and critical blows (they multiply each other), Temper (one more notch every blow), Flung Blade, and Live Iron when Static meets the notches.


      <b>Example.</b> Two heavy blows on a shield-bearer and its armour is two deep: every cut after lands 16% harder for the next 8 seconds.'
  - Id: metal.forgedanswer
    Title: Forged Answer
    Group: 
    Body: '<b>What it does.</b> Each perfect guard forges a blade from the blow you turned, and it hangs at your shoulder. Up to three wait there. Your next heavy blow that lands sends every one of them at the enemy it struck.


      <b>When it happens.</b> A perfect guard forges one; the next heavy blow that lands looses all that hang. The count shows on the screen as Blades.


      <b>The numbers.</b> 3 Shards. Three blades at most. Each flies at 16 metres a second, turning after the enemy, and strikes for 10 damage and 12 stagger. As built the blades lay no notch of their own.


      <b>Works with.</b> Sunder (the heavy blow that sends them notches as well), Practised Wrist and Edge Guard (easier perfect guards), Bright Sparks, Open Line, Buried Blades on the same heavy blow.


      <b>Example.</b> Perfect-guard a duellist''s three-blow flurry, then answer with one heavy blow: three blades follow it in for 30 more damage and 36 stagger.'
  - Id: metal.openline
    Title: Open Line
    Group: 
    Body: '<b>What it does.</b> A perfect guard throws the attacker''s weapon wide. It is held still for a moment, and for a breath after the guard your weapon strikes harder.


      <b>When it happens.</b> Every perfect guard: press the guard button just before a blow lands.


      <b>The numbers.</b> 3 Shards. The attacker is held for 1.2 seconds (elites for less; what cannot be frozen, not at all). Your weapon deals 15% more damage for 1.5 seconds after the guard, on any enemy. As built the hold is the whole of it: blows on the held enemy do not count as from behind.


      <b>Works with.</b> Sunder (a notch with the same guard), Forged Answer, Hard Return, Braced Frame, Counter Cut, Master''s Answer (the free skill comes in the same breath).


      <b>Example.</b> Perfect-guard a brute''s swing and it stands frozen with its arm thrown wide: a heavy blow lands before it can move.'
  - Id: metal.circle
    Title: Circle of Steel
    Group: 
    Body: '<b>What it does.</b> You stand with your blade raised for a breath. The first blow that reaches you, from any side, red attack or not, is turned for nothing and answered with a cut all round you that notches everything near. If nothing comes, the stance goes out and the cast is spent all the same. A dodge lets it go.


      <b>When it happens.</b> From a spell slot: cast it with that slot''s button (hold L2 and a face button, or 1 to 4), then any blow in the next 1.2 seconds.


      <b>The numbers.</b> 4 Shards, no mana: it waits 10 seconds after a cast, less with weapon play. Ready for 1.2 seconds. The answer strikes everything within 3.5 metres, all the way round, for 18 damage and 40 stagger, a heavy blow, and one notch of Sundered. As built the caught blow is not a perfect guard for your marks: it gives no mana and sets off nothing that waits on one.


      <b>Works with.</b> Sunder, Splinter (the notches it lays), Buried Blades, the charged blade (the answer is a spell, so it charges your weapon with Metal), Long Temper.


      <b>Example.</b> Ringed by three soldiers, cast it as the first lunges: the cut turns all three and notches each.'
  - Id: metal.edgeguard
    Title: Edge Guard
    Group: 
    Body: '<b>What it does.</b> The perfect guard''s moment is half again as long, and every perfect guard cuts the attacker and notches its armour. The price: the dodge and every blow held on a plain guard cost half again as much stamina.


      <b>When it happens.</b> Always on once learned: the cut comes with every perfect guard, the price with every dodge and every blocked blow.


      <b>The numbers.</b> 6 Shards. The perfect moment grows by 55%, from 0.18 seconds to about 0.28. Each perfect guard strikes everything within 1.2 metres of the attacker for 12 damage and 10 stagger, with one notch of Sundered. A dodge costs 37.5 stamina where it cost 25; a blocked blow costs 1.35 stamina a point of damage where it cost 0.9. As built a held guard still blocks as usual.


      <b>Works with.</b> Sunder (two notches from one guard), Forged Answer, Open Line, Practised Wrist, Master''s Answer, Hanging Swords, Bright Steel and Halo of Blades on the Halo branch.


      <b>Example.</b> Fight a fast duellist with the guard button alone: each of its blows met at the moment is turned, cut and notched.'
  - Id: metal.countercut
    Title: Counter Cut
    Group: 
    Body: '<b>What it does.</b> A blow that lands while an enemy is showing its own attack, winding up or swinging, is critical.


      <b>When it happens.</b> Always on once learned: any weapon blow that lands on an enemy in the middle of its attack, or holding you.


      <b>The numbers.</b> 3 Shards. A critical blow deals one and a half times its damage. The design''s extra stagger is not in it yet.


      <b>Works with.</b> Sunder (a critical blow and Sundered multiply each other), Clean Edge (critical blows 15% harder), Finishing Edge, Halo of Blades on the Halo branch (each critical blow forges a blade).


      <b>Example.</b> A brute raises its hammer: step in and land a heavy blow before it falls, for one and a half times the damage.'
  - Id: metal.splinter
    Title: Splinter
    Group: 
    Body: '<b>What it does.</b> A blow on armour notched three deep throws splinters from you through it, and they cut and notch whoever stands behind.


      <b>When it happens.</b> Any weapon blow that lands on an enemy carrying three notches of Sundered. As built the splinters fly from you through the one struck, not out of its back.


      <b>The numbers.</b> 3 Shards. A cone 5 metres long and 60 degrees wide toward the one struck: 8 damage, 8 stagger and one notch of Sundered to everything in it. At most once every 0.6 seconds.


      <b>Works with.</b> Sunder, Shatter Point (a finisher notches three deep at once), Circle of Steel, Slow Mending, Deep Bite.


      <b>Example.</b> Notch the front shield-bearer to three and keep cutting it: each cut sprays splinters into the line behind it.'
  - Id: metal.shatterpoint
    Title: Shatter Point
    Group: 
    Body: '<b>What it does.</b> A finisher on notched armour strikes a second time, and notches it three deep.


      <b>When it happens.</b> Every finisher (a heavy blow on a staggered enemy) on an enemy carrying Sundered.


      <b>The numbers.</b> 3 Shards. The second strike is 20 damage, no stagger, to everything within 1.2 metres of the one finished. Three notches of Sundered on it, which Sunder''s finisher already lays; like Sunder''s, they come only while Metal is your first element.


      <b>Works with.</b> Sunder, Splinter, Buried Blades, Slow Mending, Counter Cut.


      <b>Example.</b> Stagger a notched brute and finish it: the finisher lands, then the armour breaks again for 20 more.'
  - Id: metal.hone
    Title: Hone
    Group: 
    Body: '<b>What it does.</b> You set a sign on the enemy you face. Each of your next five weapon blows on it sets off a small burst round it that notches. With no enemy faced nothing is set and the cast is spent.


      <b>When it happens.</b> From a spell slot: cast it with that slot''s button (hold L2 and a face button, or 1 to 4). Then any weapon blow that lands on that enemy, light or heavy.


      <b>The numbers.</b> 4 Shards, no mana: it waits 9 seconds after a cast, less with weapon play. An enemy within 8 metres; the sign lasts 12 seconds or five bursts. Each burst is 1.5 metres in radius: 6 damage, 6 stagger and one notch of Sundered. As built it is a sign on the enemy, not a whetted edge on your blade.


      <b>Works with.</b> Sunder (the burst notches with light blows as well), Splinter, the charged blade (the first burst charges your weapon with Metal), Balanced Blade, quick weapons.


      <b>Example.</b> Sign the shield-bearer and land five quick light blows: it is three deep before your heavy blow.'
  - Id: metal.mastersanswer
    Title: Master's Answer
    Group: 
    Body: '<b>What it does.</b> For two seconds after a perfect guard your weapon''s skill costs no mana and comes at once, with no time to charge. At any other time it costs half again as much.


      <b>When it happens.</b> Always on once learned. A perfect guard opens the two seconds; press the skill then.


      <b>The numbers.</b> 6 Shards. Two seconds of a free skill that needs no charging; outside them the skill costs 1.5 times its mana.


      <b>Works with.</b> Open Line (the attacker is still held when the skill lands), Edge Guard, Practised Wrist, Bright Sparks, Forged Answer, and on the Katana the Iaido Slash and Answering Draw.


      <b>Example.</b> With the Katana, perfect-guard a thrust and the Iaido Slash leaves the sheath at once, free.'
  - Id: metal.buriedblades
    Title: Buried Blades
    Group: 
    Body: '<b>What it does.</b> A heavy blow on notched armour strikes a second time, harder, and notches it again.


      <b>When it happens.</b> A heavy blow that lands on an enemy carrying Sundered, once a second at most.


      <b>The numbers.</b> 3 Shards. The second strike is 24 damage and 30 stagger to everything within 1.2 metres of the one struck, with one notch of Sundered. As built there are no blades left standing in the enemy: the second strike is the whole of it.


      <b>Works with.</b> Sunder (one heavy blow lays two notches), Forged Answer, Flung Blade, Splinter, Deep Bite.


      <b>Example.</b> A notched soldier takes one heavy blow and is struck again for 24, two notches deeper.'
  - Id: metal.ricochet
    Title: Ricochet
    Group: 
    Body: '<b>What it does.</b> When a spell of yours strikes an enemy, a blade goes through it and springs on to the next enemy near, and then the next, notching each.


      <b>When it happens.</b> Each time a spell of yours strikes an enemy, at most about three times a second.


      <b>The numbers.</b> 3 Shards. 9 damage, 6 stagger and one notch of Sundered to the one struck, then to two more, leaping up to 6 metres from one to the next.


      <b>Works with.</b> Flung Blade, Grave of Swords and Hone (spells that strike often), Returning Edge, Sun Wheels on the Halo branch, Sunder.


      <b>Example.</b> Flung Blade into the front of a pack: the blade springs on through two more and all three carry a notch.'
  - Id: metal.returningedge
    Title: Returning Edge
    Group: 
    Body: '<b>What it does.</b> A great head of steel forms at your shoulder and lunges down a line before you. It strikes what it passes and carries it along, and its jaws close hard where the line ends. As built it does not fly back to you.


      <b>When it happens.</b> From a spell slot: cast it with that slot''s button (hold L2 and a face button, or 1 to 4).


      <b>The numbers.</b> 4 Shards, no mana: it waits 9 seconds after a cast, less with weapon play. It forms for 0.3 seconds, then runs 8 metres down a lane 1.5 metres wide. Each enemy passed takes 12 damage, 10 stagger and a notch of Sundered and is pushed along. Where it ends the jaws strike 1.1 metres round for 24 damage and 20 stagger, a heavy blow, and a notch.


      <b>Works with.</b> Ricochet, Sunder, Long Throw (it runs further), True Flight, the charged blade (it charges your weapon with Metal).


      <b>Example.</b> Four soldiers come down a corridor: the head runs through them and drags them together at its end.'
  - Id: metal.graveofswords
    Title: Grave of Swords
    Group: 
    Body: '<b>What it does.</b> Twelve blades hang behind your shoulders. One after another they fly by themselves at the nearest enemy, and a heavy blow that lands sends all that remain at the one it struck.


      <b>When it happens.</b> From a spell slot: cast it with that slot''s button (hold L2 and a face button, or 1 to 4). It is Metal''s larger spell.


      <b>The numbers.</b> 4 Shards, 50 mana. Twelve blades for 12 seconds. The first flies 0.6 seconds after the cast, then one every 0.55 seconds at the nearest enemy within 6 metres. Each strikes for 9 damage, 6 stagger and one notch of Sundered. Those not flown when the time is up go out.


      <b>Works with.</b> Ricochet (each blade that strikes springs on), Sunder, Buried Blades and Forged Answer on the heavy blow that sends the rest, All Blades Home, True Flight.


      <b>Example.</b> Cast it in a pack and fight on: the blades keep three notches on whoever is nearest, and a heavy blow on the brute sends the last five into it.'
  - Id: metal.allbladeshome
    Title: All Blades Home
    Group: 
    Body: '<b>What it does.</b> Lighting Temper throws five blades out from you in a fan, and they come back to you, cutting and notching what they pass both ways. Temper costs more and lasts a little longer.


      <b>When it happens.</b> Each time you light Temper with the surge button. As built the blades are thrown out fresh; conjured blades do not wait to be called home.


      <b>The numbers.</b> 6 Shards. Five blades, 14 degrees apart, flying at 14 metres a second; they turn for home after 0.6 seconds. Each strikes each enemy once going and once coming: 12 damage, 8 stagger and one notch of Sundered. Temper costs 55 mana where it cost 40, and lasts 12 seconds where it lasted 10.


      <b>Works with.</b> Temper, Long Temper, Hanging Swords, Sunder.


      <b>Example.</b> Light Temper facing a line of archers: the fan goes through them and back, and each is two notches deep.'
  - Id: metal.hangingswords
    Title: Hanging Swords
    Group: 
    Body: '<b>What it does.</b> While Temper lasts, every blow you hold on your guard counts as a perfect guard, and a sword is forged over the one who struck, up to eight. Each sword hangs over its enemy and follows it. When Temper ends, they fall.


      <b>When it happens.</b> Light Temper with the surge button, then guard. The swords fall when Temper ends.


      <b>The numbers.</b> A god''s gift, never sold; in the playtest it can be bought. The perfect moment lasts the whole of Temper, as long as the guard is raised fresh. Each guard gives 5 mana more, at most about three times a second. Eight swords at most; they fall 0.3 seconds after Temper ends, 0.11 seconds apart, each striking 1.5 metres round for 16 damage, 20 stagger and a notch of Sundered.


      <b>Works with.</b> Temper (30% less damage taken, a notch more every blow), Long Temper, All Blades Home, Sunder, Forged Answer, Open Line, Edge Guard.


      <b>Example.</b> Light Temper and stand in the middle of a pack with your guard up: every blow turns, and when Temper ends eight swords come down on them.'
  - Id: overgrowth.rootgrip
    Title: Root Grip
    Group: 
    Body: '<b>What it does.</b> A heavy blow on an enemy that carries both Tremor and Seeded sends roots up its legs and holds it where it stands. Your heavy blows also lay Tremor and Seeded together, whichever of the two you carry first.


      <b>When it happens.</b> Every heavy blow or finisher that lands. The hold comes when the enemy already carries both, at most once every 3 seconds.


      <b>The numbers.</b> Mix, 3 Shards. A heavy blow lays one stack of Tremor and one of Seeded. Your first element''s own is not laid twice: once its root is learned, the root''s stack is the one a heavy blow lays. Held still for 1.2 seconds (elites and gods for less; a few great forms cannot be held).


      <b>Works with.</b> Seeded or Tremor, Briar Patch or Stone Rise for more of either, the charged blade, Living Rampart (its perfect guard lays Tremor), Ripening, The Ground Wakes.


      <b>Example.</b> Life first: a heavy blow seeds and shakes a brute, and the next one roots it for a light chain that mends you with every cut.'
  - Id: overgrowth.moss
    Title: Moss on Stone
    Group: 
    Body: '<b>What it does.</b> Stand your ground and the ground feeds you. While you fight without rolling, you mend slowly, and thorns grow on you that cut and seed whoever strikes you.


      <b>When it happens.</b> While you have not begun a dodge for 3 seconds. The mending comes every 3 seconds in a fight (an enemy within 12 metres); the thorns with each blow that lands on you, at most once a second.


      <b>The numbers.</b> Mix, 3 Shards. 2 health every 3 seconds. The thorns: 8 damage and one stack of Seeded, 1 metre round the attacker.


      <b>Works with.</b> Root Grip, Living Rampart (guard instead of rolling), Briar Coat, Seeded, Shade.


      <b>Example.</b> Hold a doorway with your guard and never roll: the soldiers that get a blow through are seeded for your answer.'
  - Id: overgrowth.briarpatch
    Title: Thorns Take Root
    Group: 
    Body: '<b>What it does.</b> The thorns of a Seeded enemy''s death take root where they fall. The patch shakes the ground and seeds whatever walks in it. Called Briar Patch until Life''s own spell, a mark now, took that name.


      <b>When it happens.</b> Whenever an enemy carrying Seeded dies, at most once a second.


      <b>The numbers.</b> Mix, 3 Shards. A patch 3 metres in radius for 6 seconds. Every second it bites for 3 damage and one stack of Seeded; every 2 seconds it lays a stack of Tremor, which slows by 10% a stack and stops balance draining.


      <b>Works with.</b> Seeded (its death burst comes first), Fallen Seeds (a thornbush in the same place), Root Grip (what walks through carries both), Living Rampart.


      <b>Example.</b> Kill a seeded soldier in the middle of the pack: the rest wade through briar, slowed and seeded, and their balance stops draining.'
  - Id: overgrowth.thornwall
    Title: Thorn Wall
    Group: 
    Body: '<b>What it does.</b> You raise a hedge of stone and briar before you. Nothing walks through it, and no blow from its far side reaches you. When its time is up, or sooner if you strike it with a heavy blow, it bursts into thorns.


      <b>When it happens.</b> From a spell slot: cast it with that slot''s button (hold L2 and a face button, or 1 to 4). Swing a heavy blow close to it to burst it early.


      <b>The numbers.</b> Mix, 4 Shards, no mana: it waits 12 seconds after a cast, less with weapon play. The hedge stands 2.5 metres ahead, 5 metres wide, rises 0.2 seconds after the cast and stands 8 seconds. The burst reaches 5 metres from its middle: 20 damage, 25 stagger and one stack of Seeded; burst by your heavy blow it is a heavy blow. One hedge at a time. As built, touching the hedge does not cut.


      <b>Works with.</b> Seeded, Ripening, Root Grip, Briar Patch, and the charged blade: its burst charges your weapon with Life.


      <b>Example.</b> Wall off the archers while you deal with the spearman, then burst it with a heavy blow as they come round.'
  - Id: overgrowth.stoneoak
    Title: Stone Oak
    Group: 
    Body: '<b>What it does.</b> You plant a stone oak a little ahead of you. For twenty seconds its roots strike everything in a wide circle round it, again and again, seeding what they strike.


      <b>When it happens.</b> From a spell slot: cast it with that slot''s button (hold L2 and a face button, or 1 to 4).


      <b>The numbers.</b> Mix, 5 Shards, 45 mana. Planted 2 metres ahead; the circle is 5 metres in radius. It first strikes half a second after planting, then every 2 seconds, for 20 seconds: 10 damage, 15 stagger and one stack of Seeded each time. As built it strikes as a grown tree from the start; it does not grow with blows, mend in its shade or block the way, and it is not one of your grown things for Shade or Reap What Is Sown.


      <b>Works with.</b> Seeded, Ripening, Root Grip, Paid in Blood, and the charged blade: its first strike charges your weapon with Life.


      <b>Example.</b> Plant it in the middle of a room and fight inside its circle: everything there is seeded every two seconds, and every cut mends you.'
  - Id: overgrowth.livingrampart
    Title: Living Rampart
    Group: 
    Body: '<b>What it does.</b> Your guard is alive. Every blow held on it mends you a little and seeds the one who struck. A perfect guard roots the attacker where it stands and shakes the ground under it. The price: guarding costs more stamina.


      <b>When it happens.</b> Each blow you block with a plain guard, and each perfect guard.


      <b>The numbers.</b> Mix, 5 Shards. A blocked blow: 2 health and one stack of Seeded on the attacker. A perfect guard: held still for 1 second (elites and gods for less) and two stacks of Tremor (one, with Earth first and its root learned). Blocking costs 15% more stamina.


      <b>Works with.</b> Moss on Stone, Root Grip (the perfect guard lays the Tremor it needs), Bitter Rind, Briar Coat, Green Wood.


      <b>Example.</b> Block a soldier''s three-blow chain: it is seeded, you are 6 health better off, and your answer mends you more.'
  - Id: overgrowth.groundwakes
    Title: The Ground Wakes
    Group: 
    Body: '<b>What it does.</b> When your surge begins, the ground rises round you in a ring of stone and root and holds every enemy inside it, shaken and seeded. Then it flowers: a burst, and you are mended for each one it held.


      <b>When it happens.</b> Each time you light the surge with the surge button, whichever element''s surge you wear.


      <b>The numbers.</b> A god''s gift, never sold; in the playtest it can be bought. Everything within 7 metres of you is held for 2 seconds (elites and gods for less) and takes three stacks of Tremor and one of Seeded. When the hold ends, everything within 7 metres takes 15 damage and 20 stagger, and you mend 5 for each enemy held.


      <b>Works with.</b> Regrowth or Bedrock, Root Grip, Seeded, Ripening, Living Rampart.


      <b>Example.</b> Light Regrowth with four soldiers round you: all four stand held and shaken for two seconds, then you mend 20.'
  - Id: plasma.embers
    Title: Charged Embers
    Group: 
    Body: '<b>What it does.</b> A heavy blow on an enemy carrying Static sets the Static off, as Lightning''s root would, whichever of the two is your first element. Your blows also lay Burn and Static together, whichever of the two you carry first: every blow a Burn, every light blow a Static. Once your first element''s root (Cinder or Static) is learned, that element''s own is the root''s, not laid twice.


      <b>When it happens.</b> A heavy blow or finisher on an enemy carrying Static sets it off. Every blow that lands lays a Burn, and every light blow a Static.


      <b>The numbers.</b> Mix, 3 Shards. Static set off deals 7 damage a stack to everything within 4 metres, with no stagger, at most about three times a second. One stack a blow of each; of your first element''s, none beyond its root''s.


      <b>Works with.</b> Thunderclap or Flame Wave in a slot (more of either), the charged blade and the R2 strike, Arc Fire, Twin Break, Meltdown, Chain Reaction, Plasma, and the Flashover reaction when Burn and Static meet.


      <b>Example.</b> Carrying Fire first and Lightning second: your light blows burn a soldier and leave it Static, and the heavy blow that ends your chain sets the Static off into the pack.'
  - Id: plasma.arcfire
    Title: Arc Fire
    Group: 
    Body: '<b>What it does.</b> A discharge of Static carries Burn to everyone it reaches. A burn set off leaves Static on everyone it reaches. Each element''s burst plants the other.


      <b>When it happens.</b> Whenever you set off Static (a heavy blow on Static, Conductor) or a burn (Burn and Detonate, Open Furnace, Plasma).


      <b>The numbers.</b> Mix, 3 Shards. A Static discharge lays two stacks of Burn on everything within 4 metres of the one set off. A burn set off lays two stacks of Static on everything within 3.2 metres.


      <b>Works with.</b> Charged Embers, Static, Burn and Detonate, Open Furnace, Plasma, Chain Reaction.


      <b>Example.</b> Discharge a full soldier in the middle of a pack: everyone near it is now burning two deep as well as shocked.'
  - Id: plasma.twin
    Title: Twin Break
    Group: 
    Body: '<b>What it does.</b> A perfect guard sets off Burn and Static together on the one who struck. Spent together they strike half again as hard, and the blow is heavy, so it stops the enemy where it stands. If it carries only one of the two, that one is set off alone.


      <b>When it happens.</b> A perfect guard (press the guard button just before a blow lands) against an enemy carrying Burn, Static, or both.


      <b>The numbers.</b> Mix, 4 Shards. Together: 10 damage a Burn stack and 7 a Static stack, times 1.5, with 5 stagger a stack: 127.5 damage and 50 stagger at five and five. Alone, in 3 metres: Burn 10 plus 15 a stack, Static 10.5 a stack, 5 stagger a stack.


      <b>Works with.</b> Charged Embers, Kiln Stance, Stored Charge, Meltdown. Burn and Detonate spends the burn first, so the two clash.


      <b>Example.</b> A burning, charged brute swings: guard it perfectly and it takes 127 and stops dead.'
  - Id: plasma.ionised
    Title: Ionised Air
    Group: 
    Body: '<b>What it does.</b> When any affliction on an enemy reaches its full depth, an arc leaps from that enemy through three more.


      <b>When it happens.</b> The moment an affliction on an enemy fills: five Burn, five Static, and so on.


      <b>The numbers.</b> Mix, 3 Shards. 10 damage and 8 stagger to the first and to each of three more, leaping up to 5 metres from one to the next. At most once a second.


      <b>Works with.</b> Charged Embers (two afflictions to fill), Cinder, Static, Fused Core.


      <b>Example.</b> Fill a soldier''s Burn in a crowd and the arc jumps through three of its friends.'
  - Id: plasma.chain
    Title: Chain Reaction
    Group: 
    Body: '<b>What it does.</b> An enemy that dies carrying both Burn and Static bursts, and passes both on to everyone near at the depth it carried them.


      <b>When it happens.</b> The moment an enemy carrying both dies.


      <b>The numbers.</b> Mix, 4 Shards. The burst is 4 metres in radius: 18 damage, and as many Burn stacks as the dead one had. Everyone within 4 metres also takes as many Static stacks as it had. At most a few times a second.


      <b>Works with.</b> Charged Embers, Arc Fire, Catching Fire, Meltdown.


      <b>Example.</b> Kill one soldier at five and five, and the three round it start at five and five too, one blow from Meltdown.'
  - Id: plasma.ball
    Title: Ball Lightning
    Group: 
    Body: '<b>What it does.</b> You loose a slow ball of white fire that drifts after the nearest enemy. Strike it with a swing to send it fast along the swing and grow it a step, up to three. It bursts on the first enemy it meets with Burn and Static, harder for each strike. Left alone, it bursts small when its time is up.


      <b>When it happens.</b> From a spell slot: cast it with that slot''s button (hold L2 and a face button, or 1 to 4), then swing at the ball.


      <b>The numbers.</b> Mix, 4 Shards, 40 mana. It appears 1.5 metres ahead and drifts at 2 metres a second for 8 seconds; batted, it flies at 9. Burst: 2.5 metres in radius, 16 damage and 20 stagger, two stacks of Burn and of Static; each strike adds 0.7 metres, 12 damage, 10 stagger and a stack of each. At three strikes: 52 damage, 50 stagger and a heavy blow.


      <b>Works with.</b> Charged Embers, Meltdown, Fused Core, Hot Coals.


      <b>Example.</b> Bat it three times into an archer: 52 damage, and all near are five deep in both.'
  - Id: plasma.fused
    Title: Fused Core
    Group: 
    Body: '<b>What it does.</b> Your spells hit harder, and every enemy a spell strikes is left with a burn and Static.


      <b>When it happens.</b> Always on once learned; the afflictions come each time a spell of yours strikes an enemy.


      <b>The numbers.</b> Mix, 4 Shards. Spells deal 15% more damage. One stack of Burn and one of Static on each enemy a spell strikes.


      <b>Works with.</b> Flame Wave, Thunderclap, Ball Lightning, Plasma Lance, Ionised Air, Conductor.


      <b>Example.</b> A Thunderclap that forks to three enemies leaves all three burning and charged.'
  - Id: plasma.meltdown
    Title: Meltdown
    Group: 
    Body: '<b>What it does.</b> An enemy near you carrying five Burn and five Static begins to shake with light. A few moments later it bursts, far harder than either alone, and the burst spends both. Nothing stops it, and it does not harm you.


      <b>When it happens.</b> Always on once learned. It looks a few times a second for an enemy within 14 metres at full depth in both; one enemy melts at a time.


      <b>The numbers.</b> Mix, 5 Shards. It shakes for 3 seconds, then bursts: 45 damage and 60 stagger to it as a heavy blow, and half of each to everything else within 5 metres. The same enemy cannot melt again for 10 seconds.


      <b>Works with.</b> Charged Embers, Chain Reaction, Ball Lightning, Fused Core, Twin Break.


      <b>Example.</b> Fill a brute with both and roll away: three seconds later it goes up and staggers the pack around it.'
  - Id: plasma.lance
    Title: Plasma Lance
    Group: 
    Body: '<b>What it does.</b> You throw a bolt of plasma at the enemy you face that leaps on through three more.


      <b>When it happens.</b> From a spell slot: cast it with that slot''s button (hold L2 and a face button, or 1 to 4).


      <b>The numbers.</b> Mix, 5 Shards, no mana: it waits 12 seconds after a cast, less with weapon play. Reaches 11 metres to the first enemy, then leaps up to 5 metres from one to the next, four enemies in all. 30 damage, 26 stagger and two stacks of Burn on each, whichever element is first: the branch''s spells are made of Fire, and one that lands charges the blade with Fire.


      <b>Works with.</b> Fused Core (both afflictions on each), Conductor, Ionised Air, Hot Coals.


      <b>Example.</b> Four soldiers in a loose line: one cast strikes all four for 30 each.'
  - Id: fire.plasma
    Title: Plasma
    Group: 
    Body: '<b>What it does.</b> A heavy blow or a finisher on a burning enemy bursts. The burst sets off the burn on everyone it reaches and then sets each of them alight again.


      <b>When it happens.</b> Every heavy blow or finisher that lands on a burning enemy.


      <b>The numbers.</b> A god''s gift, never sold; in the playtest it can be bought. The burst is 3.2 metres in radius: 18 damage and 16 stagger. Each enemy in it that was burning takes its burn set off as well, 10 damage and 10 more a stack, and every enemy in it burns for 4 seconds afterward.


      <b>Works with.</b> Cinder, Charged Embers, Arc Fire (each burst leaves Static), Heat, Kindle.


      <b>Example.</b> Three soldiers burning five deep: a heavy blow on one bursts over all three for 78 each, and leaves them burning.'
  - Id: poison.venom
    Title: Venom
    Group: 
    Body: '<b>What it does.</b> Your weapon poisons. Every blow that lands adds a dose, a heavy blow one more, a finisher more again. The poison does not tick quietly: on a slow beat it bites for all its doses at once.


      <b>When it happens.</b> Always on once learned, while Poison is your first element: your weapon lays only your first element''s affliction, so with Poison second this mark does nothing on blows, and its doses come from your spells, the charged blade and the R2 strike instead.


      <b>The numbers.</b> 2 Shards. One dose a blow; a heavy blow lays two, a finisher four. Up to eight doses, for 6 seconds, and each new dose starts the time again. Every 2 seconds the poison bites for 2 a dose: 16 at eight. Set off, it deals 6 a dose at once: 48 at eight.


      <b>Works with.</b> Rupture and Volatile to set it off, Catching to spread it, Left to Ripen and In Time on its beat, Deeper Dose (two doses deeper), Bitter Dose (20% harder bites), Fever (one more dose a blow), and Rot Roots when a Seeded enemy is poisoned.


      <b>Example.</b> Four light blows and a heavy leave a soldier six doses deep; roll away and the next bite takes 12 from it while you are clear.'
  - Id: poison.intime
    Title: In Time
    Group: 
    Body: '<b>What it does.</b> Strike as the poison bites and your blow doses twice. For a moment after that timed blow, every blow you land is critical.


      <b>When it happens.</b> A weapon blow that lands on a poisoned enemy within a quarter of a second of its poison biting, just before or just after. The extra dose comes only while Poison is your first element; the critical moment comes either way.


      <b>The numbers.</b> 3 Shards. One dose more on the timed blow. For 1.2 seconds after it, your blows are critical (one and a half times damage). As built the timed blow itself is not made critical, only the ones after it.


      <b>Works with.</b> Venom, One Sickness (every enemy bites on one beat, so the timing is the same for all), Lance the Wound (it makes the poison bite when you choose), a heavy blow or finisher in the critical moment, Coiled Strike.


      <b>Example.</b> Watch the bubbles: as they burst, land a light blow, then a heavy in the next breath, and the heavy lands critical.'
  - Id: poison.ripen
    Title: Left to Ripen
    Group: 
    Body: '<b>What it does.</b> Poison you leave alone ripens. Each bite that comes without a fresh dose since the last is stronger than the one before. Your afflictions also last longer.


      <b>When it happens.</b> Always on once learned. Any fresh dose, from a blow, a spell or a mark, starts the ripening over.


      <b>The numbers.</b> 3 Shards. Each ripe bite adds a quarter of the bite: the first bite after a dose is as usual, the next 25% stronger, then 50%, then 75%. Every affliction you lay lasts 34% longer, so poison 8 seconds where it lasted 6.


      <b>Works with.</b> Lingering and Still Air (longer still), Slow Death (the poison never fades, so it ripens without end), Bitter Dose, Lance the Wound. It works against Venom''s every blow, so dose deep, then step back and guard.


      <b>Example.</b> Put eight doses on a brute and stop hitting it: its four bites come for 16, 20, 24 and 28.'
  - Id: poison.lance
    Title: Lance the Wound
    Group: 
    Body: '<b>What it does.</b> A perfect guard makes the attacker''s poison bite at once, and the poison in every enemy near it with it. Each bites at its own depth.


      <b>When it happens.</b> A perfect guard: press the guard button just before a blow lands.


      <b>The numbers.</b> 3 Shards. Every poisoned enemy within 5 metres of the attacker bites in the next moment, as hard as its beat would. Its own beat goes on as before, so it can bite again soon after.


      <b>Works with.</b> Venom, Left to Ripen (a ripe bite called early), In Time (strike as it bites), Volatile (it still makes poison bite, though the beat is stilled), Catching (each bite throws a dose on), Waiting Game (more mana from perfect guards), Calm Pulse.


      <b>Example.</b> Three soldiers at eight doses press you: guard the first swing perfectly and all three take 16 at once, off their beat.'
  - Id: poison.coiled
    Title: Coiled Strike
    Group: 
    Body: '<b>What it does.</b> You step through the enemy you face in an instant and come out on its far side, facing back, cutting everything on the line and poisoning it deeply. If the cut lands, your next heavy blow soon after is critical. Nothing can strike you in the step; a wall, or something too big to shove, stops you short.


      <b>When it happens.</b> From a spell slot: cast it with that slot''s button (hold L2 and a face button, or 1 to 4).


      <b>The numbers.</b> 4 Shards, no mana: it waits 10 seconds after a cast, less with weapon play. It goes up to 6 metres, ending 1.8 metres past the enemy faced (with none, 4.5 metres ahead). The cut is 1.1 metres to each side of the line: 24 damage, 25 stagger and four doses. A heavy blow within 3 seconds is critical. As built it is the step alone: the hold that coils it through three fangs is not made yet.


      <b>Works with.</b> Venom, Rupture (four doses toward full), In Time, Blister, and the charged blade: if it lands it charges your weapon with Poison.


      <b>Example.</b> Step through a shield-bearer to its back, turn, and the heavy blow you owe it lands critical.'
  - Id: poison.slowdeath
    Title: Slow Death
    Group: 
    Body: '<b>What it does.</b> Your weapon wounds far less. Your poison goes far deeper, and it never fades while the one carrying it lives.


      <b>When it happens.</b> Always on once learned. The greater depth holds while Poison is your first element; the poison stops fading either way.


      <b>The numbers.</b> 6 Shards. Weapon damage 30% less. Poison holds twelve more doses, up to twenty (twenty-two with Deeper Dose): at twenty a bite deals 40 every 2 seconds, and set off it deals 120. Poison you lay does not run out.


      <b>Works with.</b> Venom, Left to Ripen (it ripens without end), Catching, One Sickness, Volatile (it fills at twenty), Rupture (full is twenty now), Plague Bearer, Clean Blade.


      <b>Example.</b> Dose a Gate Captain twenty deep and spend the rest of the fight guarding: 40 every two seconds, and it never wears off.'
  - Id: poison.rupture
    Title: Rupture
    Group: 
    Body: '<b>What it does.</b> A heavy blow on an enemy poisoned to its full depth bursts the poison. All of it lands at once, on it and everyone close to it, and the doses are spent.


      <b>When it happens.</b> A heavy blow or finisher that lands on an enemy carrying a full dose of poison.


      <b>The numbers.</b> 3 Shards. Set off for 6 damage a dose, 48 at eight, with 4 stagger a dose, to everything within 1 metre of the enemy struck. At most about three times a second. Full is eight doses, ten with Deeper Dose and twenty with Slow Death.


      <b>Works with.</b> Venom (fill it with blows, end with a heavy), Ripe (15% harder), Wider Rupture (25% further), Buckling (40% more stagger), Rotten Fruit, Blister.


      <b>Example.</b> Eight doses on a soldier, then a heavy blow: 48 lands at once with the blow, and the soldier beside it takes the same.'
  - Id: poison.rottenfruit
    Title: Rotten Fruit
    Group: 
    Body: '<b>What it does.</b> A poisoned enemy that dies bursts, and everyone the burst reaches takes as many doses as it carried.


      <b>When it happens.</b> The moment an enemy carrying poison dies, whatever killed it.


      <b>The numbers.</b> 3 Shards. The burst is 3.5 metres in radius: 10 damage, 6 stagger, and as many doses as the dead one had, up to eight. At most a few times a second.


      <b>Works with.</b> Venom, Catching, One Sickness, Rupture and Volatile (spend the poison or pass it on: choose), Slow Death.


      <b>Example.</b> Kill a soldier at eight doses in the middle of a pack, and the two beside it start at eight.'
  - Id: poison.blister
    Title: Blister
    Group: 
    Body: '<b>What it does.</b> You raise a blister on the enemy you face. The next weapon blow you land on it breaks it in a wide burst that poisons everything round it. Left too long, it withers. With no enemy faced, nothing is raised and the slot waits all the same.


      <b>When it happens.</b> From a spell slot: cast it with that slot''s button (hold L2 and a face button, or 1 to 4). Then any blow on that enemy, light or heavy, breaks it.


      <b>The numbers.</b> 4 Shards, no mana: it waits 10 seconds after a cast, less with weapon play. An enemy within 8 metres; one blister at a time; it waits 12 seconds. The burst is 3 metres in radius round the enemy: 40 damage, 30 stagger and four doses.


      <b>Works with.</b> Venom, Rupture (four doses toward full), Rotten Fruit, Coiled Strike (step in and break it from behind), Spent Venom.


      <b>Example.</b> Blister the brute in the middle of a group, cut it once, and everyone round it is four doses deep.'
  - Id: poison.onebyone
    Title: One by One
    Group: 
    Body: '<b>What it does.</b> A mark closes under each of the nearest enemies, follows it, and a moment later a column bursts up under each in turn, throwing it into the air.


      <b>When it happens.</b> From a spell slot: cast it with that slot''s button (hold L2 and a face button, or 1 to 4).


      <b>The numbers.</b> 4 Shards, 50 mana. Up to six enemies within 10 metres of you; with fewer, the spare columns stand round the first. Half a second''s warning, then a column every 0.07 seconds, each 2.5 metres in radius: 30 damage and 20 stagger, a heavy blow, and what it strikes is thrown up for 0.8 seconds. As built the columns lay no poison and pass no depth from one enemy to the next.


      <b>Works with.</b> Venom and Blister to lay the poison first, Rupture and Volatile, and the charged blade: if it lands it charges your weapon with Poison, whose blows dose twice.


      <b>Example.</b> Six soldiers round you: all six go up at once, and you have a breath to roll clear or cut.'
  - Id: poison.volatile
    Title: Volatile
    Group: 
    Body: '<b>What it does.</b> Your poison no longer bites on its beat. It builds until it is full, then bursts by itself, spends itself and begins again.


      <b>When it happens.</b> Always on once learned. It bursts the moment any affliction fills on a poisoned enemy: usually the poison reaching full depth, but another element''s filling bursts it too, at whatever depth it has.


      <b>The numbers.</b> 6 Shards. The burst deals 7 a dose, 56 at eight, with 4 stagger a dose, to everything within 2.5 metres of the enemy. At most twice a second. Full is eight doses, ten with Deeper Dose, twenty with Slow Death (140 then).


      <b>Works with.</b> Venom, Ripe, Wider Rupture, Buckling, Lance the Wound (it still makes the poison bite), Slow Death, Rotten Fruit. Catching, In Time and One Sickness wait on bites, and there are none.


      <b>Example.</b> Eight light blows on a soldier and it goes up on the eighth, taking the two beside it with it.'
  - Id: poison.catching
    Title: Catching
    Group: 
    Body: '<b>What it does.</b> Each time poison bites, one dose leaps from that enemy to the nearest other enemy within reach.


      <b>When it happens.</b> Every bite of poison on any enemy, however it was laid.


      <b>The numbers.</b> 3 Shards. One dose to the nearest enemy within 4 metres (6 with Long Leap).


      <b>Works with.</b> Venom, One Sickness (they all bite together, so the doses fly together), Lance the Wound (more bites, more leaps), Rotten Fruit, Plague Bearer, Still Air.


      <b>Example.</b> Poison one soldier deep and keep it near its friends: every two seconds one of them gains a dose without a blow from you.'
  - Id: poison.onesickness
    Title: One Sickness
    Group: 
    Body: '<b>What it does.</b> The poison in every enemy bites on the same beat. Each poisoned enemy beyond the first that bit on the last beat makes every bite of the next one stronger. Blows on poisoned enemies give a little more mana.


      <b>When it happens.</b> Always on once learned.


      <b>The numbers.</b> 3 Shards. One beat every 2 seconds for all. Each bite is 15% stronger for every enemy beyond the first that bit on the beat before: four bitten, the next bites are 45% stronger. Weapon blows on a poisoned enemy give 10% more mana.


      <b>Works with.</b> Catching, Rotten Fruit, Swinging Censer, Share Alike and Plague Bearer to poison many, In Time (one beat to time against), Spent Venom.


      <b>Example.</b> Five soldiers poisoned eight deep: every two seconds they all bite at once for 16 each, 60% harder, 25.6 each.'
  - Id: poison.censer
    Title: Swinging Censer
    Group: 
    Body: '<b>What it does.</b> A smoking censer swings round you on its chain, dosing whatever it passes. When its time is up it flies off.


      <b>When it happens.</b> From a spell slot: cast it with that slot''s button (hold L2 and a face button, or 1 to 4).


      <b>The numbers.</b> 4 Shards, no mana: it waits 8 seconds after a cast, less with weapon play. One censer, 3 metres out, for 8 seconds, going round about twice in three seconds. It bites every 1.2 seconds whatever is within 1 metre of it: 4 damage, 4 stagger and a dose. One at a time. As built it leaves no smoke behind it.


      <b>Works with.</b> One Sickness, Catching, Plague Bearer (both poison what stays near you), Venom, and the charged blade: if it strikes it charges your weapon with Poison.


      <b>Example.</b> Cast it and stand your ground in a doorway: whatever crowds you is dosed every swing as you guard.'
  - Id: poison.sharealike
    Title: Share Alike
    Group: 
    Body: '<b>What it does.</b> You rush straight through everything before you, untouchable, and come out the far side facing back. Every enemy you pass is struck and poisoned, then a second cut lands on everyone on the line.


      <b>When it happens.</b> From a spell slot: cast it with that slot''s button (hold L2 and a face button, or 1 to 4).


      <b>The numbers.</b> 4 Shards, no mana: it waits 9 seconds after a cast, less with weapon play. Up to 7 metres along a lane 2 metres wide; a wall or something too big to shove stops you. Passing: 10 damage, 10 stagger and two doses. The cut after: the same again, so four doses on each. As built it doses each one alone: it does not yet raise them all to the depth of the sickest.


      <b>Works with.</b> One Sickness, Catching, Rotten Fruit, Plague Bearer, and the charged blade: if it lands it charges your weapon with Poison.


      <b>Example.</b> Rush through a line of three archers: each is four doses deep and you stand behind them.'
  - Id: poison.plaguebearer
    Title: Plague Bearer
    Group: 
    Body: '<b>What it does.</b> You carry the sickness. Enemies near you are poisoned without a blow, a dose at a time, deeper the longer they stay. Your flasks heal less.


      <b>When it happens.</b> Always on once learned, while an enemy is near.


      <b>The numbers.</b> 6 Shards. Every 1.5 seconds, one dose on every enemy within 4 metres of you. Flasks heal 30% less: 31.5 where they healed 45.


      <b>Works with.</b> Swinging Censer, One Sickness, Catching, Slow Death (nothing fades), Lance the Wound, Fever (its healing makes up for the flasks).


      <b>Example.</b> Guard in the middle of a pack: in twelve seconds each is eight doses deep without your blade moving.'
  - Id: poison.cleanblade
    Title: Clean Blade
    Group: 
    Body: '<b>What it does.</b> While your surge lasts the poison waits: it neither bites nor fades, and every bite it would have bitten is owed. Your blows dose once more. When the surge ends time slows, you flick the blade clean, and every bite owed by every poisoned enemy near lands at once.


      <b>When it happens.</b> Light the surge (a tap of L2, or F); it begins with whichever surge you wear. The flick comes when the surge ends. The extra dose holds while Poison is your first element.


      <b>The numbers.</b> A god''s gift, never sold; in the playtest it can be bought. One more dose a blow, on top of Fever''s. When the surge ends, every enemy within 14 metres takes one bite for each whole 2 seconds it waited, at its depth then, with 20 stagger. Fever''s 10 seconds owe five bites: 80 on an enemy at eight doses, 100 at ten.


      <b>Works with.</b> Venom, Fever, Sweet Fever (a longer surge owes more), Deeper Dose and Slow Death (a deeper bite), Plague Bearer. Lance the Wound, In Time and Catching wait on bites, and there are none while the poison waits.


      <b>Example.</b> Light Fever, dose a whole pack to eight while it waits, and let the surge run out: each takes 80 at once.'
  - Id: pyre.fuel
    Title: Fuel
    Group: 
    Body: '<b>What it does.</b> Heavy blows both poison and burn, whichever of the two you carry first. A mixed branch''s marks are the exception to the rule that weapon blows lay only your first element''s affliction.


      <b>When it happens.</b> Every heavy blow or finisher that lands.


      <b>The numbers.</b> Mix, 3 Shards. Two doses of poison and one stack of Burn a heavy blow. Your first element''s root counts against its own: with Poison first and Venom learned, one dose beyond Venom''s; with Fire first and Cinder learned, no Burn beyond Cinder''s. Poison holds up to eight doses for 6 seconds and bites for 2 a dose every 2 seconds; set off, it deals 6 a dose.


      <b>Works with.</b> Venom or Cinder, Miasma or Flame Wave in a slot (more of either), the charged blade and the R2 strike, Goes Up, Funeral Fire, Light the Pyres.


      <b>Example.</b> Carrying Poison first and Fire second: a chain ending in a heavy blow leaves a soldier deep in poison and burning with it.'
  - Id: pyre.flashpoint
    Title: Goes Up
    Group: 
    Body: '<b>What it does.</b> When a burning enemy''s poison reaches its full depth, it goes up. The poison explodes and sets alight everyone near.


      <b>When it happens.</b> The moment an affliction fills on an enemy that is burning and carries a full eight doses of poison.


      <b>The numbers.</b> Mix, 4 Shards. The poison is set off: 6 damage a dose to everything within 3 metres, 48 at eight, with 4 stagger a dose. Everything within 3 metres also takes two stacks of Burn. At most twice a second.


      <b>Works with.</b> Fuel, Cinder, Funeral Fire, Slow Burn, Searing Edge.


      <b>Example.</b> Keep a burning brute poisoned; the blow that brings it to eight doses makes it go up among its friends.'
  - Id: pyre.fireeater
    Title: Fire Eater
    Group: 
    Body: '<b>What it does.</b> You brace and breathe out a stream of green fire for two seconds, turning slowly as it burns. It poisons everything it sweeps across. A dodge lets it go.


      <b>When it happens.</b> From a spell slot: cast it with that slot''s button (hold L2 and a face button, or 1 to 4). While it pours, the stick or the cursor turns it.


      <b>The numbers.</b> Mix, 4 Shards, no mana: it waits 12 seconds after a cast, less with weapon play. A bar 5 metres long and 1.2 metres to each side, after a 0.3-second brace, for 2 seconds. It bites every quarter second for 4 damage, 3 stagger and one dose of poison: eight bites on what stays in it. The branch''s spells are made of Poison whichever element is first, and one that lands charges the blade with Poison.


      <b>Works with.</b> Goes Up (eight doses fast), Fuel, Funeral Fire, Light the Pyres.


      <b>Example.</b> Sweep it across a line of soldiers as they come up the stair.'
  - Id: pyre.funeralfire
    Title: Funeral Fire
    Group: 
    Body: '<b>What it does.</b> An enemy that dies poisoned and burning explodes, and leaves the ground burning where it fell.


      <b>When it happens.</b> The moment an enemy dies carrying both poison and Burn.


      <b>The numbers.</b> Mix, 3 Shards. A burst 3.5 metres in radius: 20 damage, 20 stagger and two doses of poison, and one stack of Burn on all within it. The ground burns 1.5 metres round for 4 seconds, biting for 5 every half second with a stack of Burn. At most twice a second.


      <b>Works with.</b> Fuel, Goes Up, Catching Fire, Wildfire.


      <b>Example.</b> Kill one poisoned, burning soldier in a crowd and the rest catch both.'
  - Id: pyre.slowfuse
    Title: Lit Fuse
    Group: 
    Body: '<b>What it does.</b> You set a fuse on the enemy you face. Your next weapon blow on it within five seconds sets off a great blast round it. With no enemy faced nothing is set, and the slot waits all the same.


      <b>When it happens.</b> From a spell slot: cast it with that slot''s button (hold L2 and a face button, or 1 to 4). Then land a blow on that enemy.


      <b>The numbers.</b> Mix, 5 Shards, no mana: it waits 12 seconds after a cast, less with weapon play. An enemy within 8 metres. The blast is 3.5 metres in radius: 40 damage, 40 stagger and two doses of poison.


      <b>Works with.</b> Fuel (make that blow a heavy one), Goes Up, Funeral Fire.


      <b>Example.</b> Set the fuse on the brute in the middle and cut it once: the whole group takes 40.'
  - Id: pyre.slowburn
    Title: Slow Burn
    Group: 
    Body: '<b>What it does.</b> Every affliction you lay works harder, Burn and poison among them: each bite, and each set-off.


      <b>When it happens.</b> Always on once learned.


      <b>The numbers.</b> Mix, 5 Shards. 30% stronger afflictions.


      <b>Works with.</b> Fuel, Goes Up, Funeral Fire, Searing Edge, Light the Pyres.


      <b>Example.</b> A five-deep burn that dealt 12.5 a second now deals over 16.'
  - Id: pyre.lightthepyres
    Title: Light the Pyres
    Group: 
    Body: '<b>What it does.</b> You kneel and drive your weapon into the ground. A line of fire runs to every poisoned or burning enemy near and follows it. Stand through three breaths, and a pillar of flame rises under each, setting off its burn and its poison. A dodge or a blow taken breaks it. With no one alight, the mana comes back.


      <b>When it happens.</b> Cast it from its spell slot (hold L2 and a face button, or 1 to 4) and stay still.


      <b>The numbers.</b> A god''s gift, never sold; in the playtest it can be bought. 60 mana. Up to six enemies within 9 metres. The three breaths take 2.2 seconds. Each pillar is 2 metres in radius: 40 damage and 40 stagger, a heavy blow, two doses of poison, plus 6 a dose of poison and 10 and 10 a stack of Burn set off.


      <b>Works with.</b> Fuel, Fire Eater, Goes Up, Cinder, Slow Burn.


      <b>Example.</b> Fight until five enemies are burning, roll clear, and light the pyres.'
  - Id: tempest.charged
    Title: Charged Air
    Group: 
    Body: '<b>What it does.</b> A heavy blow on an enemy carrying Static sets the Static off, as Lightning''s root would, whichever of the two is your first element. Your blows also lay Static and Unsteady together, whichever of the two you carry first: every light blow a Static, every blow an Unsteady. Once your first element''s root (Static or Unsteady) is learned, that element''s own is the root''s, not laid twice.


      <b>When it happens.</b> A heavy blow or finisher on an enemy carrying Static sets it off. Every light blow lays a Static, and every blow that lands an Unsteady.


      <b>The numbers.</b> Mix, 3 Shards. Static set off deals 7 damage a stack to everything within 4 metres, with no stagger, at most about three times a second. One stack a blow of each; of your first element''s, none beyond its root''s. Unsteady makes an enemy take 6% more stagger, be shoved 15% further and turn 8% slower for each stack, up to five.


      <b>Works with.</b> Thunderclap or Gust in a slot (more of either), the charged blade and the R2 strike, Thunder Lift, Slip Current, The Sky Finds Them, Falling Thunder.


      <b>Example.</b> Carrying Wind first and Lightning second: your light blows build Unsteady and Static on a soldier, and the heavy blow that ends your chain sets the Static off into its neighbours.'
  - Id: tempest.lift
    Title: Thunder Lift
    Group: 
    Body: '<b>What it does.</b> A discharge of five Static or more throws its enemy into the air. What is too heavy to leave the ground reels where it stands instead.


      <b>When it happens.</b> Whenever a discharge spends five stacks or more: a heavy blow or finisher on a full enemy, or Conductor setting one off.


      <b>The numbers.</b> Mix, 4 Shards. Thrown up for 1 second. One too heavy to lift takes 40 stagger instead.


      <b>Works with.</b> Static, Charged Air, The Sky Finds Them, Full Discharge, Single Stroke, Eye of the Storm.


      <b>Example.</b> Fill a soldier with Static and land a heavy blow: it is thrown up, helpless, while you cut the next one.'
  - Id: tempest.slip
    Title: Slip Current
    Group: 
    Body: '<b>What it does.</b> Where a dodge ends, every enemy close to you is left one deeper in Static and in Unsteady.


      <b>When it happens.</b> At the end of every dodge.


      <b>The numbers.</b> Mix, 3 Shards. One stack of Static and one of Unsteady on every enemy within 2.2 metres of where you stop.


      <b>Works with.</b> Charged Air, Thunder Lift, Blink, Storm Step, Tailwind.


      <b>Example.</b> Roll into the middle of three soldiers: all three gain a stack of each before you have swung.'
  - Id: tempest.sky
    Title: The Sky Finds Them
    Group: 
    Body: '<b>What it does.</b> An enemy you throw into the air is struck by a bolt, which leaps on to two more near it and leaves Static on each.


      <b>When it happens.</b> Each time one of your marks throws an enemy into the air, such as Thunder Lift. As built the bolt falls as soon as it is thrown up, not at the top of its rise.


      <b>The numbers.</b> Mix, 3 Shards. 14 damage and two stacks of Static to the one thrown, then the same to up to two more within 4 metres of each other.


      <b>Works with.</b> Thunder Lift, Static, Charged Air.


      <b>Example.</b> Thunder Lift throws a soldier up; the bolt strikes it and its two neighbours and leaves each two deep in Static.'
  - Id: tempest.cloud
    Title: Storm Overhead
    Group: 
    Body: '<b>What it does.</b> You call a storm over the ground before you. For ten seconds bolts fall inside its circle, each warned by a ring closing on the spot. Half of them fall where an enemy stands.


      <b>When it happens.</b> From a spell slot: cast it with that slot''s button (hold L2 and a face button, or 1 to 4).


      <b>The numbers.</b> Mix, 4 Shards, no mana: it waits 12 seconds after a cast, less with weapon play. The circle is 3 metres in radius, 1 metre ahead of you, for 10 seconds. A bolt every 0.8 seconds, 0.34 seconds after its warning ring, 1.2 metres across in radius: 14 damage, 20 stagger and one stack of Static (the branch''s spells are made of Lightning, whichever element is first).


      <b>Works with.</b> Charged Air, Static, Thunder Lift, Lodestone, Live Wire.


      <b>Example.</b> Call it over a gate as a pack comes through and fight on its edge.'
  - Id: tempest.eye
    Title: Eye of the Storm
    Group: 
    Body: '<b>What it does.</b> You become the storm: a turning column of wind and lightning round you that drags enemies in and bites them, and carries the light ones round. While it turns you walk slower, take half damage and cannot be made to flinch. Let go and it throws them all out, and a bolt meets each where it lands.


      <b>When it happens.</b> From a spell slot: cast it with that slot''s button (hold L2 and a face button, or 1 to 4), and keep holding it. Letting go ends it.


      <b>The numbers.</b> Mix, 5 Shards, 50 mana. Up to 2.5 seconds, at least half a second. The column is 3.5 metres in radius and holds up to eight. A bite every 0.4 seconds: 6 damage and one stack of Static (the branch''s spells are made of Lightning, whichever element is first). Thrown out up to 5 metres; each bolt deals 12 damage and 20 stagger.


      <b>Works with.</b> Charged Air, Slip Current, Thunder Lift, Static.


      <b>Example.</b> Swarmed by small enemies: hold it the full time, then let go and the bolts fall on every one thrown.'
  - Id: tempest.falling
    Title: Falling Thunder
    Group: 
    Body: '<b>What it does.</b> After your finisher lands, you throw the enemy skyward, vanish after it in a line of light, and come down on it as a bolt. Where you land, everything near is shocked, unsteadied and thrown back. Nothing can strike you from the throw to the landing.


      <b>When it happens.</b> Every finisher that lands (a heavy blow on a staggered enemy).


      <b>The numbers.</b> A god''s gift, never sold; in the playtest it can be bought. You land 0.34 seconds after the throw. Everything within 4.5 metres takes 22 damage, 40 stagger, three stacks of Static and three of Unsteady, and is pushed 3 metres.


      <b>Works with.</b> Charged Air, Static, Thunder Lift, Slip Current, Stored Charge.


      <b>Example.</b> Finish a staggered brute in a crowd and land among its friends with each three deep in both.'
  - Id: water.soak
    Title: Soaked
    Group: 
    Body: '<b>What it does.</b> Every blow of your weapon that lands leaves the enemy Soaked. A Soaked enemy takes more from your spells, and Static or Chill laid on it is laid on everyone standing near it as well.


      <b>When it happens.</b> Always on once learned: every weapon blow that lands, while Water is your first element (or all in). With Water second, Soaked comes from your spells, the charged blade and the R2 strike instead.


      <b>The numbers.</b> 2 Shards. Soaked is on or off and lasts 8 seconds; each blow starts it again. Spells deal a Soaked enemy 25% more damage. Static or Chill laid on it is also laid on every other enemy within 4 metres, whether they are Soaked or not.


      <b>Works with.</b> Riptide, Wellspring, Heavy Water, Deep Crack (which spends it), Drawn From the Drowned, Spreading Water, Lightning''s Static and Ice''s Chill as your second element, and the reactions Steam (with Fire) and The Ground Gives (with Earth).


      <b>Example.</b> Carrying Water and Lightning, cut three soldiers in a huddle, then Thunderclap one: the Static runs to all three.'
  - Id: water.ebbflood
    Title: Ebb and Flood
    Group: 
    Body: '<b>What it does.</b> A perfect guard brings the Flood: a splash soaks the attacker and those beside it, and for a while your blows strike harder. A heavy blow that lands brings the Ebb: for a while your guard and dodge cost half the stamina and the moment of your perfect guard is longer.


      <b>When it happens.</b> The Flood with every perfect guard (press the guard button just before a blow lands). The Ebb with every heavy blow or finisher that lands.


      <b>The numbers.</b> 3 Shards. Flood: a splash 2.5 metres round the attacker, 6 damage, 8 stagger and Soaked; then 15% more weapon damage for 5 seconds. Ebb: dodges and blocked blows cost half the stamina for 4 seconds, and the perfect guard''s moment is 22% longer for as long.


      <b>Works with.</b> Blowhole and Deep Crack, which grow from it; Spreading Water above them; Heavy Water; Undertow.


      <b>Not built yet.</b> The Flood''s longer reach and a splash on each blow: for now it is more damage and one splash on the attacker.


      <b>Example.</b> Land a heavy blow, then guard the answer perfectly with the Ebb''s wider moment: the Flood soaks it and your next cuts land 15% harder.'
  - Id: water.crack
    Title: Deep Crack
    Group: 
    Body: '<b>What it does.</b> A fist of water snaps shut on the enemy you face. A bubble as big as a body forms on it and collapses with a crack. On a Soaked enemy the water boils out of it: its Soaked is spent, and every other Soaked enemy near cracks with it. The detonator of the tree.


      <b>When it happens.</b> From a spell slot: cast it with that slot''s button (hold L2 and a face button, or 1 to 4). It closes on the nearest enemy within reach.


      <b>The numbers.</b> 4 Shards, no mana: it waits 11 seconds after a cast, less with weapon play (its Empower: 9, and 22 damage). An enemy within 7 metres; the bubble collapses 0.4 seconds after the cast, 1 metre round: 18 damage and 40 stagger. On a Soaked enemy its Soaked is spent and the crack runs on to up to six other Soaked enemies, each within 5 metres of the last: 18 damage and 30 stagger each.


      <b>Works with.</b> Soaked, Riptide and Whirlpool to soak a crowd first, Ebb and Flood, which it grows from, Spreading Water.


      <b>Not built yet.</b> Each of the others cracking where it stands and having its own Soaked spent: for now the crack runs to them as an arc of water, and they keep their Soaked.


      <b>Example.</b> Riptide three soldiers to your feet, Soaked, and snap the bubble on the middle one: all three take the crack.'
  - Id: water.crack.shape
    Title: 'Deep Crack: Ink or String of Bubbles'
    Group: 
    Body: '<b>What it does.</b> Opens two shapes of Deep Crack, chosen at any rest fire. <b>Ink</b>: the bubble is black water from the deep and bursts into a pool of ink; enemies in it lose track of you beyond three metres and stay Soaked, and you stay in plain sight. <b>String of Bubbles</b>: three bubbles in a row along the line you face, each cracking a moment after the last; aim it down a corridor.


      <b>When it happens.</b> Whenever you cast Deep Crack, as the shape it wears. Before this is bought, the single bubble is cast.


      <b>The numbers.</b> 3 Shards. Ink: a pool 1.5 metres round for 5 seconds, biting once a second for 1 damage and Soaked; what it reaches as it bursts sees no further than 3 metres for 5 seconds. String of Bubbles: a line of water 7 metres long, 2 metres wide, run out at 13 metres a second: 18 damage and 40 stagger on all it crosses, and the crack runs on from each Soaked enemy as above.


      <b>Works with.</b> Blowhole and Whirlpool to hold them in the ink; Riptide''s Breaking Swell to line them up for the string.


      <b>Not built yet.</b> Ink''s blindness only while an enemy stands in the ink (for now what the ink first reaches keeps it for 5 seconds), and String of Bubbles as three bubbles 2 metres apart (for now one running line).


      <b>Example.</b> Ink in a doorway: the archers behind it lose you, and the soldiers in it stay Soaked for the next crack.'
  - Id: water.crack.master
    Title: 'Deep Crack: Mastered'
    Group: 
    Body: '<b>What it does.</b> Snap it as your heavy blow lands on the same enemy, and every Soaked enemy in the fight cracks.


      <b>When it happens.</b> For now, a heavy blow (a finisher counts) on the enemy within 0.3 seconds after the bubble cracks on it. Deep Crack must be in a slot.


      <b>The numbers.</b> 3 Shards. The crack runs on to up to twelve Soaked enemies, each within 20 metres of the last: 18 damage and 30 stagger each.


      <b>Works with.</b> Soaked and every mark that soaks a crowd; Heavy Water; Spreading Water.


      <b>Not built yet.</b> The snap timed to the heavy blow''s landing rather than the crack''s, and each enemy cracking where it stands.


      <b>Example.</b> Soak the room with Riptide and Whirlpool, then cast on the brute in front of you and bring the heavy down as it cracks: every soaked body in the room cracks with it.'
  - Id: water.blowhole
    Title: Blowhole
    Group: 
    Body: '<b>What it does.</b> You stand on a vent in black rock. Each blow that comes is turned and drives the sea down the vent, and its spray rises a step. Let go, and the sea comes up as a spout under the attacker, harder for every step, and throws it up open to your blade.


      <b>When it happens.</b> From a spell slot: cast it with that slot''s button (hold L2 and a face button, or 1 to 4), then any blow in the next 3 seconds. If none comes, the cast is spent.


      <b>The numbers.</b> 4 Shards, no mana: it waits 10 seconds after a cast, less with weapon play (its Empower: 8, and 18 a step). Ready for 3 seconds. As built the first blow is turned and answered at once as a spout of three steps: a cone 3 metres long and 140 degrees wide, 42 damage (54 with the Empower), 66 stagger and Soaked. What it strikes begins nothing and cannot guard for 0.8 seconds.


      <b>Works with.</b> Ebb and Flood (the turned blow is a guard''s work), Deep Crack on the Soaked attacker, Heavy Water, Undertow.


      <b>Not built yet.</b> The vent itself: standing 3 seconds and turning every blow, red ones too (15 stamina each), each raising the spray a step to five, and the spout loosed when you let go, 14 a step, throwing up for 0.8 seconds at three steps and 1.2 at five. For now the first blow is turned and answered as three steps, and what it strikes is left open rather than thrown up.


      <b>Example.</b> Cast it as a brute winds up: the blow is turned, the spout answers, and the brute stands open for your next cut.'
  - Id: water.blowhole.shape
    Title: 'Blowhole: Still Water or Blown Out'
    Group: 
    Body: '<b>What it does.</b> Opens two shapes of Blowhole, chosen at any rest fire. <b>Still Water</b>: the first blow only, turned and answered at once with a thrust of water six metres straight through the attacker; a quick parry, not a store. <b>Blown Out</b>: the spout comes up under you instead and throws everything within four metres out three metres; room, not a target.


      <b>When it happens.</b> Whenever you cast Blowhole, as the shape it wears. Before this is bought, the vent is cast.


      <b>The numbers.</b> 3 Shards. Still Water: the answer is a thrust 6 metres long and 25 degrees wide, with Blowhole''s damage and stagger. Blown Out: the answer is a ring 4 metres round you with Blowhole''s damage and stagger, and everything within 4 metres is thrown 3 metres out.


      <b>Works with.</b> Deep Crack''s String of Bubbles down the line Still Water opens; Undertow to bring back what Blown Out threw.


      <b>Not built yet.</b> Blown Out''s store before the spout (as for the Learn): for now the first blow turned brings it up at once.


      <b>Example.</b> Surrounded, wear Blown Out: the first blow turned throws the whole ring of them back.'
  - Id: water.blowhole.master
    Title: 'Blowhole: Mastered'
    Group: 
    Body: '<b>What it does.</b> Let go in the same instant as a blow lands on the vent, and the spout is doubled and the vent stays for a second round.


      <b>When it happens.</b> For now, every answer, since as built the answer comes in the instant the blow lands. Blowhole must be in a slot.


      <b>The numbers.</b> 3 Shards. The answer strikes again where it lands: 42 damage, 66 stagger and Soaked within 1.5 metres. And Blowhole''s cooldown ends at once, once in 20 seconds, so it can be cast again for a second round.


      <b>Works with.</b> Ebb and Flood; Deep Crack; Heavy Water on the attacker it soaks.


      <b>Not built yet.</b> The timing (letting go within 0.2 seconds of a blow landing on the vent): for now every answer is doubled.


      <b>Example.</b> Turn a soldier''s blow, and cast again at once as the next one swings.'
  - Id: water.lift
    Title: Spreading Water
    Group: 
    Body: '<b>What it does.</b> Spreading Water, Water''s reaction lift: every reaction with Soaked in it runs on at half strength to every other Soaked enemy near.


      <b>When it happens.</b> Whenever Soaked reacts on an enemy with the other affliction it carries (Steam with Burn, The Ground Gives with Tremor, and the rest).


      <b>The numbers.</b> 3 Shards. For now an arc of water runs from where the reaction happened to up to four other Soaked enemies, each within 4 metres of the last: 10 damage and 15 stagger each.


      <b>Works with.</b> Carrying a second element: every reaction of Water''s ten; Soaked, to soak a crowd; Ebb and Flood, which it grows from; The Sea Comes In above it.


      <b>Not built yet.</b> The reaction itself running on at half strength: for now a plain arc of water.


      <b>Example.</b> Water and Fire on a huddle of soaked soldiers: Steam goes off on one, and the water carries on to the rest.'
  - Id: water.devotion
    Title: The Sea Comes In
    Group: 
    Body: '<b>What it does.</b> The Sea Comes In, Water''s Devotion: all in on Water only. Every spell leaves standing water where it lands. Enemies in water are always Soaked and slower, and in water your dodge slides further and your cooldowns run faster. Draw the fight onto your own water and stay there, as the tide takes the beach.


      <b>When it happens.</b> Only while Water is carried twice (all in). A pool is left each time a spell strikes.


      <b>The numbers.</b> 6 Shards. A pool 4 metres across where a spell strikes, at most one every 2.5 seconds, for 10 seconds, biting once a second for 1 damage and Soaked. For now everywhere, not only in water: the dodge goes half again as far, and every spell clock runs 30% faster. All in, L2 with R2 is the deep strike, Thrown on the Reef: the lash wraps the enemy and a wave throws it 5 metres away from you.


      <b>Works with.</b> Every spell of the tree; Deep Crack and Spreading Water on the soaked crowd; Undertow to draw them onto the water.


      <b>Not built yet.</b> Four pools at most, enemies in them 15% slower, and the dodge and the clocks quicker only while you stand in your own water. Thrown on the Reef''s 30 damage, 50 stagger and 0.8 seconds lying down when the enemy meets a wall, a rock or another enemy.


      <b>Example.</b> Riptide and Whirlpool lay two pools in the middle of the room; stand between them and cast again and again, a third faster.'
  - Id: water.undertow
    Title: Undertow
    Group: 
    Body: '<b>What it does.</b> A heavy blow that lands drags every enemy near you a step toward you.


      <b>When it happens.</b> Every heavy blow or finisher that lands, at most twice a second. As built it pulls everyone near, Soaked or not.


      <b>The numbers.</b> 3 Shards. Every enemy within 6 metres of you is pulled 1.5 metres in. At most once every half second.


      <b>Works with.</b> Heavy weapons that strike wide, The Tide Turns, which grows from it, Heavy Water, Whirlpool, Blowhole''s Blown Out (which throws them back out).


      <b>Example.</b> Two archers hang back while you fight a brute: each heavy blow on the brute draws them a step closer to your blade.'
  - Id: water.tide
    Title: The Tide Turns
    Group: 
    Body: '<b>What it does.</b> The tide in your hand. Press, and the ebb draws you straight back out of reach, leaving a line of wet sand. Press again within three seconds, and the flood brings you back along the line and on past where you began as a breaking wave, soaking all on the line and carrying it ahead of you.


      <b>When it happens.</b> From a spell slot: cast it with that slot''s button (hold L2 and a face button, or 1 to 4).


      <b>The numbers.</b> 4 Shards, no mana: it waits 8 seconds after a cast, less with weapon play (its Empower: 6, and the flood runs 10 metres). As built one press is the flood alone: you drive 8 metres ahead at 20 metres a second, nothing can touch you as you go, and everything on the line, 2 metres wide, takes 10 damage, 10 stagger and Soaked and is carried 2 metres on ahead of you.


      <b>Works with.</b> Undertow, which it grows from; Riptide to bring them in before the flood; Deep Crack on the line it soaks; Heavy Water.


      <b>Not built yet.</b> The ebb (drawn 5 metres straight back in 0.3 seconds, untouchable, the wet sand left behind) and the flood as the second press back along that line: for now one press is the flood, run ahead.


      <b>Example.</b> A pack closes on you: flood through it and out the far side, every one of them Soaked and stumbling.'
  - Id: water.tide.shape
    Title: 'The Tide Turns: King Tide or Out to Sea'
    Group: 
    Body: '<b>What it does.</b> Opens two shapes of The Tide Turns, chosen at any rest fire. <b>King Tide</b>: the flood comes in four metres wide and throws what it carries down for a moment, but it stops where you began; the shape for a crowd. <b>Out to Sea</b>: there is no flood; the ebb takes the enemy faced with you, drawn the five metres out, Soaked, and dropped at your feet, away from its friends. A pull, not a return.


      <b>When it happens.</b> Whenever you cast The Tide Turns, as the shape it wears. Before this is bought, the plain tide is cast.


      <b>The numbers.</b> 3 Shards. King Tide: the flood 4 metres wide and 5 metres long; what it strikes lies down for 0.6 seconds (elites half as long, gods not at all). Out to Sea: the enemy faced is drawn 5 metres toward you and Soaked.


      <b>Works with.</b> Deep Crack and Heavy Water on the crowd King Tide throws down; Blowhole and the blade on the one Out to Sea brings.


      <b>Not built yet.</b> King Tide keeping its own 5 metres when the Empower is bought (for now the Empower''s 10 metres win), and Out to Sea drawing you back with the enemy.


      <b>Example.</b> An archer behind three shields: Out to Sea brings it to your feet, alone.'
  - Id: water.tide.master
    Title: 'The Tide Turns: Mastered'
    Group: 
    Body: '<b>What it does.</b> Started in the instant a blow would land on you, The Tide Turns counts as a perfect dodge, and a flood pressed in the instant a blow would land starts no cooldown.


      <b>When it happens.</b> For now, every cast of The Tide Turns, and a cast within a second after a perfect dodge. The Tide Turns must be in a slot.


      <b>The numbers.</b> 3 Shards. What a perfect dodge gives: 12 mana and 1.5 seconds off every running cooldown. A cast within 1 second after a perfect dodge, when the spell is ready, starts no clock.


      <b>Works with.</b> The dodge; Ebb and Flood; every spell whose clock the cut shortens.


      <b>Not built yet.</b> The timing (started as a blow would land), and the flood''s own press: for now every cast gives the dodge''s mana and cuts, and a perfect dodge makes the next cast free of its clock.


      <b>Example.</b> Dodge a brute''s swing perfectly and flood through it at once: the spell is ready again before it turns round.'
  - Id: water.heavy
    Title: Heavy Water
    Group: 
    Body: '<b>What it does.</b> Striking a Soaked enemy makes your weapon break balance faster for a few seconds.


      <b>When it happens.</b> Each time a weapon blow or a spell of yours strikes an enemy that is already Soaked. Each new strike starts the time again.


      <b>The numbers.</b> 3 Shards. Your weapon''s blows deal 20% more stagger for 3 seconds. It can be set going again at most twice a second.


      <b>Works with.</b> Soaked, Whirlpool, which grows from it, Ebb and Flood, Blowhole, heavy blows and finishers, Riptide to soak first.


      <b>Not built yet.</b> The design''s form, Soaked enemies slow to recover after they strike: an enemy''s recovery cannot be changed yet, so the weapon breaks their balance sooner instead.


      <b>Example.</b> Soak a brute, then work it with light blows: its balance bar fills a fifth faster and the finisher comes sooner.'
  - Id: water.whirlpool
    Title: Whirlpool
    Group: 
    Body: '<b>What it does.</b> You open a whirlpool under the enemy you face. Enemies in it are kept Soaked and bitten, and your blows on them break balance harder: the breaker of the tree.


      <b>When it happens.</b> From a spell slot: cast it with that slot''s button (hold L2 and a face button, or 1 to 4). With no enemy faced it opens 6 metres ahead of you.


      <b>The numbers.</b> 4 Shards, no mana: it waits 10 seconds after a cast, less with weapon play (its Empower: 8, and it lasts 7 seconds). On an enemy faced within 6 metres. The whirlpool is 4 metres in radius and lasts 5 seconds. It bites every half second for 3 damage, with no stagger, and lays Soaked with each bite. Each bite leaves its enemy taking 30% more stagger for 0.7 seconds, so while it stands in the water every blow breaks it harder.


      <b>Works with.</b> Soaked, Heavy Water, which it grows from, Undertow, Deep Crack, a second element''s Static or Chill, Steam if you carry Fire.


      <b>Not built yet.</b> Enemies drawn to the middle at 1.2 metres a second, and their balance not recovering inside it.


      <b>Example.</b> Open it under a pack: for five seconds every one of them stays Soaked and breaks a third sooner under your blade.'
  - Id: water.whirlpool.shape
    Title: 'Whirlpool: Maelstrom or Rip Current'
    Group: 
    Body: '<b>What it does.</b> Opens two shapes of Whirlpool, chosen at any rest fire. <b>Maelstrom</b>: smaller and pulling hard, and at its end it throws everything inside up in a spout and down again. <b>Rip Current</b>: no pull to the middle; a lane of churning foam runs from the whirlpool''s point away from you, and enemies in it are carried down it and cannot dodge against it. Cut them as the current drags them past.


      <b>When it happens.</b> Whenever you cast Whirlpool, as the shape it wears. Before this is bought, the plain whirlpool is cast.


      <b>The numbers.</b> 3 Shards. Maelstrom: 2.5 metres in radius; when the bites on an enemy stop (the whirlpool ends, or it leaves the water), it is thrown up for 0.8 seconds and takes 50 stagger. Rip Current: each bite carries its enemy 1.25 metres away from you, two and a half metres a second, and the bites keep their churn.


      <b>Works with.</b> Deep Crack on the bodies Maelstrom throws up; Undertow and your blade on the ones Rip Current carries past.


      <b>Not built yet.</b> Maelstrom''s hard pull (3 metres a second), and Rip Current''s lane of foam 2 metres wide and 9 long for 6 seconds and its rule against dodging: for now the whirlpool itself carries what it bites away from you.


      <b>Example.</b> Maelstrom on a pair of soldiers: they churn for five seconds, then go up together for your heavy blow.'
  - Id: water.whirlpool.master
    Title: 'Whirlpool: Mastered'
    Group: 
    Body: '<b>What it does.</b> Open it under an enemy in the instant its attack mark shows, and the attack is lost as it goes in to the knees. Its cooldown is halved.


      <b>When it happens.</b> For now, the first enemy it bites on each cast. Whirlpool must be in a slot.


      <b>The numbers.</b> 3 Shards. The first enemy bitten flinches out of what it had begun, once in 5 seconds.


      <b>Works with.</b> Blowhole and Ebb and Flood, for the moment an attack begins; Heavy Water.


      <b>Not built yet.</b> The timing (the instant its attack mark shows) and the halved cooldown: for now its first bite breaks whatever its enemy had begun.


      <b>Example.</b> A brute raises its club: open the whirlpool under it and the swing never comes.'
  - Id: water.gourd
    Title: Broken Gourd
    Group: 
    Body: '<b>What it does.</b> Holding the flask button throws the flask instead of drinking it. Where it breaks it strikes and soaks everyone near and leaves a pool that keeps what stands in it Soaked. The throw also mends you a little at once. A short press still drinks.


      <b>When it happens.</b> Hold the flask button. Each throw uses a flask.


      <b>The numbers.</b> 3 Shards. Hold 0.3 seconds to throw. It flies at the enemy ahead within 9 metres, or 5 metres ahead. The burst is 2.6 metres in radius: 18 damage, 20 stagger and Soaked. The pool is 1.5 metres in radius and lasts 6 seconds, biting once a second for 1 damage and Soaked. The throw mends you 20.


      <b>Works with.</b> Drawn From the Drowned, which grows from it, to win the flask back; Deep Well; Heavy Water; Deep Crack on the soaked crowd; Steam if you carry Fire.


      <b>Not built yet.</b> The pool mending you while you stand in it: for now the throw mends a part at once.


      <b>Example.</b> A pack gathers at a door: break a gourd on the first one and every one of them is Soaked before you reach them.'
  - Id: water.base
    Title: Riptide
    Group: 
    Body: '<b>What it does.</b> Riptide, Water''s own spell, comes with the element and is never bought. A wave rises ahead of you and rolls back toward you, soaking everything in its path and carrying it to your feet, within reach of your blade.


      <b>When it happens.</b> From a spell slot: cast it with that slot''s button (hold L2 and a face button, or 1 to 4). Carrying Water, it is always yours to put in a slot.


      <b>The numbers.</b> Given with Water. No mana: it waits 6 seconds after a cast, less with weapon play; its Empower makes that 4.5. The wave rises 5 metres ahead, 90 degrees wide: 8 damage, 18 stagger and Soaked, and what it strikes is carried in to your feet.


      <b>Works with.</b> Its Empower, its two shapes and its Master; Soaked; Deep Crack and Heavy Water on what it brings; the charged blade, which its landing charges with Water.


      <b>Not built yet.</b> The Empower''s wave rising 6.5 metres away: the base spell is cast by Water''s kit, which takes only the Empower''s shorter wait.


      <b>Example.</b> Three archers at range: Riptide brings all three to your feet, Soaked, for one wide swing.'
  - Id: water.base.shape
    Title: 'Riptide: River Serpent or Breaking Swell'
    Group: 
    Body: '<b>What it does.</b> Opens two shapes of Riptide, chosen at any rest fire. <b>River Serpent</b>: a serpent of water goes out along a lane and back, and brings only the first enemy it takes, dropping it in front of you with its guard down; one target, from further. <b>Breaking Swell</b>: the wave does not come back; it rolls away from you and breaks, throwing everything in it down; the shape that makes room.


      <b>When it happens.</b> Whenever you cast Riptide, as the shape it wears. Before this is bought, the plain wave is cast.


      <b>The numbers.</b> 3 Shards. River Serpent: a lane 8 metres long and 2.4 metres wide, run at 16 metres a second: 12 damage, 30 stagger and Soaked; the first enemy it strikes is drawn 4 metres back toward you and cannot guard for 1 second. Breaking Swell: a wave 6 metres long and 90 degrees wide: 8 damage, 18 stagger and Soaked; what it strikes is thrown 3 metres away and lies down for 0.6 seconds (elites half as long, gods not at all).


      <b>Works with.</b> Blowhole and the blade on the one River Serpent brings; Deep Crack''s String of Bubbles down the line Breaking Swell clears.


      <b>Not built yet.</b> River Serpent going out and coming back, and dropping its enemy 1.5 metres in front of you: for now the serpent runs its lane and its first enemy is drawn back 4 metres.


      <b>Example.</b> A shaman behind its guards: River Serpent takes it alone, guard down, to your blade.'
  - Id: water.base.master
    Title: 'Riptide: Mastered'
    Group: 
    Body: '<b>What it does.</b> Press again within a second of the wave reaching you, and it goes out again the way it came, carrying what it brought past you and on four metres, backs turned. The tide''s return, in the hand.


      <b>When it happens.</b> For now, on everything the wave strikes. Riptide must be in a slot.


      <b>The numbers.</b> 3 Shards. For now what the wave strikes stands with its back to you for 1.2 seconds: it begins nothing, and your first weapon blow on it is critical and ends it.


      <b>Works with.</b> The charged blade; Heavy Water; every mark that answers a critical blow.


      <b>Not built yet.</b> The second press, sending the wave out again with what it brought: for now what it brings is left turned away.


      <b>Example.</b> Riptide two soldiers in and cut the nearer at once: the first blow lands on its back, critical.'
  - Id: water.drowned
    Title: Drawn From the Drowned
    Group: 
    Body: '<b>What it does.</b> When a Soaked enemy dies its water runs over the floor to you as a line of foam and fills part of an empty flask. Soak, then kill.


      <b>When it happens.</b> Each time an enemy dies while Soaked, by any blow or spell, while you carry fewer flasks than your most.


      <b>The numbers.</b> 3 Shards. Each Soaked death fills a fifth of a flask: five fill one.


      <b>Works with.</b> Soaked, Broken Gourd, which it grows from, Poured Blade and Deep Well above it, and every spell that soaks a crowd.


      <b>Not built yet.</b> The line of foam seen running to you.


      <b>Example.</b> Whirlpool a pack and cut it down: by the last body a flask is back on your belt.'
  - Id: water.poured
    Title: Poured Blade
    Group: 
    Body: '<b>What it does.</b> You call a copy of yourself in water to stand at your side. It repeats each of your weapon blows a beat late, for a share of its strength, and soaks what it strikes.


      <b>When it happens.</b> From a spell slot: cast it with that slot''s button (hold L2 and a face button, or 1 to 4).


      <b>The numbers.</b> 4 Shards, 30 mana: Water''s larger spell (its Empower: 25 mana, 35% for 15 seconds). The copy lasts 12 seconds. Each weapon blow that lands is struck again 0.2 seconds later for 30% of its damage and lays Soaked. One copy at a time.


      <b>Works with.</b> Soaked, Heavy Water, Wellspring, Drawn From the Drowned, which it grows from.


      <b>Not built yet.</b> The copy''s blows carrying all of the blow''s stagger: for now they carry none.


      <b>Example.</b> Cast it as a brute is staggered: the finisher lands, then lands again for nearly a third.'
  - Id: water.poured.shape
    Title: 'Poured Blade: Poured on the Edge or Brother at Your Back'
    Group: 
    Body: '<b>What it does.</b> Opens two shapes of Poured Blade, chosen at any rest fire. <b>Poured on the Edge</b>, its first design: no copy; a flask is poured along the weapon, and for a while its reach is longer, every blow mends and soaks, and the last blow of a chain throws a wave. It costs a flask, not mana. <b>Brother at Your Back</b>, the fisher''s brothers: the copy stands behind you facing the other way and repeats your blows on whatever is behind you; for being surrounded.


      <b>When it happens.</b> Whenever you cast Poured Blade, as the shape it wears. Before this is bought, the copy at your side is cast.


      <b>The numbers.</b> 3 Shards. Poured on the Edge: for 12 seconds a tenth of your weapon damage comes back as health; while this shape is worn the last blow of every chain throws a wave 5 metres long and 60 degrees wide, 10 damage, 15 stagger and Soaked. Brother at Your Back: the copy as above.


      <b>Works with.</b> Heavy Water and every mark that answers the end of a chain (Poured on the Edge); Undertow and Blowhole''s Blown Out when surrounded (Brother at Your Back).


      <b>Not built yet.</b> Poured on the Edge''s price in flasks rather than mana, the weapon''s reach 40% longer, and its wave only within its 12 seconds; Brother at Your Back''s copy standing behind you and facing the other way.


      <b>Example.</b> Ringed by four soldiers, wear Brother at Your Back: what comes at your back is cut as you cut what is in front.'
  - Id: water.poured.master
    Title: 'Poured Blade: Mastered'
    Group: 
    Body: '<b>What it does.</b> Make a perfect dodge while it stands, and the copy steps into the blow you left and answers the attacker at full strength.


      <b>When it happens.</b> For now, every perfect dodge while Poured Blade is in a slot, once in 2 seconds.


      <b>The numbers.</b> 3 Shards. A copy left where you stood strikes everything within 2.3 metres of it 0.3 seconds later for all of your last blow''s damage and 30 stagger.


      <b>Works with.</b> The dodge; The Tide Turns'' Master; Heavy Water.


      <b>Not built yet.</b> Only while the copy stands, and the answer aimed at the attacker: for now any perfect dodge leaves the answering copy.


      <b>Example.</b> A brute swings at you and your copy: you roll clear and the copy answers it with your heavy blow.'
  - Id: water.well
    Title: Deep Well
    Group: 
    Body: '<b>What it does.</b> You carry one more flask, but a flask no longer mends you at once. It fills a well instead, and the well mends you only while you are landing blows.


      <b>When it happens.</b> Drinking fills the well; it pays out while a weapon blow of yours has landed in the last 3 seconds and you are not at full health. The well shows on the screen as Well.


      <b>The numbers.</b> 6 Shards. Four flasks. Each flask adds 70 to the well (more with Wellspring), and the well holds 140 at most. It pays 6 health a second.


      <b>Works with.</b> Wellspring (flasks hold half again as much), Drawn From the Drowned, which it grows from, Broken Gourd (the throw still mends 20 at once).


      <b>Example.</b> Drink early in a fight, then keep cutting: the health comes back as you fight, but stop and it waits.'
  - Id: water.sea
    Title: The Sea Rises
    Group: 
    Body: '<b>What it does.</b> While Wellspring burns, press the surge button again to flood the ground round you, spending a flask. For six seconds everything in the flood is kept Soaked, and every weapon blow you land runs out across the water as a wave. Then the sea draws back to you, dragging everything with it, and breaks where you face.


      <b>When it happens.</b> Light Wellspring with the surge button, then press the surge button again before it ends. With no flask left, it says so and waits.


      <b>The numbers.</b> A god''s gift, never sold; in the playtest it can be bought. The flood is 9 metres in radius where you stood. Each wave strikes everything within 3.6 metres of the enemy struck for 40% of the blow and 8 stagger, with Soaked. At the end, everything within 9 metres of you is dragged 4 metres in; 0.55 seconds later the sea breaks in a cone 9 metres long and 120 degrees wide: 55 damage and 90 stagger, a heavy blow.


      <b>Works with.</b> Wellspring, Soaked, Heavy Water, Drawn From the Drowned (for the flask), Deep Crack after the sea breaks, a second element''s Static or Chill.


      <b>Example.</b> Flood a crowd, cut into the middle of it for six seconds, then roll clear and face them as the sea breaks.'
  - Id: wind.unsteady
    Title: Unsteady
    Group: 
    Body: '<b>What it does.</b> Every blow of your weapon that lands knocks the enemy Unsteady, one stack at a time, up to five. An Unsteady enemy loses its balance sooner, is thrown further and turns more slowly, so you can circle behind it.


      <b>When it happens.</b> Always on once learned: every weapon blow that lands, light or heavy, while Wind is your first element. With Wind as your second element the weapon lays the first element''s affliction, and Unsteady comes from Gust, the charged blade and your R2 strike.


      <b>The numbers.</b> 2 Shards. One stack a blow, five at most, lasting 6 seconds. Each stack means 6% more stagger taken, a 15% longer shove and 8% slower turning: 30%, 75% and 40% at five. During Tailwind every blow lays one more.


      <b>Works with.</b> Rising Cut (five deep throws it into the air), Indrawn Breath (its burst spends the stacks), Against the Wall, Nothing Beneath, Carried Far, and the Carried Embers reaction when a burning enemy is knocked Unsteady.


      <b>Example.</b> Four light blows and a heavy on a soldier: five deep, it takes 30% more stagger from the heavy and is often broken by it.'
  - Id: wind.rising
    Title: Rising Cut
    Group: 
    Body: '<b>What it does.</b> A heavy blow on an enemy five deep in Unsteady throws it into the air. It hangs there helpless, and each blow you land on it up there holds it up a little longer, up to three. The throw spends the Unsteady.


      <b>When it happens.</b> A heavy blow or finisher that lands on an enemy carrying five Unsteady, at most twice a second.


      <b>The numbers.</b> 3 Shards. In the air for 1 second (elites and gods for 0.6 of it). Each of the first three blows on it up there adds 0.45 seconds. What is too heavy to lift reels for a second instead and takes 40 stagger.


      <b>Works with.</b> Unsteady, Lifting Wind and Sky Dance, which grow from it, Carried Far, Nothing Beneath, the deep strike Whirl Cut, and Thunder Lift and The Sky Finds Them on the Tempest branch.


      <b>Example.</b> Five deep, a soldier takes your heavy blow and goes up: two quick light blows keep it there while you set up the third.'
  - Id: wind.lifting
    Title: Lifting Wind
    Group: 
    Body: '<b>What it does.</b> A circle is drawn under the enemy you face and follows it for a breath; then a column of wind bursts up from it, striking as a heavy blow and throwing it into the air whatever its footing. What is too heavy to lift reels instead.


      <b>When it happens.</b> From a spell slot: cast it with that slot''s button (hold L2 and a face button, or 1 to 4). With no enemy within reach the column comes up 5 metres ahead of you, and the slot still waits.


      <b>The numbers.</b> 4 Shards, no mana: it waits 9 seconds after a cast, less with weapon play (its Empower: 7). The nearest enemy within 5 metres. The column rises 0.35 seconds after the cast, 2 metres in radius: 8 damage, 40 stagger, a heavy blow and one stack of Unsteady to all in it, and 0.8 seconds in the air.


      <b>Works with.</b> Rising Cut, which it grows from; Nothing Beneath; Sky Dance; Against the Wall (it is a spell striking); the charged blade: it lands, so your next three blows carry Wind.


      <b>Not built yet.</b> The hang of a full second (1.3 seconds with its Empower): the column''s lift is the form''s own 0.8 seconds.


      <b>Example.</b> An archer behind a shield: lift the archer, step in, and keep it up with your blows.'
  - Id: wind.lifting.shape
    Title: 'Lifting Wind: Dust Devil or Turned About'
    Group: 
    Body: '<b>What it does.</b> Opens two shapes of Lifting Wind, chosen at any rest fire. <b>Dust Devil</b>: the column wanders after enemies for a while, lifting the first it reaches and then the next. <b>Turned About</b>: the column spins its enemy round to face away from you, and your first blow on its back is critical; the shape for what cannot be lifted.


      <b>When it happens.</b> Whenever you cast Lifting Wind, as the shape it wears.


      <b>The numbers.</b> 3 Shards. Dust Devil: two columns, under the two nearest enemies, 0.6 seconds after the cast. Turned About: for 1.2 seconds the enemy begins no attack and the first weapon blow on it is critical, which ends it.


      <b>Works with.</b> Rising Cut and Nothing Beneath (Dust Devil in a pack); the heavy weapons and the colossus fights (Turned About).


      <b>Not built yet.</b> Dust Devil as one column wandering for 3 seconds (for now two rise at once), and Turned About not lifting, the enemy swung round in the column, half the time for an elite and a god''s next attack swung wide (for now it is lifted too).


      <b>Example.</b> A brute too heavy to lift: Turned About, and your next cut lands critical on its back.'
  - Id: wind.lifting.master
    Title: 'Lifting Wind: Mastered'
    Group: 
    Body: '<b>What it does.</b> Cast Lifting Wind on the enemy a perfect dodge has just taken you past, and it hangs twice as long.


      <b>When it happens.</b> A perfect dodge, then Lifting Wind within a second. Lifting Wind must be in a slot.


      <b>The numbers.</b> 3 Shards. Within a second of a perfect dodge, a Lifting Wind that is ready starts no wait. Each enemy the column takes is held up for 1.6 seconds.


      <b>Works with.</b> Passing Cut and Leaf on the Wind, which keep you dodging; Nothing Beneath.


      <b>Not built yet.</b> Only the enemy you dodged past hanging twice as long: for now every enemy the column takes hangs longer, after a dodge or not.


      <b>Example.</b> Roll through a duellist''s lunge, cast as you come out behind it: it goes up for twice the time and the next cast is free.'
  - Id: wind.skydance
    Title: Sky Dance
    Group: 
    Body: '<b>What it does.</b> You throw the enemy you face into the air and go up beside it. Five rings close on it, one after another: press the light attack as each closes for a cut in time, half again as hard. Then a lane follows the stick (or the cursor) for a moment, and you throw the enemy down along it. It bursts where it lands, harder for each cut in time. Nothing can strike you from the leap to the landing.


      <b>When it happens.</b> From a spell slot: cast it with that slot''s button (hold L2 and a face button, or 1 to 4). It needs an enemy faced within 6 metres that is not still reeling from the last dance; otherwise it is not cast and no mana is spent. The heavy attack throws at once.


      <b>The numbers.</b> 4 Shards, 45 mana (its Empower: 35, and six rings). A ring every 0.34 seconds; a press in the last part of its closing is in time. Each cut deals 10 damage, 15 in time; the first lays a stack of Unsteady. The throw goes 6 metres. The landing deals 20 damage, and 6 more for each cut in time (50 at five), with 60 stagger as a heavy blow, to the one thrown and to everything within 3 metres, which is pushed 3 metres away. What cannot be lifted is danced with on the ground.


      <b>Works with.</b> Rising Cut, which it grows from; Nothing Beneath; Against the Wall (each cut is a spell striking); Unsteady.


      <b>Example.</b> Dance a brute up, land all five cuts in time, and throw it down into the soldiers behind it: 50 to each.'
  - Id: wind.skydance.shape
    Title: 'Sky Dance: Carried Off or Two Rise'
    Group: 
    Body: '<b>What it does.</b> Opens two shapes of Sky Dance, chosen at any rest fire. <b>Carried Off</b>: there is no throw; you carry the enemy down the lane and drop it on another, and both take the burst. <b>Two Rise</b>: the enemy faced and the nearest other both go up, and the rings take turns between them.


      <b>When it happens.</b> Whenever you cast Sky Dance, as the shape it wears.


      <b>The numbers.</b> 3 Shards. Carried Off: the lane is 8 metres. Two Rise: the first cut throws up everything within 3 metres of the enemy for 1.5 seconds.


      <b>Works with.</b> Against the Wall and Indrawn Breath (Carried Off into a crowd); Nothing Beneath (Two Rise keeps two up).


      <b>Not built yet.</b> Carried Off carrying the enemy and dropping it on another (for now it is thrown further), and Two Rise''s rings taking turns between two (for now the second is only lifted).


      <b>Example.</b> Two soldiers side by side: Two Rise takes both up, and the landing bursts on both.'
  - Id: wind.skydance.master
    Title: 'Sky Dance: Mastered'
    Group: 
    Body: '<b>What it does.</b> Land all five cuts in time, and you come down with Tailwind lit for four seconds at no cost.


      <b>When it happens.</b> Sky Dance strikes. Sky Dance must be in a slot.


      <b>The numbers.</b> 3 Shards. For 4 seconds your dodge carries 30% further and is safe 25% longer, and you move 15% faster: Tailwind''s own gifts, once a dance.


      <b>Works with.</b> Passing Cut, Leaf on the Wind, Closing Circle: the fight goes on in motion after the landing.


      <b>Not built yet.</b> Only when all five cuts were in time, and Tailwind itself lit (its own hanging blows and its Unsteady): for now any dance that strikes gives the dodge and the speed.


      <b>Example.</b> Five in time, thrown into a pack: you land and roll through them at once, further and safer.'
  - Id: wind.lift
    Title: Carried Far
    Group: 
    Body: '<b>What it does.</b> Carried Far: every reaction with Unsteady in it throws what it strikes out from where it happened.


      <b>When it happens.</b> Whenever Unsteady reacts on an enemy with the other affliction it carries (Carried Embers with Burn, Windthrow and the rest).


      <b>The numbers.</b> 3 Shards. Every enemy within 2.5 metres of the reaction is thrown 1.5 metres away from it.


      <b>Works with.</b> Carrying a second element: every reaction of Wind''s ten; Against the Wall, for the throw into something.


      <b>Not built yet.</b> The reactions reaching half again as far (it needs a stat for a reaction''s reach).


      <b>Example.</b> Wind and Fire on a soldier in a crowd: Carried Embers goes off and the soldiers round it are thrown back.'
  - Id: wind.nothing
    Title: Nothing Beneath
    Group: 
    Body: '<b>What it does.</b> An enemy in the air stays up as long as you keep striking it, each blow there gives double mana, and your blows no longer drop it after three. The price: your weapon is weaker against an enemy that is not Unsteady.


      <b>When it happens.</b> Always on once learned. The longer hang and the mana come with each blow that lands on an enemy in the air.


      <b>The numbers.</b> 6 Shards. Up to 23 blows hold an enemy in the air, not three; the first adds 0.45 seconds and each after a little less, about 3 seconds more in all. Blows on an enemy in the air give twice their mana. Weapon damage is 15% lower, back to full against an Unsteady enemy.


      <b>Works with.</b> Rising Cut, Closing Circle, Lifting Wind, Sky Dance, Unsteady.


      <b>Example.</b> Lift a soldier and keep cutting: it hangs for four seconds while your mana bar fills twice as fast.'
  - Id: wind.devotion
    Title: On the Wind
    Group: 
    Body: '<b>What it does.</b> On the Wind, Wind''s Devotion: all in on Wind only. Your spells have no wind-up and can be cast in the middle of a dodge or a swing without ending it, and a spell cast in a dodge carries you further along it. Nearly all of the fight is spent in motion.


      <b>When it happens.</b> Only while Wind is carried twice (all in). Then always.


      <b>The numbers.</b> 6 Shards. A spell cast in a dodge carries you 2 metres further. All in, L2 with R2 is the deep strike, Whirl Cut: the crescent becomes a small whirlwind that holds the first enemy it reaches in the air for a second.


      <b>Works with.</b> Every spell of the tree; Passing Cut and Leaf on the Wind; the deep strike.


      <b>Not built yet.</b> Spells with no wind-up, cast in a dodge or a swing without ending it, and the 2 metres added to a dodge cast in. For now every dodge carries 30% further.


      <b>Example.</b> Roll at a pack, cast Indrawn Breath in the roll, and come out of it with the pack heaped in front of you.'
  - Id: wind.passing
    Title: Passing Cut
    Group: 
    Body: '<b>What it does.</b> Where a dodge ends, a cut of wind strikes everything close to you and leaves it Unsteady.


      <b>When it happens.</b> At the end of every dodge, at most twice a second.


      <b>The numbers.</b> 3 Shards. Everything within 2.2 metres of where you stop takes 10 damage, 8 stagger and one stack of Unsteady.


      <b>Works with.</b> Closing Circle and Turned Aside, which grow from it; Leaf on the Wind; Tailwind''s longer dodge.


      <b>Not built yet.</b> The cut along the path you passed through, each enemy passed unable to turn for a moment: for now the cut comes where you stop.


      <b>Example.</b> Roll into the middle of three soldiers: all three are cut and Unsteady before you swing.'
  - Id: wind.circle
    Title: Closing Circle
    Group: 
    Body: '<b>What it does.</b> You run a full ring round the enemy you face. When the ring closes, the wind inside it rises: everything within is struck, knocked five deep in Unsteady and thrown into the air. You end where you began, facing in, and nothing can strike you while you run.


      <b>When it happens.</b> From a spell slot: cast it with that slot''s button (hold L2 and a face button, or 1 to 4). It needs an enemy faced within 5 metres; with none, it is not cast and nothing is spent.


      <b>The numbers.</b> 4 Shards, no mana: it waits 9 seconds after a cast, less with weapon play (its Empower: 7, and 1.5 seconds in the air). The ring is as wide as the gap to the enemy, 2 to 3 metres in radius. The run takes 0.7 seconds and the ring snaps shut 0.2 seconds later. All inside take 6 damage, 10 stagger and five stacks of Unsteady, and hang in the air for 1.2 seconds. What cannot be lifted reels instead.


      <b>Works with.</b> Passing Cut, which it grows from; Rising Cut and Nothing Beneath; Indrawn Breath, whose burst spends what it laid.


      <b>Not built yet.</b> Nothing can strike you for the whole run; the design asks for the first half only.


      <b>Example.</b> Two soldiers flank a brute: circle the brute and all three go up five deep.'
  - Id: wind.circle.shape
    Title: 'Closing Circle: Half Circle or Wide Circle'
    Group: 
    Body: '<b>What it does.</b> Opens two shapes of Closing Circle, chosen at any rest fire. <b>Half Circle</b>: you end on the enemy''s far side, behind it; nothing is lifted, and your first blow on its back is critical. <b>Wide Circle</b>: you run round a group, and the column takes everyone inside, but lifts each for only a moment.


      <b>When it happens.</b> Whenever you cast Closing Circle, as the shape it wears.


      <b>The numbers.</b> 3 Shards. Half Circle: a step through the enemy within 5 metres, 6 damage and 10 stagger, and for 1.5 seconds your next blow is critical. Wide Circle: an enemy faced within 7 metres, a ring up to 4 metres in radius, and 0.6 seconds in the air.


      <b>Works with.</b> Turned About (another way behind it); Indrawn Breath and Against the Wall (Wide Circle round a crowd).


      <b>Not built yet.</b> Half Circle running half the ring (for now it steps through the enemy), and the Empower''s longer hang reaching Wide Circle''s short one (an Empower''s numbers are set after the shape''s, so empowered it hangs 1.5 seconds).


      <b>Example.</b> A shield-bearer facing you: Half Circle, and the first cut lands critical on its unguarded back.'
  - Id: wind.circle.master
    Title: 'Closing Circle: Mastered'
    Group: 
    Body: '<b>What it does.</b> Started in the instant a blow would land on you, Closing Circle counts as a perfect dodge, and the ring is run round the attacker wherever it stands within eight metres.


      <b>When it happens.</b> For now, every cast of Closing Circle. It must be in a slot.


      <b>The numbers.</b> 3 Shards. What a perfect dodge gives: 12 mana and 1.5 seconds off every running cooldown.


      <b>Works with.</b> Lifting Wind''s Master and the other marks a perfect dodge sets off; Leaf on the Wind.


      <b>Not built yet.</b> The timing (started as a blow would land) and the ring run round the attacker within 8 metres; for now every cast gives the dodge''s mana and cuts.


      <b>Example.</b> A spearman thrusts: start the circle into it, and you run round it as the spear passes, mana and cooldowns paid.'
  - Id: wind.turned
    Title: Turned Aside
    Group: 
    Body: '<b>What it does.</b> A perfect guard throws everyone near you back and leaves the attacker three deeper in Unsteady.


      <b>When it happens.</b> A perfect guard: press the guard button just before a blow lands.


      <b>The numbers.</b> 3 Shards. Every enemy within 4 metres is pushed 3 metres away. Three stacks of Unsteady on the attacker.


      <b>Works with.</b> Bag of Winds and Leaf on the Wind, which grow from it; Rising Cut; Against the Wall.


      <b>Not built yet.</b> A thrown attack sent back to its thrower.


      <b>Example.</b> Ringed by four soldiers, perfect-guard the first swing: the ring is thrown back and the one who swung is three deep.'
  - Id: wind.bag
    Title: Bag of Winds
    Group: 
    Body: '<b>What it does.</b> You untie a bag of wind at your hip. Each blow you perfect-guard or perfect-dodge is caught in it, three at most, and thrown things that come near are caught too. Press again, and it opens: a cone that strikes harder for each wind held, and every thrown thing flies back at its thrower.


      <b>When it happens.</b> From a spell slot: cast it with that slot''s button (hold L2 and a face button, or 1 to 4). Then each perfect guard or perfect dodge while the bag holds a wind.


      <b>The numbers.</b> 4 Shards, no mana: it waits 10 seconds after a cast (its Empower: 8). The bag holds three winds, shown on the screen as Winds. Each perfect guard or perfect dodge lets one out as a cone of 7 metres and 60 degrees: 12 damage, 25 stagger and a stack of Unsteady.


      <b>Works with.</b> Turned Aside, which it grows from; Lifting Wind''s and Closing Circle''s Masters (more perfect dodges); Indrawn Breath.


      <b>Not built yet.</b> The bag as designed: open 8 seconds, each caught blow throwing its attacker back 2 metres and kept, thrown things caught, and a second press (or the time''s end) opening it as one cone of 12 damage and 25 stagger for each wind held, the thrown things flying back. For now the cast fills the bag and each perfect guard or dodge lets a wind out at once. The Empower''s fourth wind.


      <b>Example.</b> Cast it as a brute begins its combo: guard three blows perfectly, and three cones throw it back down the hall.'
  - Id: wind.bag.shape
    Title: 'Bag of Winds: Kept Wind or Loose Neck'
    Group: 
    Body: '<b>What it does.</b> Opens two shapes of Bag of Winds, chosen at any rest fire. <b>Kept Wind</b>: the bag does not open by itself; it keeps its winds for a long while, to be opened when you choose, such as on a staggered enemy. <b>Loose Neck</b>: nothing is kept; each wind leaves at once as a free Gust toward the enemy you next face.


      <b>When it happens.</b> Whenever you cast Bag of Winds, as the shape it wears; Loose Neck on every perfect guard and perfect dodge while it is slotted.


      <b>The numbers.</b> 3 Shards. Kept Wind: 20 seconds. Loose Neck: each perfect guard or perfect dodge throws a Gust, a cone of 5 metres and 70 degrees, 8 damage, 20 stagger and two Unsteady; a guarded attacker is also thrown 3 metres.


      <b>Works with.</b> Turned Aside and Rising Cut (Loose Neck''s Unsteady); a staggered enemy (Kept Wind).


      <b>Not built yet.</b> Kept Wind does nothing beyond the bag yet: it waits for the bag that keeps its winds. Loose Neck''s gust turned toward the enemy you next face (for now toward the one caught).


      <b>Example.</b> Loose Neck against a pack of duellists: every perfect guard throws a gust into them.'
  - Id: wind.bag.master
    Title: 'Bag of Winds: Mastered'
    Group: 
    Body: '<b>What it does.</b> Catch three winds within three seconds, and the bag bursts by itself as a whirlwind: everything within six metres goes into the air.


      <b>When it happens.</b> For now, a perfect dodge, at most once every 10 seconds. Bag of Winds must be in a slot.


      <b>The numbers.</b> 3 Shards. Everything within 6 metres of you goes into the air for a second.


      <b>Works with.</b> Rising Cut and Nothing Beneath, for the enemies in the air; Lifting Wind.


      <b>Not built yet.</b> Three winds caught within 3 seconds as what bursts the bag; for now a perfect dodge raises the whirlwind.


      <b>Example.</b> Dodge a brute''s swing perfectly in a crowd: everything round you goes up, ready for the cuts.'
  - Id: wind.leaf
    Title: Leaf on the Wind
    Group: 
    Body: '<b>What it does.</b> The dodge costs no stamina. It spends a breath of wind instead: you hold three, and time and blows win them back. With no breath left you cannot dodge. The price: you take more damage.


      <b>When it happens.</b> Always on once learned. Every dodge spends a breath; the breaths come back as you fight.


      <b>The numbers.</b> 6 Shards. Three breaths at most, shown on the screen as Breath. One comes back every 2 seconds while you hold fewer than three, and one for every three blows you land. You take 20% more damage from every blow.


      <b>Works with.</b> Passing Cut, Closing Circle, Bag of Winds, Tailwind''s longer, safer dodge.


      <b>Example.</b> Against a fast duellist, dodge three times in a row, then land three blows: a breath is back before the next swing comes.'
  - Id: wind.wall
    Title: Against the Wall
    Group: 
    Body: '<b>What it does.</b> Any enemy you throw that meets a wall, a pillar or another enemy is struck hard, harder for each Unsteady it carries; when two bodies meet, both are. The payoff every throw in the tree waits for.


      <b>When it happens.</b> For now, every time a spell of yours strikes an enemy: Gust, any spell from your slots, and the spells your marks throw.


      <b>The numbers.</b> 3 Shards. As designed: 15 damage, 6 more for each Unsteady, and 30 stagger. For now a burst 1.6 metres in radius on each enemy a spell strikes: 6 damage, 15 stagger and one stack of Unsteady.


      <b>Works with.</b> Gust and its Long Gust, Indrawn Breath''s All One Way, Sky Dance, Turned Aside, the charged blade''s Gale Edge.


      <b>Not built yet.</b> The throw meeting something (a wall, a pillar, another enemy): for now the burst comes wherever a spell strikes.


      <b>Example.</b> Gust three soldiers in a row: each takes the gust and a burst, and they shake each other with theirs.'
  - Id: wind.base
    Title: Gust
    Group: 
    Body: '<b>What it does.</b> Gust, Wind''s own spell, comes with the element and is never bought. A rush of air runs out ahead of you, striking everything in it, knocking it Unsteady and throwing it straight down the wind.


      <b>When it happens.</b> From a spell slot: cast it with that slot''s button (hold L2 and a face button, or 1 to 4). Carrying Wind, it is always yours to put in a slot.


      <b>The numbers.</b> Given with Wind. No mana: it waits 6 seconds after a cast, less with weapon play; its Empower makes that 4.5. A cone 5 metres long and 70 degrees wide: 8 damage, 20 stagger and two stacks of Unsteady, and everything in it is thrown 3 metres.


      <b>Works with.</b> Its Empower, its two shapes and its Master; Against the Wall; the charged blade, which its landing charges with Wind.


      <b>Not built yet.</b> The Empower''s third stack of Unsteady: the base spell is cast by Wind''s kit, which takes only the Empower''s shorter wait.


      <b>Example.</b> A soldier at the edge of a drop: Gust, and it is gone.'
  - Id: wind.base.shape
    Title: 'Gust: Downburst or Long Gust'
    Group: 
    Body: '<b>What it does.</b> Opens two shapes of Gust, chosen at any rest fire. <b>Downburst</b>: the wind comes down from above and spreads as a ring, throwing everything near outward; aim it at your feet to clear a ring round you. <b>Long Gust</b>: a narrow lane that throws what it takes far, for throwing one enemy into a wall, a pit or its friends.


      <b>When it happens.</b> Whenever you cast Gust, as the shape it wears. Before this is bought, the plain gust is cast.


      <b>The numbers.</b> 3 Shards. Downburst: everything within 3 metres of you, 8 damage, 20 stagger, two Unsteady, thrown 2.5 metres outward. Long Gust: a lane 2 metres wide and 10 long, 8 damage, 20 stagger, two Unsteady, thrown 5 metres.


      <b>Works with.</b> Against the Wall (Long Gust into a wall); Passing Cut and Turned Aside when surrounded (Downburst).


      <b>Not built yet.</b> Downburst aimed at a point up to 6 metres away; for now it always comes down on you.


      <b>Example.</b> Ringed by four soldiers, Downburst throws them all back two deep. An archer behind a line: Long Gust carries it off its ledge.'
  - Id: wind.base.master
    Title: 'Gust: Mastered'
    Group: 
    Body: '<b>What it does.</b> Cast Gust in the instant an enemy''s attack mark shows, and the gust turns its blow aside into empty air.


      <b>When it happens.</b> For now, every enemy Gust strikes. Gust must be in a slot.


      <b>The numbers.</b> 3 Shards. Each enemy struck flinches: what it had begun is broken, unless it is steadfast. As designed elites'' blows come 0.4 seconds late instead, and gods are not turned.


      <b>Works with.</b> Every shape of Gust; Against the Wall.


      <b>Not built yet.</b> The instant of the attack mark as the timing (it needs a trigger on an enemy''s wind-up), and the elites'' late blow: for now any gust that lands makes its enemies flinch.


      <b>Example.</b> A brute''s red overhead begins: Gust, and the blow falls on nothing.'
  - Id: wind.indrawn
    Title: Indrawn Breath
    Group: 
    Body: '<b>What it does.</b> You draw in your breath, and everything near is dragged into one place before you. Then the breath bursts out of that place, striking all of them as a heavy blow and spending each enemy''s Unsteady, harder for every stack.


      <b>When it happens.</b> From a spell slot: cast it with that slot''s button (hold L2 and a face button, or 1 to 4).


      <b>The numbers.</b> 4 Shards, no mana: it waits 11 seconds after a cast, less with weapon play (its Empower: 9, and it draws from 8.5 metres). The point is 2 metres ahead, or on an enemy that close. For 0.5 seconds everything within 7 metres of it is dragged most of the way in. Then the burst: 10 damage, 25 stagger, a heavy blow and two stacks of Unsteady to each, and each enemy''s Unsteady goes off for 6 damage and 8 stagger a stack.


      <b>Works with.</b> Against the Wall, which it grows from; Closing Circle (five deep inside the ring), Rising Cut; Catching Fire with Fire carried, since it bunches a crowd.


      <b>Example.</b> Archers spread round a room, each a few deep: draw them all to one spot, and every stack they carry bursts at once.'
  - Id: wind.indrawn.shape
    Title: 'Indrawn Breath: Held Breath or All One Way'
    Group: 
    Body: '<b>What it does.</b> Opens two shapes of Indrawn Breath, chosen at any rest fire. <b>Held Breath</b>: the draw lasts as long as the button is held, and the point walks with you; let go to burst. <b>All One Way</b>: the burst does not scatter them; all of them are thrown together the way you face. Gather a crowd, then throw it into a wall.


      <b>When it happens.</b> Whenever you cast Indrawn Breath, as the shape it wears.


      <b>The numbers.</b> 3 Shards. Held Breath: up to 2 seconds. All One Way: each enemy the burst strikes is thrown 5 metres straight away from you.


      <b>Works with.</b> Against the Wall (All One Way), Sky Dance, Bag of Winds.


      <b>Not built yet.</b> Held Breath held on its button, the point walking with you (for now the draw always lasts the full 2 seconds); All One Way''s burst not scattering them first.


      <b>Example.</b> Draw a crowd into a heap, then All One Way throws the heap into the wall behind it.'
  - Id: wind.indrawn.master
    Title: 'Indrawn Breath: Mastered'
    Group: 
    Body: '<b>What it does.</b> Cast Indrawn Breath in the middle of a dodge: the draw''s point rides with you to where the dodge ends, and the burst spends no Unsteady, so every stack stays for the next blow.


      <b>When it happens.</b> For now, every enemy the burst strikes. Indrawn Breath must be in a slot.


      <b>The numbers.</b> 3 Shards. Each enemy struck is given two stacks of Unsteady back after the burst.


      <b>Works with.</b> Rising Cut (back toward five), Closing Circle.


      <b>Not built yet.</b> A spell cast in the middle of a dodge as the timing, the point riding with you, and the burst spending nothing; for now each enemy gets two stacks back.


      <b>Example.</b> Roll through a pack and draw it in behind you: the burst lands and the pack stays Unsteady for your next heavy.'
  - Id: wind.remembers
    Title: The Wind Remembers
    Group: 
    Body: '<b>What it does.</b> While your surge lasts, every weapon blow you land leaves its cut hanging in the air where it fell, up to sixteen. When the surge ends, time slows and all of them fall again, one on the heels of the next, each half as hard as the blow it remembers.


      <b>When it happens.</b> Light the surge with the surge button (a tap of L2, or F). The cuts fall the moment it ends.


      <b>The numbers.</b> A god''s gift, never sold; in the playtest it can be bought. Sixteen cuts at most; past that, each new blow is added to the lightest cut hanging. Each falls 1.4 metres round where it was struck for half the blow''s damage, 10 stagger and one stack of Unsteady. Tailwind lasts 10 seconds for 35 mana.


      <b>Works with.</b> Tailwind, Against the Wall (each falling cut is a spell striking), Nothing Beneath, Rising Cut.


      <b>Example.</b> Light Tailwind and cut a pack sixteen times: as it ends, sixteen cuts fall on them again at half strength.'
